window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6301,"title":"Chapter 6301: Chapter 6299: The Complexity of Human Nature","paragraphs":["With his Devourer Scepter, Jie Tian flitted toward Chu Feng while attacking the chains with his black aura. The chains didn’t shatter under his attack, but they began to corrode.","Long Zhuoyan quickly changed her hand seal to unleash stronger flames to melt the chains.","“What do you mean by this?”","Long Zhuoyan took Chu Feng over to Jie Tian’s side after breaking free of the chains. She was fearless despite knowing that Jie Tian’s scepter was a formidable treasure.","“Come with me, Chu Feng.”","Jie Tian released a black aura that enveloped Chu Feng and Long Zhuoyan. This black aura didn’t hurt them; it merely transported them at an incredible speed.","“What’s with this brat?” Long Zhuoyan glanced at Chu Feng with calm eyes.","She was confident that neither Jie Tianran nor Jie Tian could stop her if she made up her mind to leave right away. She was merely confused as to why Jie Tian was helping Chu Feng, for she had heard about their enmity.","Chu Feng was also confused as to why Jie Tian was helping him, but the latter’s earlier words suggested that it might have something to do with his aunt.","“What happened to my aunt?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Tian didn’t answer the question. He continued rushing ahead, bringing Chu Feng into the forbidden land with his access token.","Chu Feng immediately understood what happened when he saw the collapsed on the ground. They were all familiar faces—Jie Shanxian, Jie Tiannian, and Daoist Starseizer.","Jie Shanxian was in a horrendous state, but Daoist Starseizer and Jie Tiannian were doing far worse.","Chu Feng felt as if a sharp knife had been stabbed into his heart.","“Is it Jie Tianran’s doing?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, I did it,” Jie Tianran’s voice boomed.","Chu Feng looked back and saw resplendent clouds swiftly heading in their direction. To be exact, these weren’t clouds like multiple layers of formidable spirit power protecting Jie Tianran.","“Jie Tianran, you harmed even your fellow brethren, senior, and daughter! How can you call yourself a human?!” Chu Feng angrily bellowed.","But Jie Tianran was unfazed. “Chu Feng, they landed in that plight because of you. You are the one who should be taking responsibility for this.”","A terrifying surge of spirit power descended from the sky upon Chu Feng and the others.","Boom!","Long Zhuoyan unleashed fearsome flames that clashed with the spirit power. The two energies intertwined and formed fiery clouds that swiftly enveloped everything but Chu Feng’s group.","Long Zhuoyan glanced at Chu Feng and said, “We should get going.”","She enveloped Jie Shanxian, Jie Tiannian, and Daoist Starseizer with her spirit power.","“Take him with us too.” Chu Feng gestured toward Jie Tian.","Long Zhuoyan extended her spirit power to Jie Tian too, but the latter channeled his black aura to stop her.","“I won’t leave with you,” Jie Tian replied.","“Are you tired of living? If he has no qualms about doing this to your mother, he won’t hesitate to do the same to you too,” Chu Feng said.","“I am my mother’s son; I cannot turn a blind eye to her plight. But my grandfather was the one who taught me everything I know. I cannot betray him. I, Jie Tian, will live and die as a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!”","Jie Tian walked up to Jie Tiannian and kneeled on the ground. “Mother, I don’t think I can repay you for giving birth to me anymore. If there is a next life, I will serve you like an ox to repay this debt.”","Jie Tiannian was so weak that she couldn’t even speak. She looked at her kneeling son and took in his disfigured face and his cracked soul. Two streams of warm tears flowed down her cheeks.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng’s surroundings suddenly retreated. Long Zhuoyan was taking him away with her.","“He’s channeling that scepter with his life force. He won’t survive even if that old thing spares his life,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Chu Feng felt uncomfortable. He had always viewed Jie Tian as an unscrupulous person, just like Jie Tianran. Were it not for today’s events, he would have never known that Jie Tian could put his life on the line to defy the grandfather he respected so much to save his mother.","Human nature was truly complex.","The flames around Long Zhuoyan had faded, replaced by a thin layer of spirit power that could breach any formation.","Jie Tianran didn’t pursue them; Instead, he retracted his spirit power before descending to Jie Tian’s side. His face was ghastly pale, suggesting that he had paid a hefty price for his earlier burst of power.","“You have acted foolishly, Tian’er.” Jie Tianran’s wrathful eyes were surprisingly devoid of killing intent.","Remaining on his knees, Jie Tian kowtowed vehemently to Jie Tianran. “I have let down grandfather’s expectations in me. Please punish me for my actions.”","What happened next shocked Jie Tian.","Jie Tianran pulled him up and handed him a black pill.","“What are you waiting for? Eat it!” Jie Tianran stuffed the pill into Jie Tian’s mouth. “It’s a relief that the Devourer Emperor was prepared for this situation. This pill can alleviate the Devourer Scepter’s backlash and save your life. Otherwise, even I can’t save your life.","“Tian’er, how can you be so foolish as to risk your life to go against me? I gave you that scepter for self-protection, not to seek death!”","The Devourer Scepter’s backlash shouldn’t have cost Jie Tian’s life. He landed in this plight because he desperately channeled the Devourer Scepter to attain more power to oppose Jie Tianran. Needless to say, that worsened his backlash.","“Grandfather, w-why are you saving me?” Jie Tian looked at Jie Tianran in confusion.","His body was still gradually weakening, but the pill he had just taken had transformed into a surge of energy that kept him together. He might have a chance of surviving this ordeal at this rate.","“You’re my grandson. How can I leave you in the lurch?” Jie Tianran replied.","Jie Tian was taken aback. There were words he wanted to say but struggled to vocalize.","Jie Tianran saw through Jie Tian’s thoughts. “You’re confused why I am saving you despite having no qualms about killing your mother. Did you think I truly intended to kill your mother?","“I’m merely disappointed in her for siding with an outsider, and I thought this was a chance for you to temper your character. It’d suffice as long as you can harden your heart to be vicious when the situation calls for it. I would have stopped you if you made a move. No matter what, she’s still my daughter.","“Your mother’s afflicted with a gu that only I can lift. Now that Chu Feng has taken her, I fear that she won’t be able to survive anymore.”","Jie Tianran let out a worried sigh.","Jie Tian was stunned. He realized that he had committed a grievous mistake and regretted his actions."]},{"number":6302,"title":"Chapter 6302: Chapter 6300: There’s Still a Way to Rescue Them","paragraphs":["Chapter 6300: There’s Still a Way to Rescue Them","Jie Tian wanted to say something, but he couldn’t even muster the strength to speak anymore. The backlash was still siphoning away his life force. The only thing keeping him alive was the pill fighting the backlash.","Still, he had no idea whether he would survive this ordeal. It didn’t take long before he lost consciousness.","Jie Tianran was prepared for this.","He took out a transparent bowl, which enlarged as soon as it left his hand to cover Jie Tian. Then, he planted eight flags emanating the Ancient Era’s aura around the bowl. The flags began fluttering as they absorbed the nearby natural energies, which they manifested into an aura and infused into the bowl.","Once all was done, Jie Tianran exhaled deeply before plopping down on the floor in exhaustion. He was in a terribly weakened state.","“This is troublesome. I didn’t expect Chu Feng to find such a backing,” Jie Tianran murmured worriedly.","It was not that he didn’t want to give chase but that he had no confidence in defeating the other party.","“Do you know anything about that woman? Her flames don’t appear to be pure spirit power. I suspect that they are mixed with her bloodline power, granting them incomparable ferocity,” Jie Tianran asked.","“That’s Long Zhuoyan. She’s known as the Dragon Clan’s demoness and one of the top ten Ancient Era’s world spiritists. She was not bragging. At her peak, she could have obliterated your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion across a galaxy. Fortunately, she was severely affected by what happened in the Ancient Era, causing her cultivation to severely regress. Otherwise, it’ll be tough to deal with her unless I make a full recovery.”","That left Jie Tianran even more worried.","The means of one of the Ancient Era’s top ten world spiritists were not to be scoffed at. Just the thought of what she was capable of left him with chills.","“Don’t worry. I have crossed paths with Long Zhuoyan; I know a bit about her. There’s no way she would become Chu Feng’s backing. It’s probably just a temporary exchange of interests. Her escape suggests that she has realized that you aren’t that easy either.","“All Ancient Era’s experts realize that the world of cultivation has been swept by huge changes; its environment is no longer suited for cultivation. If she wishes to recover as soon as possible, she would have to enter the Ninth Galaxy as soon as possible.”","Jie Tianran asked, “Are you sure that she’ll leave and not protect Chu Feng?”","The voice inside his body replied, “She was nicknamed demoness because of her selfishness. There’s no reason for her to stall her own future over him. With her talent, there is a chance she could become the strongest world spiritist in this generation if she grasped the initiative.”","“It sounds like she harbors wild ambitions. Will she be a potential enemy in the future?” Jie Tianran asked.","“She was a fearsome foe in the past, but her cultivation has regressed. While recovering one’s cultivation is much easier than cultivating from scratch, it shouldn’t be tough for you to surpass her given your talent and with my support. But that’s a thing for the future. For now, we can only hope that she’ll leave as soon as possible and not get involved with God’s Era,” the voice said.","“She won’t have a chance to recover to her peak if she insists on getting involved. I have already claimed the initiative in God’s Era. It shall become my foundation to dominating the world of cultivation. She’s courting death if she trifles with me despite her regressed cultivation,” Jie Tianran declared with confidence in his deep, old eyes.","He was intimidated by Long Zhuoyan’s title as one of the top Ancient Era’s world spiritists, but according to the voice in his body, she was nowhere near her peak now. Her decision to escape reflected her leak of confidence.","At the very least, she wasn’t that big of a threat just yet.","With that, he took out a couple of pills, popped them into their mouth, and began meditating to recuperate from his injuries.","...","Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng escaped into a teleportation passageway.","A layer of recovery spirit power enveloped Jie Tiannian and the others, but the three of them showed no signs of recovering. On the contrary, their life force was still gradually leaking away. The one with the worst injuries was none other than his aunt, Jie Tiannian.","He hadn’t spent much time with his aunt, but the latter’s consideration warmed his heart. He rarely felt such concern from his kin. He didn’t expect her to be reduced to this state on their next meeting.","“Is she truly that little pervert’s daughter?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Yes, she’s my aunt,” Chu Feng replied.","“They have been afflicted with severe gu poison. That little pervert has some means, and he sure is vicious to do this to his own daughter. But you don’t have to worry. There’s a way to save them once you return to the Totem Dragon Clan, and it will depend on your little friends’ means,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“My friends?” Chu Feng was confused.","“I’m talking about the Totem Dragon Clansmen.”","“Will I require that help?”","“Haa. Neither that little pervert nor the gu he planted in those three is worth a mention to me, but it is tricky for me now. Cultivation is indeed important. My cultivation has regressed so much that things that were previously easy to me have become arduous,” Long Zhuoyan explained.","“Big sister, how confident are you at lifting the gu? Is there anything I can do to help? Can you tell me the method to do so? If it’s inconvenient for you, I can do it myself too,” Chu Feng said.","He was indebted to these three people, not to mention that Jie Tiannian was his aunt. He had to save them by hook or by crook.","Instead of directly answering the question, Long Zhuoyan spoke in a tone reminiscent of narrating a story, “I don’t remember what happened. I was already out of my shell by the time I woke up. I am aware of means to protect the soul, but that’s an escape means used only in times of desperation.","“Furthermore, my soul is severely impaired, which led to a significant regression in my cultivation. From that, I understood that I must have encountered an extremely dangerous situation and was lucky to have escaped with my life.","“This gave the Totem Dragon Clan the chance to exploit my shell. I was far weaker back then than I was now; I couldn’t do anything except for catching my breath. Naturally, I don’t have the means to reclaim my shell either. That’s also partly the reason I spared the Totem Dragon Clan at your plea.","“I have accepted the fact that someone is bound to find my shell, and anyone in the Totem Dragon Clan’s place is bound to make use of it. The cultivators of your era grew by picking up things left by us, Ancient Era’s cultivators, and similarly, we, Ancient Era’s cultivators, also grew up picking up the treasures left behind by Immemorial Era’s cultivators. It’s understandable.","“At least the Totem Dragon Clan has some conscience. While using my shell to enhance their bloodlines, they also worship me as their ancestor. They would pay their respects to me several times each year, which is why I know far more about the Totem Dragon Clan than your friends. They have forged quite a few treasures using my body, and they are currently stored in their forbidden land.","“I am from a True Dragon Clansman. The items forged out of my body harness extraordinary true dragon energy. If you can extract the true dragon energy from those treasures and refine it with a formation, you should be able to lift the gu poison with ease,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Big sister, you are from the True Dragon Clan. You should have true dragon energy in you too, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“I do, but...”","“It’s your cultivation?” Chu Feng finally pieced the clues together. It was not without a reason that Long Zhuoyan kept mentioning cultivation throughout the conversation.","“Indeed. My little brother is a sharp one. Yes, it’s my cultivation. Given my cultivation back then, the true dragon energy in my shell is far stronger than what I have in me right now. Don’t blame me for not helping you. It wasn’t easy for me to survive. Even now, I’m still in a severely weakened state. I don’t have the luxury to arbitrarily use my true dragon energy to save others. You understand, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked with a smile.","“Of course. Big sister, you have already helped me a lot. I’ll repay you in the future,” Chu Feng replied.","“I believe you, little brother.” Long Zhuoyan’s smile widened."]},{"number":6303,"title":"Chapter 6303: Chapter 6301: My Eyes Are Opened","paragraphs":["Chapter 6301: My Eyes Are Opened","Meanwhile, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, Long Chengyu, and the others had already arrived at the Totem Galaxy.","They didn’t talk about the Heavenly Temple Aura, though the Totem Dragon Clan didn’t probe too deeply into what they had done either. The Totem Dragon Clan was more concerned about whether Long Zhuoyan, their Lord Ancestral Dragon, would let them off the hook.","The Totem Dragon Clan only exhaled in relief when Long Zhuoyan returned with Chu Feng.","Long Zhuoyan continued to conceal her appearance and keep her distance from the Totem Dragon Clan, but her attitude was amicable compared to before. They cooperated with her when she asked to retrieve several treasures from the Totem Dragon Clan’s forbidden land.","These treasures were from Long Zhuoyan, after all.","The Totem Dragon Clan wouldn’t hesitate to offer Long Zhuoyan anything she demanded, including their lives.","...","Chu Feng, the other junior prodigies, and the Totem Dragon Clan’s upper echelons were gathered in the Totem Dragon Clan’s forbidden land.","Jie Shanxian, Daoist Starseizer, and Jie Tiannian were lying on the ground.","Not far away from them was a humongous formation that pierced into the sky. This formation was Long Zhuoyan’s handiwork.","Three treasures were placed in the formation. They were all cultivation resources, but their energies were running out after years of usage. They were only tightly guarded and preserved because they were related to Long Zhuoyan.","Long Zhuoyan had demanded for more items, but the others had completely lost their true dragon energy over time.","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, elders, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and the other juniors were gathered around the formation.","There were other cultivators like Huahua and Xia Xingchen who were currently residing in the Totem Dragon Clan too, but the Totem Dragon Clan imposed the highest level of confidentiality on this matter since it involved Long Zhuoyan, so not even they were informed about this.","While the crowd was busy, Long Zhuoyan sat on an imposing chair and chatted with Chu Feng.","“Big sister, there isn’t much true dragon energy left. Will it be enough?” Chu Feng was worried.","“You’ll be able to treat them as long as you can extract and refine the true dragon energy inside those treasures. However, it won’t be easy to pull it off.”","When the preparations were almost complete, Long Zhuoyan stood up and addressed the Totem Dragon Clansmen. “I’ll say a few things first. If not for Chu Feng, your Totem Dragon Clan would have ceased to exist. These three people are important to my little brother, so you must save them no matter what it takes.","“The extraction and refinement of true dragon energy is no easy feat; you may even lose your life. But I’m sure you know what you must do.”","The Totem Dragon Clansmen replied resoundingly to Long Zhuoyan’s words, “We understand!”","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and the others stepped into the formation core to channel the formation. They already knew what they must do. They had to activate the formation with their bloodline power to extract the remaining true dragon energy.","But this was easier said than done.","It didn’t take long for tight knits to form on their forehead. They clenched their jaws as their faces began warping in pain.","The first one to struggle were the elders, followed by the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief. Surprisingly, Long Chengyu and Long Muxi lasted the longest. It would appear that what made a difference in this formation was not one’s cultivation but bloodline.","But even Long Chengyu and Long Muxi’s complexions soon turned awry.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen visibly became weaker as time passed. It wasn’t just about the pain anymore. At this rate, they might lose their lives.","But none of them chose to give up. This was their chance to repay Chu Feng and their Lord Ancestral Dragon. They had to give it their all, even at the cost of their lives. Their tenacity was clear for all to see, including Chu Feng.","However, their effort wasn’t paying off well. Not the slightest true dragon energy was being extracted. At this rate, the Totem Dragon Clansmen would die before any true dragon energy was extracted.","“Big sister, can I try channeling the formation?” Chu Feng asked.","“If you’re tired of living, you can go and give it a try. I guarantee that you’ll die without a sliver of doubt,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","“Can the formation only be channeled by those who have inherited the Dragon Clan’s bloodline?” Chu Feng refused to give up.","“Little brother, you have a formidable bloodline, but the True Dragon Bloodline is the most domineering bloodline power in the world. Other bloodline powers willl be suppressed by the true dragon energy. My formation further amplifies the prowess of the True Dragon Bloodline, making it the dominant power within the formation.","“Only those who have inherited the Dragon Clan’s bloodline can channel the formation. If outsiders intervene, the true dragon energy will detect their presence and attack them. The backlash will take their life.","“The true dragon energy has been outside my body so long that it has become an independent entity, though it stopped short of developing sentience. I won’t be able to do anything if it attacks you. Let them do it instead. They owe you a favor anyway. They can repay you with their lives. I’ll take their lives if they give up here.”","Long Zhuoyan leisurely rested on the chair as she spoke. Her tone showed how little she thought about the Totem Dragon Clansmen’s lives, and she wouldn’t bat an eyelid if they died. Despite her amicable attitude to Chu Feng, she was extremely harsh to the Totem Dragon Clan.","“Big sister, are there other ways to treat my three elders?” Chu Feng asked.","“There is no other way. I won’t be able to do anything without the true dragon energy.” Long Zhuoyan shrugged.","Upon receiving his answer, Chu Feng leaped into the formation core. He channeled his bloodline power and fused it into the formation.","“Are you tired of living?!” Long Zhuoyan shot to her feet in shock.","GRAR!","Ferocious dragon roars echoed from the three treasures and shook the palace. Three dragon silhouettes emanating terrifying auras swiftly manifested in the formation, occupying almost its entire area.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen were stunned to see the dragon silhouettes. As entities manifested from the True Dragon Bloodline, the Totem Dragon Clan felt subservience toward them from the bottom of their souls.","Long Zhuoyan frowned. She formed a hand seal, ready to intervene at any moment. She could turn a blind eye to the Totem Dragon Clan, but not Chu Feng.","Bzzzt!","Provoked by the three dragon silhouettes, Chu Feng’s bloodline power also manifested as humongous entities. Just their eyes looked as if eighteen suns had suddenly appeared in the sky, but they were even larger than the sun.","The nine lightning beasts had manifested!","The crushing pressure they emanated forced the three dragon silhouettes to return to their respective treasures obediently.","Following that, the nine lightning beasts began to contract from enveloping the sky to just enveloping the formation.","Three golden auras seeped out of the three treasures and drifted toward a container inside the formation.","Even the knowledgeable Long Zhuoyan widened her eyes and blurted out, “Bloody hell. My eyes have been opened today.”","She knew that Chu Feng had succeeded."]},{"number":6304,"title":"Chapter 6304: Chapter 6302: Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6302: Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain","On the other hand, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu remained worried. Unlike Long Zhuoyan, they couldn’t tell if Chu Feng succeeded.","Long Zhuoyan bellowed at the Totem Dragon Clan, “You bunch are useless! Where do you find the gall to call yourselves the descendants of the Dragon Clan? You still have to count on my little brother to rescue you in the end!","“Enough, enough. Get out of the formation. If you can’t help, the least you can do is not get in the way. You’ll only burden my little brother if you die in the formation.”","The Totem Dragon Clansmen quickly retreated from the formation.","Anyone else witnessing this sight would be dumbstruck. The Totem Dragon Clan might have encountered several setbacks recently, but it was still a galaxy overlord. To think that they would dare not even refute when someone was insulting them to their faces!","But the Totem Dragon Clansmen weren’t angered by Long Zhuoyan’s insult. On the contrary, they lamented their weakness even though they were frail from channeling the formation, with some even being on the verge of death.","Weng!","A gentle wave of spirit power suddenly enveloped the Totem Dragon Clansmen, healing their frail bodies.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen hurriedly bowed in gratitude, for the spirit power had come from Long Zhuoyan. However, Long Zhuoyan acted as if she couldn’t hear their thanks. She had a surprisingly tender heart despite her venomous mouth.","Extracting the true dragon energy was no easy feat. Despite Chu Feng’s bloodline completely suppressing the True Dragon Bloodline, it still took him some time to fully extract the true dragon energy inside the three treasures.","Fortunately, the process was only lengthy. It didn’t take much of a toll on Chu Feng.","“How frustrating. What kind of monster is this little brother of mine?” Long Zhuoyan murmured as she approached Chu Feng.","The spirit power enveloping her body prevented everyone else except for Chu Feng from perceiving her appearance.","“I was lucky,” Chu Feng replied.","“You were lucky. You jumped in after I told you it was dangerous. Are you not afraid of death?” Long Zhuoyan scoffed.","“It was a gamble.”","“Gambling on whether I am right or not?”","“No, I was gambling that you wouldn’t leave me to the lurch,” Chu Feng admitted.","He knew better than to undermine Long Zhuoyan’s judgment, which was why he wasn’t confident of pulling it off. What he was confident in, however, was that Long Zhuoyan could channel the formation, just that she didn’t want to because it was a burden.","He believed that she wouldn’t turn a blind eye to his plight if something happened to him. This wasn’t just blind faith, he truly believed that he was worth that much to her.","“You brat. You’re even scheming against me now!” Long Zhuoyan laughed. She wasn’t angry at Chu Feng for his decision. On the contrary, it further raised her opinion of him.","“Big sister, is this enough?” Chu Feng passed the container containing the true dragon energy to Long Zhuoyan.","“It’s more than enough. I can nourish my body with the leftovers,” Long Zhuoyan smiled.","With a grand wave of her sleeves, Long Zhuoyan constructed a profound recovery formation over Jie Shanxian and the others. She took out a fingernail-sized portion of true dragon energy and infused it into the formation core.","“Come and channel the formation,” Long Zhuoyan instructed Chu Feng, gesturing at the empty formation core.","“Do I channel it with my bloodline power?” Chu Feng asked.","“Your bloodline power is potent enough to suppress the true dragon energy, so it should work well too. However, you shouldn’t rush the process. This gu poison is a tricky one; you’ll have to let the energy slowly permeate into their bodies. Since you are willing to put your life on the line for these three, I’m sure you wouldn’t mind spending a bit more time healing them too, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Of course,” Chu Feng replied as he stepped into the formation core.","“Bad news, clan chief!”","An elder suddenly barged into the room with an anxious face.","“Didn’t I sternly instruct the clansmen not to disturb me no matter what happens?” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief replied with a hint of ire.","“Go and do what you have to. You aren’t needed here anyway,” Long Zhuoyan casually said.","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief first brought the elder somewhere else before receiving the report, not wanting to disturb Chu Feng and Long Zhuoyan. However, he soon returned to the room and looked at Chu Feng.","“Elder Clan Chief, did something happen?”","Chu Feng hadn’t entered the formation core yet. He sensed that something major must have happened for the elder to barge in here despite strict orders otherwise.","“Something has indeed happened. Why don’t you come out to take a look too?”","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief took out an observation treasure and handed it over to Chu Feng. Looking into the observation treasure, Chu Feng and the others saw the silhouette of a meandering mountain range at the Divine Body Galaxy.","The highest mountain peak resembled a sharp sword, and three words were inscribed on it: Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","The mountain range was illusory, but the three words were tangible. In particular, the character for ‘Bloodline (血)’ resembled a gate.","“It’s the legendary Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain?” Xianhai Shaoyu and the others were shocked.","“Yes, it is exactly as recorded.” The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief nodded.","“What’s the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s a place that nourishes one’s bloodline, and it’s exceptionally effective on juniors. I saw it before in the Ancient Era, but I didn’t expect it to still be around. However, the energy harnessed inside a remnant is bound to be limited. I reckon the energy inside the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is much less than before.","“Well, it is still the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain nevertheless, so little brother, you can consider taking a look. However, you should make haste; your kin won’t last much longer than this,” Long Zhuoyan said as he glanced at Jie Tiannian and the others lying on the ground.","“Big sister, the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is the real deal?” Chu Feng asked.","Xianhai Shaoyu and the others might have heard about the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, but Long Zhuoyan was the only one here who knew whether it was the real deal or not. She was a powerhouse in the Ancient Era, after all.","“It is the real deal,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","Chu Feng looked at Wang Qiang and the others and said, “Go ahead without me. Take care. I shan’t be joining you.”","With that, he stepped into the formation core to channel the formation.","“Big brother, I’ll stay behind to accompany you,” Little Fishy said.","She would rather spend more time with Chu Feng than to grasp this fortuitous encounter.","“Don’t. It would be foolish not to grasp a fortuitous encounter presented to us, not to mention that big sister has confirmed that it’s the real deal. You should go ahead first. I’ll join you if I can make it in time,” Chu Feng replied.","He had to stay inside the formation to channel it, but it didn’t hinder him from chatting with others.","“B-b-brother, I’m not too bothered about the fortuitous encounter, but its appearance in the Divine Body Galaxy might draw the attention of A-A-Ancient Era’s races. I’m worried about the Divine Body Heavenly M-M-Mansion, so I’ll have to make a trip back,” Wang Qiang said.","“Be careful,” Chu Feng said.","Beneath Wang Qiang’s rowdy personality was a loyal soul. The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion had treated him kindly, so he was bound to be worried about them at times like this.","Little Fishy was conflicted.","Chu Feng saw through her and advised with a smile, “Be good and listen to me. With your talent, you’re bound to benefit from this fortuitous encounter. However, you should call your family members along too. Wang Qiang right—the Ancient Era’s races might be there. You should bring someone there to protect you.”","Xianhai Shaoyu tugged on Little Fishy’s sleeves and said, “My little sis, Chu Feng is right. You can’t help him even if you stay here. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is a legendary remnant. You shouldn’t miss it.”","He sent her a voice transmission, “Yu’er, you should enter the remnant for our clan’s sake, even if not for yourself. Many clansmen are counting on us for protection. We must become stronger as soon as possible.”","Hearing those words, Little Fishy nodded. “I’ll go.”","Having made up their minds, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu made their way to the Divine Body Galaxy under the escort of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and the Totem Dragon Clansmen insisted on staying behind with Chu Feng. They knew they couldn't help him, but their guilt didn't allow them to go. While it was a pity to miss this fortuitous encounter, if they went, the guilt they felt could severely hinder their path of cultivation.","It was not worth the trade-off.","Thus, Chu Feng didn’t try to persuade them otherwise.","There were many powers with observation means similar to the Totem Dragon Clan, so it didn’t take long for news about the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain to spread far and wide. Many parties quickly made their way to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","However, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was an exception. They chose to remain in isolation despite Jie Tianran’s return."]},{"number":6305,"title":"Chapter 6305: Chapter 6303: Survivor of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect, Long Xiaoxiao","paragraphs":["Chapter 6303: Survivor of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect, Long Xiaoxiao","Days passed in a flash.","Chu Feng remained in the Totem Dragon Clan’s forbidden land all this while, but the Totem Dragon Clansmen evacuated the area to not disturb him. Thus, the only ones in the forbidden land now were Chu Feng and Long Zhuoyan.","During which, they received news from Little Fishy and the others regarding the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","Many powers had gone to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, both present-era cultivators and Ancient Era’s races alike. Most were foreign faces, but there were also familiar faces like the Huangfu Heavenly Caln.","Little Fishy and the others concealed their appearances and maintained a low profile, thus avoiding conflicts with others. They were sending news back, not just to report their safety, but also to inform Chu Feng that the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain had yet to officially open, so he could rush over to meet up with them once he was done with his business.","Based on what they had observed, they were indeed fortuitous encounters in the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain waiting to be uncovered.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng had finally removed the gu poison and stabilized the conditions of Jie Shanxian, Daoist Starseizer, and Jie Tiannian. Long Zhuoyan spent most of her time resting on her chair, either resting or cultivating.","Jie Shanxian and the others remained unconscious in the recovery formation.","Chu Feng looked at them from outside the formation, his worry not lessening in the least. Despite having extracted their gu poison, he had only managed to save their lives. It would take them a long time to recover, and it was unlikely they would ever return to their peak.","Their bloodlines had been plundered, resulting in the loss of their cultivation. This meant that they were no more than mortals now.","There was a vast difference between mortals and cultivators. For instance, Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer were already advanced in age. Without their cultivation, their lifespans would be severely limited. It was hard to tell how much longer they could live.","“Big sister, is there a way to restore the two elders’ bloodlines?” Chu Feng asked Long Zhuoyan.","He was referring to Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer.","Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer’s bodies were completely ruined, such that Chu Feng, with his current capabilities, couldn’t find a way to heal them. Even if he found compatible bloodlines for them, there was no way to fuse them into their bodies.","They were crippled for good.","In contrast, Jie Tiannian was still young, and Jie Tianran appeared to have shown mercy to her. There was still a chance she could recover, though she would have to recultivate.","“Their bodies are so thoroughly destroyed that you can’t transplant a compatible bloodline into them. Without their cultivation, their lifespans will be limited. They are unlikely to live for long,” Long Zhuoyan opened her eyes and replied.","Her verdict was the same as Chu Feng’s, but she was far more credible given that she was a top world spiritist in the Ancient Era. Her cultivation might have regressed, but the knowledge she had remained. Her words were as good as a death sentence to Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starsezier.","Chu Feng looked at the unconscious Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer with pained eyes.","He had no way of knowing for sure how the two had fallen into Jie Tianran’s hands and landed in such a tragic plight, but he had a feeling it was related to him.","“You have tried your best. That is their fate. Little brother, come with me to the Ninth Galaxy,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Big sister, I don’t intend to go yet,” Chu Feng replied.","“You aren’t going? You already know that your mother is in the Ninth Galaxy. Are you intending to exact vengeance on their behalf?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“The three elders landed in this plight because of me. If I don’t stop Jie Tianran, more of my acquaintances will suffer the same fate. I can’t just turn a blind eye to this,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s fine too. You might just have a shot at obtaining God’s Era’s power,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","“Big sister, do you know something about God’s Era?” Chu Feng asked.","“That thing has been around since the Ancient Era, and it appears quite frequently. It’s just that no one has obtained its true legacy thus far. You, however, are an extraordinary one. You might just have a chance at it.” Long Zhuoyan looked at Chu Feng with a sliver of expectation.","“I’ll try my best at God’s Era. Big sister, when do you intend to set off?” Chu Feng asked.","“Soon. I’ll set off right after conditioning my body,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","Chu Feng wasn’t too disappointed by the news. It was a pity to lose Long Zhuoyan’s backing, but he had survived well without her thus far. Her appearance was a surprise, and it was only out of worry for his mother that he had Long Zhuoyan bring him to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","There was nothing for him to worry about now that he knew his mother was safe and sound.","He was confident of dealing with Jie Tianran alone.","Chu Feng suddenly frowned. He reached into his Cosmos Sack and took out a glowing bead.","He had previously deciphered the True Dragon Chessboard in the Dragon Breath Spring Chamber, which prompted Long Mucheng to make a request out of him. However, he needed another person to fulfill the request.","Unfortunately, Long Mucheng was still searching for the person, and she handed him a bead and asked him to keep a lookout for the person too. According to her, the bead would glow if the person was in the vicinity.","“You’re searching for someone?” Long Zhuoyan asked. She easily saw through the bead.","“Yes.” Chu Feng nodded.","“It seems to be someone important. It’ll take them a while to recover anyway, so why don’t you handle this first?” Long Zhuoyan quickly added, “Do you need me to accompany you?”","Chu Feng was about to answer when the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief suddenly flew over. He first greeted Long Zhuoyan with a bow, “Paying respect to Lord Ancestral Dragon.”","Long Zhuoyan replied in annoyance, “Get straight to the point. Haven’t I told you many times not to call me Lord Ancestral Dragon? Call me Lord Long instead.”","“Yes, Lord Long.”","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, despite his high stature and age, remained uptight in front of Long Zhuoyan like a child standing before an adult. He dared not to even breathe loudly.","“Chu Feng, you have a friend named Long Xiaoxiao, right? You two participated in our Totem Dragon Clan’s Trial of the Strongest in the Saint Dragon Ancient Remnant,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“Yes, Xiaoxiao is my close friend. Elder, did something happen?” Chu Feng asked.","“The remnants of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect believe that our Totem Dragon Clan is responsible for their sect’s downfall and attacked our territory. We have captured all of them, and the disciple of one of the culprits is Long Xiaoxiao.","“I haven’t dealt with them yet because I remembered that Long Xiaoxiao is your friend. I had my men bring them here for the time being,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Elder, where are they now?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll bring you over.”","The clan chief brought Chu Feng to where Long Xiaoxiao and the others were imprisoned. Along the way, Chu Feng noticed the bead in his hand glowing with increasing brightness.","“Could this bead be pointing to someone in Xiaoxiao’s party?” Chu Feng wondered."]},{"number":6306,"title":"Chapter 6306: Chapter 6304: Meeting Xiaoxiao’s Master Once More","paragraphs":["Chapter 6304: Meeting Xiaoxiao’s Master Once More","Chu Feng finally came face to face with Xiaoxiao’s group.","Except for Xiaoxiao, the other members of the party were from the older generation. Some were familiar faces to Chu Feng, but there were also foreign faces too.","Long Xiaoxiao’s master, Ningyu Shangren, was there too.","Chu Feng hadn’t been able to see through her cultivation the previous time they met, but he could do so this time. She was a rank eight True God level cultivator.","This might not be much to the current him, but Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragons were unreachable myths when he first met Ningyu Shangren. Even the galaxy overlords were only at pinnacle True God level and True Dragon.","Rank eight True God level was indeed formidable to him back then.","“Chu Feng?”","Long Xiaoxiao and the others looked at Chu Feng with conflicted eyes when he stepped into their line of sight. They had heard about Chu Feng and the unbelievable feats he had pulled off.","Ningyu Shangren was the most astounded one of all.","Her first meeting with Chu Feng was when he had just traveled from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy to the Totem Galaxy for the first time, and he was still extremely weak back then. She had already noticed that he would go on to do great things in the future, but she could have never thought that he could grow to this extent within such a short time.","“Paying respect to elder.”","Chu Feng bowed respectfully to Ningyu Shangren regardless of their current positions. It was because he knew she had treated Long Xiaoxiao well.","This made Ningyu Shangren feel even more conflicted. She was no fool. She could already figure out that Chu Feng was the reason their party wasn’t dead yet despite having attacked the Totem Dragon Clan’s territory.","Despite Chu Feng’s relationship with the Totem Dragon Clan and his current standing, he still treated her with the same respect as before even after knowing what they had done. Very few people would be able to do the same.","Chu Feng must have known about their deed by now, yet he still","“Elder, did you attack the Totem Dragon Clan because of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s destruction?” Chu Feng asked.","“Chu Feng, I’ll be frank and admit that we played a part in stoking Long Lin’s rebellion. Our Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect is indeed at fault here. However, the Totem Dragon Clan went too far by massacring all of our people. They didn’t even spare the innocent children! We have to exact this vengeance!” Ningyu Shangren said.","She clearly relayed her stance as a Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmember.","“Elder, the Totem Dragon Clan has nothing to do with the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s massacre. You are going after the wrong person,” Chu Feng replied.","“Rubbish! All major powers except the Totem Dragon Clan have entered God’s Era then. The Totem Dragon Clan is the only one that has the power to pull this off. How else could the culprit be other than them?” an old man refuted.","“Many Ancient Era’s powers have refrained from entering God’s Era too. The Totem Dragon Clan is not the only one capable of this feat. Besides, I am not here to debate with you. I can’t care less about what you think.” Chu Feng coldly glanced at the old man and the other remnants of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect.","He turned to the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and said, “Elder Clan Chief, can you do me a favor and not harm Ningyu Shanren and Long Xiaoxiao?”","Upon hearing Chu Feng’s words, Ningyu Shangren anxiously turned to Long Xiaoxiao.","Shortly after, Long Xiaoxiao sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng.”","All she did was call his name.","She could have done so openly, but she did it via voice transmission.","Chu Feng deduced that Ningyu Shangren must have urged her to plead with him to spare the other remnants of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect, but Long Xiaoxiao was too embarrassed to say it.","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief replied, “Young friend Chu Feng, you’re being too polite. No matter who they are and the grudge between them and our Totem Dragon Clan, we have no qualms sparing anyone you want. Be it two people, twenty thousand, or twenty million, our clan will not turn down your request.”","This declaration shocked not just Long Xiaoxiao and Ningyu Shangren but the remnants of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect too.","They had heard about Chu Feng’s close ties with the Totem Dragon Clan, but they didn’t expect him to command such influence in the Totem Dragon Clan. The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief even lowered his attitude when talking to Chu Feng as if the latter were his boss.","“Young friend Chu Feng, for you to be so certain that the Totem Dragon Clan is not responsible for the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s massacre, could it be that you know something?” Ningyu Shangren asked.","“Elder, I shall speak candidly. We don’t have to explain anything to you because you were at fault in the first place. The Totem Dragon Clan is justified to go on a massacre after what you have done to them. We owe no moral obligation to you. I only pleaded on your behalf because of Long Xiaoxiao.”","Ningyu Shangren was stunned. She lowered her head in shame.","They had aided Long Lin in his rebellion to kill the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and its upper echelons. They were the ones who started this war, so they couldn’t complain even if the Totem Dragon Clan massacred every last one of them.","“Xiaoxiao knows best what kind of person I am. I wouldn’t lie to her given our ties. I accompanied the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief to the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect, but the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect was already destroyed by the time we arrived.","“You should have been able to tell that no ordinary cultivator was behind the massacre of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect. If the Totem Dragon Clan was behind it, there would have been evidence, given the sheer number of people murdered. Have you found anything suggesting it was the Totem Dragon Clan’s doing?” Chu Feng asked.","Long Xiaoxiao quickly added, “Master, I can vouch for Chu Feng’s credibility. If he says that the Totem Dragon Clan isn’t behind it, it must be the case. Besides, you also deduced that the Totem Dragon Clan might not be behind the massacre.”","Ningyu Shangren fell silent. She did reserve her doubts regarding the massacre, just that the other Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmembers insisted that the Totem Dragon Clan was behind it and were determined to make a move against them.","She had no choice but to accompany them. Little did they expect the Totem Dragon Clan to have grown far stronger than before. It should have been an easy territory to claim, but there were surprisingly many masked experts guarding the area.","They were captured despite their strength.","There were only two paths in front of them—death or subservience to Chu Feng. They could survive this ordeal if Chu Feng spoke on their behalf.","So, she turned to the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmembers and said, “What are you waiting for? Hurry up and apologize to young friend Chu Feng.”","“Why should we apologize? We didn’t come here with the intent of leaving this place alive. We’ll depart this world as proud Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmembers!”","Blue flames suddenly blazed from the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmembers and reduced them to ashes. In the blink of an eye, Ningyu Shangren and Long Xiaoxiao were the only survivors in their party.","“Master!” Long Xiaoxiao anxiously grabbed Ningyu Shangren’s hand, fearing that she would end her own life too.","At the same time, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief exerted his oppressive might to prevent Ningyu Shangren from ending her life.","“Don’t worry, I don’t plan to end my life. I still have to avenge the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect,” Ningyu Shangren replied as she glanced at the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sectmembers who had already turned into ashes.","She understood them well. They would rather live than die, but they didn’t trust Chu Feng and the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief.","All of a sudden, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief narrowed his eyes. He sensed powerful auras outside."]},{"number":6307,"title":"Chapter 6307: Chapter 6305: Chu Feng’s Steadfast","paragraphs":["Chapter 6305: Chu Feng’s Steadfast","Before the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief could take a closer look, the people outside had already barged in. They were experts from the Dragon Breath Clan, led by Long Mucheng.","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief was surprised by Long Mucheng’s appearance. The latter had previously left to attend to other business. Who could have thought that she would suddenly return at this moment?","A mere glance at the glowing bead in Long Mucheng’s grasp was enough for Chu Feng to understand why she was here. She must have come for Long Xiaoxiao.","Long Mucheng first glanced at Long Xiaoxiao and Ningyu Shangren before turning her sights to Chu Feng. “Chu Feng, she is...?”","She thought Chu Feng had also come here under the bead’s guidance.","“Xiaoxiao, come with me for a moment,” Chu Feng said as he led Long Xiaoxiao out.","“What’s wrong, Chu Feng?” Long Xiaoxiao asked in confusion.","Chu Feng took out the bead. They had already traveled a far distance away from the prison, but the bead continued to glow brightly.","“That person who barged in earlier is Long Mucheng, a Dragon Breath Clansman. The Dragon Breath Clan has been searching for two people to help them with a request. One of them is me, but they haven’t been able to find the other person so they asked me to help them. This bead is a tool that guides me to the other person,” Chu FEng said.","“Is the other person me?” Long Xiaoxiao pointed at herself.","“It has to be,” Long Mucheng interjected from behind. She had caught up with them at some point.","Chu Feng could tell from Long Mucheng’s expression that this matter was extremely important to her.","“Allow me to introduce the two of you. Elder, this is my good friend, Long Xiaoxiao. Xiaoxiao, this is Elder Long Mucheng,” Chu Feng said.","Long Xiaoxiao obediently bowed to Long Mucheng. “Junior pays respect to Elder Long.”","“You don’t have to be so polite.” Long Mucheng supported Long Xiaoxiao up before turning to Chu Feng. “Who could have thought the two people our Dragon Breath Clan has been looking for are good friends? Is this heaven’s will or a coincidence?”","“Elder, what do you need us to do?” Chu Feng asked.","“I need to trouble you to help us decipher an item. It’ll greatly benefit our clan if you succeed, but more importantly, we would also be fulfilling that lord’s mission,” Long Mucheng replied.","“May I ask who is the lord you’re referring to?” Chu Feng asked.","“My apologies, Chu Feng, but that lord prefers to maintain a low profile. It isn’t convenient for me to reveal his identity,” Long Mucheng replied.","“I understand. When should we decipher it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Right now,” Long Mucheng said.","Eggy immediately protested in Chu Feng’s ears, “That won’t do. Didn’t Little Fishy send a message earlier urging you to head to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain after saving your aunt and the others?”","Chu Feng also asked aloud, “Elder, is this matter that urgent?”","“Chu Feng, are you intending to head to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain? It is indeed a golden opportunity. I can understand you not wanting to miss this chance. However, deciphering this item has been the long-time wish of our Dragon Breath Clan. It wasn’t easy for us to find the two of you, and I don’t want anything to go wrong.","“Chu Feng, I promise you two that as long as you give it your all, regardless of whether you succeed or not, our Dragon Breath Clan will put our lives on the line to ensure your safety. I’m begging you here.”","Long Mucheng fell to her knees; she was kneeling not just to Chu Feng but to Long Xiaoxiao too.","“Elder, please get up. I’ll help you, all right?” Chu Feng quickly pulled Long Mucheng up.","He had a grasp of Long Mucheng’s character. She had helped him several times thus far and was trustworthy.","“All right, all right. Let’s help her then.” Even Eggy also took a step back.","She knew Chu Feng well. As important as fortuitous encounters were, Chu Feng valued his friendships more than that.","After obtaining Long Xiaoxiao’s consent, Chu Feng first returned and told the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief to free Ningyu Shangren. He then paid a visit to Long Zhuoyan to explain the situation. Only then did he leave with Long Mucheng.","Long Mucheng called practically everyone from the Dragon Breath Clan to go with them. Even those who were in their closed-door training were urged to come out of seclusion to help out. This further showed just how important this matter was to the Dragon Breath Clan.","“I’m sorry, Chu Feng,” Long Xiaoxiao suddenly whispered along the way.","“What’s with the sudden apology? Is it because of your master and the others?” Chu Feng asked.","“I was oblivious to what my master and the others did. My master only told me everything because she thought that she might die in this assault. I forced her to take me with her. I know you are on good terms with the Totem Dragon Clan, but my master’s safety was at stake, so I couldn’t divulge her movements to the Totem Dragon Clan. I... didn’t know what to do.” Long Xiaoxiao lowered her head, feeling conscience-stricken.","On the one hand was the master who nurtured her, and on the other hand was a power who was on close terms with her good friend. This put her in a spot.","“It’s fine, Xiaoxiao. There are bound to be things in the world that are beyond our control. The important thing is that you, Long Xiaoxiao, are my good friend. Nothing in this world can affect our relationship,” Chu Feng said.","Long Xiaoxiao looked as if a huge weight had been lifted from her shoulders. She smiled at Chu Feng. “You haven’t changed in the least despite having come so far. You’re still the same person I know from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.”","She looked at Chu Feng with gleaming eyes.","It hadn’t been too long since she parted ways with Chu Feng, but many things had happened in the meantime.","The Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","The Luck Saint Realm.","The Immemorial Massacre Sea.","Chu Feng’s feats were nothing short of extraordinary.","Long Xiaoxiao had also grown a lot, but she hadn’t accomplished much, having been living under her master’s protection. She thought that there was bound to be some distance between them now that Chu Feng had become the strongest junior in the world of cultivation.","But now that they were reunited, she realized that Chu Feng was the same as before. It was hard to believe, but the fame and power didn’t change him.","And she liked how steadfast he was.","The Dragon Breath Clan’s destination was in the Totem Galaxy, but it was not located in any realm but in the middle of space.","Upon arriving at their destination, Long Mucheng took out an ancient key. It was over three meters long and resembled a weapon when she held it with both hands."]},{"number":6308,"title":"Chapter 6308: Chapter 6306: Dharma Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6306: Dharma Emperor","Long Mucheng slowly twisted the massive ancient key. She made mild positional adjustments that caused different sections of the keys to light up.","After a few adjustments, the key finally lit up entirely.","Long Mucheng’s face lit up with delight.","She quickly formed hand seals that made the runes inside the key surface.","With that, she finally lifted the key high and inserted it into the space before her. Astonishingly, the inserted portions of the key vanished into a void as if there was a hidden keyhole in front of them.","Clicking sounds could be heard as she twisted the key.","Boom!","The space suddenly shook as a brilliant light poured out. A thousand-meter-tall silver gate appeared before the crowd, with the key inserted in its keyhole.","Long Mucheng pushed the gate open, revealing a lush realm with verdant mountains and refreshing streams.","“Why is it that small?” Eggy asked.","The realm beyond the silver gate was big enough that a mortal couldn’t fully explore it in their lifetime, but cultivators of Chu Feng’s caliber could see the realm’s boundaries in the distance.","Compared to the other vast realms Chu Feng had been in, this realm was small. Even Chu Feng could construct far larger realms with his current prowess, though it might take some time.","That being said, this was no ordinary formation realm.","Chu Feng didn’t notice this hidden realm before Long Mucheng opened it, which showed how expertly concealed it was.","A world spiritist capable of such masterful concealment could have easily created a far larger realm, which was why Eggy was confused by the realm’s small size.","“This realm seems rather unique, elder,” Chu Feng remarked to Long Mucheng, hoping to gather more information from her.","Long Mucheng understood what Chu Feng was driving at, so she explained, “Indeed, but I’m afraid I don’t have much of a clue about the realm. I only know that this is the place where the lord stored their treasure. The treasure should be safe. No expert can open this place without the key and the corresponding hand seals and chants.”","Long Mucheng pulled out the key and flaunted it before stowing it away.","“Chu Feng, wait here for me.” Long Mucheng closed the silver gate before venturing deeper into the formation realm with the Dragon Breath Clansmen.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng examined the realm with curious eyes.","His instincts as a world spiritist told him there was something extraordinary about this small realm. Its aged air suggested that this place had existed since the Immemorial Era.","“It’s an Immemorial Storage Realm,” Long Zhuoyan’s voice suddenly echoed in Chu Feng’s ears.","Chu Feng looked to the side and saw Long Zhuoyan standing right next to him. She wasn’t there earlier. On top of that, Long Xiaoxiao seemed oblivious to Long Zhuoyan’s presence even though she was right beside Chu Feng.","Clearly, Chu Feng was the only one who could see Long Zhuoyan here.","Knowing that Long Zhuoyan didn’t want to reveal herself, he communicated with her via voice transmission, “Big sister, what brings you here?”","“I was curious to see what your friend is capable of, as well as what the Dragon Breath Clan needs your help to decipher,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","“You’re quite a curious one, big sister. What’s the situation with this Immemorial Storage Realm? It looks extraordinary,” Chu Feng asked.","“In essence, it is no different from your Cosmos Sacks and spatial formations. Think of it as a safer and more resilient storage space. Based on what I know, the Immemorial Storage Realm can be classified into four tiers, namely Iron, Bronze, Silver, and Gold.”","“Is this a Silver-tier Immemorial Storage Realm?” Chu Feng asked, recalling the silver gate he had to cross to enter this formation realm.","“That’s right.” Long Zhuoyan nodded.","“It must be quite rare,” Chu Feng remarked.","“Indeed.” Long Zhuoyan nodded once more.","“The ‘lord’ Elder Long Mucheng spoke about must be a formidable figure.”","Long Zhuoyan surprisingly didn’t refute Chu Feng’s words. “He’s indeed a formidable figure, perhaps an acquaintance even.”","“Acquaintance? Elder, do you know who Long Mucheng’s ‘lord’ is?” Chu Feng asked.","Long Zhuoyan was a powerhouse in the Ancient Era. Someone whose strength she acknowledged must be anything but simple. This led Chu Feng to think that Long Mucheng’s ‘lord’ was more incredible than he had initially thought.","“I need to verify it. I’ll let you know later,” Long Zhuoyan replied with a faint smile.","The world suddenly shook. The tremors originated from a lake inside the formation realm. Something massive was slowly rising from the lake.","It was a rectangular, wooden box of over ten thousand meters in length. It resembled a sword container or a coffin. It was old, but nowhere as old as this Immemorial Storage Realm. It must have been moved into this Immemorial Storage Realm afterward.","“It’s him. No wonder, no wonder.” Long Zhuoyan revealed a deep smile.","“Big sister, who is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t know who Long Mucheng’s ‘lord’ is, but I know the owner of that item,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Who is it?”","“Little brother, are you familiar with Divine Bodies?”","“Yes, I am familiar.”","“Tell me the Divine Body Ranking.”","1: Indestructible Divine Body","2: Heavenly Demon Divine Body","3: Four Symbols Divine Body","4: Nirvana Divine Body","5: Dharma Divine Body","6: Heavenly Lightning Divine Body","7: Blazing Sun Divine Body","8: Brilliant Moon Divine Body","9: Resurrection Divine Body","10: Four Fiends Divine Body","“Is that correct, big sister?” Chu Feng asked.","He had learned about the Divine Body Ranking from Wang Qiang, but the knowledge in the present era was inherited from the Ancient Era. He didn’t know how accurate this ranking was, so he sought Long Zhuoyan’s confirmation.","“Yes, it’s correct. The owner of that item is the master of the Dharma Divine Body. He was known as the Dharma Emperor in our era,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Dharma Emperor? He must be extremely powerful then!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","He had learned from the Three Saints Monstrous Clan that the strongest monstrous beasts were revered as saints, whereas the strongest humans were revered as emperors.","However, strength was merely the minimum requirement. Individuals had to accomplish something earth-shattering to enjoy those esteemed titles.","The Dharma Emperor must have been an extremely powerful and influential figure back in his era.","“He’s just adequate. He lost to me,” Long Zhuoyan replied with a smile."]},{"number":6309,"title":"Chapter 6309: Chapter 6307: The Grudge Back Then","paragraphs":["Chapter 6307: The Grudge Back Then","“Heavens! I knew you were powerful, big sister, but I didn’t know you were this strong! I have heard that only the most formidable figures in the Ancient Era are revered as emperors. If you defeated someone revered as an emperor in the Ancient Era, doesn’t that mean you are also...?”","Chu Feng looked at Long Zhuoyan with widened eyes. Could she have been an Emperor-tier powerhouse too?”","Looking at Chu Feng’s astonished expression, Long Zhuoyan burst into laughter.","“Hahaha! I am no pushover, but I had a capable assistant with me when I defeated the Dharma Emperor. I bet you have heard about that person.” Long Zhuoyan intentionally kept Chu Feng in suspense.","“Who is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“You’re a world spiritist. You should at least know who the strongest world spiritist in the Ancient Era is, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“World Spiritist Emperor Qin Jiu?!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","“Yes, that’s right,” Long Zhuoyan replied.","“Big sister, you’re acquainted with the World Spiritist Emperor?” Chu Feng’s interest was piqued.","The World Spiritist Emperor was a truly formidable figure.","Chu Feng’s exceptional strength as a world spiritist could be greatly attributed to the Ruler’s Bloodline he inherited from his mother. However, when he first left the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, his world spiritist technique lagged far behind his peers.","He couldn’t even defeat Bai Yunqing back then.","It was after acquiring World Spiritist Emperor Qin Jiu’s legacy that his world spiritist techniques improved by leaps and bounds, allowing him to claim the advantage even against prodigies like Jie Tian, who had been carefully nurtured by Jie Tianran from a young age.","He might have never met Qin Jiu before, but he viewed the latter as his master and felt indebted to him.","If Long Zhuoyan was acquainted with Qin Jiu and still alive, could Qin Jiu be alive too? If possible, he would love to meet the World Spiritist Emperor in person.","“I’ve met him several times. We did somewhat become friends later, but that was my first meeting with him. Back then, he was not the World Spiritist Emperor yet. Both of us were still rising stars in the world of cultivation. We have built up a fair reputation, but it was nowhere near the extent of commanding respect from the entire world. In contrast, the Dharma Emperor was already revered as an emperor by then.","“You have to understand that the Ancient Era was far from peaceful. There had been so many wars that there were only five Emperor-tier figures alive then.” Long Zhuoyan even opened her palm to emphasize her point.","Chu Feng was hooked on the story. He was curious to know what happened among Long Zhuoyan, Qin Jiu, and the Dharma Emperor, so he patiently listened without interrupting her.","Long Zhuoyan continued, “Most of the remnants you see now are either left behind by earlier cultivators of the present era or those from the Ancient Era. There aren’t many Immemorial Era’s remnants around because the people of my era have unearthed practically all of them.","“But back then, there were some Immemorial Era’s remnants that hadn’t emerged yet. It happened during the emergence of an Immemorial Era’s remnant. The remnant naturally drew in many people.","“Shortly after I entered the remnant, Qin Jiu approached me and proposed a partnership. I was proud and aloof then, not to mention that Qin Jiu was a stranger, so I planned to turn him down. But Qin Jiu gave me a compelling reason to accept his request—his world spiritist technique was superior to mine. Thus, I gave in and accepted his partnership.","“It was only later that I learned how sly he was. He realized right from the start that this remnant had something to do with our Dragon Clan, and that I, a Dragon Clansman, have an advantage in the remnant. That was why he approached me for a partnership.”","Long Zhuoyan sounded displeased when she spoke about this matter. It felt like she had fallen for Qin Jiu’s ploy and was exploited.","“What happened next?” Chu Feng urged.","“We naturally reached the end of the remnant, but much to our surprise, someone else managed to do the same—the Dharma Emperor. Many notable figures gathered when the remnant emerged, but the Dharma Emperor remained hidden. As soon as I saw the Dharma Emperor, I realized the remnant was greater than I expected. Otherwise, someone of his caliber wouldn’t have joined the commotion.","“Of course, I panicked at the sight of the Dharma Emperor. He was already a renowned figure standing at the peak of the world of cultivation then, whereas I was merely a rising star. Even the Qin Jiu then wasn’t a match for the Dharma Emperor, let alone me.","“But Qin Jiu remained perfectly calm. He got straight to the point and said that the remnant could only be cleared by the two of us, and the Dharma Emperor had no choice but to work with us if he wanted to obtain its rewards.”","A smirk gradually formed on Long Zhuoyan’s face as she recalled that day. There was a brief silence before she continued, “It still shocks me when I think about it now. Where does he find the galls to request the Dharma Emperor to cooperate with us?”","She turned to Chu Feng and added, “But what shocked me more is that the Dharma Emperor actually agreed to it. As it turned out, the Dharma Emperor was almost useless in the remnant. Qin Jiu and I did the bulk of the work, and the Dharma Emperor only contributed in a few parts. Eventually, we cleared the remnant and obtained its power.”","Chu Feng couldn’t help but ask, “What kind of power is it?”","“It’s a power left behind by the Immemorial Era’s Dragon Clan. It harnesses the ability to enhance one’s bloodline. It is a power that can greatly benefit the three of us, so a conflict naturally arose when it came to the distribution of the power.","“I was much more cowardly then. I would have been thankful if someone as powerful as the Dharma Emperor shared even a tiny portion with us. The 10% he offered already surpassed my imagination. On top of it, it would be worthwhile if we could get on close terms with the Dharma Emperor over this.","“To my surprise, Qin Jiu rejected the Dharma Emperor’s offer. He even threatened the Dharma Emperor to split the reward equally, or he would get nasty. I honestly thought Qin Jiu was out of his mind back then, and I prayed hard that I wouldn’t be implicated in this madness.”","Long Zhuoyan suddenly stopped the story here and turned to Chu Feng. “What do you think happened next?”","“Big sister, don’t keep me in suspense,” Chu Feng urged.","“There’s no way the Dharma Emperor would play along with Qin Jiu. He tried to coerce us into submission. That was my first time witnessing the strength of an Emperor-tier expert. Much to my surprise, his overwhelming strength failed to hurt me and Qin Jiu.","“Qin Jiu had prepared a hand. There was no need for the Dharma Emperor to intervene while we were clearing the remnant. Qin Jiu laid a trap for him by asking him to help, and the Dharma Emperor fell for it. Through that, Qin Jiu obtained the power to suppress the Dharma Emperor in the remnant.”"]},{"number":6310,"title":"Chapter 6310: Chapter 6308: Lord Xuantian","paragraphs":["Chapter 6308: Lord Xuantian","“But Qin Jiu didn’t make an attempt on the Dharma Emperor’s life right away. He opted for self-preservation, but he also used the remnant’s formation to seal off a small portion of the Dharma Emperor’s Divine Body.","“According to Qin Jiu, the seal wouldn’t affect the Dharma Emperor’s cultivation and fighting prowess, but it would limit his future growth. He did so because the remnant’s formation could only seal off that much, and this was the most effective way he could coerce the Dharma Emperor into giving in.","“The Dharma Emperor understood the position he was in and gave in. I only obtained some cultivation resources out of the remnant, but I heard Qin Jiu used this to coerce the Dharma Emperor into helping him many times, though I don’t know if the Dharma Emperor ended up helping him or not.","“Many years passed, and countless incidents happened. The reputation of Qin Jiu and I slowly grew, and he became the only world spiritist to attain the title of ‘Emperor’. However, he wasn’t fond of the title and continued to use his name, Qin Jiu.","“By then, Qin Jiu had obtained the most powerful Immemorial Era’s world spiritist legacy and was no longer afraid of the Dharma Emperor. Even though the Dharma Emperor had used his strength to exploit us back in the remnant, he isn’t a wicked person through and through. He had a decent reputation. I thought that it was about time to resolve this matter.","“One day, Qin Jiu invited me over to discuss the removal of the seal placed on the Dharma Emperor’s Divine Body. But once I was there, he made a terrible suggestion—he said that we shouldn’t return the Dharma Emperor’s power that easily. The seal might be minor, but it would impede the Dharma Emperor’s future cultivation.","“As long as the seal remained, we could continue coercing the Dharma Emperor to do our bidding. He was the one who tried to take advantage of us in the first place, so he shouldn’t blame us for doing the same here. I thought those words made sense, so I agreed to it.”","A mischievous smile formed on Long Zhuoyan’s lips. She spoke as if this was all Qin Jiu’s ploy, but who could say for sure what the truth was?","Chu Feng had heard about Long Zhuoyan’s reputation as a demoness despite descending from the Dragon Clan’s main lineage. It would be truly naive of him to think of her as an innocent lady who was merely misled by Qin Jiu.","“Chu Feng, the Dharma Emperor sounds pitiful,” Eggy remarked.","Eggy was no kind soul too, yet she made such a comment. This showed how pitiful the Dharma Emperor was to have his weakness grasped by these two vicious hyenas.","Qin Jiu would indeed be going too far if he was still thinking of exploiting the Dharma Emperor despite the latter helping him on various matters all this while.","“What happened next?” Chu Feng asked.","“I asked Qin Jiu if those rumors were true, and whether he had coerced the Dharma Emperor to help him behind my back without sharing the benefits with me.”","Chu Feng was rendered speechless. That isn’t the point at all!","“Qin Jiu admitted that he had requested help from the Dharma Emperor several times, but it was not coercion but partnership. They were mutually beneficial exchanges, where they split the benefits equally between them.","“He also told me that the Dharma Emperor is not as simple as he looks, though he didn’t elaborate more on the matter. He warned me to be careful of the Dharma Emperor. He thought that it wouldn’t do to continue holding the Dharma Emperor’s Divine Body hostage after so long, and that we needed to give him some hope so that the latter wouldn’t act up.","“Thus, he changed the sealing formation and the unsealing requirement. He came up with a chessboard and proclaimed that anyone who can decipher the chessboard will be capable of lifting the Dharma Emperor’s seal. I left a few beads that would allow one to find Dragon Clan descendants with stronger bloodlines.","“As long as the Dharma Emperor can meet these two requirements, he would be able to lift the seal on his Divine Body.”","Long Zhuoyan looked at Chu Feng with a gleeful smirk.","Chu Feng finally understood what was going on here.","The Dragon Breath Clan must be seeking to unseal the Dharma Emperor’s Divine Body, and the culprits behind the seal were none other than World Spiritist Emperor Qin Jiu and Long Zhuoyan.","“In the end, it turns out that you’re behind this.” Chu Feng looked at Long Zhuoyan and sighed.","“Indeed. That’s why I’m curious to know what your friend is capable of.” Long Zhuoyan glanced at Long Xiaoxiao. “I was the one who left the beads behind, after all.”","Chu Feng belatedly realized that Long Zhuoyan was able to see through the bead’s function right away not because she was knowledgeable, but because it had come from her.","“Big sister, it should be easy for you to decipher the seal then,” Chu Feng asked.","But Long Zhuoyan shook her head. “Qin Jiu intentionally modified the sealing formation to prevent the Dharma Emperor from demanding our Dragon Clansmen to lift his seal. Your friend is a descendant of the Dragon Clan, but she isn’t from the main lineage. I’m curious to know how strong her bloodline is.","“As for the chessboard, Qin Jiu said that someone who can decipher it can surely see through the formation’s opening. Little brother, are you the one who deciphered the chessboard?” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Yes.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Then I’m sure you’re fine. The crux to lifting the seal lies with your friend,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Weng!","Countless rays of light shot out from the massive sword container-like object. Upon careful inspection, the rays of light formed a map filled with many swiftly-moving entities, and it gave off a dangerous aura.","Shoosh!","Long Mucheng, who stood before the sword container-like object, waved her sleeves and tossed out several scrolls. The scrolls enlarged and unfurled into massive portraits harnessing formations.","These portraits surrounded the sword container-like object and suppressed the dangerous aura emanated by the map.","“This feeling...” Chu Feng narrowed his eyes.","Long Mucheng flitted over to Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao and said, “Chu Feng, Xiaoxiao, this is the item you have to decipher.”","“Elder, that item looks dangerous,” Long Xiaoxiao asked.","Despite being beside Chu Feng, she couldn’t see Long Zhuoyan and was thus unaware of the conversation that had transpired between the two. That being said, she had realized that the sword container-like object was the item that she and Chu Feng had to decipher, so she had been keeping a close eye on it.","“Don’t worry, you will be safe even if you fail? Those scrolls are left behind by that lord. You can put your heart into deciphering the item,” Long Mucheng said.","Chu Feng asked, “Elder, is that lord’s surname ‘Qing’?”","Long Mucheng was stunned. “Why do you ask that?”","“I have lived in the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm’s Nine Provinces Continent from a young age, and an incredibly talented figure appeared there ten thousand years ago. It was rumored that a golden aurora covered the sky the day he was born. Four massive beasts raced through the sky and roared, shaking the continent.","“He was extremely intelligent even as an infant. He started speaking within a month and was able to walk upright within two. He began learning the zither, chess, calligraphy, and drawing when he was one, and he was familiar with all the classics by the time he was five.","“People began cultivating at ten on that continent, but he reached Origin Realm at nine, Profound Realm at eleven, and Heaven Realm at thirteen. Despite his young age, he had already become the strongest entity on the Nine Provinces Continent.","“The remnant he left behind was coveted by all major powers on the Nine Provinces Continent, but in truth, there was not a single person in the entire Ancestral Martial Lower Realm who could clear his remnant.","“I obtained his legacy by coincidence, which is why I am familiar with him despite not having met him before. I sensed his aura in those portraits,” Chu Feng explained.","Long Mucheng chuckled. “What a coincidence. I didn’t expect you to know Lord Xuantian too!”"]},{"number":6311,"title":"Chapter 6311: Chapter 6309: Waiting For the Fish to Enter the Net","paragraphs":["Chapter 6309: Waiting For the Fish to Enter the Net","“Chu Feng, I didn’t mean to conceal the lord’s identity from you.","“It happened ten thousand years ago, before the emergence of the Ancient Era’s races, and Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragons were still legends from the earlier years of the present era. Our Dragon Breath Clan was small, but we were powerful. No one would dare to snub us.","“However, a series of events happened afterward that nearly led to our clan’s extinction. It was Lord Xuantian who rescued us.”","As Long Mucheng spoke, the Dragon Breath Clansmen also looked over. The gratitude reflected in their eyes showed how they felt toward Qing Xuantian.","Chu Feng and Eggy also realized something.","The Dragon Breath Clan should have been powerful even back then. If Qing Xuantian had the means to save them, it would mean that he was already very powerful back then.","“Lord Xuantian’s strength is unfathomable. I have no doubt that he could topple the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if he wanted to rule over the world of cultivation. The only reason he remains relatively unknown is due to his low profile. That’s why I have never told anyone else about him,” Long Mucheng explained.","“I understand. Elder, do you know where Elder Xuantian is?” Chu Feng asked.","The Moon Immortal, who had possessed Su Mei and Su Rou’s bodies, had been looking for Qing Xuantian all this while. Ever since leaving the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, Chu Feng hadn’t heard anything about the Moon Immortal, Su Rou, or Su Mei.","With a storm brewing in the world of cultivation, Chu Feng was worried that they would meet with danger.","“Lord Xuantian entered the Ninth Galaxy many years ago. Before he left, he told our clan to breach this item, saying that our bloodline will undergo a metamorphosis if we succeed,” Long Mucheng said.","Long Zhuoyan said via voice transmission, “Someone, likely that Qing Xuantian guy, added another formation on top of that sealed item. By releasing the item’s seal, the energy buried here will be released as well. That power is probably what will help the Dragon Breath Clan’s bloodline undergo a metamorphosis.”","Chu Feng realized that despite the formidable prowess of his Heaven’s Eyes and Long Zhuoyan’s regressed spirit power, the latter’s judgment was still not something he could hope to match.","He didn’t notice the power hidden in this land.","“Chu Feng, Xiaoxiao, just give it a try and don’t stress yourself out. It’s fine if it doesn’t work,” Long Mucheng said.","Her eyes were expectant despite her words.","“Elder, I’ll give it my best.”","Chu Feng had been examining the sealed item while conversing with Long Mucheng. He had some clues as to what he should do, but he wasn’t certain if it was the right direction.","“Xiaoxiao, do you have the means to channel your bloodline power?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, I do.” Long Xiaoxiao nodded.","“I’ll construct a formation. You should be able to better channel your bloodline power through the formation. You’ll be the crux to breaching this formation,” Chu Feng said as he passed a pill to her. “Take this. It’ll help in the channeling of your bloodline.”","Unlike martial power and spirit power, bloodline power was not as easy to channel. However, the difficulty could be reduced through auxiliary means such as pills and formations.","“All right, I’ll listen to you,” Long Xiaoxiao replied with a radiant smile before popping Chu Feng’s pill into her mouth. She displayed absolute confidence in him.","Chu Feng continued observing the sealed item.","“What’s wrong? Is it tough?” Eggy asked.","“It’s the opposite. I’m conflicted because the solution isn’t as complicated as I thought it would be,” Chu Feng replied.","He didn’t want anything to go wrong, so he assessed the formation over and over again, but he remained uncertain about the solution he had come up with.","“Does the formation have any hidden tricks to it?”","“That’s what I suspect, but I’m not finding anything despite poring over the formation over and over again. The Dharma Emperor must have engaged many world spiritists to remove the seal. It can’t be as simple as I think it is, or else the other world spiritists should have lifted it by now.”","“Chu Feng, there are three possibilities to this situation.","“One, there might be something deeper hidden inside the formation. Two, the solution could be that simple, but the other world spiritists failed to find a suitable Dragon Clansman to breach the formation. Three, it’s possible the solution is only obvious to you, and that other world spiritists are unable to figure it out. You shouldn’t forget that you possess Heaven’s Eyes. It is capable of seeing things that other world spiritists can’t.","“I’m leaning toward the third possibility. I know you sincerely wish to help the Dragon Breath Clan, and you’re worried the breaching process might go awry and Long Xiaoxiao could get injured as a result. But things are not always that complicated. You need to trust yourself more. You are the person I have chosen, so take pride in that. I believe in you,” Eggy said.","“Your words make sense.”","Eggy’s words knocked sense into Chu Feng. Blind confidence was foolish, but so was a lack of confidence. Since he couldn’t find anything else, he should have more faith in his judgment.","So, he began constructing a series of formations. Each formation was extremely small, but they chained together like a massive army, tightly surrounding the sealed item. It looked complicated, but it didn’t take him much time to complete it.","“Xiaoxiao, enter the formation core and channel your bloodline power. Aside from that, I want you to pay close attention to my instruction. Crush this teleportation talisman as soon as I tell you to retreat.”","Chu Feng handed Long Xiaoxiao a teleportation talisman in case something went awry.","“Mm.” Long Xiaoxiao nodded.","“Young friend Chu Feng, are you going to breach the formation now?” Long Mochuan, a Dragon Breath Clan’s world spiritist, flew to Chu Feng’s side.","Long Moxiao, the Dragon Breath Clan’s chief world spiritist, also landed before Chu Feng. He didn’t utter a word, but the worry in his eyes said it all.","With their spirit powers above Chu Feng’s, they could see how simplistic Chu Feng’s formation was. The sealed item was extremely important to their clan, and they found it unbelievable that such a simple formation could breach its formation.","“Elders, this is the solution I have derived,” Chu Feng explained.","“This...” The two world spiritists frowned.","On the one hand, they knew how formidable Chu Feng was and knew better than to underestimate him just because his spirit power was weaker. In the first place, it was thanks to Chu Feng’s sharp judgment that they managed to break free of their imprisonment.","Still, they couldn’t shake off their worry.","“We’ll do as Chu Feng says,” Long Mucheng interjected.","As the Dragon Breath Clan’s leader, her words carried weight.","Long Mochuan patted Chu Feng’s shoulder and said, “Young friend Chu Feng, I apologize for doubting you. It’s not that I don’t trust you but this matter is simply too important to us. Please don’t mind me and do what you believe is right.”","Long Moxiao didn’t say a word, but he gave an affirmative nod.","Then, the two world spiritists took their leave.","Chu Feng glanced at Long Xiaoxiao. The latter nodded before entering the formation.","Everyone tensed up at this moment, including Chu Feng. Due to that, he didn’t notice Long Zhuoyan’s disappearance.","A humongous formation channeled using a powerful treasure surreptitiously sealed off this Immemorial Storage Realm as if a net awaiting the arrival of the fish."]},{"number":6312,"title":"Chapter 6312: Chapter 6310: The Ninth Galaxy, the Green-robed Man","paragraphs":["Chapter 6310: The Ninth Galaxy, the Green-robed Man","Long Xiaoxiao entered the formation core and began channeling her bloodline power. The formations emanated an imposing golden glow, and dragon roars could be vaguely heard.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal, and the formations shot countless golden beams resembling arrows at the sealed item. This seemingly chaotic barrage was calculated, and it caused the map manifested by the sealed item to warp.","Soon, the sealed item began to crack before shattering into pieces.","As the seal shattered, a blinding light suddenly appeared in the sky. Something appeared to have sealed off this formation realm, though the light swiftly vanished as if it had never been there.","The sealed item vanished, not leaving the slightest trace behind.","“Is it a success, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","“The seal has been lifted,” Chu Feng replied as he looked around for Long Zhuoyan.","The blinding light had only appeared for an instant, but Chu Feng could tell that it was a formidable sealing formation. It was not related to the sealed item, so he suspected that it was Long Zhuoyan’s doing.","But why did the sealing formation only appear for an instant? What was it seeking to seal?","Meanwhile, Long Zhuoyan was in the sky, holding onto golden treasure. The treasure looked normal at first glance, but one could tell that it was a cage upon closer examination.","She turned her gaze to the Ninth Galaxy.","“I couldn’t stop that power. Could the Dharma Emperor still be alive?” Long Zhuoyan murmured.","...","Deep in the Ninth Galaxy, there was a terrifying realm of chaos.","No one knew what was the cause of it, but no other realm existed within a huge radius around this realm. The area was pitch-black except for the dim light shining from the realm, but the light only felt eerie.","Despite the weak light, the realm was massive. On top of that, it was bright on the realm; there was no area on the realm where light didn’t shine on. The light was iridescent and beautiful, but it was also exceedingly dangerous.","The light consisted of purple lightning, blue flames, red tornadoes...","These powers clashed against one another like ferocious beasts fighting for supremacy, and each harnessed the destructive prowess to destroy a realm. Their presence made this place a realm of death.","Unsurprisingly, no plants and animals lived on this realm. Even cultivators dared not to step foot here.","Yet, a middle-aged man with long white hair and a green robe was cultivating in the middle of this realm. The devastating powers eroded one another, but for some reason, they avoided him.","All of a sudden, a powerful wind entered this realm and suppressed all powers. It seeped into the middle-aged man’s body at such an unbelievable speed that a mortal wouldn’t have noticed it at all.","The middle-aged man opened his eyes. Disbelief could be seen in his deep gaze. He quickly closed his eyes once more to inspect his body. He was much calmer when he opened his eyes once more, and he smiled in delight.","“I didn’t expect the Dragon Breath Clan to pull it off. Outstanding juniors must have emerged in that suppressed world of cultivation,” the middle-aged man remarked.","Suddenly, he turned to the sky and looked into distant space. A humongous monstrous beast was swiftly traveling across space, with each step traversing the distance of many realms. Yet, its footsteps were so light that it caused not the slightest disturbance. Even its body was concealed, so most people wouldn’t have noticed it.","As the monstrous beast came closer, its appearance became apparent. It was a crocodile monstrous beast with a human head, a body covered in crocodile scales, and a giant crocodile tail. Its body was shockingly huge.","This eerie realm was vast as it was, but it was not as big as the crocodile monstrous beast’s head.","The crocodile monstrous beast stopped a short distance away from the middle-aged man. With a fearful heart, it carefully relayed its voice into the realm, “Milord?”","“What’s wrong?” the middle-aged man asked.","“Milord, I have something to report.” The crocodile monstrous beast bowed.","“Go ahead.”","“It’s about the world spiritist who just entered this area, Jie Ranqing. I followed your instructions and relayed your invitation to her, but she turned down your offer. Should I teach her a lesson?”","“Did she give a reason for the refusal?”","“No, she didn’t say anything else.”","“The people of the current generation have quite the character.”","“She’s too arrogant. As per milord’s instructions, I prepared a meeting gift and was polite throughout, but she refused to even accept the meeting gift. What disrespect! I considered teaching her a lesson, but I held back because you told me not to be impolite, so I returned to seek your opinion first,” the crocodile monstrous beast said.","“Forget it.” The middle-aged man dismissed the matter with a wave of his hand.","“We aren’t going to do anything? Milord, didn’t you say that she has extraordinary world spiritist techniques, and that you can greatly raise your strength if she comes under your command,” the crocodile monstrous beast asked.","“I am indeed in need of her world spiritist techniques, but there’s no need to push it if she’s reluctant. We’ll see how it goes in the future.”","“Milord, you’re too good-tempered! How can we let things slip just like that?” the crocodile monstrous beast exclaimed.","“Are you aware of the Immemorial Chaos Clan’s plight?” the middle-aged man asked.","“I am. I was once injured by the Immemorial Chaos Clan’s grand elder, so I have been thinking about confronting them for that. But their clan was suddenly decimated one night. A bizarre green flame devoured the starfield and continues to burn even to this day. No one was able to put it out.","“Some say it’s an expert who possesses a unique bloodline. Others say it’s a formation constructed by a powerful world spiritist. I went to take a look myself, and the flame truly exists; it doesn’t seem like a formation at all. It should be a cultivator with a unique bloodline.”","“Since you went there to take a look, do you think you can withstand those green flames?” the middle-aged man asked.","“The green flame’s intense heat can be felt a huge distance away from the starfield. I had to observe it from far away. I’d be reduced to ashes if I were to be afflicted by those green flames.” The crocodile monstrous beast awkwardly scratched his head. “It must have been the deeds of a formidable powerhouse.”","“Yet, you still dare to trifle with Jie Ranqing?”","“What does this have to do with Jie Ranqing?” The crocodile monstrous beast was initially confused, but it quickly realized what the middle-aged man was getting at. Its eyes widened in shock, and its mouth opened so wide as if it was going to devour the realm. “Milord, c-c-c-could Jie Ranqing be the one behind those green flames?”","“She’s indeed the one behind it. I’m stopping you not because I’m good-tempered but because I don’t want to watch you leap to your death,” the middle-aged man said."]},{"number":6313,"title":"Chapter 6313: Chapter 6311: The Three Zenith Emperors","paragraphs":["Chapter 6311: The Three Zenith Emperors","“Isn’t Jie Ranqing from the present era and still very young? Is her talent so scary that it rivals the Ancient Era’s Three Zenith Emperors?” The crocodile monstrous beast found this matter hard to believe.","As an Ancient Era’s entity, it was in the process of recovering its cultivation, which should have been much faster than cultivating from scratch. Even so, it still took tens of thousands of years for it to recover to its current level.","Yet, Jie Ranqing wielded strength surpassing it despite her extremely young age. The rate she was growing at was terrifying.","It couldn’t think of anyone who rivaled her, perhaps except for those three legendary figures in the Ancient Era. But even being on the same pedestal as those three would make Jie Ranqing a frightening individual.","Those three were born in the later years of the Ancient Era, but with their overwhelming talent, they pushed the era to a new zenith, which was why they were later revered as the Three Zenith Emperors.","“Those three?” The mention of the Three Zenith Emperors made the middle-aged man fall into reminiscence. He had crossed paths with those three, so he had a good grasp of their strength. “I can’t say for sure how Jie Ranqing compares to those three. Those three have already proved themselves, whereas Jie Ranqing hasn’t reached their level yet. However, I think that she has the potential. Alternatively, her swift growth could also be due to the suppression of her talent.”","“Suppression of her talent?” The crocodile monstrous beast was perplexed.","“I don’t know what happened in the final years of the Ancient Era, but we know for sure that a formidable power had divided the world of cultivation. Only the Ninth Galaxy retains its original form, whereas the remaining eight galaxies have contracted to an unbelievable degree. That causes not only the natural energies to become extremely thin, but it also has a suppressing effect on one’s talent.","“Unfortunately, there are incredible treasures that remain in those eight galaxies. If the cultivators in those eight galaxies can obtain legacies that even our Ancient Era’s cultivators failed at despite the thin natural energies and the suppression of their talent, they must be extraordinary indeed. Such people would grow at an unbelievable speed once they enter the Ninth Galaxy.","“Rather than the cultivators who have been growing in the Ninth Galaxy all along, it is those who came from the other eight galaxies who are much more unfathomable. I am certain Jie Ranqing belongs to the latter category,” the middle-aged man said.","“Milord, that reminds me. God’s Era has never appeared since the inception of the current era. Could it be in the other eight galaxies?” the crocodile monstrous beast asked.","“I didn’t hear anything about God’s Era while I was there, but some time has passed since I entered the Ninth Galaxy. I have no way of knowing whether it appeared there afterward,” the middle-aged man replied.","“Milord, do you know what kind of power is hidden in God’s Era?”","“Do you know?”","“I heard that it contains the world’s strongest power.”","“It’s a power no one has obtained. Who can ascertain it’s the strongest in the world?”","“That’s true. Rumors are unreliable. Who knows? There might be nothing in God’s Era at all,” the crocodile monstrous beast replied with a fawning smile as he suddenly remembered that the middle-aged man before him had failed to conquer God’s Era too.","No one in the Ancient Era was able to conquer God’s Era, which was how its reputation had spread so far.","“Do you have anything else to report?” the middle-aged man asked.","“I have nothing else to report. Lord Dharma, I’ll take my leave now,” the crocodile monstrous beast said as it bowed deeply.","The middle-aged man immediately interjected, “I told you I have nothing to do with the Dharma Emperor. I am Qing Xuantian.”","“Pardon me for my foolish remark.”","The crocodile monstrous beast realized it had misspoken and quickly slapped itself. To it, the middle-aged man was none other than the Dharma Emperor it had served in the Ancient Era, which was why it called him that out of habit.","“You may go now.” The middle-aged man waved his hand.","After the crocodile monstrous beast left, the middle-aged man sat down and began cultivating. However, he was unable to focus. A slight frown formed on his face. Moments later, he opened his eyes and murmured contemplatively, “Who could have the means to lift Qin Jiu’s seal? Did another formidable individual appear in the eight galaxies?”","...","On Chu Feng’s side, the Immemorial Storage Realm had started changing again.","A massive formation surfaced on the lands, and a brilliant golden light gushed into the sky. Resounding dragon roars shook the world.","The Dragon Breath Clansmen had already entered the formation to accept the formation’s energy with faces beaming with excitement.","However, Long Mucheng, Long Moxiao, and Long Mochuan had yet to enter the formation. They were busy shoving Cosmos Sacks to Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao.","This formation appeared after the sealed item was unsealed, leaving no doubt that it was left specifically for the Dragon Breath Clan. Long Mucheng and the others were extremely grateful to Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao that they decided to give them the compensation right away.","“Take it, Xiaoxiao. It’s their token of goodwill,” Chu Feng said.","He had already accepted his portion, but Xiaoxiao was hesitant to accept hers because she wasn’t close to Long Mucheng.","“Thank you, elder.”","Long Xiaoxiao accepted the Cosmos Sack before flashing a radiant smile at Chu Feng.","The resources inside Chu Feng’s Cosmos Sack wasn’t of much use to him—he was not lacking in those—but Long Xiaoxiao, as a descendant of the Dragon Clan, had much to benefit from the Dragon Breath Clan’s resources.","“Miss Xiaoxiao, our Dragon Breath Clan are descendants of the Dragon Clan too. If you don’t mind, why don’t you become my disciple?” Long Mucheng suddenly said.","She had sensed how formidable Long Xiaoxiao’s bloodline was when she breached the formation earlier, and she didn’t want to miss out on someone with so much potential, not to mention that Long Xiaoxiao was on close terms with Chu Feng.","The Dragon Breath Clan had a high opinion of Chu Feng’s potential. Naturally, it would be worthwhile to get on closer terms with Chu Feng’s friends to deepen their ties.","“This...” Long Xiaoxiao glanced hesitantly at Chu Feng.","It was common for cultivators to have multiple masters, so it wasn’t a problem for her to become Long Mucheng’s disciple. It was just that she didn’t know how Chu Feng’s relationship with Long Mucheng was, so she wanted to consult his opinion first.","Before Chu Feng could reply, a voice echoed, “She can’t be your disciple.”"]},{"number":6314,"title":"Chapter 6314: Chapter 6312: Long Xiaoxiao’s New Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 6312: Long Xiaoxiao’s New Master","Long Zhuoyan revealed herself in mid-air, but no one other than Chu Feng could see her true appearance. She emanated a brilliant light that made her look like a silhouette amid the sun in others’ eyes.","The Dragon Breath Clan tensed up as if they were faced with a formidable enemy.","Even those who had entered the formation to cultivate quickly came out and drew their weapons. Long Mucheng pulled Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao behind her as she questioned, “Who dares to intrude on our Dragon Breath Clan’s territory?”","“Elder, she’s one of our own,” Chu Feng quickly cleared the air.","“She’s one of our own?” Long Mucheng was stunned.","But Long Zhuoyan scoffed in disdain, “Who’s one with the likes of them?”","The Dragon Breath Clansmen had barely breathed a sigh of relief when they heard those words. Their anger shot through the roof as they brandished their weapons, threatening to teach Long Zhuoyan a lesson.","Boom!","An oppressive might suddenly crushed the Immemorial Storage Realm.","Silence followed.","Everyone in the Dragon Breath Clan felt the threat of death. They couldn’t even let out pained moans, let alone utter a word.","“Big sister, I’m on good terms with these elders. They don’t mean to disrespect you; they merely don’t know who you are,” Chu Feng interjected, fearing that Long Zhuoyan would vanquish the Dragon Breath Clan in a fit of anger.","In his eyes, Long Zhuoyan was more than capable of that.","Chu Feng quickly sent a voice transmission to everyone in the Dragon Breath Clan, informing them of Long Zhuoyan’s identity.","As a matter of fact, the Dragon Breath Clansmen had realized the severity of the matter from the moment they felt Long Zhuoyan’s oppressive might. They were relieved when they learned that the person before them was the Totem Dragon Clan’s ‘Lord Ancestral Dragon’, as well as someone whom Chu Feng was on close terms with.","Thankfully, Long Zhuoyan retracted her oppressive might after Chu Feng’s intervention. The Dragon Breath Clan regained their freedom.","“Our deepest apologies for our earlier disrespect, milord. We were unaware of your identity,” Long Mucheng and the Dragon Breath Clansmen apologized to Long Zhuoyan.","Long Zhuoyan completely ignored their apology and instead turned to Chu Feng, “Little brother, hurry up and finish your conversation with them. I’m taking the two of you out of here.”","With that, Long Zhuoyan disappeared into thin air.","However, the crowd knew that she was still here, especially since the Immemorial Storage Realm was still in a sealed state.","“Chu Feng, it seems that lord doesn’t want me to take Miss Xiaoxiao as my disciple,” Long Mucheng spoke to Chu Feng via voice transmission because she was worried that she might misspeak and inadvertently displease Long Zhuoyan.","She then turned to the crowd and addressed them, “Chu Feng, our Dragon Breath Clan is grateful to you and Miss Xiaoxiao for helping us fulfill Lord Xuantian’s mission. We have no way of repaying you. Feel free to ask anything of us once we complete our cultivation. We’ll march up a mountain of blades or descend into a sea of flames at your command!”","“Elder, there’s no need to stand on ceremony. You have already compensated us for our effort,” Chu Feng replied as he took out the Cosmos Sack he had just received and waved it around. “You should start cultivating so that the formation doesn’t go to waste.”","Chu Feng could tell that the formation harnessed extraordinary energy. The Dragon Breath Clan would undergo a metamorphosis if they could make full use of this opportunity.","Once they were done chatting, Long Mucheng opened the Immemorial Storage Realm.","Long Zhuoyan revealed herself and stepped out first. Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao bade farewell to the Dragon Breath Clan and watched the Immemorial Storage Realm close back up before quickly catching up with Long Zhuoyan.","“Waaa! She’s so beautiful!” Long Xiaoxiao suddenly remarked in awe.","Chu Feng realized that Long Xiaoxiao could see Long Zhuoyan’s true appearance too.","“You’re Long Xiaoxiao, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Yes, milord. I am Long Xiaoxiao.”","Long Xiaoxiao was a highly sociable person. She smiled as she bowed, maintaining a respectful but not too restrained attitude. It made her very likable.","Long Zhuoyan smiled as well. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “You’re on good terms with her?”","“We have been friends for a long time, and we have been through difficult times too.” Chu Feng could tell that Long Xiaoxiao’s talent had caught Long Zhuoyan’s attention, so he didn’t hide his close ties with Long Xiaoxiao.","Long Zhuoyan turned to Long Xiaoxiao once more and said, “Not bad. You must have a good character to receive such high praise from my little brother. My little brother should have secretly filled you in about my background by now. So, are you willing to be my disciple?”","Long Xiaoxiao glanced at Chu Feng.","“It’s up to you,” Chu Feng replied.","Long Xiaoxiao kneeled before Long Zhuoyan and said, “Disciple Long Xiaoxiao pays respect to master.”","Long Zhuoyan’s smile widened. She pulled Long Xiaoxiao up and said, “Don’t be in such a rush to acknowledge me as your master. I’m not done with my words yet.”","Long Xiaoxiao’s face stiffened up as she began to panic. She knew this was a rare opportunity that could change her life for good and she didn’t want to miss it.","“You’ll have to enter the Ninth Galaxy with me if you wish to take me as your master. My little brother won’t be going in for the time being, so you’ll be separated from him for a long time,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Long Xiaoxiao breathed a sigh of relief. She was glad to hear that Long Zhuoyan wasn’t turning her down.","“Big sister, Xiaoxiao has been cultivating all this while. We rarely meet,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, will you be entering the Ninth Galaxy too?” Long Xiaoxiao asked.","“Of course. My mother is waiting for me in the Ninth Galaxy,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s good to hear.” Long Xiaoxiao beamed a smile.","“Are you willing to come with me?” Long Zhuoyan asked once more.","“Yes, I am willing,” Long Xiaoxiao replied without hesitation.","“We’ll be setting off now. You won’t be able to accompany Chu Feng to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain,” Long Zhuoyan added.","“I am willing to go wherever my master goes. Master, you are my greatest fortuitous encounter; everything else pales in comparison,” Long Xiaoxiao replied.","“Lass, you have a sweet tongue.” Long Zhuoyan’s chuckle showed that she was fond of Long Xiaoxiao too.","“Little brother, God’s Era has appeared many times in the Ancient Era, but no one has been able to clear it. You can give it a try, but don’t force it. The world of cultivation is very different from how it was in the Ancient Era. I can’t give you any advice about the Ninth Galaxy as I don’t know what’s going on there either, but I can offer you some pointers about the eight galaxies.","“Other than God’s Era, there’s another hidden dimension in the vicinity of the Ninth Galaxy. This hidden dimension is a massive space encompassing countless realms. It is an enigmatic place that even I am unable to see through. Such places are usually very dangerous. It’s one thing if it reveals itself or someone else finds it, but I’d strongly advise you not to get involved.”","Long Zhuoyan’s words were so grim that it made Chu Feng realize that the world of cultivation was filled with unknown dangers."]},{"number":6315,"title":"Chapter 6315: Chapter 6313: Rank Three True God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6313: Rank Three True God","“I understand, big sister,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is there anything else you two want to talk about? Let it all out now. It’ll be a long time before you can meet again,” Long Zhuoyan told Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao.","“Take care, Chu Feng. Don’t push yourself too much. You should prioritize your safety no matter the situation. I’ll be waiting for you in the Ninth Galaxy,” Long Xiaoxiao said.","“Don’t worry, I’ll be there in no time,” Chu Feng replied.","Long Xiaoxiao chuckled. She had tremendous confidence in Chu Feng too. She turned to Long Zhuoyan and said, “Master, I’m done speaking my piece.”","“That’s all?” Long Zhuoyan was baffled. “You aren’t going to hug or anything?”","Long Xiaoxiao’s eyes reddened. She did harbor such a thought, but despite her composed front, being in the presence of a powerhouse like Long Zhuoyan still intimidated her. She dared not to let herself loose.","“Are you embarrassed? Shall I excuse myself for a moment?” Long Zhuoyan smiled in mischief.","Long Xiaoxiao’s face further reddened.","Chu Feng gentlemanly stepped forward and embraced Long Xiaoxiao. She was a close friend who had toiled through tough times with him. There was no saying when they would meet again. A hug wouldn’t have been out of place here.","Chu Feng’s sudden embrace flustered Long Xiaoxiao. By the time she snapped out of her daze and wanted to lean against his chest, he had already let go.","“Take care, Xiaoxiao,” Chu Feng said.","“You too,” Long Xiaoxiao replied gently.","“That’s all?” Long Zhuoyan asked once more.","“What else do you want, big sister? Do you want to come here so that the three of us can have a hug together?” Chu Feng smiled.","He knew Long Zhuoyan better, which allowed him to be less restrained around her.","“You punk.” Long Zhuoyan rolled her eyes. “If you two are done, I still have a few words for my little brother. You come here.”","Long Zhuoyan beckoned to Chu Feng, and the latter walked over.","“I have already warned you about whatever is out there, but since I’m your big sister, I can’t leave just like that. I’ve been to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain before, and resources are very important in that place. Take this. It’ll come in handy.”","Long Zhuoyan handed a palm-sized transparent stone to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng asked as he took the stone, “Big sister, how do I use this?”","The stone looked ordinary, and he couldn’t sense any energy in it.","“You’ll know once you enter the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. You should also assimilate this,” Long Zhuoyan said as she flicked her palm.","Before Chu Feng could see what she had on her palm, she was already pressing her hand against Chu Feng’s dantian area. Gentle energy harnessing martial enlightenment flowed into his dantian.","“Thank you, big sister.”","Chu Feng was overjoyed.","Knowing he had just received an invaluable cultivation resource, he quickly sat down to assimilate it on the spot. The sheer energy he had just received was enough for him to make a breakthrough on the spot.","Boom!","Nine-colored lightning crackled in space.","“Oh? My little brother’s phenomenon sure is shocking.”","Even Long Zhuoyan was impressed by the nine-colored lightning. She had seen nine-colored lightning phenomena before, but they had never been at this scale. Granted that she had heard rumors about it, it was still shocking to witness it in person.","The scale of the phenomenon usually correlated to the extent of one’s talent. This astounding phenomenon gave her a better grasp of how powerful Chu Feng’s Heavenly Lightning Bloodline was. At the very least, it surpassed what she had seen in the Ancient Era.","The nine-colored lightning whizzed down, but Chu Feng emerged unscathed. The lightning eventually dissipated.","Chu Feng’s cultivation advanced from rank two to rank three True God level.","As soon as he opened his eyes, Long Zhuoyan asked, “How are you feeling?”","“I feel great. Your cultivation resource is amazing,” Chu Feng replied with a beaming smile.","“I could have helped you advance a few more cultivation ranks, but advancing gradually will be more beneficial to your future. I have met many people with decent talent and ample resources, but they advance their cultivation so quickly that their foundation becomes unstable. This led to them meeting a bottleneck due to a gap in their enlightenment,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“I understand,” Chu Feng smiled.","“Good.”","Long Zhuoyan opened a teleportation passageway in the middle of space with a wave of her sleeves.","Long Xiaoxiao was flabbergasted, but Chu Feng was unsurprised. Long Zhuoyan used to be one of the top figures in the Ancient Era, after all. Her means were bound to be anything but ordinary.","“This teleportation passageway leads straight to the entrance of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. You’re heading there, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Mmhm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Hurry along.” Long Zhuoyan pushed Chu Feng into the teleportation passageway.","A cloud manifested beneath Chu Feng’s feet as he entered the teleportation passageway, greatly increasing the speed of his travel.","Eggy’s voice echoed in his ears, “Chu Feng, shouldn’t you warn Long Xiaoxiao to be wary of that big sister of yours? That woman was known as a demoness in the Ancient Era.”","“There’s no point mentioning that when Xiaoxiao has already chosen to follow Long Zhuoyan. She’s bound to encounter other dangers in the world of cultivation anyway, so it would be wiser for her to go with Long Zhuoyan. Besides, my big sister seems to be a reliable person, though she seems to have her own thoughts about things...” Chu Feng said.","He had wanted to ask Long Zhuoyan if she was the one who had constructed a formation around the Immemorial Storage Realm to stop the sealed energy from escaping. But on second thought, he decided not to probe.","He already had an answer in his mind anyway, and Long Zhuoyan likely had her reason for doing it secretly too.","He could at least sense goodwill from Long Zhuoyan.","“That’s true. Good and evil are two sides of a coin. I bet many think you are a villain too! ” Eggy said with a laugh.","“That’s true.” Chu Feng chuckled.","That was why he didn’t think he was a good person. In the first place, there was no way to satisfy everyone, so he was never concerned about how others viewed him. All that mattered to him was to keep a clear conscience."]},{"number":6316,"title":"Chapter 6316: Chapter 6314: First Lesson: Be Unscrupulous","paragraphs":["Chapter 6314: First Lesson: Be Unscrupulous","Long Xiaoxiao and Long Zhuoyan watched as Chu Feng left.","“Xiaoxiao, you’ll have to work hard,” Long Zhuoyan suddenly remarked.","“Master, I’ll work hard on my cultivation so as to not let you down,” Long Xiaoxiao promised.","But Long Zhuoyan wasn’t satisfied with that answer. “I don’t just mean working hard in a conventional manner. It’s not about meeting my expectations. You have to work far harder on top of that. Do you know why?”","“I was born humble. It is my blessing to have you as my master, and I mustn’t let you down,” Long Xiaoxiao said.","“What nonsense are you spouting?” Long Zhuoyan shook her head. “I know you’re fond of my little brother.”","“Master, I...” Long Xiaoxiao’s face turned red.","Due to Long Zhuoyan’s presence, she had held herself back from embracing Chu Feng even though she really wanted to do it. Yet, the other party still saw through her. She wondered if her feelings for Chu Feng were that obvious.","Long Zhuoyan burst into laughter. “That further confirms it. Your face wouldn’t turn red otherwise.”","“Master, you...” Long Xiaoxiao’s face further reddened. It turned out that Long Zhuoyan was sounding her out.","Long Zhuoyan wrapped her arm around Long Xiaoxiao’s shoulder as if getting intimate with a fellow sister. Her hearty attitude was unlike how masters usually treated their disciples.","But Long Xiaoxiao preferred this. She had seen how Long Zhuoyan interacted with Chu Feng, and she would be delighted if she could bare her heart to Long Zhuoyan and talk about anything under the sun too.","But what Long Zhuoyan said next cooled Long Xiaoxiao’s heart.","“It’s normal for you to be fond of my little brother. My little brother is very outstanding. I’d have been moved too if not for our massive age difference. But Xiaoxiao, you have to understand a fact. It’s normal for people to fancy good things. What you find great, others can find it great too. You shouldn’t take your closeness with him for granted. If you want to be with him, you have to become worthy of him.","“Feelings are important in a relationship, but for the relationship to last long, you will have to be on the same footing as him. Even parents would favor a child over the other, let alone someone whom you don’t have blood ties with. You’ll have to work very hard to get what you want.”","Long Xiaoxiao nodded. “I understand, master, but I don’t ask for Chu Feng to fancy me. I just hope to be able to do something for him when he’s in need of help. He has helped me a lot, and I wish to do the same for him too.”","The corners of Long Zhuoyan’s lips further crept upward into an enigmatic smile.","“Xiaoxiao, I don’t doubt your words, but that only shows your lack of self-confidence. Would you turn down my little brother if he says he wants to be with you?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","Long Xiaoxiao fell silent, and Long Zhuoyan didn’t urge her for an answer either. She saw through Long Xiaoxiao—the latter felt a sense of inferiority when it came to Chu Feng, which was why she dared not dream of even being with him.","Long Zhuoyan was trying to make her aware of her feelings so that she could have a clearer goal in mind.","A long time later, Long Xiaoxiao meekly answered, “I want to be with him.”","“I can’t hear you,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Long Xiaoxiao was stunned, but she tightened her fists and spoke even louder, “I want to be with him! I want to stand beside Chu Feng instead of being a baggage to him!”","Long Xiaoxiao shouted her wish as she looked at the direction where Chu Feng left. Her eyes reflected determination like never before. Her eyes were now set on a new goal.","Long Zhuoyan patted Long Xiaoxiao’s head with a satisfied smile. “That’s more like it. My disciple shouldn’t be so timid as to dare not even court the man she likes. But Xiaoxiao, the road to becoming strong is fraught with dangers. I’m bringing you down a path unlike how you have lived before. This shall be your first lesson.”","Long Zhuoyan grinned at Long Xiaoxiao.","“Please enlighten me, master.” Long Xiaoxiao stood upright as she looked at her master with a serious expression.","Long Zhuoyan suddenly opened her palm, revealing a pill emanating a red aura.","Goosebumps covered Long Xiaoxiao’s body as she suddenly felt terror like never before.","The pill was the size of a fingernail, but upon closer examination, she could tell that it was made up of countless bloodied skeletons who seemed to have lives of their own. She could even hear their miserable cries.","Long Xiaoxiao opened her mouth in fright as she instinctively took a step back.","However, Long Zhuoyan stuffed the red pill into her mouth before sending waves of spirit power over to hasten the diffusion of the pill, till the pill was fully fused with Long Xiaoxiao’s soul.","“Xiaoxiao, this is a gu poison. You’ll suffer a fate worse than death if you ever think about rebelling against me. Don’t blame me for this. I have suffered so many setbacks in the world of cultivation that I must have everything under my control.","“This is my first lesson. Scruples should be the least of your concern if you wish to rise through the ranks in the world of cultivation,” Long Zhuoyan said before releasing Long Xiaoxiao.","Long Xiaoxiao fell to her knees.","Long Zhuoyan frowned, thinking that Long Xiaoxaio was going to beg for mercy.","However, Long Xiaoxiao first kowtowed to her before raising her head. Her fear had yet to dissipate, but her eyes were more determined than ever.","“Master, I’ll never betray you. May this gu poison torture me to death if I ever think about rebelling against you.”","Long Zhuoyan was surprised to hear that. “You don’t blame me for what I did?”","“No. It’s an honor for someone from a humble background like me to become master’s disciple. I understand why master is guarded against me, but you’ll know what kind of person I am over time and come to trust me. I don’t fear the gu poison because I know that I will not rebel against master,” Long Xiaoxiao replied.","Long Zhuoyan was startled. “Good. As expected of someone my little brother trusts. There is something special about you. You are qualified to be my disciple. Come, I’ll show you the true world of cultivation.”","She waved her sleeves, and another teleportation passageway appeared. She grabbed Long Xiaoxiao’s hand and led her in.","This teleportation passageway led to the Ninth Galaxy."]},{"number":6317,"title":"Chapter 6317: Chapter 6315: Steel Peak","paragraphs":["Chapter 6315: Steel Peak","Long Zhuoyan was extremely meticulous.","Chu Feng found himself standing in the middle of a realm from the moment he stepped out of the teleportation formation, but not a person noticed him. Powerful concealment energy had enveloped him and the teleportation passageway’s exit from the moment they appeared.","Needless to say, it was Long Zhuoyan’s doing.","Countless figures, both monstrous beasts and humans, filled the earth and the sky.","There were gigantic monstrous beasts who were over tens of thousands meters tall, but even they paled in comparison to the humongous spirit formation gate that towered in this realm. It was so big that it couldn’t be measured using conventional units; it extended beyond the realm into space.","It was the entrance to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain and the reason so many experts had come to this realm.","“Chu Feng, is there any reaction from Little Fishy’s tracking talismans?”","Little Fishy had sent several tracking talismans back with her message, linked not just to her but Xianhai Shaoyu and Wang Qiang too. Chu Feng would be able to locate them using the tracking talisman as long as they were in each other’s vicinity.","“There’s no reaction yet. It’ll probably only work after I enter the spirit formation gate.”","Chu Feng flitted toward the spirit formation gate while maintaining his concealed state. He had to remain on his guard, not just against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion but for other powers who coveted his Genesis Bloodline too.","To those with strength and ambition, Chu Feng was practically a walking treasury. That was also why he thought Long Zhuoyan was trustworthy, for she had the strength to plunder his treasures but didn’t do so.","Chu Feng passed through the spirit formation gate and entered another realm.","Despite the majestic spirit formation gate, the realm on the other side looked no different from other realms. If one had to point out something special about this realm, it would be that it was covered in verdant mountains.","A mountain in the far distance particularly caught Chu Feng’s attention. One of its peak resembled a sharp sword piercing in the sky. Furthermore, that mountain would flicker in and out of appearance as if it didn’t belong to this realm.","That mountain was the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, but unlike the projection outside, this one was the real deal. Naturally, it was also much smaller than the projection outside.","“It’s reacting now.”","Chu Feng took out the tracking talisman. It was pointing toward the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. He immediately got moving.","At the same time, he took out the stone Long Zhuoyan gave him when they parted ways. It was previously transparent, but it had turned golden and was emanating a blinding light.","“Hm? This stone is reacting too. Are you able to tell what it’s for?” Eggy asked.","“There’s a connection between this stone and the mountain peak.”","Chu Feng couldn’t sense much at the start, but the feeling he got from the stone got increasingly salient as he approached the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","“This stone harnesses considerable energy, and it’s linked to the rewards in the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. No wonder my big sister said that the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is very dependent on resources. This stone is the resource,” Chu Feng said.","“Your big sister has done you a huge favor this time. The resource she gave you looks anything but simple,” Eggy remarked.","“I think so too.” Chu Feng stowed the stone away.","As Chu Feng got closer to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, he noticed that the place wasn’t open yet. The mountain was still sealed off by a barrier, so a huge crowd was waiting around the mountain. Temporary palaces were erected on nearby peaks, and the sky was filled with flying warships, war chariots, and palaces.","A glowing steel mountain peak could be seen in the distance.","It was a treasure, though Chu Feng couldn’t see through it. Words were inscribed on its face, saying that only those with corresponding resources could benefit from the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. Those who sought better resources could scale the mountain peak.","Chu Feng spent a while observing the steel mountain before saying, “I sense the Ancient Era’s aura from that steel mountain. I wonder which Ancient Era’s power it is from. It is enveloped in an isolation barrier that only allows juniors through.”","Wang Qiang’s tracking talisman pointed to the steel mountain peak, whereas Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s tracking talismans pointed to the foot of the steel mountain peak.","Chu Feng couldn’t decipher anything else from his surroundings, so he decided to make a move. He soon found Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu, as well as their parents and grandfather, on a simple-looking warship near the steel mountain.","They had disguised themselves, but Chu Feng could tell it was them from their facial features.","“Big brother!”","“Brother Chu Feng, you came at a good time!”","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and the others rushed forward to greet Chu Feng.","“It seems like the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain isn’t open yet. What’s the situation with the steel mountain peak?” Chu Feng asked.","“Big brother, I was about to tell you about that,” Little Fishy said.","It turned out that stones of different colors that harnessed remnants within them had been appearing in this realm recently. These stones emanated auras similar to that of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, which led many to believe that they were linked","However, there were too many people and too few stones. Fights broke out over the stones, and many people had died as a result.","“Big brother, these are the stones.”","Little Fishy took out thirteen stones and passed them to Chu Feng.","These thirteen stones were extremely small, only the size of a fingernail, and they emanated faint lights reminsicent of sparks that could go out at any moment. These stones were silver in color, but they looked turbid and unpure.","Chu Feng could sense a connection between these silver stones and the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, but none of them came close to matching Long Zhuoyan’s golden stone.","“There are differences in the stones’ qualities. These thirteen stones are of slightly better quality, but the best ones are on that steel mountain peak,” Little Fishy said.","“You have been there?” Chu Feng asked.","“Mmhm. That steel mountain was left there by an Ancient Era’s power known as the Zhao Immortal Clan. There are many Zhao Immortal Clansmen on that steel mountain, and you can obtain these stones by defeating them in a duel. Wang Qiang challenged the strongest one there, but it turned out that fellow was not a junior. He ended up losing the duel.”"]},{"number":6318,"title":"Chapter 6318: Chapter 6316: Wang Qiang Returns","paragraphs":["Chapter 6316: Wang Qiang Returns","“But the steel mountain peak is enveloped by a barrier that only allows juniors to enter.”","Chu Feng was perplexed.","“We noticed that detail too, which led us to think that there would only be juniors on the steel mountain peak. We didn’t expect to encounter someone older there. He claims to be slightly beyond a hundred years of age and argued that it is fair,” Little Fishy scoffed in anger.","“Zhao Daobin’s clan has quite the means,” Eggy remarked.","Chu Feng had heard about the Zhao Immortal Clan.","While the God Clan’s Shen Bai was going on a massacre at the Immemorial Massacre Sea’s entrance, an old man named Zhao Daobin from the Zhao Immortal Clan suddenly appeared.","He was a powerful cultivator, being at rank three Heavenly God level, but he couldn’t defeat Shen Bai due to the God Clan’s unique ability. Right as Shen Bai was about to kill Zhao Daobin, the Divine Deer suddenly intervened and saved all of them.","Zhao Daobin, despite his arrogance, was grateful to Chu Feng and told him about the God Clan’s legend.","“How strong are they?” Chu Feng asked.","“There are a hundred people up there. I don’t know how strong the others are, but the one Wang Qiang challenged should be the strongest. His base cultivation is rank four True God level, but he can raise his fighting prowess to rank seven True God level with his bloodline power.","“Wang Qiang is at rank three True God level, but he can also raise his fighting prowess to rank seven True God level,” Little Fishy replied.","Chu Feng realized that the Zhao Immortal Clansmen were formidable foes. “Is Wang Qiang still unable to defeat the other party despite raising his cultivation to rank seven True God level?”","“We didn’t see how the battle went, but Wang Qiang lost. My brother and I wanted to challenge that person to rescue Wang Qiang, but the latter told us via voice transmission to leave him be. He said that we can’t risk exposing ourselves here, and it would be unwise for us to be trapped there too,” Little Fishy said.","“What happens to those who lose?” Chu Feng asked.","“Those who lose will have to do something for them. We don’t know what exactly it is, but they promised that the deed would not pose a threat to our lives. We were evicted from the mountain because we didn’t challenge that guy,” Little Fishy said.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief added, “This happened yesterday. Yu’er and Shaoyu informed me of the matter as soon as they returned. We wanted to march into the mountain to save Wang Qiang, but we couldn’t overcome the restriction on the mountain.”","Little Fishy continued the story, “My brother and I went up again afterward, but we couldn’t find Wang Qiang. We asked the Zhao Immortal Clansmen for his whereabouts, but they said that we weren’t qualified to know that.”","“We were worried about Wang Qiang, so we challenged the Zhao Immortal Clansmen. However, they said that we have lost our rights to challenge them when we forfeited the day before,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Aren’t they too much?”","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu looked frustrated when they talked about the matter.","“He should be fine. Wait here for me. I’ll head up to see what’s going on. Little Fishy, you should take these back.” Chu Feng handed the silver stones back to Little Fishy.","Little Fishy refused the silver stones and said, “Big brother, let’s go up together.”","The others also expressed their desire to follow him.","Chu Feng knew that he wouldn’t be able to dissuade them, so he said, “Fine, let’s go together, but you should keep these resources.”","“You take them, big brother. They’ll come in useful later on. I have more,” Little Fishy replied.","Xianhai Shaoyu winked at Chu Feng. “Take them. It’ll make my little sister happy.”","These silver stones were nothing compared to Long Zhuoyan’s golden stone, but they were the better resources Little Fishy had collected over the last few days.","“I have something better. I can share it,” Chu Feng said as he took out the golden stone.","“My gosh! Chu Feng, where did you get that from?”","The crowd was stunned to see the golden stone. They could sense that the golden stone was also connected to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, but its quality was so high that what they had collected so far felt like dirt in comparison.","“It was from big sister,” Chu Feng replied.","“Big sister? No wonder,” Little Fishy remarked.","Xianhai Shaoyu and the others nodded in realization too. They knew that the Totem Dragon Clan’s Lord Ancestral Dragon had become Chu Feng and Little Fishy’s big sister.","Chu Feng wanted to split the stone apart and share it with the rest. Even though the stone wasn’t big either, it was so high quality that even a grain of it was superior to the silver stones. Of course, Chu Feng also wouldn’t be so stingy as to share only a grain of it.","Weng!","Chu Feng fused his spirit power into the golden stone, only for a formation to suddenly surface. It was a powerful sealing formation carrying Long Zhuoyan’s aura.","“A formation?” Chu Feng frowned.","He didn’t notice this formation until now. Long Zhuoyan must have set up the formation in a way that it wouldn’t surface unless he tried to split the golden stone apart.","“Your big sister must have planted the formation there because she doesn’t want you to share the resource with others. I have to say that she really knows you well,” Eggy said mirthfully.","She didn’t mind Chu Feng sharing the golden stone with Little Fishy as she was fond of her too, but she didn’t like him sharing the golden stone with the others as well. But she kept her silence because she knew that she wouldn’t be able to dissuade Chu Feng from it.","The situation worked in her favor.","“Big sister must have known you would try to split the golden stone, so she planted that formation there in advance to stop you.” Little Fishy burst into laughter. She was amused by Long Zhuoyan’s foresight.","“I didn’t expect big sister to do this.” Chu Feng looked awkward.","Now, it just felt like he was flaunting the golden stone to them.","“Don’t worry about it, my brother. That elder gifted that golden stone to you. Even if not for that, we would still have to conquer this trial with our strength,” Xianhai Shaoyu smiled.","“Didn’t you mention earlier that there are better resources on the steel mountain? Let’s get them,” Chu Feng said.","So, the group began making their way up the steel mountain. Chu Feng first disguised his appearance before removing his concealment.","As soon as they stepped out of the palace, they spotted a figure flying toward them.","The faces of Chu Feng and the others lit up. That figure had disguised himself, but they could still recognize him at a single glance.","Before Chu Feng could utter a word, a voice transmission was relayed to his ears, “Brother, y-y-you’re here! That’s g-g-great! I was worried that you couldn’t make it in time.”","By the time he finished the sentence, he had already landed on the warship.","“Wang Qiang, are you all right?” Xianhai Shaoyu and the others were overjoyed to see Wang Qiang, especially since he looked unscathed.","“What c-c-could have happened to me? It’s no big deal to me,” Wang Qiang replied with a grin.","But Chu Feng grabbed his wrist and channeled a wave of spirit power into his body. Seconds later, he frowned. “How can this be considered fine?”"]},{"number":6319,"title":"Chapter 6319: Chapter 6317: The Zhao Immortal Clan’s Zhao Cangjing","paragraphs":["Chapter 6317: The Zhao Immortal Clan’s Zhao Cangjing","Xianhai Shaoyu and his parents placed their hands on Wang Qiang’s body to inspect his condition. Only then did they realize that despite the latter appearing fine on the surface, his body was extremely frail as if someone had depleted his vitality.","“I’m fine. I just need some time to r-r-recover. Don’t worry about m-m-me. I can’t be a sore l-l-loser, right?” Wang Qiang was unfazed by it.","“What happened? What did they make you do that depleted your bloodline?” Chu Feng asked.","“They had me help them refine s-s-something that depleted my bloodline, but it’s fine. I didn’t hurt my c-c-core. It’s only a matter of time before I r-r-recover,” Wang Qiang replied.","Chu Feng already had some conjectures based on his observation, and Wang Qiang’s story was aligned with that. The situation was acceptable, but he couldn’t stand seeing his brother getting bullied by others.","“Is that person very strong?” Chu Feng asked.","“H-h-he is quite strong, and he has means too. But he shouldn’t be a match for you i-i-if you have reached rank three True God level,” Wang Qiang said.","“What a coincidence. I have reached rank three True God level,” Chu Feng replied.","“Big brother has made a breakthrough too?” Little Fishy exclaimed in delight.","However, the happiest one of all was none other than Wang Qiang.","“W-w-what are we waiting for? Let’s go! We need to g-g-get even for me!” Wang Qiang said.","“Let’s go then. I was planning to meet them anyway,” Chu Feng replied.","So, Chu Feng, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu made their way to the Steel Peak. The peak was covered by a layer of spirit power that obscured the area while restricting access to only juniors.","Chu Feng stopped right before the spirit power layer to observe it.","Wang Qiang and the others stopped as well.","A while later, Chu Feng chuckled. “I see.”","“What is it?” Eggy asked.","Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and Xianhai Shaoyu looked at Chu Feng with curious eyes.","“This spirit power is very strong; it is nigh impossible to overcome its restriction. It is also equipped with detection capabilities, possibly allowing them to detect the cultivation of those passing through the spirit power,” Chu Feng told Wang Qiang and the others via voice transmission.","Other than them, a steady stream of junior cultivators was also entering the mountain.","“It has such an effect?” Wang Qiang and the others were stunned.","They had passed through the spirit power, but they didn’t realize that it could gauge their cultivation. Soon, they widened their eyes in realization.","“No wonder the woman I f-f-first challenged rejected me, saying I was too ugly. That sent me spiralling into self-doubt. How an I-I-I be ugly? She must have known I was a rank three True God level cultivator and that she wasn’t a match for m-m-me! Damn it! They were c-c-cheating all this while!” Wang Qiang was infuriated.","“That seems to be the case. I tried challenging a weaker cultivator to see what I could get, but that person rejected my challenge under the excuse that he was cultivating. But while Brother Wang Qiang was sparring with that golden-haired young man, that fellow accepted someone else’s challenge and won.","“Yu’er secretly told me then that they were picking their opponents, but I shrugged it off. She was right all along!” Xianhai Shaoyu exclaimed.","“See. I told you there’s something off about them,” Little Fishy said.","“Don’t worry, I have a way to deal with that.”","Chu Feng formed a series of hand seals. It looked like nothing was happening on the surface, but layers of spirit power enveloped his soul, forming a formation that emanated the aura of a rank nine Half-God level cultivator.","“Let’s go.”","Chu Feng finally entered the mountain peak.","As he had expected, a discreet aura infiltrated his body when he stepped through the spirit power, but it only reached the formation enveloping his soul. The chances were that he had successfully deceived the spirit power.","The mountain peak was not small, but it wasn’t big enough.","There were a hundred stone plates at the center of the mountain peak. These stone plates were around ten meters in diameter, and a person was seated on each of them. There were both men and women among them, and they looked young.","They wore glowing golden robes that flaunted their strength and nobility, emanating auras that indicated that they were anything but ordinary.","They were Zhao Immortal Clansmen, and there would be rewards for defeating them.","The hundred stone plates floated at different altitudes, indicating their strength.","The one seated on the highest stone plate was a golden-haired man. He had fair skin and decent looks, but his eyes were icy-cold. He gave off a dangerous feeling that pushed others away.","While Chu Feng and the others were assessing him, he was doing the same. However, he merely cast a glance at Chu Feng and the others before turning his sights back onto Wang Qiang.","“You have returned. Do you want a rematch?” the golden-haired man asked.","“Zhao Cangjing, I-I-I’ll rechallenge you! Do you dare accept?” Wang Qiang asked.","Everyone seated on the stone plates instinctively looked at Wang Qiang. They were perplexed by how Wang Qiang knew the golden-haired man’s name.","“You’re too weak now. I’ll merely be bullying you. However, I’m in a good mood now. I’m willing to give that girl a chance if she wants to challenge me,” Zhao Cangjing said as he looked at Little Fishy.","“What’s wrong with that fellow? I thought he said Little Fishy wasn’t qualified to challenge him earlier? Why did he suddenly change his tune?” Eggy was confused.","“He might have used a skill that depleted himself while battling Wang Qiang, so he wasn’t confident of defeating Little Fishy in a weakened state. After all, Little Fishy is at rank three True God level as well, just like Wang Qiang,” Chu Feng replied.","“That man is despicable,” Eggy scoffed.","Little Fishy turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Big brother, can I fight him?”","Instead of answering the question, Chu Feng turned to Zhao Cangjing and asked, “Does it mean that my two friends are qualified to challenge you people now?”","Zhao Cangjing shook his head. “I gave them a chance, but they didn’t take it. Now, they don’t call the shots anymore. That girl only has the option to choose between challenging me or not. She doesn’t have the right to choose her opponent.”","“What about me?” Chu Feng asked.","“Hahaha!’","Laughter echoed throughout. It was not just Zhao Cangjing but all the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","“You can choose whichever opponent you want,” Zhao Cangjing said after his laughter.","“Good.” Chu Feng smiled."]},{"number":6320,"title":"Chapter 6320: Chapter 6318: Time to Change the Rules","paragraphs":["Chapter 6318: Time to Change the Rules","“Who’s that fellow? He’s so arrogant.”","Many juniors were gathered on the mountain peak. Some planned on challenging the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, but the majority were assessing the situation.","Some arrived early and saw many people challenging the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, only to land in defeat. From that, they realized that this challenge was not a godsend opportunity.","The chances of success were so slim that they hadn’t seen anyone succeed.","Chu Feng’s group had disguised themselves so that no one recognized them. For unfamiliar faces to speak such big words was nothing short of arrogance.","“You wish to challenge me?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“Does no one in your group dare to accept my challenge?” Chu Feng asked.","Those words made the Zhao Immortal Clansmen burst into laughter.","A man seated on one of the lower stone plates pointed at Chu Feng and scoffed, “Hahahaha! You sure are an arrogant one. Very well, I’ll play with you.”","But Chu Feng waved his hand, saying, “You? You aren’t qualified.”","“I’m not qualified? A mere rank nine Half-God dares say I’m not qualified?”","The man released his aura as he spoke, revealing himself as a rank one True God level cultivator.","His words piqued cold glares from the Zhao Immortal Clansmen. He had given them away by revealing Chu Feng’s cultivation prematurely, indicating that they didn't fear Chu Feng because they knew his cultivation level.","But Chu Feng didn’t nitpick on that. “It doesn’t matter what my cultivation is. I am challenging you right now. Do you dare to accept my challenge?”","Chu Feng took out a dozen fingernail-sized golden stone fragments with a flick of his wrist.","“What the... Where did he find such good resources?”","Everyone’s eyes lit up at the sight of the golden stone fragments, including the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","Chu Feng had forged those stones using his spirit power. Other than their smaller sizes, their perceived quality was on par with the golden stone he had received from Long Zhuoyan.","The stone fragments he had were of so high quality that others desired them.","“Where did you get that from?” a Zhao Immortal Clansman asked. He spoke in a forceful manner that made it clear that he wouldn’t let this matter slip until he got his answer.","On the other hand, Zhao Cangjing, who defeated Wang Qiang, asked, “What do you mean by this?”","“The people here desire your resources, but what I want is different. You defeated my friend earlier and made him pay a price. I am here to get even for him. Let’s make things fair. If you defeat me, I’ll let you have all these. If you lose, I’ll be taking all your resources,” Chu Feng said.","“I’ll play with you.”","“Leave it to me.”","Many Zhao Immortal Clansmen took up Chu Feng’s challenge, including those on higher stone plates.","But Chu Feng shook his head and said, “Since I brought out these resources, don’t you think the rules ought to change? I’ll be the one deciding who to fight now. You, you, you, you...”","Chu Feng pointed at thirty of the hundred Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","The crowd was stunned.","Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu exchanged looks. They sensed that Chu Feng was up to no good.","“So who are you challenging?” an impatient Zhao Immortal Clansman asked.","“Isn’t it clear? I’m challenging all thirty of you at once,” Chu Feng replied.","“You want to fight thirty of us at once? Hah! Are you trying to paint as unscrupulous individuals who gang up on the weak?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“I just don’t want to waste time by challenging you one by one. That’s too much of a hassle. Don’t worry, I’m the one proposing the challenge here. There are many eyes here; no one would think that you are ganging up on me. They would only think that I’m arrogant.”","Chu Feng glanced at the crowd. “Right?”","“He’s indeed arrogant.”","“The resources he has are tempting though.”","The crowd voiced out.","The ones Chu Feng pointed out didn’t accept the challenge right away. Instead, they turned to Zhao Cangjing.","Zhao Cangjing nodded and tossed out a sphere. The sphere was only ten meters wide, but it contained a mini formation realm.","The challenge was usually held on the stone plate, which could turn into a dueling ring for that purpose, but it would be difficult for so many people to fight simultaneously on the stone plate. This mini formation realm allowed people to see inside, making it an ideal substitute.","The thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen leapt off their stone plates and prepared to enter the formation realm.","“Hold on. I have already brought out my resources, so shouldn’t you show yours too?” Chu Feng asked.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen turned to Zhao Cangjing once more.","Zhao Cangjing nodded.","A Zhao Immortal Clanswoman looked at Chu Feng in contempt and said, “Do you think we would be sore losers? Here, take a look yourself.”","She took out a Cosmos Sack and waved it. Thirty or so stone fragments drifted out from within. These stone fragments were higher quality than what Little Fishy planned to give Chu Feng.","The other twenty-nine people also took out their resources. They were all stone fragments, but their quality was higher than what the first woman offered.","“Woah!”","The crowd salivated at the sight of those stone fragments.","“But none of those resources match that fellow’s golden stone fragment. Where did he find those kind of good resources?”","The crowd could tell Chu Feng’s resources were far better than the thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","“Not bad. At least you have some sincerity,” Chu Feng said before entering the mini formation realm.","The thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen did the same too.","The crowd outside gathered around the mini formation realm, not wanting to miss this battle.","“Let’s place the resources at the entrance. Whoever wins gets to take it all away. How does that sound?” Chu Feng suggested as he placed the golden stone fragments at the entrance.","“Sure.”","This time, the Zhao Immortal Clansmen didn’t bother seeking Zhao Cangjing’s opinion and placed their stone fragments at the entrance too.","“The strongest wins, right? Are there any restrictions?” Chu Feng asked.","“There are no restrictions. As long as you can defeat us, you can take our resources. I hope you won’t be a sore loser. You’re the one who challenged the thirty of us together,” the Zhao Immortal Clanswoman said.","“Yes, yes. Can we start already?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course.”","Without any hesitation, a Zhao Immortal Clanswoman flitted behind Chu Feng. At the same time, she revealed her cultivation as a rank one True God level, though by the time she was behind Chu Feng, her cultivation had already risen to rank two True God level.","The other twenty-nine also revealed their cultivation—their cultivation was roughly on the same range as the Zhao Immortal Clanswoman.","Uwa!","Miserable cries echoed. The crowd was dumbstruck.","The Zhao Immortal Clanswoman crumbled to the floor. The same happened to the other twenty-nine too.","Chu Feng revealed his spirit power—rank three True Dragon.","By the time the crowd snapped out of their daze, Chu Feng had already walked out of the mini formation realm with all the resources placed at the entrance."]},{"number":6321,"title":"Chapter 6321: Chapter 6319: Rank Three True Dragon? Rank Seven True Dragon!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6319: Rank Three True Dragon? Rank Seven True Dragon!","“He’s a rank three True Dragon World Spiritist?!”","The crowd stared at Chu Feng with their mouths agape. In particular, the outsiders no longer viewed Chu Feng in disdain. Many were so frightened that they sent private messages to Chu Feng to apologize for their earlier disrespect.","A rank three True Dragon World Spiritist junior was unheard of!","There was no doubt in their mind that he had a formidable background! He was most likely not a present-era junior from a prodigy from a powerful Ancient Era clan.","“You aren’t a junior! You’re cheating!”","The thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen rushed out.","“How could I enter this place if I’m not a junior?” Chu Feng asked.","“You must have cheated!”","A Zhao Immortal Clanswoman pointed at Chu Feng with hardened eyes, convinced the latter was not a junior.","“This is a treasure to gauge whether a person is a junior or not.”","Not wanting to waste his breath, Chu Feng flicked his wrist and took out a treasure to test one’s age. He was going to prove himself!","But right before Chu Feng crushed the treasure, he flitted into the middle of the thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","Pah!","The treasure shattered. A golden light gushed out and enveloped Chu Feng and the thirty Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","The crowd widened their eyes in shock. Chu Feng had used a common treasure that most recognized, so they knew there wasn't a problem with it.","What was problematic was the Zhao Immortal Clansmen’s reaction to the treasure. More than half of them weren’t juniors.","“Some of us are indeed not juniors here, but it isn’t me,” Chu Feng looked at the Zhao Immortal Clanswoman as he spoke. The latter wasn’t wrapped in the golden light, which showed she wasn’t a junior.","The Zhao Immortal Clanswoman didn’t expect Chu Feng to make such a move. Her face turned crimson, and she struggled to find the words to refute him.","It was Zhao Cangjing who intervened.","“We never said that we were all juniors, but none of us exceeds two hundred years of age,” Zhao Cangjing explained.","“Is that fair?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s up for us to decide. You can choose not to challenge us if you find it unfair,” Zhao Cangjing said.","“Fewer people would have challenged you if you said that in advance,” Chu Feng pointed out.","The crowd secretly whispered among themselves through voice transmission, criticizing the Zhao Immortal Clansmen for their shameless actions.","Chu Feng was right. The Zhao Immortal Clansmen did have the right to determine the rules, but they should have made it clear beforehand instead of concealing that they were not juniors.","A voice from the crowd shouted, “That guy is right. You can dictate the rules here as the organizers, but you should have informed us beforehand. This mountain peak is shrouded in a spirit power layer that only grants access to juniors. This misled us into thinking that it would be a duel between juniors. Yet, it turned out that most of you aren’t juniors. This is deception!","“So what if you aren’t beyond two hundred years of age? Even a difference of a few years can mean a lot when it comes to prodigies like us!”","The crowd panicked upon hearing those words. They shared the same thoughts, but they dared not voice them aloud as they couldn’t afford to offend the Zhao Immortal Clan.","The crowd quickly parted to reveal a lone woman.","This woman looked ordinary, and it was impossible to perceive her cultivation level too. However, she looked extremely calm, so much so that it was hard to believe she didn’t have a powerful backing.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen looked at the woman with hostile eyes, but none of them said a word. They still cared about their reputation, so they were reluctant to do anything overboard in public.","“I already said that we’re the ones who decide the rules. It’s up to us to decide whether to divulge our ages or not. You can choose not to challenge us if you think it is unfair,” Zhao Cangjing re-emphasized his stance, not sounding apologetic in the least.","He then turned to Chu Feng with wrathful eyes and asked, “Do you want to continue the challenge, rank three True Dragon World Spiritist?”","By now, it was apparent to him that the other party had taken them for a ride. This explained why the other party was unfazed despite a Zhao Immortal Clansman exposing that they already knew that he was a rank nine Half-God level cultivator in advance.","It turned out that the other party majored in spirit power.","“I can continue if you’re willing to accept my challenge,” Chu Feng replied.","“Very well. Who do you intend to challenge?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“You...” Chu Feng pointed at Zhao Cangjing.","Zhao Cangjing was overjoyed when he heard those words. He couldn’t wait for Chu Feng to challenge him so that he could teach him a lesson.","But Chu Feng then continued, “Everyone aside from you.”","“What did you say?” Zhao Cangjing was startled.","“I said I’m going to challenge everyone except for you. Are my words that hard to comprehend?” Chu Feng asked.","“Hah...” Zhao Cangjing burst into laughter. “Do you take our clansmen to be pushovers?”","Zhao Cangjing turned to the other Zhao Immortal Clansmen. “Go, show that rank three True Dragon World Spiritist what our Zhao Immortal Clan is capable of.”","All the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, except Zhao Cangjing and the thirty clansmen whom Chu Feng had defeated, entered the mini formation realm. They placed their resources at the entrance before turning to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng entered the mini formation realm too.","Little Fishy couldn’t help but worry.","“I-i-it’s fine. Don’t you know what my brother is capable of? He’s more than capable of dealing with such small fries,” Wang Qiang calmly reassured her.","“Come, let’s begin,” Chu Feng said.","Countless bursts of energy simultaneously attacked Chu Feng right away. The Zhao Immortal Clansmen dared not to let their guard down after witnessing the earlier defeat of their brethren, so they unleashed their strongest means right from the get-go.","Despite them raising their cultivation, their strongest member was only at rank six True God level. Needless to say, they weren’t a match for Chu Feng.","On top of being a rank three True Dragon World Spiritist, Chu Feng’s spirit power fighting prowess commanded heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting four cultivation ranks. Ordinary rank three True Dragons and True Gods weren’t a match for him.","None of the Zhao Immortal Clansmen could stop Chu Feng's spirit power. Their attacks unraveled before they could even touch Chu Feng, and miserable cries ensued.","All the Zhao Immortal Clansmen collapsed.","“That fellow... Am I seeing things?”","The crowd couldn’t believe their eyes. Even Zhao Cangjing found the situation inconceivable.","It was truly bizarre how Chu Feng’s spirit power was only at the level of a rank three True Dragon, yet it harnessed fighting prowess on par with a rank seven True Dragon. It was rare for world spiritists to even boast heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting one rank.","But Chu Feng could rival opponents four cultivation ranks stronger than him!","This was unheard of!","“Who’s that fellow? Is he truly a junior?”","The crowd was in shock. This news was even greater than the truth behind this peak. This would surely cause a huge stir once the others learned about it.","Chu Feng swooped up all the resources before leaving the mini formation realm. These resources were much better than what the earlier thirty had.","Shoosh!","As soon as Chu Feng stepped out, Zhao Cangjing tossed a talisman paper at Chu Feng.","The talisman paper blew up as soon as it came close to Chu Feng, and a powerful shockwave swiftly devoured him."]},{"number":6322,"title":"Chapter 6322: Chapter 6320: Yet To Go All Out","paragraphs":["Chapter 6320: Yet To Go All Out","That talisman paper was actually a tool to determine if Chu Feng was a junior, but the result left Zhao Cangjing disappointed.","“What’s wrong? Do you still doubt my age?” Chu Feng scoffed.","“What’s your name?”","This was the first time Zhao Cangjing had asked for a challenger’s name. The name of such a strong junior was worth remembering.","“I’ll let you know my name if you defeat me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Defeat you? Do you finally have the courage to challenge me?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“I’m thinking of challenging you, but well... I don’t know if you’re qualified,” Chu Feng remarked.","“I’m not qualified?”","Rage seethed in Zhao Cangjing’s eyes. Chu Feng was insulting him.","“Why should I challenge you if you can’t offer me anything of equivalent value?” Chu Feng asked as he took out all the resources he had obtained from the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","Now that he had more resources, Zhao Cangjing ought to offer something of equivalent value to match what he was putting on the line.","“Hah, I see!” Zhao Cangjing sneered.","He took out a hundred silver stone fragments with a flick of his wrist. These stone fragments were of higher quality even though they were still silver.","“Young master!”","Many Zhao Immortal Clansmen exclaimed in shock.","They knew that Zhao Cangjing had only allocated ten silver stone fragments for this challenge, but he was taking out a hundred of them to challenge Chu Feng. What if this was part of Chu Feng’s ploy, and he was stronger than he had shown thus far?","But they were faced with Zhao Cangjing’s cold glare before they could say a word. His eyes told them that he wouldn’t be as useless as them.","Chu Feng fiddled with his conjured golden stone fragments and said, “If that’s all you are offering, you can only take back what your clansmen lost if you defeat me. You won’t be able to take what I have.”","“Are you fleecing me now?” Zhao Cangjing’s eyes turned cold.","“I’m merely asking you to put something of equivalent value on the line. Why do you say that I’m fleecing you? Besides, it shouldn’t matter if you’re confident of defeating me, right? You’re much older than me. You can’t be intimidated by me, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Trying to provoke me? Fine, I shall let myself fall for your trick.”","Zhao Cangjing grandly waved his arms, and four hundred golden stones appeared in the sky above him. “I’ll use these resources to challenge you to a battle. If you defeat me, I’ll let you go, and you can take all these resources away with you. However, if you lose to me, not only will you have to hand all your resources back to me, but you and your stuttering friend will have to do my bidding before you are allowed to leave.”","Without waiting for Chu Feng’s answer, Zhao Cangjing entered the mini formation realm and placed all the resources at the entrance. He flitted to the center of the formation realm before turning to look at Chu Feng once more. “Do you dare?”","“I’ll play with you,” Chu Feng replied.","He entered the formation realm and placed all the resources at the entrance too.","“Let me know whenever you are done preparing, lest you later claim that I have taken advantage of you,” Zhao Cangjing said.","“Oh? You’re allowing me to make preparations?” Chu Feng asked.","“Go ahead.”","“Sure. I’ll make some preparations then.”","Chu Feng sat down and began forming a series of hand seals.","“Young master, you mustn’t give him time to prepare! He is a world spiritist. Who knows what kind of formation he’ll come up with if you give him time?”","Many Zhao Immortal Clansmen warned Zhao Cangjing. In truth, there was no need for their reminders, as Zhao Cangjing had already realized that he had made a misstep just from Chu Feng’s attitude.","However, his pride wouldn’t allow him to take back his words, so he said, “Let him construct whatever he wants. I’d like to see what kind of formation he can come up with.”","He used a provocative tone, hoping that Chu Feng would know some shame and stand up to confront him directly.","But he regretted those words right away.","Chu Feng remained focused on the formation, not reacting to the provocation at all.","Even though there wasn’t the slightest pulsation of spirit power, Zhao Cangjing began to feel nervous. He knew that powerful world spiritists were capable of constructing formations in their bodies.","“Hey, I might have given you time to prepare, but you shouldn’t be so shameless. Don’t you think it’s wrong to keep everyone waiting for you?” Zhao Cangjing continued his provocations.","“You are the one who told me to prepare, but now you’re hindering me from my preparations. Fine, I’ll make do with this much.” Chu Feng stood up and faced Zhao Cangjing. “Are you done with your preparations?”","“I’m waiting for you to make your move.”","Zhao Cangjing flicked his wrist, and a God Armament spear appeared in his grasp. He manifested and imbued three layers of auras into his body, raising his cultivation to rank seven True God level.","“He’s strong! That explains why he dared to accept the challenge even after seeing how strong that fellow is!”","The spectators were shocked by Zhao Cangjing’s strength.","The other battles were fought in a formation realm within the stone plate, and this formation realm didn’t allow spectators to watch. Thus, most spectators had no idea how strong the Zhao Immortal Clansmen were before Chu Feng’s appearance.","“Take a good look. I’m going to make my move.”","Shoosh!","Chu Feng raised his finger and released a burst of spirit power light at Zhao Cangjing.","As soon as Chu Feng made a move, Zhao Cangjing brandished his spear and unleashed a golden light beam at Chu Feng’s spirit power light.","Boom!","Surprisingly, Chu Feng’s tiny spirit power light bundle didn’t dissipate in the face of Zhao Cangjing’s golden light beam. On the contrary, it suddenly enlarged.","Terrifying pressure could be felt from the spirit power light.","But Zhao Cangjing didn’t panic. He leaped into the air and morphed into a golden dragon of over tens of thousands of meters long.","“Rank three God Taboo, Immortal Dragon Spearmanship!”","The golden dragon rushed toward Chu Feng with unstoppable might.","But as soon as the golden dragon came into contact with the spirit power light, Zhao Cangjing panicked. It was like a loach bumping into a metal pot; he immediately had an ominous feeling.","However, it was too late.","The previously hardened spirit power light suddenly became fluid like water. It opened up and engulfed Zhao Cangjing. He struggled with all his might, but he couldn’t break free.","The spirit power light rapidly sapped Zhao Cangjing’s martial power. It only took moments before the golden dragon dissipated.","By the time the formation was released, Zhao Cangjing had already collapsed on the floor. Even getting up was arduous for him.","The crowd was stunned, especially those from the Zhao Immortal Clan. They did consider the possibility of Zhao Cangjing falling in defeat, but they didn’t expect such a one-sided fight. It was a fight between peers, but the powerful Zhao Cangjing couldn’t fight back at all!","“I have finished constructing that formation from the moment I stepped in here,” Chu Feng said as he stowed away the resources and prepared to leave.","“Hold it right there!” Zhao Cangjing shouted.","Chu Feng turned around.","Zhao Cangjing was standing on his two feet even though he shouldn’t have had the strength for that. A golden aura reminiscent of a raging inferno flowed from his body, granting him far greater power than the bloodline power he had released earlier.","“You think you have won, but I haven’t gone all out yet.” Zhao Cangjing glared at Chu Feng.","“That’s enough, Zhao Cangjing,” a voice echoed from the outside.","It was from the ordinary-looking woman who had criticized the Zhao Immortal Clan for their unfair practices. A layer of spirit power washed over her, causing her appearance and clothes to change. Her facial features became more delicate, and her disposition became colder.","More importantly, her clothes turned into a golden robe identical to the ones worn by the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","Shocked, all the Zhao Immortal Clansmen hurriedly bowed deeply and greeted her, “Paying respect to the young miss!”","The woman must have been a notable figure in the Zhao Immortal Clan. Even Zhao Cangjing was intimidated by her.","“Zhao Cangjing, don’t embarrass our Zhao Immortal Clan,” that woman said.","Zhao Cangjing was reluctant to let things slip, but he still retracted the power. He immediately crumbled weakly to the ground, but he still mustered his strength to raise his head and glare at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng was hardly intimidated by his glare. On the contrary, he chuckled and said, “You said you didn’t go all out earlier. Well, how do you know that I have gone all out then?”","Zhao Cangjing was stunned. His eyes widened as his rage eroded to fear. Perhaps he had suddenly regained his rationality, or he simply wasn’t dumb in the first place, but he understood what Chu Feng was getting at.","It dawned on him that if Chu Feng could overwhelm him with a single formation, the chances were that he would have stronger aces up his sleeve.","On top of that, Chu Feng had remained composed throughout as if everything was under his control. That further convinced him of his conjecture. It made him think that even if he had gone all out, he still wouldn’t have been a match for the world spiritist before him."]},{"number":6323,"title":"Chapter 6323: Chapter 6321: Zhao Tingxue","paragraphs":["Chapter 6321: Zhao Tingxue","Having said his piece, Chu Feng took his leave.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen immediately encircled Chu Feng, blocking his path. They didn’t intend to let him leave just like that.","But a glance from the woman sent them stepping back right away.","If not for this woman, the Zhao Immortal Clansmen would have surely attacked Chu Feng to retrieve their resources. So, Chu Feng clasped his fist toward the woman and said, “Thanks.”","“You need not thank me. That’s what you deserve. Allow me to introduce myself. I am Zhao Tingxue, the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief’s daughter,” the woman said.","The crowd finally understood why the Zhao Immortal Clansmen were so respectful to her. It turned out that she was the clan chief’s daughter.","Zhao Tingxue was satisfied with the crowd’s reaction. This was the effect she wanted when she revealed her identity. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “How should I address you?”","“Wu Ming (Nameless).”","“You don’t have a name?” Zhao Tingxue was perplexed.","“My name is Wu Ming,” Chu Feng replied.","He didn’t want to reveal his identity yet. While the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Zhao Daobin owed him a favor, he thought it was unwise to reveal his identity until he gathered more information about the Zhao Immortal Clan.","Besides, there was no guarantee that Zhao Daobin was trustworthy.","Zhao Tingxue might have done him a favor, but similarly, it was still too early to trust her.","“I see. Young master Wu Ming, may I know the names of your companions?” Zhao Tingxue turned her gaze to Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Wu Sheng (Soundless),” Little Fishy replied.","“Wu Qu (Disinterested),” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“Wu De (Virtueless),” Wang Qiang replied.","Both Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu turned to Wang Qiang. They were not surprised by the lack of his stutter but his name. Chu Feng, on the other hand, smiled as he was already used to this side of Wang Qiang.","“Ah, you must be from the clan. That explains it. Would you and your companions be interested in coming over for a chat?” Zhao Tingxue said.","She waved her arm, and a palace rose from the ground. It was a treasure.","“My apologies, Miss Zhao. We have other business to attend to,” Chu Feng rejected the offer after some thought.","“Young master Wu Ming, it’s just a short chat. It won’t too long. I’m willing to offer you for it. Besides, I’m at the same cultivation level as Zhao Cangjing. We won’t be able to stop you from leaving,” Zhao Tingxue said.","She took out a hundred silver stone fragments and displayed her rank four True God level cultivation.","Chu Feng had won 500 silver stone fragments from Zhao Cangjing, but that was from a duel, and it wouldn’t have been that much if he hadn’t provoked the other party beforehand.","Zhao Tingxue’s offer was very generous.","“What do you think?” Chu Feng asked Little Fishy and the others.","“I’ll follow you,” Little Fishy replied.","“Brother Wuming, you can choose on our behalf,” Xianhai Shaoyu smiled.","“This miss has shown such sincerity. It w-w-would be impolite of us to continue turning her down.” Wang Qiang walked up to Zhao Tingxue and took the hundred silver stone fragments.","He already knew Chu Feng’s decision.","“This way, please.” Zhao Tingxue escorted Chu Feng and the others into the palace, but she stopped at the entrance and turned to the gloomy Zhao Cangjing. “Zhao Cangjing, you come in too.”","“Me?”","Zhao Cangjing had healed up a fair bit, but he was still in a very weakened state. His expression made it clear that he was reluctant to enter.","“Come in,” Zhao Tingxue repeated once more.","Seeing her commanding eyes, he weakly made his way toward the palace.","By the time Zhao Cangjing followed Zhao Tingxue into the palace, Chu Feng and the others had already taken their seats.","Wang Qiang glanced at Zhao Cangjing and said, “Miss Zhao, y-y-you’re so beautiful and kind. How is it that the other Zhao Immortal Clansmen are so a-a-arrogant and unreasonable?”","That pricked Zhao Cangjing’s nerve, but before he could say anything, Zhao Tingxue raised her hand to stop him. Zhao Cangjing had no choice but to swallow his words back in.","“Zhao Cangjing, aren’t you going to apologize to these gentlemen?” Zhao Tingxue asked.","Zhao Cangjing was stunned. “Tingxue, why should I...”","Zhao Tingxue interjected before he finished his words, “You should have duly informed others that you aren’t a junior when you set up this challenge. Shouldn’t you apologize when you have done wrong?”","Zhao Cangjing still refused to lower his head. “Why should I be blamed for their greed?”","Zhao Tingxue didn’t argue with Zhao Cangjing. Instead, she turned to Chu Feng and the others and bowed in apology. “Allow me to apologize to you on behalf of my clansmen. Zhao Cangjing is the grandson of our Zhao Immortal Clan’s Enforcement Elder Zhao Daobin. His parents passed away when he was still a child, so Elder Zhao Daobin dotes on him a lot, resulting in his hot-headed temperament. However, he isn’t a bad person at heart.”","Zhao Cangjing’s face darkened. “Tingxue, why are you telling these to outsiders?”","“I’m merely introducing you. Have I said anything inappropriate?” Zhao Tingxue asked.","Zhao Cangjing was tempted to argue, but he eventually swallowed his words. He didn’t know that Zhao Tingxue’s introduction surprised Chu Feng.","“Zhao Cangjing is Zhao Daobin’s grandson? Wow, the world of cultivation sure is a small place. I wonder if Zhao Daobin will side with his grandson or benefactor if he learns about this matter,” Eggy said.","“There’s nothing wrong with his challenge. The only issue here is the lack of a warning that some clansmen there aren’t juniors. It isn’t that big of a deal,” Chu Feng replied.","Zhao Tingxue dragged Zhao Cangjing into a seat before settling down. She turned to Chu Feng and said, “Young master Wu Ming, may I know where you obtained your resource from?”","Chu Feng had expected as much. The resources he had brought out were fake, but they were an imitation of what Long Zhuoyan had given him. He took out the resources and passed them over to Zhao Tingxue.","Both Zhao Tingxue and Zhao Cangjing were astonished. They knew these resources were much better than what they had, so they quickly grabbed some to examine them.","Weng!","As soon as they touched the resources, the resources suddenly dissipated as spirit power.","“Huh?” Zhao Cangjing was confused.","Zhao Tingxue burst into laughter. “Incredible, young master Wu Ming. Your forged resources had me fooled.”","“Forged?” Zhao Cangjing was stunned before realization struck him. He shot to his feet with veins popping at his temples. He glared at Chu Feng and roared, “You bastard! I’ll slaughter you!”"]},{"number":6324,"title":"Chapter 6324: Chapter 6322: Her Motive","paragraphs":["Chapter 6322: Her Motive","Boom!","A surge of rank seven True God level martial power trapped Zhao Cangjing before he could make a move. It was Zhao Tingxue.","She had invoked the Zhao Immortal Clan’s bloodline power and was wrapped in three layers of divine, golden aura, raising her cultivation to rank seven True God level.","“Tingxue, he dares to deceive us!” Zhao Cangjing spat through gritted teeth.","“He deceived you, not us. You only have yourself to blame for being foolish enough to be tricked. Now, sit quietly and stop embarrassing yourself.” Zhao Tingxue pressed her palm down, and Zhao Cangjing sat back down.","Seeing that Zhao Tingxue refused to side with him, Zhao Cangjing could only give up on making a move and huff angrily.","Zhao Tingxue turned to Chu Feng and asked, “You are present-era cultivators, right?”","“That’s right,” Chu Feng replied.","Little Fishy quickly added, “Aren’t you born in this era too? I don’t understand why you insist on claiming that you’re from the Ancient Era. That era has already long passed us by.”","Zhao Tingxue chuckled. “We can’t forget our roots, right?”","“But it’s not as if the present-era cultivators popped out from a stone,” Little Fishy pointed out.","Zhao Tingxue merely smiled in response, not elaborating further on her viewpoint.","Chu Feng knew that both present-era cultivators and Ancient Era cultivators descended from the Ancient Era; the present-era cultivators did not just suddenly appear in this era.","It was just that all living beings fell asleep in between the two eras, resulting in a gap in history. That was the reason behind the distinction between the Ancient Era and the present era.","Those whose clans or sects had prospered in the Ancient Era preferred to identify themselves as Ancient Era cultivators.","On the other hand, the ancestors of present-era cultivators were weak in the Ancient Era, living as either ordinary mortals of weak servants. Powers like the Zhao Immortal Clan wouldn’t even consider taking them in as servants; they were no different from ants.","For some reason, powerful clans like the Zhao Immortal Clan were restrained by some force in the present era, and it was only in recent days that the seal began lifting.","Meanwhile, the weaker cultivators in the Ancient Era weren’t trapped when they regained consciousness. This gave them a chance to obtain all kinds of heritages and rise through the ranks.","Despite the rise of present-era cultivators, powers like the Zhao Immortal Clan still looked down on the present-era cultivators, thinking that they were a bunch of ragtags who had gotten lucky. Their disdain for present-era cultivators went so deep that they felt hostile toward them.","To draw a distinction between themselves and those whom they viewed as ants, they identified themselves as Ancient Era cultivators despite being born in the present era,","“Don’t worry, I harbor no hostility toward you. As present-era cultivators, you must be lacking in understanding about the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. To be honest, I am interested in getting on close terms with you. Our Zhao Immortal Clan knows a fair bit about the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, so I can provide some information to you,” Zhao Tingxue said.","Wang Qiang quickly replied, “Miss Z-Z-Zhao, you’re truly beautiful and kind! Just saying, you can’t take back your resources anymore now that I-I-I have accepted them.”","“Don’t worry, that’s my greeting gift. I won’t ask you to return it.” Zhao Tingxue smiled. “More mountain peaks will appear when the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain opens. Each peak has a formation, and these resources will be required to awaken the formation.","“These resources are similar to keys; they have to properly matched. Some peaks require more resources, whereas some require fewer. Once you begin awakening a formation, you can’t stop halfway through. You’ll be eliminated if you don’t have sufficient resources for the awakening.","“But there is a way to figure out how much resources is required for a peak.”","Zhao Tingxue waved her arms, and a massive portrait unfurled before their eyes.","There were ten mountain peaks on the portrait. They didn’t look any different at first glance, but Zhao Tingxue pointed out the differences among them—these ten peaks signaled the difference in resources needed.","“Countless mountain peaks will appear once the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain opens, but they can be broadly classified under these ten. Please remember these mountain peaks and select from them when the time comes,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“The rewards are higher for peaks that require more resources, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Indeed, but peaks that require more resources are more demanding on one’s intelligence. Based on our records, our predecessors have once awakened the two peaks that require the most resources, but they weren’t able to comprehend anything from them.","“Some say that those two peaks are a trap, but there are also those who conjecture that the ones who awakened those peaks simply failed to reach the minimum intelligence level required to claim the reward. In any case, I don’t recommend you to awaken those two peaks. Of course, it’s just my recommendation; you are free to give it a try too. Perhaps, your intelligence level might be sufficient,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Do each person only have a single try?” Chu Feng asked.","“You can only awaken one mountain, and you’d be eliminated right away if you fail,” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“If I can comprehend the formation, will I be able to receive the rewards right away?” Chu Feng asked.","“Not exactly. You’ll only receive the formation’s energy if you comprehend the formation, but that’s not enough. There must be enough people who successfully obtain the formation energies for the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s Fortuitous Sun to rise.","“The Fortuitous Sun will emanate Fortuitous Light once it rises to the top. It will allow the formation energy to fuse with one’s body, metamorphosizing one’s bloodline,” Zhao Tingxue explained.","“There must be quite a few people who successfully metamorphosized, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Indeed. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain has opened many times before, but the energy inside is limited. There should be very little energy left in it. But since it still exists, we should still be able to benefit from it,” Zhao Tingxue said.","She continued to trade some pleasantries with Chu Feng and the others before allowing them to leave without probing too deep into their backgrounds.","After Chu Feng left, she stopped the challenge and closed the Steel Peak before returning to their palace with Zhao Cangjing.","“Tingxue, I don’t understand. They obviously came to mess with us. Why did you let them take our resources and even tell them the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s secret?” Zhao Cangjing looked indignant.","Even though he was the one managing the Steel Peak, its true mastermind was none other than Zhao Tingxue.","Zhao Tingxue’s gentle smile had vanished, replaced with a scheming sneer. She raised her head and looked out the window, her eyes confident as if everything was in her grasp.","“The one who defeated you is very strong. The stutterer whom you defeated is decent as well. It’d be a waste if we don’t properly exploit them for their value,” Zhao Tingxue replied."]},{"number":6325,"title":"Chapter 6325: Chapter 6323: Entering the Mountain, Exposed?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6323: Entering the Mountain, Exposed?","“Do you think I told you to set up this challenge to make fun of juniors? No, I wanted to see what the people here are capable of, and I am satisfied with the outcome,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Tingxue, has Zhuyin... really grasped the Immortal Feather Cloak?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“She can already raise her cultivation by a rank, but it’s still unstable. Whether it’ll work out or not depends on this. If Zhuyin can enhance her bloodline and fully grasp the Immortal Feather Cloak, she would have a chance to compete for God’s Era’s power. We must not miss God’s Era’s benefits,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Tingxue, I heard the Ye Immortal Clan has emerged too. Is that true?” Zhao Cangjing asked with a cautious tone.","“Yes, the Ye Immortal Clan has broken free of their seal too and is on the move. They are likely after God’s Era’s power too. This operation is very important, which is why my father activated the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain despite the cost,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Don’t worry, I’ll do my best to ensure the successful opening of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain,” Zhao Cangjing said.","“The thinning of natural energies resulted in our strength being nowhere close to our predecessors in the Ancient Era, but there are many talents in the juniors of this generation. We should be able to activate the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain without a hitch. But what’s more important is how many of them will be of use to us. I hope those few people won’t let us down,” Zhao Tingxue said with a sigh.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and the others had already returned to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s warship and shared what happened with Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather.","“Looks like the Zhao Immortal Clan is not to be underestimated. The God Clan isn’t the only troublesome Ancient Era’s race. Our foundation is still lacking,” Little Fishy’s grandfather sighed.","Their encounter with the God Clan had shaken him up.","“Elder, it’s only a matter of time before we surpass them,” Chu Feng said.","“I’m already at a bottleneck, but I have confidence in you all,” Little Fishy’s grandfather replied with a smile.","“Big brother, do you think Zhao Tingxue’s words are credible?” Little Fishy asked.","“My observations align with what she shared,” Chu Feng replied.","“I guess not all Zhao Immortal Clansmen are bad. At least Zhao Tingxue is a decent person,” Little Fishy said.","“It’s still too early to judge her nature. All this proves is that the information she has provided us has some credibility, but we shouldn’t lower our guard around her just yet.”","Chu Feng turned to Wang Qiang and patted his shoulder. He stared at Wang Qiang but didn’t utter a word.","“W-w-what’s wrong?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Did Zhao Cangjing defeat you with that Immortal Dragon Spearmanship?”","“Y-y-yes, that move was very powerful. What formation d-d-did you use to neutralize it? It’s incredible,” Wang Qiang asked.","“It’s one of Heaven Tome’s slaughter formations, named Heavenly Pulse Malaise Formation. It specializes in dealing with individuals who raise their fighting prowess using their bloodlines, but it has to be constructed in advance, and the world spiritist has to be stronger than the individual, or else it will be hard for the formation to work its effect,” Chu Feng explained.","“Incredible. Your world spiritist techniques are getting u-u-unfathomable.” Wang Qiang shot a thumbs up at Chu Feng.","“My formation would be useless against you.” Chu Feng pointed out.","“Brother, you’re f-f-flattering me. I’m not that formidable.”","Chu Feng continued in voice transmission, “Putting all things aside, the secret skill you obtained at the Huangfu Heavenly Clan is superior to his rank three God Taboo Immortal Dragon Spearmanship. You intentionally lost to him, didn’t you? What are you hoping to obtain by losing to him? Or rather, what’s your goal?”","“What goal could I have? I-I-I am just careless,” Wang Qiang replied cheerily.","Chu Feng didn’t continue probing since Wang Qiang was reluctant to speak. Instead, he said, “Brother, you can tell me if you need help. I might be able to help you.”","“I’m fine,” Wang Qiang replied with a smile.","“The barrier is dissipating. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is opening.”","A huge commotion could be heard outside. Chu Feng and the others looked over and saw the barrier enveloping the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain dissipating.","Many people rushed toward the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, and they would abruptly vanish upon reaching a certain radius of the mountain. However, Chu Feng and the others had already anticipated such a situation.","The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain that they saw before them was superficial; it contained another realm within it. Most likely, as Zhao Tingxue had mentioned, there would be countless peaks inside the spatial realm.","“Let’s split the resources,” Chu Feng said as he took out all his resources.","He shared them with Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather too, but he didn’t bother taking a portion himself. In his view, these resources, even when put together, came nowhere close to being as valuable as the golden stone he had received from Long Zhuoyan.","Just the golden stone was enough for him.","“This wouldn’t do, young friend Chu Feng. You won these!” Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather turned down the resources.","“Elders, we’re still counting on you to protect us. Why don’t you think of it as a protection fee?” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Y-y-yes, protection fee.” Wang Qiang took out the silver stone fragments he had taken from Zhao Tingxue and split them with the crowd.","“It’s fine. We aren’t participating in the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, so we don’t have any use for the resources. We’re here to protect you. It’s all good as long as you get something good out of this trial,” Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather said adamantly.","So, Chu Feng split the resources among Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Wang Qiang.","Wnag Qiang and the others understood Chu Feng’s personality and didn’t insist on him taking a portion too.","Once the resources were distributed, Chu Feng and the others made their way toward the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. They entered the barrier and found themselves transported into a realm made up of countless peaks.","However, the barrier also rendered all their disguise ineffective, so they reverted to their original appearances."]},{"number":6326,"title":"Chapter 6326: Chapter 6324: Eighth Zhao","paragraphs":["Chapter 6324: Eighth Zhao","But Chu Feng and the others weren’t discovered, thanks to the intervention of Little Fishy’s Heavenly God level parents and grandfather. To be doubly safe, Little Fishy’s parents activated their bloodline and raised their cultivation from rank one to rank three Heavenly God level.","It would be tough for normal people to notice them.","“Why are m-m-masks not working? Do we have to r-r-reveal our true identities in this place?” Wang Qiang’s treasure mask turned transparent the moment he placed it on his face.","“It’s fine. There shouldn’t be a problem as long as we don’t split up,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s t-t-true. We have three H-H-Heavenly Gods protecting us,” Wang Qiang pointed out gleefully.","But Chu Feng’s true ace was the Divine Deer, who had regained her energy. To be safe, he asked, “Elder Divine Deer, will you be able to take us out of here if something happens?”","“Yes, I can do it. There’s a way if you don’t want to reveal yourself—try using the warship,” the Divine Deer replied.","“All right.”","Chu Feng took out a warship with a wave of his hand. Much to his delight, the warship didn’t turn transparent even as he and the others entered it.","“Great! We don’t have to worry about revealing ourselves anymore,” Little Fishy exclaimed.","While having three Heavenly Gods on their side was reassuring, they could never be too prepared when dealing with the enigmatic Ancient Era’s races. It was better to err on the side of caution.","But the Divine Deer told Chu Feng, “You can only channel the warship to move around. You mustn’t use martial power or spirit power on the warship, or the warship will turn transparent.”","Chu Feng relayed those words to Little Fishy and the others.","Wang Qiang tried exerting his martial power, and the warship immediately turned transparent.","“What t-t-the?” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“If a battle breaks out, it wouldn’t matter whether we reveal ourselves or not. It’s all good if we can remain in the warship while searching for a peak,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“T-t-that’s true.” Wang Qiang nodded.","So, Chu Feng and the others channeled the warship to venture deeper into the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","“Elder, you seem to know much about the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. What else do you know about this place? Share it with me,” Chu Feng asked the Divine Deer.","The Divine Deer had become more amicable since he acquired what the other party needed at the peak of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Immemorial Bloodline Tower. She was more willing to answer his questions now and would even take the initiative to chat with him at times.","In fact, she was the one who told him about Long Zhuoyan’s identity.","“Zhao Tingxue’s information is on point except for the hardest two peaks. You can grasp something from the hardest two peaks, just that few people can pull it off. You can give it a try. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain doesn’t have much energy left anyway. You should aim for the best since you’re here; I doubt that the other peaks will be of much use to you anyway,” the Divine Deer said.","“All right,” Chu Feng replied. He turned to Wang Qiang, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Little Fishy, and asked, “Have you decided on which peak to challenge?”","“Brother, d-d-do we have enough resources to activate the hardest peak?” Wang Qiang asked.","“We do,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’ll challenge the h-h-hardest one!” Wang Qiang said.","“Big brother, what are your thoughts?” Little Fishy asked.","“I’m also thinking of challenging the hardest peak,” Chu Feng replied.","“Let’s go with that,” Little Fishy replied.","“Hold on! Aren’t you forgetting me? I haven’t decided yet!” Xianhai Shaoyu exclaimed.","“Which one do you want?” Little Fishy asked.","“The hardest one,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“You need help.” Little Fishy rolled her eyes.","So, Chu Feng and the others began looking for four hardest peaks situated near one another. There were plenty of hardest peaks around, but it was hard to find four in the same area.","They were so invested in their search that they didn’t notice a huge army comprising over a thousand warships entering the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. Even the smallest warship could house a million people, and all bore the Zhao Immortal Clan’s flags.","At the front of the formation was an imposing warship. Despite its majestic scale, it was only carrying several people in its massive palace.","In the heart of the warship, there was a round table and several wooden stools. A couple of people sat around casually as they ate together. Surprisingly, they were all faces that Chu Feng would have recognized.","Not only were Zhao Tingxue and Zhao Cangjing there, but there were also Zhao Cangjing’s grandfather, Zhao Daobin, and the father-daughter duo Chu Feng had met in God’s Era, Eighth Zhao and Zhao Zhuyin.","“Tingxue, is there no news about Chu Feng?” Eighth Zhao ate a slice of meat as he asked.","“Lord Father, we haven’t found Chu Feng yet, but our people are searching for him. Since disguise means don’t work in the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, we’ll surely find him if he’s here,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“It’ll be a huge pity if Chu Feng isn’t here.” Eighth Zhao felt so regretful about this that even the meat in his mouth didn’t seem as fragrant anymore.","“You have a high opinion of Chu Feng, father.” Zhao Zhuyin smiled.","“What do you mean I have a high opinion of him? Who’s the one who keeps singing praises of him to me? Those who don’t know better might think that you’re interested in him,” Eighth Zhao said heartily.","“What nonsense are you spouting!” Zhao Zhuyin rolled her eyes.","Laughter broke out in the palace.","The man whom Chu Feng recognized as Eighth Zhao was none other than the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. Despite his hearty personality, no one other than Zhao Zhuyin dared to speak to him casually in view of his high position.","Not even Zhao Tingxue, who was his daughter too, dared to do so.","“Lord Father, it should be fine even if Chu Feng doesn’t come. I discovered a formidable junior,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“A formidable junior? How formidable is he?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“A rank three True Dragon World Spiritist,” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“Rank three True Dragon World Spiritist?! Are you sure he’s a junior?” Eighth Zhao’s eyes widened in shock. Even his chopsticks came to a halt.","Zhao Daobin and Zhao Zhuyin were astounded too.","“He had incredible fighting prowess too. He easily defeated Zhao Cangjing even after the latter raised his cultivation to rank seven True God level,” Zhao Tingxue added.","“What?! A world spiritist with a heaven-defying battle power of four cultivation ranks?” Eighth Zhao was stunned.","Zhao Tingxue and Zhao Daobin were shocked.","“Big sister, are you sure he’s a junior?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","“There’s no doubt about it. Zhao Cangjing can confirm that,” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“Yeah, I had my doubts, so I used my means to verify it. He is indeed a junior,” Zhao Cangjing replied awkwardly.","“Doesn’t that make him more formidable than Chu Feng? Is he a present-era junior or an Ancient Era junior? What’s his name?” Eighth Zhao asked."]},{"number":6327,"title":"Chapter 6327: Chapter 6325: A Friend In Need","paragraphs":["Chapter 6325: A Friend In Need","“He should be a present-era junior. He said his name is Wu Ming (Nameless), but it should be a fake name,” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“Wu Ming? That’s quite the name, no matter whether it’s fake or not,” Eighth Zhao remarked.","“He has a cultivator friend. The friend is weaker than him, but he’s still a formidable individual. Zhao Cangjing barely scraped a victory against him,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Oh? What’s his name?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“It’s a stutterer named Wu De (Virtueless),” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“Wu De? Doesn’t sound like the name of an upright person. Birds of the same feather flock together—since they are friends, they should be the same type of people. They have character, but their personality requires verification,” Eighth Zhao commented with a smile.","Zhao Zhuyin and the others chuckled. They could tell that Eighth Zhao was joking.","It was Zhao Tingxue and the others’ problem that they were so restrained in front of Eighth Zhao. Zhao Zhuyin had never been restrained before Eighth Zhao; if anything, she spoke her mind and did whatever she wanted.","An elder’s voice suddenly echoed outside, “Lord Clan Chief, we have found them.”","“Let’s go.” Eighth Zhao put down his chopsticks and led the group out.","A vast expanse of mountain peaks appeared before their eyes.","Eighth Zhao reached into his Cosmos Sack and took out a scroll. He unfurled the scroll. Depicted on it were nineteen mountain peaks, with one in the center and the remaining eighteen surrounding it as if guarding it.","Despite the countless mountain peaks around him, he could still spot scenery identical to that in the scroll. That was what they were looking for.","“Construct the formation!” Eighth Zhao ordered.","The Zhao Immortal Clan’s elders, who were on standby, made a move. They began working on the eighteen surrounding peaks, but they avoided the center peak.","Eighth Zhao and the others, however, had their eyes set on the center peak. That peak was their goal.","“Father, is that the mountain you have picked out for me?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","“Indeed. Do you like it, Zhuyin?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Isn’t that the second hardest peak? I want to challenge the hardest one,” Zhao Zhuyin said.","“My good daughter, our clan records state that only three people have ever cleared the hardest peak in the Ancient Era.”","“I know. It’s the Three Zenith Emperors who pushed the Ancient Era to its peak. Father, do you think that I’m not on par with the Three Zenith Emperors?”","“No, I believe that my daughter can surpass the Three Zenith Emperors.”","But Zhao Zhuyin laughed at those words. “You’re the only one who thinks so. I don’t think I have it in me. I have that much self-awareness. I’m not even confident of clearing this second-hardest peak. Father, are you sure we should challenge this one?”","“My good daughter, the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain doesn’t have much energy left. You won’t be able to metamorphose your bloodline if you can’t clear the second-hardest peak.","“Our ancestors bought the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain from the World Spiritist Emperor at an exorbitant price so that when an unprecedented prodigy appears in our clan, we can stake our all on them. I have decided to stake the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain on you. If you fail, I won’t be able to face our Zhao Clan’s ancestors in the netherworld. I’ll be eternally pinned to a pillar of humiliation and be spat at by our descendants till the end of time.”","Zhao Zhuyin quickly raised her hand to interject, “Fine, I’ll activate this one. I’ll do my best, but I can’t guarantee success.”","“That’s good enough.” Eighth Zhao nodded.","But he turned around to look at Zhao Daobin right after, and the latter caught his drift and took his leave.","The other warships departed as well, leaving just the warship that Eighth Zhao and the others were riding on. But not a single person on the warship was worried.","Putting aside the fact that those constructing formations on the surrounding eighteen peaks were the Zhao Immortal Clan’s top-notch experts, just Eighth Zhao alone was enough to let them rest at ease.","“Will it take long?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","“It’ll take some time. There’s no rush. We have plenty of time anyway,” Eighth Zhao said.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and the others were still searching for four hardest mountain peaks. Instead of traveling straight, they moved in a zig-zag to not miss any corners.","In the meantime, the crowd had already realized that there were formations on the mountain peaks, and the key to obtaining the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s energy was to activate the formations.","Naturally, many people tried it, but most ended in failure because they didn’t know that activating the formations required resources. Those who failed were transported out of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","Several people were gathered in front of where Chu Feng and the others were traveling, and there appeared to be a conflict.","Coincidentally, one of the people involved in the conflict was Chu Feng’s friend—the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s most talented prodigy, Qin Xuan.","But Qin Xuan showed none of his usual flair. He was lying on the ground in pain, with blood seeping from the corner of his lips. He clenched his jaws in anger as he tried to get back to his feet, but the foot on his head kept him firmly down.","The master of the foot was a short, hunched old man dressed in a daoist robe. He was accompanied by several other people dressed in the same daoist robe.","Quite a few spectators were gathered in the area, suggesting that it had been some time since the outbreak of the conflict. All of them recognized Qin Xuan, and some of them recognized the old man as well.","The old man was the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster.","Some time ago, someone from the Bluehue Monastery got into a conflict with Qin Xuan, prompting the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster to confront Qin Xuan to back his people up. But when the sectmaster realized that he was dealing with the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s Qin Xuan, he was so frightened that he kneeled down and begged for forgiveness.","How could the Bluehue Monastery offend the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect when it was a mere ant before it?","With such a history behind them, the crowd wasn’t surprised to see the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster settling the scores with Qin Xuan now.","But times had changed.","The Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect had been massacred, so Qin Xuan no longer had his backing. On top of that, the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster had advanced to rank nine Half-God level many years back.","While Qin Xuan was only at rank eight Half-God level, he had the means to raise his cultivation. Yet, he was unable to rival the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster, no matter how they fought.","The answer was soon revealed.","The Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster had reached True God level. This explained why Qin Xuan couldn’t defeat the sectmaster even though he could raise his cultivation by three ranks.","“Qin Xuan, I heard the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Yuwen Yanri had long reached True God level, so why are you still stuck at Half-God level? Didn’t you enter God’s Era too? I don’t think you are deserving of your reputation as a prodigy. Without the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect, you are nothing at all!” the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster sneered.","The crowd coldly watched the scene. They found it cathartic to watch someone in a high position being dragged down from their high horses, not to mention that there was no reason for them to help Qin Xuan.","But Chu Feng and the others just so happened to witness this scene."]},{"number":6328,"title":"Chapter 6328: Chapter 6326: True Man","paragraphs":["Chapter 6326: True Man","Chu Feng knew that making a move would reveal his identity, but he didn’t hesitate to leap out of the warship and flit over.","“I dare you to kill me. If I survive this ordeal, I swear that I’ll destroy your monastery,” Qin Xuan spat through gritted teeth.","“Kill you? How can I let you off that easily? I shall make you my dog, but I don’t like to hear you bark. Let me start by severing your tongue.”","The Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster whipped out a sword and plunged it toward Qin Xuan’s mouth.","Pu!","Blood splattered. The crowd was stunned, including Qin Xuan and the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster.","“Move your foot away from my friend’s head, or I’ll make a move,” Chu Feng’s voice echoed.","He was standing right behind the Bluehue Monastery’s sectmaster.","“C-Chu Feng?!”","The crowd was stunned. It would be hard to find anyone in the world of cultivation who didn’t know Chu Feng.","The sectmaster was horrified. He wouldn’t dare offend someone who had the guts to mess with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","But before he could utter a word, Chu Feng harrumphed. “Looks like I need to make a move.”","Shoosh!","Chu Feng flicked his arm, and the sectmaster’s legs were severed.","At the same time, three figures flitted forth and took their positions behind Chu Feng—Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Xianhai Yu’er? Xianhai Shaoyu?”","“I thought the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had been destroyed? How are they still around?”","The crowd was shocked to see Xianhai Shaoyu and Xianhai Yu’er.","“Who says our Immortal Sea Fish Clan has been destroyed?”","Three figures silently appeared behind Chu Feng and the others. It was Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather.","“Paying respect to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief!”","The spectators hurriedly lowered their heads and greeted the trio. These three were famed powerhouses of the world of cultivation. In particular, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief was reputed to be a figure second only to Jie Tianran.","Chu Feng supported Qin Xuan to his feet and fed him a pill.","“Brother Chu, I owe you another one,” Qin Xuan said with a head hanging in shame.","“Don’t speak nonsense. What’s with these people? Is there a grudge between you and them?” Chu Feng asked.","“A few years back, I saw Bluehue Monastery’s disciples and elders bullying the weak, so I stepped in and killed them. Later, their sectmaster confronted me, only to kneel and apologize when he realized it was me. He even punished the disciples who reported me.","“I thought that the sectmaster was a good person because of that, but he attacked me right away when we met earlier. He said that he was the one who ordered the attack back then, and that I was foolish for trusting him. I am indeed... foolish,” Qin Xuan said bitterly.","“I see. All right.”","With a wave of his sleeves, Chu Feng beheaded everyone from the Bluehue Monastery. They didn’t even get an opportunity to beg for mercy.","This horrified the spectators.","To make things worse, Chu Feng turned his gaze toward the spectators and declared, “Remember this, Qin Xuan is my friend. I won’t stop anyone from messing with him; just be prepared to face the consequences if I learn about it.”","“We wouldn’t dare!”","Even the boldest spectator anxiously expressed their stance. The timid even knelt out of fright and lowered their heads, fearing that Chu Feng would behead them too in a fit of anger.","However, Chu Feng and the others vanished before they knew it. They had returned to their warship.","“Ey, I went overboard,” Chu Feng sighed.","“W-w-what’s wrong?” Wang Qiang and the others were confused.","“I wanted to avenge Brother Qin, but I don’t know if it’s a good thing to tie his name to mine,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, are you worried about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? I’m not scared of that. Were it not for your intervention, I would have died today. You are my friends. Since the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is your enemy, that makes them my enemy too,” Qin Xuan said.","He suddenly turned to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and said, “Lord Clan Chief, I heard the Immortal Sea Fish Clan faced a mishap. Was that... staged?”","“Mm.” The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief nodded.","“Brother Qin, the Totem Dragon Clan is not responsible for what happened to the Immortal Dome Heavenly Sect,” Chu Feng said.","“I know. I couldn’t find any traces of the Totem Dragon Clan behind the incident,” Qin Xuan said.","“Qin Xuan, it’s because I s-s-see you as a friend that I’m saying this even though you might not like it. The Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect has never treated you as o-o-one of them, and your sectmaster is trash through and through.","“Other powers devoted their resources to nurturing their juniors when there was a revelation that a junior would claim God’s Era’s power. The Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect should have bestowed upon you their best resources, but the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s sectmaster...” Wang Qiang said.","Qin Xuan suddenly interjected, “I know. I’m not a fool. I know better than anyone how the sectmaster treats me. But even if the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect doesn’t cherish me, it is still the place where I was born and raised. I might have died elsewhere if not for the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect.","“There are kind people in the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect who don’t deserve to die. I can’t let this matter rest. I won’t forgive the person behind the incident,” Qin Xuan declared.","“Qin Xuan, I have been through something similar, but I’m more fortunate since my clansmen are still safe and sound. I might not be able to help you with much, but these should be of use to you.” Xianhai Shaoyu handed some stone fragments to Qin Xuan.","“I have some too.” Little Fishy also handed hers over.","“H-h-here’s mine.” Wang Qiang took out some too.","“This won’t do. It’s not easy to obtain these resources.” Qin Xuan shook his head.","He was rejecting out of politeness, but it was clear that he did want the resources. His prodigy peers, with the support from their respective sects and clans, had advanced to True God level, but he was still stuck at Half-God level.","His desire to become strong was greater than ever.","“Take it if you think of us as your friends,” Chu Feng advised.","Xianhai Shaoyu and the others were prudent in the amount of resources they offered Qin Xuan—they made sure that they still had enough resources to activate the hardest peak. They were aiding Qin Xuan while ensuring that they wouldn’t be negatively impacted.","“You don’t need to b-b-be polite with us.”","“Just take it.”","Wang Qiang and the others stuffed the resources into Qin Xuan’s hands.","Qin Xuan fell silent.","The next moment, everyone stiffened up.","Qin Xuan had started sobbing. Tears flowed down his cheeks and fell on the floor.","Chu Feng and the others couldn’t help but feel sorry for Qin Xuan. They still remembered how domineering he had been the first time they met. Back then, he was the most talented prodigy of the Heavenly Dome Galaxy.","Yet, before they knew it, the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect had been destroyed, and Qin Xuan lost his home and backing.","Even minor sects that were previously terrified of him dared to climb over his head now. Such a drastic change in circumstances would have been tough for anyone to swallow.","Chu Feng’s appearance was a ray of hope to him. It made him realize that there were people who were unconditionally good to him regardless of his circumstances. He was not crying out of sorrow; he was moved.","“Sorry, I couldn’t hold it in.” Qin Xuan raised his tear-stained face and apologized.","Chu Feng grabbed his shoulder and said, “Don’t worry, brother. Crying is not embarrassing. There is no rule that a man can’t cry. But once you are done, you have to wipe away your tears and do what you must. A true man will stand firm in the face of adversity.”","“Mm.” Qin Xuan nodded."]},{"number":6329,"title":"Chapter 6329: Chapter 6327: A Friend?!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6327: A Friend?!","Next, Chu Feng told Qin Xuan how he should select a peak in the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. Qin Xuan’s resources, coupled with what he had received from Wang Qiang and the others, were enough to activate the third hardest peak.","Thus, Qin Xuan set his eyes on the third-hardest peak.","After some searching, Chu Feng and the others finally found the ideal area. They each took a peak and proceeded to activate them.","Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather guarded them from the warship.","Activating a peak was simple—they just needed to fuse resources into it. The tough part was grasping the formation’s energy.","The group swiftly activated five peaks, and energy gushed into the sky. The energy released by the hardest peak was much greater than that of the other peaks.","Chu Feng and the others sat down on their respective peaks, closed their eyes, and focused on grasping the energy. Only Chu Feng and Qin Xuan looked unfazed; the others had tight frowns, and their faces scrunched now and then.","It was the same even for Little Fishy.","“The rumors must be true. The energy on the hardest peak is difficult to grasp.”","Little Fishy’s mother and grandfather couldn’t help but worry as they kept a close eye on Little Fishy’s and Xianhai Shaoyu’s conditions. Meanwhile, Little Fishy’s father focused more on their surroundings, keeping a close eye out for strangers.","The formations had caused a huge ruckus, and Chu Feng and the others’ figures could be seen through the energy.","Chu Feng was now so famous that he became the center of attention no matter where he went. Witnessing him make history was a bragging right in itself, so people were gathering in the area. As the news spread further, the situation could eventually become uncontrollable.","Given the ongoing chaos in the world of cultivation, this commotion might draw the attention of someone who harbored malice toward them.","And Little Fishy’s father had already spotted a few suspicious figures.","“What’s wrong?” Little Fishy’s mother noticed his tension.","Rather than worrying about Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s failure, he appeared to be more concerned about impending danger.","“Remember how we spotted quite a few Zhao Immortal Clansmen while searching for somewhere suitable? It didn’t look like they were searching for peaks; they were scouting the area.","“Just earlier, I spotted a Zhao Immortal Clansman. When he saw Chu Feng and the others, he turned around and returned the direction where he came from. He must be reporting this matter to someone. I wonder what the Zhao Immortal Clan is planning,” Little Fishy’s father replied.","“We couldn’t even faze the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Steel Peak. If they harbor malice toward us, it’s unlikely that we’ll be able to stop them,” Little Fishy’s mother replied worriedly.","Little Fishy’s father didn’t speak a word, but his eyes hardened with conviction.","Little Fishy’s grandfather sighed. “I thought I would be unrivaled after advancing to Heavenly God level, but I still feel as stifled as ever. I hate this feeling. Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan has to repay the debt we owe young friend Chu Feng, and I have lived long enough. Be it the Zhao Immortal Clan or what dogshit clans, I’ll drag them down to hell if they dare come after us!”","Little Fishy’s parents nodded. They had also made up their minds to protect Chu Feng and the others to their dying breath.","Their worries were not unfounded, and the news soon reached Eighth Zhao’s ears.","“Young friend Chu Feng activated the hardest peak? This won’t do. He mustn’t fail. We have to stop him!” Eighth Zhao frowned.","He glanced at Zhao Zhuyin.","She had activated the peak Eighth Zhao had meticulously chosen for her and had entered the same meditative state as Chu Feng. She was surrounded by a humongous protective formation that spanned the nearby peaks.","This protective formation was constructed by the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, but it was emanating an identical aura to the Fortuitous Bloodline Formation.","Under the formation’s protection, Zhao Zhuyin’s breathing remained stable, and her expression remained calm. It looked like she had it all under control.","Eighth Zhao turned to Zhao Daobin. “I’ll leave Zhuyin to you.”","“Lord Father, are you heading there personally? You can leave it to us,” Zhao Tingxue said.","“Young friend Chu Feng is very important. Even I’m not confident of stopping the activation, let alone the rest of you. It looks like Zhuyin will succeed anyway, so I’ll deal with Chu Feng’s side,” Eighth Zhao said before flitting off.","“Is Chu Feng that important? We’ll have to use that treasure to terminate an activated formation. That’s the safety precaution we prepared for Zhuyin!” Zhao Tingxue asked Zhao Daobin.","“Chu Feng is indeed extraordinary. Let’s trust the clan chief’s judgment on this,” Zhao Daobin said, but his eyes reflected his skepticism.","On the other side, Chu Feng and Qin Xuan remained stable, but Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and Xianhai Shaoyu’s frowns were deepening, and even their complexions were turning increasingly pale.","“Will there be side effects if they fail?” Little Fishy’s mother nervously walked to and fro the warship.","Little Fishy’s father and grandfather didn’t say much, but their worried faces said it all.","All of a sudden, the three of them looked southwest.","Little Fishy’s parents unleashed their bloodline powers, raising their cultivation to rank three Heavenly God level.","Bam!","A powerful force shattered the warship.","At the same time, a powerful gush of martial power formed a humongous barrier around the surroundings.","“It’s true! The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief is here!”","“Their auras... They must have reached Heavenly God level, right?”","“As expected of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.”","By the time the crowd realized what was going on, they were already enveloped within the humongous martial power barrier. The sight of Little Fishy’s parents shook their hearts.","Some of them had already heard about Chu Feng’s rescue of Qin Xuan, and that his party included the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief. Prior to this revelation, none of them knew that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief had already reached Heavenly God level.","Weng!","The martial power barrier released a blinding light, and pillars of immortal energies gushed into the sky. The barrier’s exterior resembled the water surface, while giant fishes manifested and swam within the barrier. It was majestic and powerful.","From the barrier, the crowd felt devastating power.","“That is no ordinary formation. It is the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s clan-protection formation!” a knowledgeable elder revealed the barrier’s identity.","The crowd wondered what prompted the three Heavenly Gods to work in unison to construct such a huge martial power barrier. Who were they guarding against, for experts of their caliber to be so vigilant?","“Looks like I have been discovered,” a voice echoed.","Eighth Zhao appeared in the sky. Looking at his clothes, the crowd immediately understood why the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief was so vigilant.","“The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, right? I am the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. You don’t have to be so cautious of me. I am Chu Feng’s friend.”","Eighth Zhao’s words shocked everyone, including Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather.","The unfathomably powerful Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief was Chu Feng’s friend?"]},{"number":6330,"title":"Chapter 6330: Chapter 6328: It’s You?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6328: It’s You?","“You’re acquainted with young friend Chu Feng?” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“We’re old friends now.” Eighth Zhao laughed.","“I’m glad to hear that. Young friend Chu Feng is in a critical phase of grasping the formation’s energy. I constructed this formation as a precaution, so pardon my offense.” The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief clasped his fist apologetically.","He remained wary despite Eighth Zhao’s light-hearted and friendly attitude. He found that he couldn’t see through Eighth Zhao’s cultivation; he wouldn’t have noticed him in the first place if not for him enveloping the area with a treasure that could detect Heavenly God level cultivators.","“I came here for that. Young friend Chu Feng activated the wrong peak. That is the hardest one, which is nigh impossible to succeed in. However, I have a way to reverse it. I can still make it in time if you remove the formation now and let me in. Nothing can be done once he fails,” Eighth Zhao said.","“My apologies, Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. I can’t do that,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“This concerns young friend Chu Feng’s future. I’ll have to resort to forceful measures if you don’t step aside,” Eighth Zhao said as he released his oppressive might.","Little Fishy’s father and grandfather quickly formed a hand seal. Countless fishes gushed out from the formation and rushed at Eighth Zhao.","However, these fishes disintegrated upon coming into contact with the oppressive might, almost as if tofu crashing into a boulder.","The sky shook. Everyone inside the formation fell over; only the mountain peaks remained firmly in place.","By then, countless cracks had already appeared on the formation. Blood was seeping from the corner of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief’s and others’ lips.","All these destructions were caused by the oppressive might. The difference in power couldn’t have been clearer.","“A rank four Heavenly God!” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief exclaimed.","He had expected as much, but he was still crushed by despair when he felt the other party’s strength. That being said, he was already prepared for this situation.","Without hesitation, Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather formed a hand seal and released blood-red auras into the formation, causing the formation to turn bizarre. On the one hand, the formation emanated an eerie, bloody aura. On the other hand, it felt powerful and divine.","“Haa, I said I’m doing this for young friend Chu Feng’s sake. Why are you putting your lives on the line to stop me? I went easy because you are on close terms with him. I hope you don’t think you can stop me by risking your lives. Not only are you sacrificing your lives in vain, but you are also hindering young friend Chu Feng’s future. Step aside now!” Eighth Zhao said.","His smile had vanished, and there was a cold glint in his eyes. He made it plenty clear that he wasn’t joking. He would pay no heed to the safety if they continued standing in his way.","“My apologies, Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. Young friend Chu Feng is grasping the formation’s energy and cannot sense what’s happening, so I can’t verify your relationship with him. I can’t let you stop his formation,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“I understand, and I don’t blame you for it. You shouldn’t blame me for this too.”","Eighth Zhao narrowed his eyes. He was going to make a move.","Overwhelming killing intent shrouded the area. It seeped through the barrier, such that everyone could clearly feel it.","Boom!","Just then, the world suddenly shook.","A light pillar pierced through the barrier and shot into the sky. It was coming from Chu Feng’s mountain peak.","That peak was already glowing before, but the light pillar made it appear a hundred times more majestic than before. Nine-colored lightning and formidable spirit power could be seen within the light pillar—they were Chu Feng’s Heavenly Lightning Bloodline and Ruler’s Bloodline.","“What in the world? Did young friend Chu Feng succeed?” Eighth Zhao was at a loss for words.","Boom!","Thunder boomed from the sky. The nine-colored lightning and spirit power began spreading outward, enveloping the realm in the blink of an eye. The phenomenon could be spotted even from the place where Zhao Daobin and Zhao Tingxue were.","“What a formidable phenomenon. Did someone succeed in grasping the formation?” Zhao Cangjing asked his grandfather, Zhao Daobin.","“According to the records, those who succeed in grasping the formation will produce a phenomenon based on their bloodline, but the scale of this phenomenon... It can only be produced from the hardest peak,” Zhao Daobin said.","Zhao Cangjing and Zhao Tingxue couldn’t believe what they were hearing.","“What? Someone succeeded in grasping the hardest peak’s formation?” Zhao Cangjing exclaimed in disbelief.","“I can already guess from the phenomenon who it is,” Zhao Daobin added.","“Chu Feng?” Zhao Tingxue asked.","“The Heavenly Lightning Bloodline and that spirit power; in the present world of cultivation, it could only be Chu Feng,” Zhao Daobin replied.","“That fellow is that formidable?” Zhao Cangjing asked.","“He’s an extraordinary one.” Zhao Daobin wasn’t as surprised as his grandson.","Zhao Tingxue looked at the phenomenon as she murmured, “Chu Feng... Now I’m curious to see you in person.”","...","More and more people were gathering around Chu Feng. Those who had arrived late could only watch from outside the barrier.","Eighth Zhao looked at the sight with a smile. He suddenly thought of something and turned to the trio from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. “You can stop depleting your life force now. Young friend Chu Feng has succeeded in grasping the formation. You’re just sacrificing yourself in vain at this rate.”","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and the others realized from those words that Eighth Zhao had decided to stop his attack. Is he truly doing this for Chu Feng’s sake? Is that why he is giving up after seeing Chu Feng’s success?","They stopped fusing their life force into the barrier but didn’t remove it. They were ready to reinforce it if Eighth Zhao did anything suspicious.","The phenomenon soon dissipated, and the overwhelming formation energy from the mountain peak flew into Chu Feng’s body.","Chu Feng finally opened his eyes. What he saw made his body tense up.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s formidable barrier and the injuries sustained by the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and the others led him to think that a powerful enemy had attacked.","“Young friend Chu Feng.” Eighth Zhao waved at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng recognized the other party right away.","“Elder Zhao? What are you doing here? Are you from the Zhao Immortal Clan?”","Chu Feng was initially surprised, but he quickly noticed the other party was wearing the Zhao Immortal Clan’s robe. It was hard not to notice the robe when it radiated a brilliant golden light.","“Young friend Chu Feng, it has been a while. I forgot to introduce myself then. I am the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief,” Eighth Zhao said with a smile.","“You are the clan chief? Doesn’t that make Zhao Tingxue your daughter?” Chu Feng’s astonishment deepened.","“Tingxue is my daughter. How do you know her?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Ah, I just met her.” Chu Feng smiled.","“You met her? She told me that she didn’t see you.” Eighth Zhao was perplexed.","“I used a fake name,” Chu Feng explained.","Realization dawned upon Eighth Zhao. “Ah, you are that Wu Ming fellow?”"]},{"number":6331,"title":"Chapter 6331: Chapter 6329: The Fortuitous Sun Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6329: The Fortuitous Sun Appears","“Yes, it’s me.” Chu Feng chuckled.","“No wonder. You played my Tinguxe like a fiddle. She told me she found someone even more formidable than Chu Feng. In the end, it’s still you,” Eighth Zhao said with a helpless sigh, but he quickly asked, “I’m curious. Who’s Wu De (Virtueless)?”","Chu Feng knew there was no hiding this matter, so he turned to Wang Qiang and said, “It’s my friend, Wang Qiang.”","But when he saw Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu’s conditions, he hurriedly formed a hand seal and relayed his voice transmission to them via a formation. He taught them a method and shared what he had grasped from the formation.","Otherwise, they might fail and be eliminated at this rate.","Under Chu Feng’s guidance, Little Fishy’s condition was the first to stop deteriorating. Soon, Wang Qiang and Xianhai Shaoyu’s conditions stopped deteriorating as well. They were starting to gain control over the formation.","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief. He had already done all he could, and the rest depended on their intelligence.","Shortly after, another phenomenon appeared. Qin Xuan had succeeded.","But the crowd was numb to it after having witnessed Chu Feng’s phenomenon. Most of them couldn’t tell how difficult the mountain peaks were; they could only gauge the relative difficulty via the phenomenon.","Compared to Chu Feng’s phenomenon, Qin Xuan’s feat felt like nothing.","Eighth Zhao, who understood how difficult the third hardest peak was, wasn’t surprised either. He had once met Qin Xuan in God’s Era and knew that the latter had some substance to him. Rather, he was more interested in Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Wang Qiang.","Those three were challenging the hardest peak, a trial that Zhao Zhuyin dared not touch.","He could accept someone as monstrously talented as Chu Feng clearing the hardest peak, but the same couldn’t be said when it was anyone else. This was a feat that only the three Zenith Emperors had accomplished in the Ancient Era, after all!","Weng!","But soon, a light pillar gushed from Little Fishy’s peak. The sky morphed into an ocean filled with humongous fish swimming freely. It was a phenomenon!","It was far greater than the phenomenon Qin Xuan had produced, enveloping the entire realm.","Shortly after, another terrifying aura rippled as four ferocious behemoths emerged in the sky. These behemoths were so imposing that it felt like they could destroy galaxies and devour the sun and the moon.","Wang Qiang had succeeded too!","Moments later, Xianhai Shaoyu’s peak triggered a phenomenon as well. It resembled Little Fishy’s phenomenon, and it was no weaker than hers.","“They all succeeded?”","Eighth Zhao looked conflicted. He couldn’t believe what he had just witnessed. Granted that these three phenomena combined were still slightly lacking compared to what Chu Feng had triggered earlier, they were still spectacular in their own right.","Soon, the three phenomena returned into Little Fishy and the others’ bodies respectively, but this felt like an assault to them. Their faces distorted, and fresh blood spurted from their mouths. They collapsed on the peak and fainted.","Everything fell silent after.","“W-what happened?”","The crowd was dumbstruck. In particular, Eighth Zhao was confused.","The trial was over.","If those three had failed, they would have been transported out of the realm. In other words, they should have cleared the trial, but why were they inflicted with severe injuries then?","Was it a success or a failure?","Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather and Chu Feng flitted to Little Fishy’s, Xianhai Shaoyu’s, and Wang Qiang’s sides to check their conditions. But none of them dared to make a reckless move. Instead, they turned to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng lifted Wang Qiang with one hand and grabbed his pulse with his other.","Wang Qiang’s pulse was very weak due to the extreme disturbance in the energies within him, but his vitals were still stable.","“Elders, there’s no need to worry. You see, I saw them struggling with their formations, so I shared my insights with them. The earlier phenomena indicate that they have succeeded. I suspect the formation here has some degree of sentience; it might have punished them after it realized they had received help. Since the formation has punished instead of evicting them, they should be fine as long as we let things run its course.”","Chu Feng discreetly shared his conjecture with Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather.","“That’s a relief.”","Chu Feng’s words put their minds at ease. They had also inspected Little Fishy’s and Xianhai Shaoyu’s conditions, and their vitals were stable too despite their extreme energies disturbance.","Just then, a peculiar sound echoed from the distant earth. It was not the roar of a ferocious beast nor the sound of fighting. It sounded more like a call from this realm.","The crowd looked in the sound’s direction with confused eyes. A humongous silhouette was slowly surfacing from the earth. It resembled the sun, but it was many times larger than the sun. It was radiant, but the radiance was confined within the silhouette itself.","The crowd was intrigued by this sight, but Eighth Zhao revealed a relieved smile.","“It’s the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s Fortuitous Sun! The Fortuitous Sun only emerges if enough people obtain the formation energy. When the Fortuitous Sun reaches the top of the sky, it will emanate the Fortuitous Light, which facilitates the fusion of the formation energy into one’s body, thus metamorphosing one’s bloodline,” Eighth Zhao explained.","Chu Feng had already heard this from Zhao Tingxue.","Judging from the extremely slow movement of the Fortuitous Sun, it would take some time before it reached the top of the sky.","“How are the three young friends?” Eighth Zhao flitted over to Chu Feng’s side and asked.","“Their injuries are considerable, but their vitals are stable. They should recover with some rest, though I don’t know how long it will take,” Chu Feng replied.","“That was quite the commotion earlier. It’s a blessing that they are fine. Young friend Chu Feng, do you think they have succeeded in grasping the formation energy?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“I didn’t expect these three young friends to possess such talent.”","Chu Feng’s answer prompted Eighth Zhao to reassess Little Fishy and the others, his eyes reflecting not just surprise but doubt too."]},{"number":6332,"title":"Chapter 6332: Chapter 6330: Voice Transmission","paragraphs":["Chapter 6330: Voice Transmission","“Young friend Chu Feng and Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, it’ll take time for the Fortuitous Sun to rise to its peak. There’s nothing to do but to wait now that you have grasped the formation energy, so why don’t you rest at my place?”","Eighth Zhao turned to Chu Feng and added, “You can catch up with Zhuyin too.”","It wouldn’t be good for Chu Feng and the others to turn down Eighth Zhao’s invitation, so they followed him to where Zhao Zhuyin was.","Even from a distance away, Chu Feng could see the formation constructed around Zhao Zhuyin.","“Chu Feng, is that a supporting formation?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, but the supporting formation shares the same aura as the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. The Zhao Immortal Clan must have a deep understanding of this place,” Chu Feng replied.","“Interesting. It looks like we aren’t the only ones they invited,” Eggy said.","Other than Zhao Zhuyin and the formation around her, there was a massive floating warship resembling a huge city, consisting of multiple palaces, squares, and gardens. On the warship, there were not only Zhao Immortal Clansmen but also other juniors.","Chu Feng could spot Zhao Immortal Clansmen escorting more juniors onto the warship.","“Paying respect to clan chief.”","Zhao Daobin led a group, including elders, Zhao Tingxue, and Zhao Cangjing, forth to greet Eighth Zhao. This huge procession drew the attention of many on the warship.","“Young friend Chu Feng, it has been a while,” Zhao Daobin greeted Chu Feng, too.","Chu Feng returned the greeting.","The other Zhao Immortal Clansmen assessed Chu Feng. Despite Chu Feng’s resounding reputation, this was the first time they were meeting him.","“Lord Father, aren’t you going to introduce them?” Zhao Tingxue urged Eighth Zhao.","Zhao Cangjing stood by the side with a polite smile, looking obedient and friendly.","“What’s there to introduce? You two already know each other!” Eighth Zhao laughed.","Zhao Tingxue was perplexed. She thought her father had misunderstood her, so she clarified, “Lord Father, this is my first time meeting young master Chu Feng.”","“What first time meeting? He’s Wu Ming!” Eighth Zhao replied.","Zhao Tingxue was stunned. Zhao Cangjing looked as if someone had stuffed feces down his throat.","Faced with their questioning eyes, Chu Feng replied with a smile, “It’s me.”","Zhao Cangjing felt incredibly awkward. He tried to squeeze out a smile, but to no avail.","Zhao Tingxue quickly came to terms with the situation and smiled, “I was wondering how the world of cultivation could have so many talented individuals, from the renowned young master Chu Feng to the elusive Wu Ming. Little did I know they are the same person!”","“Pardon me, Miss Tingxue. I didn’t want to reveal my identity then,” Chu Feng replied.","“I understand. Young master Chu Feng, I noticed a majestic phenomenon earlier. You must have grasped one of the formations. Is it the hardest peak’s formation?” Zhao Tingxue asked.","“Young friend Chu Feng and these three young friends have all grasped the hardest peak’s formations.” Eighth Zhao gestured to the unconscious Little Fishy and the others.","“Lord Father, these three cleared the hardest peak too?” Zhao Tingxue was baffled.","“Indeed. Didn’t you see the phenomena they induced?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“I noticed it, but it was so distant that I thought it was the second hardest peak,” Zhao Tingxue replied.","“Oh? Did their phenomena not envelop the entire realm?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Lord Clan Chief, the other phenomena are smaller than the one induced by young friend Chu Feng,” Zhao Daobin replied.","“I see. That’s to be expected. The hardest peak’s formation is too difficult. Even though they have grasped the formation too, only young friend Chu Feng cleared it unscathed. It’s normal for there to be a difference in their phenomena,” Eighth Zhao said.","From those words, Zhao Tingxue understood that Little Fishy and the others had to pay a price to grasp the formation, and that was the reason they were currently unconscious.","Weng!","A light pillar gushed into the sky. Shortly after, a divine light pulsated outward.","It was Zhao Zhuyin’s phenomenon.","It was nowhere on par with the phenomenon induced by Chu Feng or even Little Fishy and the others, but it still awed many present. To be fair, it only paled in comparison to the four of them.","The first thing Zhao Zhuyin did after grasping the formation was to look for Eighth Zhao and the others, but when she saw Chu Feng, her face beamed with joy.","“Father.” Zhao Zhuyin first went to Eighth Zhao’s side before turning to Chu Feng. “It has been a while.”","“It has been a while,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","After trading pleasantries, Zhao Zhuyin learned that Chu Feng and his friends had cleared the hardest peak.","Shortly after, Zhao Tingxue and Zhao Cangjing excused themselves under the pretext that they would activate a mountain peak each. They had previously planned to leave after Zhao Zhuyin succeeded.","Chu Feng and the others were brought to a palace to rest. There, Eighth Zhao took out an emerald bead bracelet, which also shared the same aura as the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","It should have been impossible to intervene in Little Fishy and the others’ conditions, but this emerald bead bracelet was designed to treat injuries from the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. There was no better treasure to help Little Fishy and the others.","Thanks to the emerald bead bracelet, the energies rampaging inside Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and Xianhai Shaoyu slowly calmed down, though they remained unconscious.","That greatly raised Chu Feng’s already positive impression of Eighth Zhao and Zhao Zhuyin. Despite being the chief of an Ancient Era clan, Eighth Zhao harbored no hostility toward present-era cultivators.","Chu Feng was in a good mood during the banquet till he received a voice transmission that made him tense up.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you should find a chance to take your friends out of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, and don’t come back.”"]},{"number":6333,"title":"Chapter 6333: Chapter 6331: Apology and Compensation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6331: Apology and Compensation","It was from Zhao Daobin.","Chu Feng was taken aback. He instinctively glanced at Zhao Daobin, only to see the latter still chatting merrily with Little Fishy’s grandfather. But there should be no outsiders here, so who is Zhao Daobin guarding against?","“Elder, can you tell me the reason?” Chu Feng anxiously asked via voice transmission while keeping a composed exterior.","“Young friend Chu Feng, allow me to return the favor I owe you for saving me from the God Clan. I’m not in a position to say too much. Do as I say. I won’t do anything detrimental to you,” Zhao Daobin replied.","“What’s going on, Chu Feng? Does Eighth Zhao intend to harm you? Or is Zhao Daobin up to something?” Eggy also heard the voice transmission and asked.","“It’s all possible,” Chu Feng replied.","At the same time, he called out to the Divine Deer, “Elder.”","The Divine Deer immediately replied, “Don’t worry, the Zhao Immortal Clan won’t be able to harm you under my watch.”","Chu Feng’s heart was put at ease.","The Divine Deer could independently judge how dangerous the situation was and activate its power. That was how it saved him, Zhao Daobin, and the others from Shen Bai back then.","“Zhuyin, it’s about time. Don’t forget what you have to do,” Eighth Zhao suddenly said.","“Got it,” Zhao Zhuyin replied before walking up to Chu Feng.","“Here, let’s have a toast. I’ll have to leave after this.” Zhao Zhuyin’s face was flushed from all the alcohol she had drunk. While cultivators didn’t get drunk on alcohol, it emboldened them.","“Cheers.” Chu Feng raised his wine cup and downed its contents.","Zhao Zhuyin gulped down her alcohol before revealing a satisfied smile. She turned to Eighth Zhao and said, “Father, take care of my friend.”","“Don’t worry, he’s my friend too,” Eighth Zhao smiled.","Zhao Zhuyin took her leave under the elders’ escort.","Eighth Zhao waved his sleeves, and the other elders left as well, leaving just Zhao Daobin and Chu Feng’s group in the room.","Eighth Zhao stood up and walked up to Zhao Daobin.","Pah! Pah!","He struck Zhao Daobin’s shoulders twice before saying, “Our Zhao Immortal Clan’s enforcement elder sure is a loyal friend. Is it because young friend Chu Feng saved you from the God Clan?”","Most people had no idea what was going on, but Chu Feng’s heart clenched up. It was now clear to him that the person Zhao Daobin was guarded against was Eighth Zhao.","Despite communicating via voice transmission, Eighth Zhao still overheard their conversation.","Zhao Daobin unhesitatingly turned around and kneeled before Eighth Zhao. But instead of begging to be spared, he said, “Lord Clan Chief, young friend Chu Feng is a good person, and I owe him a favor. I beseech you to spare young friend Chu Feng and the others on my account.”","Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather realized what was going on and shot to their feet. They quickly grabbed Little Fishy and the others before pulling Chu Feng and Qin Xuan behind them. They looked warily at Eighth Zhao as they asked, “Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, what are you planning?”","“Haa~” Eighth Zhao sighed.","Boom!","He suddenly released a brilliant golden light—it was his bloodline power. Everyone in the room sensed his cultivation rising from rank four to rank five Heavenly God level.","“Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, don’t bother using your life force ignition means. It’s futile even if you deplete the entirety of your life force,” Eighth Zhao said.","He was forcing everyone to submit to him by sheer force!","“Elder, I don’t understand what’s going on,” Chu Feng suddenly interjected.","“As expected of young friend Chu Feng. I see fluster on the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief’s face, yet you are perfectly composed,” Eighth Zhao teased.","But Chu Feng was in no mood to joke around. “Elder Zhao, may I ask a question? Have I made a misjudgment?”","Eighth Zhao lowered his shame. “Young friend Chu Feng, you have stumped me right there. I was planning to tell you the truth. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain was opened by our Zhao Immortal Clan; our ancestors bought this place at a hefty price in the Ancient Era.","“I activated it now for Zhuyin’s sake. As you can see, Zhuyin is decently talented. She is a step away from attaining the highest talent ever in our Zhao Immortal Clan. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is her greatest opportunity.”","Chu Feng asked, “Those who have grasped the formation energy will be of use to her?”","“That’s right. The first step is the activation of the formations on the mountain peak, and the second step is grasping the formations’ energies. There’s still a third step—enlightenment. We constructed that formation around Zhuyin’s peak to boost her intelligence.","“There are two phases to enlightenment. The first phase is to grasp the formation energy, which you have already succeeded at. But Zhuyin can achieve the second phase with the help of our treasures and formation, and the second phase allows her to obtain your formations’ energies,” Eighth Zhao explained.","“So, we are just puppets. Elder, you were worried that I would fail to grasp the formation not because you didn’t want me to miss this fortuitous encounter, but that you didn’t want to lose me as a puppet,” Chu Feng replied.","“Haa, this concerns not just Zhuyin’s but our Zhao Immortal Clan’s future. I have no choice,” Eighth Zhao said as he supported the kneeling Zhao Daobin back to his feet.","He brought out a massive stash of natural oddities and treasures with a wave of his sleeves, then, with a clench of his fist, all the items flew into a Cosmos Sack.","“Young friend Chu Feng, we won’t let your effort be in vain. This is our compensation to you.” Eighth Zhao handed the Cosmos Sack to Chu Feng.","“What if I refuse to help?” Chu Feng tossed the Cosmos Sack back.","Eighth Zhao sighed. He slowly made his way up to Chu Feng. What he did next astounded everyone, including Zhao Daobin. He kneeled before Chu Feng.","“Young friend Chu Feng, I earnestly admire you, and I don’t want to lose you as a friend. I know what I have done today betrays your trust, but I have no choice but to do this for Zhuyin’s sake. Allow me to apologize to you,” Eighth Zhao said."]},{"number":6334,"title":"Chapter 6334: Chapter 6332: Negotiation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6332: Negotiation","Zhao Daobin was shocked because he had watched the clan chief grow up. He knew that Eighth Zhao had never kneeled to anyone other than his deceased parents and their ancestors.","It was unthinkable to Zhao Daobin that he would kneel to Chu Feng.","Eighth Zhao stood up and said, “Young friend Chu Feng, my grandparents were dead by the time I was born. I have never kneeled to anyone other than my parents. I kneeled to you not just to preserve our friendship but also for my daughter, Zhuyin, and the Zhao Immortal Clan. I could have coerced you into doing my bidding, but it’s nowhere as effective as convincing you.”","“So, you plan to coerce me if I refuse?” Chu Feng pointed out what was between the lines.","“While I have a high opinion of you, I shoulder my clan’s fate. I can even give up my life for my clan. Needless to say, I won’t hesitate to take someone’s life too,” Eighth Zhao replied.","“Chu Feng, shall I take you away now?” the Divine Deer asked.","“It’s fine for now, elder.” Chu Feng told the Divine Deer before addressing Eighth Zhao. “I have an idea of what’s happening, but I still don’t have the full picture. Why don’t you share the details with me? I’ll reconsider it.”","“Sure.”","Eighth Zhao took out an ancient scroll that had been passed down from the Ancient Era. It was a method that predecessors in the Ancient Era had devised.","According to the scroll, there were three steps to clearing the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain.","The first step was to activate the formation.","The second step was to grasp the formation energy.","The third step was to assimilate the formation energy.","The third step was the simplest. It simply involved waiting for the Fortuitous Sun to rise to the top of the sky, though it required the help of others who had activated the formation.","The second step was also fairly simple. One just had to fuse the energies that others had gathered in the trial.","The hardest hurdle was the first step, activation. It required talented individuals to activate and grasp the formations, before offering up the powerful formations energies they had obtained to an individual.","“Does Zhao Zhuyin know about this?” Chu Feng asked.","“I was about to talk to you about that. She knows we have made elaborate preparations, but she doesn’t know we’ll be siphoning other people’s formation energies. Given Zhuyin’s character, she will refuse it if she learns about it. That’s why I need you to persuade her,” Eighth Zhao said.","“You need me to persuade your daughter, too? That’s another price,” Chu Feng replied.","“Feel free to state your demands. I can add more if it’s not enough,” Eighth Zhao said as he passed the Cosmos Sack to Chu Feng.","This time, Chu Feng accepted it. He had browsed through the treasures; it was not of much use to him, but there was no reason for him to turn it down.","“My other condition is for you to release everyone else,” Chu Feng said.","“That won’t do.” Eighth Zhao shook his head.","“The fusion process poses a threat to one’s life. Not everyone can withstand the pressure. Besides, the formation energy I have gathered should be enough,” Chu Feng replied.","“I have to ensure everything goes well,” Eighth Zhao insisted.","“I can guarantee Zhao Zhuyin’s success, and my formation energy is enough to advance her bloodline, but I don’t want my friends to risk their lives and others to die for this,” Chu Feng said.","“I understand. You won’t help us unless I free them,” Eighth Zhao pointed out.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“You’re threatening me.”","“You can think of it that way.”","“I can also threaten you with your friends’ lives.”","“No, you can’t. I can leave right now with my friends if I want to, and you can’t stop me. Ask your enforcement elder how I rescued him from the God Clan that day.”","“I’ve already heard the story from Elder Daobin. Do you take me to be the same as the God Clansmen? If I was there, I would have destroyed the God Clan.”","“You can give it a try if you doubt me.”","Eighth Zhao stared at Chu Feng. Seeing the latter’s confident demeanor, he suddenly laughed. “Young friend Chu Feng, there’s no need to do this when we can talk things out. Why don’t we do this? You first help Zhuyin activate the fusion formation, and I’ll be able to verify whether the energy Zhuyin obtains is sufficient. If what you said is true, I’ll let your friends go.","“As for the others, you aren’t close to them. I’ll set up a dueling ring and let them freely pick anyone from my clan who is of the same cultivation level as them to fight with. As long as they win, I’ll let them leave. What do you think?”","“The format is fine, but you mustn’t take their lives,” Chu Feng said.","“Of course.” Eighth Zhao smiled.","“All right, let’s do that then.”","“I’ll be troubling you to talk to Zhuyin, young friend Chu Feng.”","“All right, but they have to come with me.”","Chu Feng had to ensure that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and the others remained in his vision.","“This way.”","Eighth Zhao led the way, and Chu Feng’s group followed him.","On the way, Little Fishy’s grandfather sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, saying, “Don’t force yourself, young friend Chu Feng. If it comes down to it, I’ll put my life on the line to create an opening for you to escape.”","Little Fishy’s parents also sent a similar message to him.","“Don’t worry, elders. This matter might be tricky, but it won’t threaten my life. Besides, Brother Shaoyu and Yu’er have already grasped the formation energy, and they’ll receive the benefit once the Fortuitous Sun rises to the top. Not to mention I require this energy too,” Chu Feng explained.","“But aren’t you going to offer your energy to Zhao Zhuyin?” Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather were confused.","“I have my ways. You don’t have to worry about me,” Chu Feng replied.","Seeing Chu Feng’s confidence, Little Fishy’s grandfather and parents could only let things slip. They knew deep down that even if they risked their lives, their chances of escaping from Eighth Zhao remained slim.","Qin Xuan didn’t bother saying a word because he knew there was nothing he could do to help. His eyes brimmed with worry and frustration.","It didn’t take them long to find Zhao Zhuyin. The latter was seated inside a special palace filled with formations.","Zhao Zhuyin reacted more vehemently than Chu Feng had expected when she learned what they were going to do.","“No way! I disagree!”"]},{"number":6335,"title":"Chapter 6335: Chapter 6333: Activation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6333: Activation","“Zhuyin, I am doing this for you. Do you remember me telling you I activated the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain for you? All preparations are in order. You mustn’t let my efforts go down in vain,” Eighth Zhao persuaded with a subservient voice.","He was afraid that his treasured daughter would turn him down.","“Are there no other ways to do it? Does Chu Feng have to do it?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","That question made others realize that Zhao Zhuyin was not averse to taking other people’s formation energy—she wasn’t that irresolute. She didn’t want to sacrifice Chu Feng because she cared for him.","Eighth Zhao understood Zhao Zhuyin’s thoughts. Zhao Zhuyin wouldn’t hesitate to sacrifice others in her pursuit of power, but she couldn’t do the same to people whom she cared about.","Thus, Eighth Zhao turned to Chu Feng.","“There are other ways to pull it off, but I can do it the best. On top of that, I’ll benefit from the process as well. It’s two birds with one stone,” Chu Feng replied.","“How can you benefit from activating the formation when it consumes your formation energy?” Zhao Zhuyin was skeptical.","“I mean it. If you do as I say, we’ll both benefit from this,” Chu Feng replied.","“Really?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","“Yes,” Chu Feng nodded.","“Then... how do we proceed?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","Eighth Zhao breathed a sigh of relief. It went smoother than he had expected.","Having made up their minds, Chu Feng began helping Zhao Zhuyin with activating her formation. They used the treasures prepared by the Zhao Immortal Clan, but the specific arrangements were all decided by him. He was the master in this field.","Eighth Zhao observed by the side while using his treasure to heal Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and Xianhai Shaoyu. He needed to keep an eye on Chu Feng in case the latter played tricks.","To his relief, the overall formation remained the same even though there were slight tweaks in the details.","Soon, the formation was complete, and Chu Feng and Zhao Zhuyin sat opposite each other in its middle.","Chu Feng placed a hand on Zhao Zhuyin’s forehead and the other on her dantian.","“Miss Zhao, remember one thing when you close your eyes later. Accept my energy and go with my flow. I won’t harm you. You need not worry about me either; this will be beneficial not just to you but to me as well. Can you do it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Mm.” Zhao Zhuyin nodded, displaying great trust in Chu Feng.","Chu Feng began channeling his energy into Zhao Zhuyin’s body.","This was a lengthy process, so much so that they remained in the same posture even after Zhao Tingxue and Zhao Cangjing had returned from grasping their respective formation energy, and Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Wang Qiang regained their consciousness.","The first thing Little Fishy and the others saw upon regaining consciousness was a weakened Chu Feng and a spirited Zhao Zhuyin. When they learned about what had happened, the three of them glared murderously at Eighth Zhao.","Little Fishy would have made a move on the spot if not for her parents and grandfather telling her that Chu Feng was doing it of his own volition.","But as Chu Feng grew weaker and weaker, Little Fishy couldn’t suppress the killing intent in her eyes.","Eighth Zhao was unbothered by it. He was strong enough to shrug off what Little Fishy and the others thought about him.","A while later, Eighth Zhao waved his sleeves, turning the palace walls transparent. This allowed them to see the situation outside.","There was a humongous square in the distance, and those who had grasped the formation energy were gathered there. They were divided into two sides—the present-era cultivators and the Ancient Era cultivators.","Several figures led by Zhao Cangjing descended from the sky—they were all Zhao Immortal Clansmen. Most of them were juniors, but some were slightly older than that.","“Has it begun?”","Xianhai Shaoyu and Wang Qiang looked over. Only Little Fishy kept her eyes on Chu Feng.","All three of them knew these people were in trouble.","Shortly after Zhao Cangjing landed, Zhao Daobin descended from the sky, but he stopped above the square. He gazed down loftily on the crowd as he spoke, “I am Zhao Daobin, the Zhao Immortal Clan’s enforcement elder. I don’t like to beat around the bush, so I’ll get straight to the point. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain was opened by our clan, so we get to decide who is entitled to the energy here. Those from the Ancient Era’s races are our guests, so feel free to take a seat.”","Elders from the Zhao Immortal Clan stepped onto the square and brought Ancient Era cultivators who had grasped the formation energy to the spectator stand.","The present-era cultivators panicked. It was blatant discrimination!","What Zhao Daobin said next further fanned their unease.","“You stole the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s formation energy without our clan’s permission. That is a crime punishable by death.”","The present-era cultivators anxiously explained themselves and begged for mercy. They felt indignant as the Zhao Immortal Clan had never mentioned this at all.","But in truth, the accusers understood how wronged the accused were. The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain was a trap laid by the Zhao Immortal Clan.","“Do you think it is right to take from a field just because its owner isn’t around? What’s done is done. I don’t want to hear your excuses. You’re fortunate that our clan chief’s friend spoke up on your behalf, so we decided to give you a chance. However, it’s up to you whether you can take advantage of the opportunity or not.","“Those who have grasped the formation energy can select any Zhao Immortal Clansman of the same cultivation level as their opponent. If you can defeat our clansmen, we’ll let you and your people go. You’ll also be able to reap the benefits of the formation when the Fortuitous Sun rises to the top of the sky. But if you fail, you’ll have to remove the formation energy from your body the way we request.”","Someone immediately asked, “Elder, is the process of removing the formation energy from our body harmful?”","Zhao Daobin smiled. “Of course.”","“May I know... how harmful it will be?” the person asked once more.","“There are some who recover with some rest, but there are also those who die on the spot. Based on our estimates, the latter is more likely,” Zhao Daobin said.","The present-era cultivators turned pale."]},{"number":6336,"title":"Chapter 6336: Chapter 6334: Contempt From the Ancient Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 6334: Contempt From the Ancient Era","Countless figures rushed to the square. They were present-era cultivators looking to rescue their juniors.","But they were stopped by a powerful oppressive might before they could get close. Pained wails echoed. Some got off with just bleeding heads, whereas others fainted on the spot.","“You should weigh yourself before causing trouble in our Zhao Immortal Clan’s turf. This is the only warning you’ll get. Make another reckless move, and I’ll take your life.” Zhao Daobin coldly eyed everyone present.","It was completely different from how he had treated Chu Feng. He might have acknowledged Chu Feng and spoken up for the latter’s behalf in front of their clan chief, but that was a different story. Someone who could become a clan’s enforcement elder couldn’t be soft-hearted.","Faced with Zhao Daobin’s overwhelming strength, the present-era cultivators dared not even beg for mercy, let alone muster the courage to save their brethren.","“The only way to escape from here is to defeat our clansmen. Otherwise, you’ll merely be implicating your clan in this.” Zhao Daobin turned his gaze back to the trapped present-era juniors in the square.","They were all juniors—the Zhao Immortal Clan had picked them out for Zhao Zhuyin.","Seeing there was no other choice, the present-era juniors picked their duel opponents and began fighting. However, they quickly landed in defeat.","Despite being of the same cultivation level, none of the present-era cultivators was a match for the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","“The present-era cultivators are useless.”","“What do you expect? They wouldn’t have fared so badly in the Ancient Era if they were truly capable.”","“They merely picked up on our trash while we were trapped. It’s laughable how they think they are a big deal.”","Even those from the other Ancient Era’s races mocked the present-era cultivators, but no one in the square dared to refute them. How could they when they were losing so badly?","Those who had yet to fight became even more prudent with their selection. They hoped to pick a weak opponent so that they could safely leave this place.","Wang Qiang and Qin Xuan heard the scoffs too.","“I am a present-era cultivator too. I shall fight on their behalf, too,” Qin Xuan abruptly declared.","“You want to fight too? Sure. You can free ten people from the square if you can defeat a single person of the cultivation level, but you will have to hand over your formation energy if you lose,” Eighth Zhao said.","Qin Xuan was about to accept the offer when a hand clasped his mouth, stopping him from speaking. It was Wang Qiang.","“Brother Qin, there’s n-n-no need to do this. We don’t know t-t-those people anyway. Why are you putting your life on the line for them?” Wang Qiang advised.","But Qin Xuan still accepted the offer despite having his mouth clasped.","“Brother Wang Qiang, I am a present-era cultivator. I might have lost my sect, but I still have my dignity. I can’t let the Ancient Era cultivators look down on us. I’ll prove that our ancestors were only weaker in the Ancient Era due to a lack of opportunity. We are, in no way, inferior to them!” Qin Xuan spoke with conviction. He had made up his mind.","“Fine.” Wang Qiang had no choice but to release Qin Xuan.","The palace door opened, and Qin Xuan descended onto the square.","However, Xianhai Shaoyu also darted out with him.","“Brother Shaoyu, y-y-you haven’t recovered from your injuries yet! Why are you doing this?” Wang Qiang exclaimed, but Xianhai Shaoyu didn’t even turn his head back. He had also made up his mind.","“Haaa~” Wang Qiang sighed.","He was more annoyed than worried.","“They let their r-r-recklessness get the better of them. It’s one thing if they win, b-b-but if they lose, my b-b-brother would have to clean up after them,” Wang Qiang spoke unhesitatingly in front of Little Fishy, as well as her parents and grandfather.","Little Fishy and the others were worried about Xianhai Shaoyu.","Xianhai Shaoyu, Little Fishy, and Wang Qiang were in a feeble state from the formation’s backlash. They wouldn’t stand much of a chance against the Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies in their current state.","“Qin Xuan?”","“Xianhai Shaoyu?”","“They have been captured too?”","Qin Xuan and Xianhai Shaoyu’s appearance caught the crowd’s attention. The Ancient Era cultivators looked upon the sight expectantly, having heard their names. In particular, Xianhai Shaoyu’s reputation was resounding.","Only a duel involving such prodigies was exciting to watch.","As for the present-era cultivators, they tasted despair instead of excitement, especially when they saw Xianhai Shaoyu. If the powerful Immortal Sea Fish Clan was no match for the Zhao Immortal Clan, resulting in Xianhai Shaoyu’s capture, their chances of escaping were bleak.","But their eyes changed when they heard Zhao Daobin’s announcement.","“You’re very lucky. These two young heroes have chosen to stand up for you. They will be able to free ten people of their choice if they can defeat an opponent of the same cultivation level as them,” Zhao Daobin said.","Cheers erupted. The present-era cultivators expressed their gratitude toward Qin Xuan and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Young friends, by the same cultivation level, I’m not referring to your base cultivation, but your highest cultivation after invoking your bloodline and other means. If your cultivation exceeds the limit you have stated during the battle, we will terminate the duel, and you’ll have to pick a new opponent,” Zhao Daobin told Xianhai Shaoyu and Qin Xuan.","His attitude toward them was much better than how he treated other present-era cultivators, though their close relations with Chu Feng played a huge part in that.","“I understand the rules,” Qin Xuan replied.","He raised his cultivation to the maximum level before turning to the Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies.","“Who’s willing to be my opponent?”","Shoosh!","A woman flew out and stood before Qin Xuan. The light shrouding her dissipated, revealing her appearance. She wasn’t beautiful, but she commanded an air of valiance that most men lacked.","She unleashed her bloodline power upon landing, showing that her cultivation was comparable to Qin Xuan’s.","Clang!","The woman drew a God Armament and pointed it at Qin Xuan. “I am a junior too, so don’t accuse me of taking advantage of you if you lose.”","Qin Xuan also drew a God Armament. He charged at the woman without saying a word. As he swung his blade, he abruptly vanished, but a torrential rain of swords rushed at the woman.","It was a God Taboo Martial Skill—the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s clan-protection martial skill, Heavenly Dome Sword Punishment!","Qin Xuan unleashed his strongest attack right from the get-go, showing how seriously he took this battle.","However, the Zhao Immortal Clanswoman didn’t panic in the least. She tightened her grip on her God Armament and raised a purple aura around her. She waited till the swords were about to reach her before diving in with her blade.","Despite the relentless onslaught of swords, she avoided them with phantom-like agility. Even those she couldn’t avoid were easily deflected by her blade.","Due to the difference in cultivation, most people couldn’t read into the intricacies of the battle and thought that Qin Xuan had the upper hand. But Wang Qiang shook his head.","“H-h-he should have listened to me. Now he’s just e-e-embarrassing himself.”","Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather sighed as well. The Zhao Immortal Clanswoman was dealing with Qin Xuan’s killing blow with ease despite having yet to get serious; the duel would be over in a jiffy once she got serious.","True to their expectations, the woman suddenly leaped into the sky and thrust her sword forth.","Psh!","Fresh blood spurted. A figure emerged from the void.","It was Qin Xuan, but his body was stabbed by the woman.","Qin Xuan stared at the woman in disbelief. He had no idea how the Zhao Immortal Clanswoman saw through his hiding spot.","The Zhao Immortal Clanswoman coldly sneered, “Weakling.”","Killing intent flared in her eyes."]},{"number":6337,"title":"Chapter 6337: Chapter 6335: I’ll Be Your Opponent","paragraphs":["Chapter 6335: I’ll Be Your Opponent","The Zhao Immortal Clanswoman, perhaps due to her little regard for human life or out of sheer disdain for Qin Xuan, emanated killing intent.","Weng!","Before she could make a move, she was crushed by an oppressive might, preventing her from launching any killing blows. It was from Zhao Daobin.","“Don’t go too far,” Zhao Daobin warned before retracting his oppressive might.","The woman heeded Zhao Daobin’s warning and pulled out her God Armament sword. She pointed her blade at Xianhai Shaoyu and said, “You’re next.”","But Xianhai Shaoyu ignored her. He unleashed his bloodline power, raising his cultivation to rank seven True God level.","The woman was startled. There was no need for Xianhai Shaoyu to answer her question, for his cultivation was the best answer. She was unworthy of dueling with him.","“I’m the only one you can challenge with your cultivation. I didn’t expect the Immortal Sea Fish Clan to have someone competent,” Zhao Cangjing said as he stood forth.","He also raised his cultivation to rank seven True God level.","“So be it.”","Xianhai Shaoyu drew his God Armament sword and tossed it into the sky. He formed a hand seal.","“Rank three God Taboo, Sea of Sword Reincarnation!”","He changed his hand seal, and the sword he threw out transformed into countless glowing swords that gushed forth like waves. His God Taboo Martial Skill enveloped the sky, leaving no room for Zhao Cangjing to escape.","“Interesting—a killing move right from the start. You must want to end it quickly. But you didn’t attack me right away. You might have done that out of etiquette, but you’re underestimating me. You’ll have to pay a price for underestimating your enemy,” Zhao Cangjing said.","He whipped out his God Armament spear. He remained confident despite the overwhelming prowess of the swords in the sky.","Xianhai Shaoyu didn’t bother replying.","“Rank three God Taboo, Immortal Dragon Spearmanship!”","Zhao Cangjing leaped into the sky, morphed into a golden dragon, and charged at Xianhai Shaoyu. But before his attack could land, the countless swords in the sky suddenly turned to him, morphed into sword dragons, and simultaneously attacked him from all directions.","Terrifying shockwaves rippled from the clash between the golden dragon was the sword dragons.","The victor was immediately made apparent.","Zhao Cangjing’s golden dragon was formidable; the sword dragons couldn’t hope to hurt him, though they slowed him down considerably. By the time he reached Xianhai Shaoyu, the latter had already evaded the attack.","Swords relentlessly charged at Zhao Cangjing, wave after wave. It looked as if he was buried by a sea of swords.","Zhao Cangjing could neither see nor sense where Xianhai Shaoyu was.","“This is similar to what Qin Xuan used earlier, but such means don’t work on our clansmen,” Zhao Cangjing said calmly.","His eyes began glowing. It didn’t take him long to find Xianhai Shaoyu’s silhouette amid the sea of swords. Without hesitation, he charged over.","But his attack failed yet again.","It was not because the Xianhai Shaoyu he found was fake, but that the sea of swords was constantly attacking and hindering him. It was as if this martial skill was activated with the intent to slow him.","No matter how hard Zhao Cangjing tried, Xianhai Shaoyu would always escape before he could reach him.","To make things worse, Zhao Cangjing’s speed only further slowed with time, and he was starting to feel pain. This made him realize that the situation was worse than he had expected.","“I see. He’s stalling for time. This martial skill grows stronger with time,” Zhao Daobin murmured the answer from mid-air.","Zhao Cangjing had realized the same too, but he couldn’t do anything. He was going to be defeated at this rate.","“Hm?”","Just then, Zhao Cangjing noticed Xianhai Shaoyu’s face subtly scrunching despite the latter’s attempts to control his expression.","“A fight of attrition? I’ll accompany you!” Zhao Cangjing sneered.","He stopped going on the offense, and the massive golden dragon around him contracted. This greatly enhanced his defensive prowess.","“Why did he stop attacking? Did he give up?”","Other cultivators on the square were confused.","But Xianhai Shaoyu’s parents and grandfather didn’t think that Zhao Cangjing had given up. Instead, they felt worried on Xianhai Shaoyu’s behalf.","Zhao Cangjing had opted for defense despite knowing that Xianhai Shaoyu’s martial skill strengthened with time because he knew Xianhai Shaoyu was in a feeble state, and this martial skill was extremely strenuous on him.","Soon, the ocean of swords halted its offense and instead receded.","Zhao Cangjing thought Xianhai Shaoyu was going to surrender when...","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Swords gushed down on Zhao Cangjing like a waterfall. The attack was far more concentrated and dangerous than before.","It was as if the ocean of swords only served to slow Zhao Cangjing, whereas this was the true attack!","Whoosh!","Countless swords fell on the golden dragons and shattered. Xianhai Shaoyu was still unable to tear through the golden dragon, especially after it had reinforced its defense.","In truth, Zhao Cangjing was being pushed to his limit. He crouched under the golden dragon with knitted eyebrows and clenched jaws. Blood seeped from his nose, mouth, and ears. He even began bleeding from his eyes and skin later on.","“Damn it! This fellow is so powerful?” Zhao Cangjing couldn’t believe his eyes. How could this fellow launch such a powerful attack when he’s in a feeble state?","But the attack abruptly weakened shortly after.","Zhao Cangjing lifted his head.","The ocean of swords had begun receding. Xianhai Shaoyu was barely standing by using his sword to support himself. His face was pale, and his lips were purple. His body was wobbling so much that he struggled to keep his balance.","Zhao Cangjing stood up and dissipated his golden dragon, knowing Xianhai Shaoyu was at his limit.","“You must be dumb to challenge me to a battle of attrition in that state. The earlier backlash from the formation must have eroded your intelligence,” Zhao Cangjing sneered.","Xianhai Shaoyu smiled too, but it was in self-deprecation. His body suddenly tilted sideways, and he collapsed to the ground.","Just then, a pair of gentle hands supported him. It was his little sister, Little Fishy.","“I’m sorry. I was useless. I brought shame to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan yet again,” Xianhai Shaoyu murmured.","“Don’t worry. I’ll clean up after you,” Little Fishy said as she moved Xianhai Shaoyu to the side.","Then, she whipped out a God Armament sword and pointed it at Zhao Cangjing. “I’ll be your opponent.”"]},{"number":6338,"title":"Chapter 6338: Chapter 6336: The Victor Has Been Decided","paragraphs":["Chapter 6336: The Victor Has Been Decided","Little Fishy vanished and reappeared before Zhao Cangjing. Her cultivation had risen to rank seven True God level as well.","She whipped out her sword and thrust it straight toward Zhao Cangjing’s chest. This blade wasn’t intended to take his life, but it would still inflict severe injuries on him.","Zhao Cangjing sensed the sharpness and decisiveness of Little Fishy’s attack. He could tell from this stab that she was more formidable than Xianhai Shaoyu. Not daring to get careless, he retreated while raising his God Armament spear to deflect the attack.","But Little Fishy’s sword changed its trajectory in response to Zhao Cangjing’s movement. The thrust transformed into a sweep aimed at his arm.","Zhao Cangjing did his best to avoid her, but blood still splattered. Looking at his bloodied arm, which had a cut so deep that it exposed his bone, killing intent flared in his eyes.","Shoosh!","A loud whooshing sound echoed before he could make a move. Little Fishy’s sword was once again rushing toward his chest.","Zhao Cangjing attempted to avoid the blade this time, but Little Fishy was faster than him.","“Damn it!” Zhao Cangjing cursed.","A golden light emerged from his body and formed a protective barrier around him, reminiscent of armor. He had decided to use his martial skill first.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen knew that martial skill—it was a rank three God Taboo Martial Skill that specialized in defense. It boasted even greater defensive prowess than the Immortal Dragon Spearmanship he had used when fighting against Xianhai Shaoyu.","His choice of martial skill showed that he was taking this duel seriously, but it also showed that he was frightened.","What happened next shocked everyone except for Little Fishy’s family members.","Zhao Cangjing stopped evading after activating his defensive martial skill. He was confident of blocking Little Fishy’s attack. But blood began flowing from his chest.","Little Fishy’s sword had pierced through his prided martial skill and stabbed into his chest.","“You...” Zhao Cangjing looked at Little Fishy’s God Armament sword and swiftly figured out the reason behind this anomaly.","She had concentrated a powerful offensive martial skill on her sword, and it was impeccably executed to conceal all traces, retaining only its might. He wouldn’t have known without taking a closer look.","“You have lost!” Little Fishy said as she pulled her sword out from Zhao Cangjing’s chest.","Zhao Daobin closed his eyes and sighed, knowing his grandson had been defeated.","Anyone with common sense could tell that Little Fishy could have claimed Zhao Cangjing’s life there and then. All she needed to do was to unleash the power of the martial skill imbued in her sword, and Zhao Cangjing’s soul would be shattered.","From the moment the sword pierced his body, she was already the victor.","But as Little Fishy turned around to return to Xianhai Shaoyu’s side, Zhao Cangjing suddenly shouted, “It’s not over yet. Where are you going?”","She turned around and saw Zhao Cangjing enveloped in a golden aura reminiscent of an inferno. His fighting prowess grew considerably.","That was the means he had intended to use against Chu Feng, but Zhao Tingxue stopped him.","“That d-d-dog thing! Is he being a sore loser?” Wang Qiang cursed.","He turned to Eighth Zhao as if asking the latter if he was going to intervene.","“His action lacks honor, but that lass backed away before Zhao Cangjing surrendered.”","Wang Qiang knew from those words that Eighth Zhao wasn’t planning to intervene. He spat, “S-s-screw them. They are all the s-s-same!”","Eighth Zhao was unfazed. He looked at Little Fishy with interest, commenting, “That lass is formidable. It’s a pity she’s too weak, or else Zhao Cangjing would have been no match for her even if he uses our clan’s Immortal Feather Cloak.”","The other Zhao Immortal Clansmen also realized that Little Fishy was a formidable opponent. Otherwise, Zhao Cangjing wouldn’t have been forced to use Immortal Feather Cloak. That was their Zhao Immortal Clan’s strongest bloodline power, and very few clansmen could pull it off.","Shoosh!","Zhao Cangjing made the first move. He copied Little Fishy’s trick and imbued his God Armament spear with a martial skill, greatly amplifying its destructive prowess. He also wrapped his body in the martial skill.","Little Fishy calmly fought back with her God Armament sword.","The spear clashed with the sword. Sparks flew. Shockwaves rippled.","This time, Little Fishy no longer had the overwhelming superiority.","The Immortal Feather Cloak didn’t raise Zhao Cangjing’s cultivation, but it greatly boosted his speed and strength. Little Fishy’s previous advantage against him became non-existent.","Wang Qiang could tell through his sharp eyes that Little Fishy’s defeat was inevitable. It was not because Little Fishy was weak but because she was simply too frail.","He knew that he would suffer the same fate too even if he intervened. He couldn’t defeat Zhao Cangjing in his current state.","This prompted him to turn his gaze to Chu Feng, but what he saw only pained his heart.","Chu Feng’s condition was nowhere better than Xianhai Shaoyu; his face was as pale as a sheet of paper. He was much skinnier than he was before he entered the formation.","If Chu Feng didn’t regain consciousness soon, Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Qin Xuan would be in deep trouble. Their defeat wasn’t a big deal, but handing over the formation power would surely greatly damage their bodies.","But Wang Qiang was not hoping for Chu Feng to regain consciousness. Rather, he hoped the formation would take longer, till Little Fishy lost.","Chu Feng was bound to be in a worse state after activating the formation. To defeat Zhao Cangjing with such a frail body, he would likely have to use a means that would sacrifice his future growth.","As Wang Qiang expected, Little Fishy was so weak that she was soon overwhelmed.","Right as Zhao Cangjing was about to hurt Little Fishy, a powerful voice reminiscent of a divine edict boomed, “Don’t go too far!”","It was Eighth Zhao!","Zhao Cangjing was about to stab Little Fishy’s chest to avenge his earlier humiliation, but he had no choice but to hold back after hearing the clan chief’s order.","“I have lost.”","Little Fishy dispelled her bloodline power, causing her cultivation to revert to rank three True God level. She had already reached her limit, and it would be pointless to continue dragging it out.","Zhao Cangjing’s action might have been dishonorable, but Little Fishy had to concede that she had gotten careless by not forcing him to admit defeat. Thus, she didn’t bother arguing her case and instead admitted defeat.","The present-era cultivators fell into despair.","To them, Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu were prodigies who could represent them. Their defeat spelled a loss not just for them but for all present-era cultivators."]},{"number":6339,"title":"Chapter 6339: Chapter 6337: Challenging All of Them","paragraphs":["Chapter 6337: Challenging All of Them","Before Chu Feng’s emergence, Xianhai Shaoyu had occupied the title of the strongest prodigy in the present era. And Little Fishy’s talent was rumored to have surpassed her brother’s.","The two of them were worthy of being the representatives of the present era juniors.","Yet, they had fallen in defeat today.","“What about Chu Feng? Why isn’t he doing anything? Isn’t he here too?” a voice in the crowd suddenly echoed. It was a questioning tone as if interrogating a criminal.","The other present-era cultivators also began voicing out.","“That’s right! Where’s Chu Feng? Isn’t he the strongest present-era junior?”","“He made a huge splash in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith and opposed even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He should be here too. He just saved Qin Xuan not long ago and massacred one of our present era’s sects!”","“The Ancient Era’s cultivators are oppressing us now, yet he is nowhere to be found despite being a present-era cultivator. He is only fearless when before us, present-era cultivators, but he hides like a tortoise when it comes to the Ancient Era cultivators.”","“Pui! He’s not worthy of being our present era’s strongest prodigy! No wonder the Ancient Era’s cultivators look down on us so much!”","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and the others were infuriated to hear those words.","“What nonsense are you spouting?” Little Fishy glared at the crowd, looking as if she would slaughter them all.","“Is there anything wrong with what we said? Chu Feng acts mighty before us present-era cultivators as if nothing can scare him, so why is he hiding before Ancient Era cultivators here? He only dares to act tough on his home turf.”","The crowd was no longer afraid of Little Fishy, knowing they would likely die here. What was there to fear when their fates were already sealed?","“You’re courting death!”","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu stepped forth to teach those slanderers a lesson.","Boom!","But their attacks were neutralized before they could land. The elders of those present-era juniors had intervened.","“You’re venting on fellow present-era cultivators after losing to Ancient Era prodigies. I guess that’s all there is to Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen,” one of the present-era elders scoffed.","They would never have dared to speak to Little Fishy like that in the past, but their true colors were showing now that their fates were sealed.","Uwa!","Cries of agony ensued. The elders who had stopped Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s earlier attacks collapsed to the ground, having sustained severe injuries.","Zhao Daobin had stepped in!","“They are esteemed guests of our Zhao Immortal Clan. How dare you make a move on them?” Zhao Daobin roared.","The faces of the present-era cultivators turned pale. They belatedly realized that the Zhao Immortal Clan saw Xianhai Shaoyu and the others differently from the rest of them.","They had misread the situation. Now that the Zhao Immortal Clan had gotten involved, they immediately fell silent. They were the ones who only dared to act tough in their home turf.","Their attitudes maddened Zhao Daobin, so he continued, “You’re mere ants in the eyes of our Zhao Immortal Clan. We don’t need to negotiate with you to obtain your formation power. Why do you think we even bothered allowing you to challenge our prodigies?","“Let me tell you—it’s because of Chu Feng. We gave you this chance because he promised to do us a favor. If not for him, you wouldn’t have even been granted this opportunity!”","...","“This...”","The present-era cultivators exchanged looks. Those who had insulted Chu Feng looked ashamed of themselves.","A brilliant radiance suddenly shone from the hall where Chu Feng and the others were. The light dissipated, and Zhao Zhuyin and Chu Feng stepped out.","“Chu Feng, how are you feeling?” Zhao Zhuyin quickly supported Chu Feng.","Her face was glowing red, and she looked full of energy. She was even radiating a faint light. She must have benefited a lot from the formation.","In contrast, Chu Feng was emaciated, and his skin was extremely dry as if someone had sucked the moisture out of his body. It would have been tough to recognize him without taking a close look.","“I’m fine.” Chu Feng pushed aside Zhao Zhuyin. He turned to Eighth Zhao and asked, “Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, how’s the formation I activated?”","“It’s perfect. Young friend Chu Feng, you live up to your reputation,” Eighth Zhao complimented. He meant those words from the bottom of his heart, and his glowing eyes were proof of that.","“I told you my formation energy is enough. You don’t need those people,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, you don’t need to stand up for them. They aren’t worthy,” Zhao Zhuyin said.","Despite being occupied with the activation of the formation, they could still sense what was happening outside. Naturally, they also heard the present-era cultivators slandering Chu Feng.","“Young friend Chu Feng, the rules are the rules, but I can make an exception on your account. You can freely pick any prodigy present to challenge, regardless of their cultivation. If you defeat them, you can take one person away with you.”","Eighth Zhao was doing Chu Feng a favor. He thought the people whom Chu Feng was concerned about were just Qin Xuan, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Little Fishy.","Chu Feng was so strong that it was questionable if the Zhao Immortal Clan’s juniors could threaten him despite his weakened state, so he decided to let Chu Feng pick any opponent he wanted. That was as good as letting the three of them go.","“You said it yourself.”","Chu Feng flew above the square.","“Who’s that?”","No one recognized the emaciated man who had suddenly appeared out of nowhere, though Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and even the wounded Qin Xuan flew to his side right away.","“Chu Feng.”","“Big brother.”","The three of them supported Chu Feng. They could sense his frailness and were worried.","“Chu Feng? Is that Chu Feng?”","“Why is he in that state?”","The crowd was baffled.","“He’s in this state because he’s vying for a chance with you. We could have stayed out of this battle, but your performance was too disappointing. The ones who disgraced the present-era cultivators are you!” Qin Xuan spat.","The crowd lowered their heads in shame.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu paid no heed to the crowd. They were only concerned about Chu Feng’s safety.","“I’m fine.” Chu Feng flashed a radiant smile at Little Fishy despite his emaciated state.","He turned to Zhao Daobin and said, “I, Chu Feng from the present era, would like to challenge the Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies.”","Zhao Daobin had received orders from Eighth Zhao, so he asked, “Young hero Chu Feng, who do you want to challenge? Feel free to choose anyone.”","“I’ll challenge everyone,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6340,"title":"Chapter 6340: Chapter 6338: As a Cultivator","paragraphs":["Chapter 6338: As a Cultivator","“You want to challenge all of them?”","Jaws dropped when the crowd heard Chu Feng’s words.","Even Little Fishy had fallen to Zhao Cangjing. Chu Feng was strong, but he was struggling to keep his balance now. Yet, he wanted to challenge all of the Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies?","Everyone thought he was out of his mind.","“Young hero Chu Feng, you don’t have to do this. I know our clan chief has altered the rules, allowing you to take a person away for each clansman you defeat, but are these people worth you going this far?” Zhao Daobin advised.","The crowd widened their eyes in realization. The present-era cultivators, in particular, looked at Chu Feng with eyes filled with reverence.","“That Chu Feng is an interesting one.”","On the Ancient Era’s spectator stand, there were two women, one old and one young, who stood out because they kept their distance from the other Ancient Era’s powers. Both of them commanded an air of nobility despite the sharp difference in their ages.","But youth usually conferred an advantage in the appeal factor. The young woman had pink eyes, and her irises resembled a flower petal. She was beautiful.","The one who had just evaluated Chu Feng was the older woman.","“Canhua, what are your thoughts about Chu Feng? He should be one of the few juniors in the current era who can rival you,” the old woman asked the young woman.","“He doesn’t look like a wise man. As for his strength, that waits to be seen,” the young woman said. He’s playing the hero","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and the others backed away upon seeing Chu Feng’s determination to take the battle. The only ones left in the massive square were Chu Feng and thousands of Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies.","They stood opposite each other.","“Chu Feng, are you trying to play the hero? I won’t go easy on you just because you’re in a weakened state.” Zhao Cangjing glared at Chu Feng. He had been harboring a grudge against Chu Feng, and this was his chance to return the favor.","“I’ll defeat all the prodigies in the Zhao Immortal Clan, and you... can’t stop me,” Chu Feng said.","“Very well. Give it a try.”","Zhao Cangjing whipped out his God Armament spear once more. He was much more excited facing off with Chu Feng than with Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy despite Chu Feng’s terrible state.","Chu Feng conjured a formation sword and gripped it tightly. Spirit power flowed from his body, calming his disturbed aura, though his face remained pale and his body remained emaciated.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng suddenly vanished.","“AH!”","A scream ensued.","Chu Feng had charged into the ranks of the Zhao Immortal Clansmen and knocked out a prodigy.","He knocked out two more prodigies before the crowd realized what was going on. He didn’t severely injure them, but his sword was imbued with a formation that temporarily incapacitated them.","“Hmph!”","Zhao Cangjing charged at Chu Feng with his God Armament spear.","But Chu Feng was faster. Each time Zhao Cangjing was about to reach him, he would abruptly vanish and take down several more Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","It dawned on Zhao Cangjing that the spirit power enveloping Chu Feng’s body didn’t just calm his aura; it also raised his movement speed.","In the blink of an eye, Chu Feng had already taken down fifty Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","The stronger Zhao Immortal Clansmen were already cooperating to encircle Chu Feng, but it was to no avail. The weaker clansmen were terrified. They were worried that they would be the next one to fall under Chu Feng’s sword.","“His spirit power seems to only be at rank three True Dragon.” The young woman named Canhua looked to the old woman beside her for answers.","“He’s indeed at rank three True Dragon, but his fighting prowess is on par with stronger rank seven True Dragon World Spiritists. Above all, he’s running circles around the Zhao Immortal Clansmen. He has the guts to do this on the Zhao Immortal Clan’s turf. I like him.”","The old woman couldn’t conceal her astonishment as she spoke.","“Chu Feng, don’t you underestimate me!” Zhao Cangjing roared.","Golden flames blazed from him as he unleashed his Immortal Feather Cloak Golden once more. His speed grew several-fold, and he finally caught up with Chu Feng.","Without hesitation, he thrust his spear into Chu Feng’s body while the latter was busy slashing down the other Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","As soon as his spear plunged into Chu Feng’s flesh, he realized something was amiss. He felt like he was stabbing a formation rather than human flesh. Furthermore, the lack of blood oozing from Chu Feng’s body confirmed his unease.","Chu Feng’s body trembled before abruptly multiplying into hundreds of Chu Fengs, which immediately charged into the ranks of the nearby Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","“Damn it!” Zhao Cangjing gnashed his teeth and shouted, “Construct the Spiritist Sealing Immortal Formation!”","He formed a hand seal, and a surge of bloodline power gushed into the sky.","The other Zhao Immortal Clansmen followed suit. Even those who had been incapacitated formed the hand seal and unleashed a surge of bloodline power too.","“Haaa!”","The spectating Zhao Immortal Clansmen looked conflicted. Zhao Daobin even sighed.","The purpose of the formation was to restrain world spiritists, whereas the battle between Chu Feng and the Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies was a friendly duel. It wasn’t appropriate for them to use this formation. Such an action would bring dishonor to them even if they won the battle.","The Spiritist Sealing Immortal Formation swiftly enveloped the square.","Bam!","Bam!","Bam!","...","The hundreds of Chu Feng on the square exploded into spirit power. The Chu Fengs on the square were all formation entities.","The spirit power flowed toward where Chu Feng stood against the Zhao Immortal Clansmen at the start of the battle. The real Chu Feng had been standing there all along, not taking a single step.","The realization that he had been frantically chasing after a formation like a fool made Zhao Cangjing was infuriated that he wanted to rip Chu Feng into shreds.","“Take him down!” Zhao Cangjing roared.","He chose to leave the final blow to the weaker clansmen to emphasize his superiority over Chu Feng.","Four Zhao Immortal Clansmen, three men and a woman, raised their cultivation level to rank six True God and charged at Chu Feng.","Gah!","Miserable cries followed.","All four Zhao Immortal Clansmen had collapsed at Chu Feng’s feet.","He was no longer holding a formation sword as if his spirit power had been sealed off, but his body was enveloped in blinding lightning.","He had activated the Lightning Mark, the Lightning Armor, and the Lightning Wings, but there was another power resembling flames that the crowd was unfamiliar with. With these four powers, he raised his cultivation from rank three True God level to rank seven True God level.","“Lightning Aura!” Canhua blurted out.","The crowd widened their eyes in astonishment.","“Lightning Aura? Isn’t that the legendary power of the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline?”","Zhao Cangjing’s complexion darkened. He thought that victory would be theirs once they suppressed Chu Feng’s spirit power, but who could have thought that he would be such a strong cultivator too?","“You can remove your formation,” Chu Feng suddenly said.","“Ah?” The crowd was dumbstruck.","“Your formation is intended to restrain world spiritists, right? It doesn’t work on me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Stop finding excuses. Why would your formation dissipate if it doesn’t work on you? All world spiritists are powerless before our clan’s Spiritist Sealing Immortal Formation!” Zhao Cangjing retorted.","“Is that so?” Chu Feng laughed.","He conjured another formation sword that looked identical to the one he had before.","Even Zhao Daobin and the others felt incredulous, let alone Zhao Cangjing. Was Chu Feng capable of overcoming their formation’s restraint?","Chu Feng pointed his formation sword at Zhao Cangjing. “I merely chose to defeat you as a fellow cultivator.”"]},{"number":6341,"title":"Chapter 6341: Chapter 6339: Had it Coming","paragraphs":["Chapter 6339: Had it Coming","“That’ll depend on how capable you are,” Zhao Cangjing said as he unleashed his oppressive might, enveloping the square.","But his oppressive might was as good as non-existent before Chu Feng.","Chu Feng whipped out his God Armament sword, the Frenzy Tsunami Saber, and stepped forward with the disposition of a flood dragon emerging from the sea. He charged at the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, completely unfazed by the oppressive might.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen were horrified. Somehow, Chu Feng felt much more terrifying to them now than when he was fighting with his spirit power earlier.","“Retreat now!” Zhao Cangjing roared as he stepped in front of the Zhao Immortal Clansmen.","His God Armament spear glowed golden as he flung it in a sweeping motion, unleashing a golden beam of light. The golden beam first struck the ground before abruptly rising to form a towering wall between them.","“Divine Might!” Chu Feng bellowed.","The surrounding space tore as powerful oppressive might descended from the sky and crushed Zhao Cangjing’s towering martial power wall, leaving countless cracks on it.","Chu Feng raised his Frenzied Tsunami Saber and swung it toward the martial power wall.","Boom!","The clash induced powerful shockwaves that shook the world. The martial power wall shattered in a single strike.","Without hesitation, Zhao Cangjing lifted his spear and thrust it toward Chu Feng’s neck.","But Chu Feng easily dodged it with a sidestep before flitting past Zhao Cangjing to take down the Zhao Immortal Clansmen behind him.","Zhao Cangjing tried to pursue him, only to find he couldn’t catch up.","“That martial skill!” Zhao Cangjing widened his eyes in disbelief.","Chu Feng shouldn’t have been able to avoid him that easily. He was only able to do so because Divine Might had suppressed his fighting prowess.","Immortal Feather Cloak was already Zhao Cangjing’s strongest skill. There was nothing else he could resort to if even he still couldn’t rival Chu Feng after activating Immortal Feather Cloak. He couldn’t only watch helplessly as the Zhao Immortal Clansmen collapsed one after another.","In the blink of an eye, all the Zhao Immortal Clansmen except for Zhao Cangjing had collapsed.","“I have said that you can’t stop me.” Chu Feng finally turned his attention toward Zhao Cangjing. His eyes were filled with disdain.","Zhao Cangjing clenched his jaws. His eyes were overflowing with killing intent. He knew that Chu Feng was doing this to humiliate him/","AHHHH!","Zhao Cangjing roared like a ferocious beast. An even more intense golden flame gushed from his body. He wasn’t planning to give up.","Chu Feng remained fearless. He was confident of defeating Zhao Cangjing.","But right as he was about to make his move and end this battle, Zhao Cangjing suddenly collapsed to the floor. His golden flame dissipated, and his bloodline power receded, causing his cultivation to revert to its original level.","Zhao Cangjing continued glaring at Chu Feng with widened eyes, but the truth was that he had lost consciousness. Fresh blood flowed from his mouth and nose, and his aura quickly declined.","He had reached his limit, and this was the hefty price he had to pay for invoking Immortal Feather Cloak.","Seconds later, the lightning around Chu Feng dissipated, and he reverted to his feeble state. Unable to keep his balance, he could only watch helplessly as his body fell forward.","But four people caught him before he crashed into the ground—Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Wang Qiang, and Qin Xuan.","At the same time, Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather appeared behind them too.","A huge uproar erupted. The present-era cultivators, including those who had insulted Chu Feng earlier, were all now cheering for him. His name reverberated across the realm.","They felt excited and relieved as if they had been granted a new life. They were aware of the new rule set by the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief—Chu Feng could save a person for each Zhao Immortal Clansman he defeated.","They could all be saved.","While the crowd was exultantly chanting Chu Feng’s name, Chu Feng slowly raised his head and looked at the present-era cultivators. “Why are they so excited?”","“W-w-why else? They’re happy because y-y-you saved them,” Wang Qiang replied.","“Saved them? When did I say I’m going to save them?” Chu Feng asked.","“Ah?”","Chu Feng’s words stumped everyone.","Zhao Daobin asked, “Young hero Chu Feng, are you not planning to take those people away?”","“I don’t plan to take away anyone other than those around me,” Chu Feng replied.","The present-era cultivators looked as if they had been struck by a bolt of lightning. Their excitement vanished, replaced by fluster.","“We’re sorry, young hero Chu Feng. We should never have said those words. But we are just too weak and have no choice but to entrust our hopes to you. You can punish us however you like, but please take us away with you. We’re begging you!”","Those who insulted Chu Feng earlier tried to explain their actions. Many of them tearfully apologized with an earnest attitude.","“Why should my brother save y-y-you just because you’re weak?” Wang Qiang scoffed.","“Indeed! Young hero Chu Feng isn’t obliged to save us. We couldn’t even have challenged the Zhao Immortal Clan’s juniors if not for him. He wanted to save us, but you repaid gratitude with enmity and insulted him. You have no right to ask him to save you!”","Many cultivators spoke up against those who had insulted Chu Feng. Those were the ones who didn’t speak badly about Chu Feng from the start to the end.","“Do you think you have the right to ask me to save you then?” Chu Feng sneered.","“Young hero Chu Feng, we didn’t insult you earlier. We respect you from the bottom of our hearts. We were moved when we heard you paid a hefty price so that we could have a chance to challenge the Zhao Immortal Clan’s juniors. Please take us away with you! We don’t want to die in the hands of the Ancient Era’s races. We’re willing to serve you!”","Those people looked at Chu Feng with pitiful eyes.","“You might not have insulted me, but you didn’t speak up for me either. You don’t owe me, but neither do I owe you. I challenged the Zhao Immortal Clan’s juniors because I am a present-era cultivator; it has nothing to do with you. If you want to leave this place, do it with your strength.”","Chu Feng turned to Little Fishy and said, “Yu’er, let’s go.”","Their group vanished from the square. The Zhao Immortal Clan didn’t stop them.","The faces of present-era cultivators left behind paled in despair.","Someone tried to follow Chu Feng out of here.","Boom!","As soon as he rose into the air, he exploded into a bloody fog. He didn’t even have the chance to shout.","Zhao Daobin’s silent stare made his stance clear. Anyone else who tried to escape would meet with the same fate.","The present-era cultivators looked pitiful, but no one present had sympathy for them. These people had it coming."]},{"number":6342,"title":"Chapter 6342: Chapter 6340: It’s Not a Lie; It’s the Truth","paragraphs":["Chapter 6340: It’s Not a Lie; It’s the Truth","“Chu Feng!”","“Big brother!”","In the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain, Wang Qiang and the others looked at Chu Feng with worried eyes. Little Fishy even teared up.","Chu Feng was even feebler than before. It felt like he was on the verge of death. None of the pills they fed him were working.","“Should we leave this place first?” Little Fishy’s mother proposed.","While the Zhao Immortal Clan didn’t stop them from leaving this place, she was worried they would renege on their promise.","“S-stay here,” Chu Feng mustered the final sliver of his strength to say these words before passing out.","“What should we do?” Little Fishy’s mother was at a loss.","She could usually call the shots as the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief’s wife, but she dared not arbitrarily decide on Chu Feng’s behalf. Thus, she turned to her daughter instead.","“Let’s heed his words,” Little Fishy said.","“We shouldn’t let Chu Feng’s effort go to waste, but we should find somewhere safe,” Little Fishy’s father said. He took Chu Feng and the others as far away from the Zhao Immortal Clan’s base as possible","Next, they just had to wait for the Fortuitous Sun to rise to the top of the sky before leaving this land.","Meanwhile, the Zhao Immortal Clan was also waiting for the Fortuitous Sun to rise.","Piercing screams that sounded more wretched than pigs in an abattoir echoed on the massive square of their floating warship, but it was coming from cultivators—the present-era cultivators. The Zhao Immortal Clansmen were extracting the formation energy inside their bodies.","They would have been lucky if their mouths only frothed up and their eyes rolled upward; those with weaker constitutions had already breathed their last.","But their formation energy didn’t go to Zhao Zhuyin.","Chu Feng had single-handedly fulfilled her breakthrough requirement. She already had enough formation energy in her.","Furthermore, Chu Feng’s formation energy was unique. Eighth Zhao was worried that the formation energy’s special traits would be altered if Zhao Zhuyin assimilated other formation energies too, so he decided against it.","Eighth Zhao was only taking their formation energies to punish them.","In contrast to the present-era cultivators’ tragic plight, the Ancient Era cultivators excitedly waited for the Fortuitous Sun to rise, having collected a huge amount of formation energies themselves.","Zhao Zhuyin stood at the peak of the unique palace. The Zhao Immortal Clansmen looked at her with nervous eyes, though they also kept their distance from her.","“Don’t worry, Zhuyin. You can do it.” Eighth Zhao rooted for Zhao Zhuyin from afar.","Zhao Zhuyin smiled in response, though it looked incredibly unnatural due to her extreme nervousness. She was worried about failure.","Her father was taking a gamble on her by activating the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain for her, and he had made thorough preparations for her sake. If she still failed despite that, she would be letting down her father and her clan.","She couldn’t shoulder responsibility for that.","The Fortuitous Sun finally rose to the top of the sky. A brilliant light enveloped the world.","The weaker ones couldn’t open their eyes. Even Heavenly Gods like Eighth Zhao found their sight severely limited. It was a good thing Eighth Zhao was close enough to keep an eye on his daughter’s condition.","“It’s a success! I knew Zhuyin would succeed. She’s the person our Zhao Immortal Clan is waiting for.” Eighth Zhao was overjoyed when he saw Zhao Zhuyin’s formation energy leaking out under the Fortuitous Sun’s brilliance.","Soon, he turned his attention to the spectator stand.","Many Ancient Era cultivators had assimilated their formation energies too, but Eighth Zhao’s eyes were focused on the woman named Canhua. She had induced a massive phenomenon that no one except for Zhao Zhuyin could compete with.","But Zhao Zhuyin only induced such a phenomenon thanks to their meticulous preparation, whereas that woman did it with her ability.","“Tianjian Canhua—she lives up to her reputation.” Eighth Zhao was awed by that woman’s talent, but he didn’t envy her. Instead, he looked at his daughter with a wide smile.","The fact that such a prodigy had lost to his daughter showed his hard work hadn’t been in vain.","Hu!","A strange whirlwind suddenly swept across the realm, blowing the brilliant light away. The Fortuitous Sun continued to glow brightly, and its effects on the cultivators didn’t lessen, but its brilliance was no longer as blinding as before.","The crowd slowly regained their vision, allowing them to see the rays of the Fortuitous Sun.","Those who had absorbed the formation energies were shrouded in the Fortuitous Sun’s light rays. The stronger the formation energy, the more intense the light ray.","However, the strongest light ray was not focused on Zhao Zhuyin. Instead, it was cast at a location far from where they were.","Eighth Zhao and the others were stunned. The crowd turned to Eighth Zhao for answers. In particular, Zhao Zhuyin thought she would receive the brightest light from the Fortuitous Sun, and she couldn’t believe that someone had received an even brighter light ray than her.","“Could it be Chu Feng?” someone murmured.","He was the only one capable of pulling that off. Furthermore, after taking a closer look, they realized there were several bright light rays cast in that location other than the brightest one. While these light rays weren’t as bright as Zhao Zhuyin’s, they were also not to be made light of.","This naturally reminded the crowd about Chu Feng’s friends.","“Stay here,” Eighth Zhao ordered before heading toward the brightest light ray.","It didn’t take him long to reach his destination. Unsurprisingly, it was Chu Feng’s group. Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Qin Xuan were basked in light rays, but the brightest one was on Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had made a full recovery, even though not much time had passed. That brightest light ray must have healed him.","Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather eyed Eighth Zhao vigilantly, ready to make a move if the latter attempted something. Even Little Fishy, Qin Xuan, and the others tensed up.","They had been worried about Chu Feng too, and it was only when the Fortuitous Sun reached the top of the sky that they finally understood why he didn’t want to leave. It turned out he would benefit from the Fortuitous Sun too, and his benefit was the greatest of them all.","They panicked when the blinding light dissipated. They tried everything they could to conceal Chu Feng’s blinding light, fearing that the Zhao Immortal Clan would come after them, but it was to no avail.","In the end, what they feared the most still happened.","In contrast to them, Chu Feng was calm. “You’re here?”","“Young friend Chu Feng, can you answer my doubts?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Ask whatever you want.”","“Didn’t you lose your formation energy? How are you benefiting from the Fortuitous Sun?”","“Didn’t I tell your daughter that I’m helping myself by helping her?” Chu Feng answered.","Eighth Zhao widened his eyes. “That... I thought you made that up to convince her.”","Chu Feng had indeed said those words to Zhao Zhuyin, but Eighth Zhao shrugged that off as a white lie. It was unthinkable for Chu Feng to benefit from the Fortuitous Sun after giving up his formation energy to Zhao Zhuyin?","But it was clear now that Chu Feng meant his words."]},{"number":6343,"title":"Chapter 6343: Chapter 6341: About Your Grandmother","paragraphs":["Chapter 6341: About Your Grandmother","Chu Feng noticed Eighth Zhao’s look of disbelief and continued, “It’s normal that you find it incomprehensible. Your understanding of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain doesn’t go deep enough.”","“You’re saying our Zhao Immortal Clan doesn’t understand the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain? This place belongs to us!” Eighth Zhao exclaimed.","“You mentioned that the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain’s trial consists of two layers: the first layer allows one to grasp the formation energy, and the second layer allows one to siphon other people’s formation energy. However, there’s a third layer here.”","Eighth Zhao was astonished. “Third layer?”","“Yes, the third layer is first to take in the formation energy, then expend it. Only when one’s condition is pushed to the limit can one obtain the greatest possible energy from the Fortuitous Sun,” Chu Feng replied.","“...” Eighth Zhao frowned.","He struggled to accept this theory, but neither could he refute it, as it had already happened to Chu Feng.","“So, you’re saying you grasped the third layer and intentionally gave away your formation energy? You insisted on challenging our Zhao Immortal Clan’s prodigies despite being frail from helping Zhuyin activate her formation to push yourself to the limit?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Yes, but that’s the easy part. The hardest part is depleting the formation energy. It’s fortunate you have made ample preparation to help Zhao Zhuyin achieve the second layer,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“In other words, our preparations ended up benefiting you,” Eighth Zhao said.","Chu Feng didn’t answer the question. Instead, he asked with a smile, “Elder, why do you think there’s a second layer to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain?”","Eighth Zhao narrowed his eyes. He had an ominous feeling, especially when he saw the sly look on Chu Feng’s face, but he couldn’t resist his curiosity. Thus, he asked, “Those who have grasped the second layer are there to serve those who have grasped the third layer?”","“That’s how you choose to understand it,” Chu Feng smiled.","Regardless of whether it was spoken aloud or not, they knew deep down that Eighth Zhao’s words were the truth.","“Hahahaha!” Eighth Zhao suddenly burst into laughter. “Young friend Chu Feng, I have underestimated you.”","With that, he turned around and left.","“He’s leaving just like that?” Qin Xuan asked.","He had been scared out of his wits, especially when Chu Feng confessed the truth. He was worried that the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief would go on a rampage in a fit of rage.","Chu Feng shared the same worry as well, though he wasn’t afraid of Eighth Zhao as he had the Divine Deer to fall back on. His earlier words were a test, and they would determine how he treated the Zhao Immortal Clan in the future.","The Fortuitous Sun didn’t remain in the sky for too long. By the time the Fortuitous Sun dissipated, Chu Feng’s face was glowing red.","“How is it? Have you recovered your bloodline?” Eggy asked anxiously.","Chu Feng had previously gone all out against the God Clan to rescue Little Fishy, and that impaired his bloodline. While it might be too optimistic to think that the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain could help him achieve a full recovery, it would still be good if he could recover some.","“The Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain is formidable. If it had been at its peak, I might have made a full recovery. I can sense a change in my bloodline, even with the little energy it has remaining. I should be able to use my bloodline skills once more if I spend some time recuperating using the Bloodline Soul Puppet’s method,” Chu Feng said.","“Really? This trip turned out to be fruitful!” Eggy was overjoyed.","Chu Feng’s bloodline skill was an exceptionally powerful skill that allowed him to transcend a major cultivation level. Were it not for that bloodline skill, he wouldn’t have been able to bring down the God Clan even with the Heavenly Lightning Nine Slashes.","He couldn’t use it now due to his bloodline impairment. Being able to use that bloodline skill once more meant that his bloodline had mostly recovered.","“How are you feeling, big brother?” Little Fishy flitted to Chu Feng’s side, grabbed his wrist, and began inspecting his condition.","Wang Qiang pounced up in shock and nervously looked at Little Fishy. “Hey hey! Let g-g-go right now! Are you out of your m-m-mind?!","Shocked, Little Fishy hurriedly released her grip. She thought that her actions had inadvertently injured Chu Feng.","“Aren’t you a b-b-bold one? Look at my brother’s r-r-red face! He’s obviously overnourished! How can a b-b-beautiful woman like you touch him at a time like this? Aren’t you worried about h-h-him claiming you as his on the spot?!” Wang Qiang shouted.","Xianhai Shaoyu and the others rolled their eyes.","Little Fishy blushed furiously. Despite her young age, she was not ignorant about those things.","“Scram!” She performed a roundhouse kick on Wang Qiang’s face, sending him flying out of her sight.","Wang Qiang’s mouth was crooked when he returned. “Bloody hell! Were you t-t-trying to kill me? C-c-can’t you take a joke?”","The crowd smiled at Wang Qiang’s grumble. He had already gotten off light for daring to crack such a joke to Little Fishy.","“I’ve benefited a fair bit. What about the rest of you?” Chu Feng asked.","“My bloodline was enhanced, and my fighting prowess went up,” Little Fishy said.","“Same for me, too,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“Not as much as you, but i-i-it’s still decent,” Wang Qiang replied with a smile. He was used to speaking casually to Chu Feng.","Just then, Chu Feng and the others simultaneously raised their heads to look at the horizon. Two figures were standing there. They were the old woman and the young woman from the square.","“Do you need something from us?” Chu Feng asked.","“I am Tianjian Canhua, and the elder beside me is Tianjian Jiumeng. We’re from the Heavensword Sacred Palace,” Tianjian Canhua said.","“Heavensword Sacred Palace?” Chu Feng narrowed his eyes.","This was not his first time hearing about that power.","While he was at the Nine Realms Immortal Region, he reunited with Zhang Yingxiong and met two powerful youths. One was Tuoba Tianxue, and the other was Tuoba Yijian. Later, he learned that they were from a powerful Ancient Era power—the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","“Do you remember Tuoba Yijian and Tuoba Tianxue?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","“Yes. They are from the Heavensword Sacred Palace, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“You know they are from the Heavensword Sacred Palace?” Tianjian Canhua was taken aback. “That makes things easier. They often mention you to me, and they are always full of praise for you. I thought they were exaggerating, but I see now they were being conservative with their opinion.”","“You’re flattering me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, I didn’t come here just to offer my greetings. I have something to tell you, and I believe it should be important to you,” Tianjian Canhua said.","“What is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s regarding your grandmother,” Tianjian Canhua replied."]},{"number":6344,"title":"Chapter 6344: Chapter 6342: Song Luoyi’s Whereabouts","paragraphs":["Chapter 6342: Song Luoyi’s Whereabouts","“My grandmother?”","Chu Feng already knew that his mother had entered the Ninth Galaxy. While Su Rou and Su Mei were being held hostage by the Moon Immortal, the latter was doing it because she had no other choice.","As for the Chu Heavenly Clansmen and his friends from the Ancestral Lower Galaxy who had disappeared, he had a gut feeling that they were safe.","His grandmother was the only one left in the world of cultivation whom he was worried about. Even though he knew that his grandmother was powerful, her mental state was worrying.","“May I talk to you in private?” Tianjian Canhua said.","They left the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain together and made their way onto a warship.","The warship was humongous, but there were only hundreds of people on its deck. These people were dressed in white, and they carried Heavensword Sacred Palace’s tokens on their waists. Their demeanor and aura relayed their strength.","“Paying respect to Miss Canhua.”","“Paying respect to Elder Jiumeng.”","But they still respectfully greeted Tianjian Canhua and Tianjian Jiumeng.","Tianjian Canhua led them deeper into the warship before eventually stopping in front of a palace’s entrance. She glanced at the people behind Chu Feng.","Chu Feng caught her drift and said, “I trust them.”","Hearing that, Tianjian Canhua opened the palace doors and ushered the group in. She sat down and said, “Your grandmother should still be alive.”","“How do you know?” Chu Feng remained vigilant.","He had been searching for his grandmother, but how would Tianjian Canhua know about this? Unless she had investigated him.","“Tuoba Tianxue and the others had a high opinion of you, so we conducted a background check. Your grandmother, Song Luoyi, was from the Golden Dragon Flame Sect. Her talent made her an eyesore to Jia Lingyi, who went on to obliterate the Golden Dragon Flame Sect.","“However, your grandmother is likely to be alive. The flames that destroyed the Pill Dao Immortal Sect resembled those of the Golden Dragon Flame Sect, just that they were far more potent. Furthermore, we recently found an old woman who wields means that resemble the flames that destroyed the Pill Dao Immortal Sect.”","Chu Feng anxiously asked, “Where is that old woman?”","Instead of answering right away, Tianjian Canhua asked, “You knew that your grandmother is still alive too?”","She took out a portrait and unfurled it. It depicted a disfigured old woman dressed gracefully. She was Chu Feng’s grandmother, Song Luoyi.","“Is she your grandmother?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","Chu Feng spent a moment in thought before nodding. It didn’t matter whether he admitted to it or not; the other party was already convinced she was his grandmother. Thus, he decided to go with it so that he could ask about her whereabouts.","“Where’s my grandmother?” Chu Feng asked.","“She’s in a hidden realm. We happen to be heading there too. Shall we travel together?” Tianjian Canhua suggested.","“All right,” Chu Feng said. He turned to Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather and asked, “Elders, why don’t you return with Yu’er and Brother Shaoyu first?”","Little Fishy interjected, “Big brother, I’ll go with you.”","“Young friend Chu Feng, I’d like to go too if I’m not a burden to you,” Little Fishy’s grandfather said.","“What are you saying, elder? You aren’t a burden. I’d be thankful to have you with me; I’m just worried that I’m imposing on you,” Chu Feng replied.","“You aren’t imposing on us. Our priority at hand is to protect you all, right?” Little Fishy’s grandfather asked.","Little Fishy’s parents nodded in agreement.","Chu Feng understood what they were getting at. While top-notch experts like Eighth Zhao were beyond their means to deal with, they were still Heavenly God level cultivators. If possible, they would still like to offer their aid to Chu Feng.","They were afraid of death, but they were willing to risk their lives to repay their debt to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng didn’t want to turn down their goodwill. Besides, the Divine Deer’s ability could only be used once before it had to be recharged. Ideally, it would still be best to have Heavenly God level cultivators to back him up.","Qin Xuan went up to Chu Feng and said, “Brother Chu Feng, I am grateful for your help at the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain. I hope you’ll be able to find Elder Song, but I shan’t accompany you for this trip.”","Chu Feng asked, “Brother Qin, what do you intend to do next?”","“I’ll continue searching for the culprit who destroyed the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect. Otherwise, I’ll enter the Ninth Galaxy and test the waters there,” Qin Xuan replied.","“That’s a good idea. I’m intending to head to the Ninth Galaxy soon, too,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re intending to head there too, Brother Chu Feng?” Qin Xuan was surprised.","Chu Feng told Qin Xuan about the news he had heard about the Ninth Galaxy.","Qin Xuan’s eyes lit up. He had been afraid of the Ninth Galaxy due to a lack of information; he only wanted to head there because the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect had been destroyed, and he didn’t have anywhere else to go.","It was only after hearing Chu Feng’s words that he realized that the Ninth Galaxy was filled with fortuitous encounters, where he could further his cultivation.","Chu Feng and the others bade Qin Xuan farewell.","“Farewell, Brother Chu, Brother Xianhai, Brother Wang Qiang, and Miss Yu’er.” Qin Xuan clasped his fist at them one by one before taking his leave.","“Is anyone else leaving?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","“That’s all,” Chu Feng replied.","Tianjian Canhua waved her sleeves.","The warship began to move, accelerating while emanating a bright light. Spirit power shrouded the warship, and it suddenly slipped into a teleportation passageway without going through a teleportation formation.","“What a formidable treasure!” Little Fishy and the others were awed.","They had seen treasures with similar abilities, but not one at the scale of this humongous warship.","Tianjian Canhua assigned a palace for each of Chu Feng’s group to rest in, but Chu Feng picked a palace with multiple rooms to share with the others. Tianjian Canhua hadn’t done anything suspicious yet, but he didn’t know her well enough to trust her. He thought it would be safer to stay together with Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy.","Tianjian Canhua understood his intention, so she respected his decision and didn’t attempt to dissuade others.","In the palace...”","“M-M-Miss Canhua, I have a question to ask. You m-m-mustn’t get angry,” Wang Qiang said.","“Don’t bother asking if you think it’ll anger me,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“All right. I’ll b-b-be asking the question now. Why are you called C-C-Canhua (Withered Flower) when you’re so beautiful? What an inauspicious name!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","Boom!","The palace suddenly turned piercingly cold.","Tianjian Jiumeng coldly uttered, “Watch your words.”","But Tianjian Canhua pointed at her eyes and said, “My name came from my mother.”","“Ahhh, I s-s-see.” Wang Qiang widened in realization when he saw the flower petal in Tianjian Canhua’s eyes. “I was b-b-brash.”","“It’s fine. Many people are curious about my name. Personally, I like it,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“It’s a good name. There’s a nice ring to it,” Little Fishy agreed.","“Miss, can you at least tell us which galaxy we’re heading to if it’s not convenient to reveal the exact location?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s close to the Ninth Galaxy,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“The Ninth Galaxy?” Chu Feng was surprised.","“You’ll know once you get there. It’s not a place anyone can enter, so your grandmother is an extraordinary person.” Tianjian Canhua stood up. “It’ll take some time to reach our destination, so rest well and inform our sectmembers if you require anything.”","Tianjian Canhua and Tianjian Jiumeng made their way to another palace.","Tianjian Jiumeng asked, “Canhua, are you sure you want to do this?”","“Mm.” Tianjian Canhua nodded.","Tianjian Jiumeng’s complexion turned grim."]},{"number":6345,"title":"Chapter 6345: Chapter 6343: The Hidden World That Mustn’t Be Entered","paragraphs":["Chapter 6343: The Hidden World That Mustn’t Be Entered","“Canhua, this matter has major implications. You should reconsider it,” Tianjian Jiumeng advised.","“I have thought things through before coming to this decision. You need not worry about it. Besides, don’t you have a high opinion of Chu Feng too?” Tianjian Canhua smiled. She was confident and composed as if everything was in her grasp.","Tianjian Jiumeng realized that Tianjian Canhua had already properly considered the matter, so she decided to speak no further.","...","Meanwhile, the phenomena at the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain vanished, and the realm collapsed. Everyone within the realm was transported out.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen left in advance. Gathered in its main warship were its elites.","“Why do all of you look so vexed?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","All the Zhao Immortal Clansmen, except for her father, Eighth Zhao, looked glum.","Zhao Zhuyin had enhanced her bloodline and advanced her cultivation by a rank. It was just frustrating that the greatest beneficiary of the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain wasn’t her, despite the huge amount of resources her clan had poured into it.","This was also the reason the crowd was frustrated.","“Lord Father, why don’t we capture Chu Feng since he has schemed against us? We can take his energy for ourselves,” Zhao Tingxue proposed.","Zhao Zhuyin frowned.","Before she could say a word, Eighth Zhao replied, “It’s a mutually beneficial relationship. There’s no scheme here.”","“But...”","Zhao Tingxue wanted to argue, but Eighth Zhao interjected, “Many people have entered the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain since the Ancient Era, but no one has deciphered the third layer. Yet, Chu Feng did it. Zhuyin’s second layer might have paved the way for his third layer, but she wouldn’t have benefited so much out of it if not for him. This deal was mutually beneficial.”","“Lord Clan Chief is right,” Zhao Daobin said.","The other elders nodded in agreement.","They were displeased because the Zhao Immortal Clan had gotten the shorter end of the stick, but Eighth Zhao was the one who called the shots here. Since he had already made his stance clear, it would be unwise to say too much now.","But there were always people who couldn’t read the situation, such as Zhao Daobin’s grandson, Zhao Cangjing.","“In my humble opinion, it’s all thanks to Lord Clan Chief’s meticulous planning that Miss Zhuyin succeeded in making a breakthrough. What has Chu Feng contributed here? He wouldn’t have had this opportunity if not for Lord Clan Chief opening the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain! Chu Feng has benefited too much from our resources. We shouldn’t have let him leave so easily,” Zhao Cangjing harrumphed.","“How do you know Chu Feng didn’t contribute? Even though he didn’t do as much as our clan did, he accomplished something that no one else could. That, in itself, makes him irreplaceable.”","Zhao Cangjing’s complexion turned pale. He realized that Eighth Zhao had an exceedingly high opinion of Chu Feng.","“Cangjing, you might be one of our Zhao Immortal Clan’s most outstanding juniors, and we’re counting on you to prop up our clan in the future, but you are too short-sighted. There are many benefits to befriending Chu Feng. On the contrary, if you make an enemy out of him, he could become the one who destroys our clan in the future,” Eighth Zhao continued.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen were taken aback, especially since they knew how powerful their clan chief was. Once again, it showed just how highly their clan chief thought of Chu Feng.","“Back when those lords first appeared in the Ancient Era, many people coveted their treasures and sought to suppress them with their powerful background. However, those people and their respective powers ultimately disappeared from the face of the world.","“You need to be more discerning. You can oppress and take advantage of others, but I won’t protect you if you mess with the wrong person. Do you understand me?” Eighth Zhao’s eyes turned cold as he said those words.","This was a warning.","“I understand,” Zhao Cangjing and everyone else in the hall replied.","Zhao Zhuyin looked at her father with a tinge of admiration.","She could tell that Zhao Cangjing harbored hatred for Chu Feng, but no Zhao Immortal Clansmen would dare make a move on Chu Feng after hearing those words.","Eighth Zhao issued several more instructions before concluding this meeting.","Soon, Eighth Zhao and Zhao Zhuyin were the only ones left in the hall.","“You’re still here. Do you need something from me?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Father, why don’t you go all out to support Chu Feng if you have such a high opinion of him?” Zhao Zhuyin asked.","“And what would an all-out support entail?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“If our clan befriends Chu Feng and backs him the way the Totem Dragon Clan and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan do, Chu Feng will repay the favor in the future. Our future will be secured,” Zhao Zhuyin said.","“What makes you so certain our Zhao Immortal Clan can defeat the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? Have you forgotten who took the lead in God’s Era?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“But that doesn’t mean Jie Tianran is stronger than you,” Zhao Zhuyin retorted.","“Have you considered what will happen to our clan if he is stronger than me?”","“I haven’t thought that far ahead.” Zhao Zhuyin’s voice became meeker as it struck her that she might have been taking her clan’s strength for granted. Like her clansmen, she looked down on all present-era powers, including the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Our Zhao Immortal Clan’s future can only be secured by you and not Chu Feng. We can’t entrust our fate in the hands of an outsider. I have a high opinion of Chu Feng, but our paths diverge.","“If he requests our help, we will help him if it’s within our means. Otherwise, we will candidly turn him down. If the rumors are true, he won’t harbor animosity against us for that.","“You should never gamble your future or our clan’s fate on an outsider. That isn’t befriending him but ingratiating yourself to him. Not to mention the outcome would be dire if you lose the bet,” Eighth Zhao said.","“I... should have thought deeper into it.” Zhao Zhuyin lowered her head, ashamed.","But Eighth Zhao didn’t berate her. “You haven’t been through much. I don’t blame you for lacking depth in your judgment. But Zhuyin, you are going to take my position as the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief in the future. You must prioritize our clan’s interest above all things. You would know what to do if you take that to mind,” Eighth Zhao said.","“I understand.” Zhao Zhuyin nodded.","...","Some time later, Chu Feng and the others emerged from the teleportation passageway and found themselves in the middle of space. There was a massive spatial tear ahead of them.","Passing through the spatial tear, they were still in vast space, but somehow, things felt different. It felt like they had entered somewhere new.","“H-h-holy! What is this place?”","Chu Feng and the others could tell that they were no longer in the world of cultivation, yet this place was as vast as the world of cultivation.","Not only did Wang Qiang blurt a vulgarity, but Little Fishy and the others were also stunned.","They had lived in the world of cultivation for a long time, but they had never heard about this place before, not even from their ancestral records.","Even Eggy stood up and widened her eyes. “Chu Feng, could this be the place that your big sister told you not to enter?”","Before they parted ways, Long Zhuoyan had warned Chu Feng about a hidden world located near the Ninth Galaxy. The hidden world was a humongous place comprising many other realms, but for some reason, she couldn’t see through it.","For that reason, she advised Chu Feng not to enter it."]},{"number":6346,"title":"Chapter 6346: Chapter 6344: The Heavenly Sacred Temples Origin","paragraphs":["Chapter 6344: The Heavenly Sacred Temple's Origin","Looking at the vast expanse of space in front of him, Chu Feng suddenly felt incredibly uneasy. Unlike the starry world of cultivation that embodied hope, this vast space felt desolate like death.","Deep in this space, a woman dressed in white was reading an ancient scroll in a tower.","She was Tianjian Qingyuan, a prodigious member of the Heavensword Sacred Palace descending from the Ancient Era. The present Heavensword Sacred Palace revered her as their ancestor. Given her background and strength, she deserved that level of respect.","But she couldn’t care less about that. She had no intention of intervening in the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s affairs, evident from how few people got to see her.","All of a sudden, she stood up and cast her gaze at the depths of this desolate space. Fear was reflected in her eyes.","Blue irises reminiscent of frost appeared in her vacuous eyes. This pair of eyes seemed capable of seeing through everything. Yet, she looked confused.","“Am I imagining things?” Tianjian Qingyuan murmured doubtfully, but her eyes lit up shortly after as if she had seen something. “No, it isn’t my imagination. What could be the reason behind this sudden change? Could it be because of those children?”","She cast her eyes on the warship at the entrance, specifically Chu Feng and the others.","On the warship, Chu Feng and the others turned to Tianjian Canhua and asked, “Miss Canhua, what is this place?”","“I don’t know either,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“How did you find this place?” Chu Feng asked.","“An elder told us, but she isn’t familiar with this place either,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“Chu Feng, this place gives me the creeps,” Eggy said.","If even the fearless Eggy was feeling uneasy here, this place must be dangerous.","“Few places can evoke such dread in me. Chu Feng, you have to tread carefully,” Eggy said.","She didn’t tell Chu Feng to retreat, knowing how much he cherished his grandmother. It wasn’t easy for him to catch wind of his grandmother’s news, so he couldn’t give up so easily.","Chu Feng turned to the Divine Deer and asked, “Elder, do you know this place?”","“I have never heard of this place. It’s my first time here. Try not to venture too deep, or else I might not be able to save you if you meet with a mishap.”","Chu Feng felt even more uneasy. The Divine Deer was his strongest life-preservation means. This place must be very dangerous if even the Divine Deer wasn’t confident of saving him.","“Where’s my grandmother?” Chu Feng asked Tianjian Canhua. He wanted to find his grandmother as soon as possible.","“I’ll bring you there,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","The warship was moving extremely fast. They passed through countless realms; most realms were pitch black and devoid of life, but there were still a handful of realms that emanated light.","The warship finally landed in a realm.","This realm looked no different from the world of cultivation’s realms—it was neither a spatial realm nor a formation realm; it was a naturally occurring realm.","Venturing deeper into the realm, they soon arrived before an ancient palace bearing the words ‘Heavensword Sacred Palace’.","“Is my grandmother inside?” Chu Feng asked.","He couldn’t see through the palace with his Heaven’s Eye, and that made him feel nervous. Could the Heavensword Sacred Palace be even stronger than the Zhao Immortal Clan? Did my grandmother barge into the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s territory?","Tianjian Canhua didn’t answer the question. “Young friend Chu Feng, your friends will have to wait outside.”","“Go in and take a look. I should be able to protect them if something happens,” the Divine Deer said.","So, Chu Feng followed Tianjian Canhua into the palace.","The palace wasn’t big. They soon arrived before a door that led into a formation realm.","The formation realm was empty except for a humongous sword that pierced through the heaven floating in mid-air. This sword appeared to be forged out of white jade. It emanated a faint light, but the power it harnessed was tremendous.","“Is this where the Heavensword Sacred Palace passes down its legacy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Young friend Chu Feng is truly discerning. You were able to see through that?” Tianjian Canhua smiled.","Her attitude was gentler and more casual now that they were alone.","“I don’t understand, Miss Canhua. How can you not know this place when your sect’s legacy lies here?” Chu Feng asked.","“We moved here,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","That explanation sounded reasonable, so Chu Feng shifted back to the main topic at hand, “Why did you bring me here? Where’s my grandmother?”","“You’re familiar with the Heavenly Sacred Palace, right?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","“I have been there before. It’s a mysterious land containing countless treasures,” Chu Feng replied.","“What else do you know?”","“That’s all I know.”","“The Heavenly Sacred Palace used to be a power in the world of cultivation.”","Chu Feng’s eyes gleamed with curiosity. He had always thought the Heavenly Sacred Palace was just a treasure vault; he didn’t think that it was an organization that used to exist.","“It was the strongest power that dominated the world of cultivation in the Immemorial Era. It had 36 sacred palaces under its command, and each sacred palace wields formidable power.","“But for some reason, upon reaching the Ancient Era, the Heavenly Sacred Palace transformed into a place that one could only enter with Heavenly Sacred Beads. Only 17 of the 36 sacred palaces were left, and our Heavensword Sacred Palace is one of them.”","Eggy was taken aback. “The Heavensword Sacred Palace has such a background?”","Chu Feng also realized that he had underestimated the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","Seeing through Chu Feng’s thoughts, Tianjian Canhua added, “Our Heavensword Sacred Palace was a powerhouse in the Ancient Era, and we were only a faction in the Heavensword Sacred Palace. Our Heavensword Sacred Palace possesses one of the strongest bloodlines in the world, towering above the Heavenly Bloodline and all Divine Bodies.”","Tianjian Canhua formed a hand seal. The humongous sword in the sky vibrated before unleashing powerful sword auras.","Chu Feng could sense just how powerful the sword auras were.","“Young friend Chu Feng, how do you find my bloodline power?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","“It’s formidable,” Chu Feng replied.","“You can wield this bloodline power too,” Tianjian Canhua said.","Me?” Chu Feng was confused.","“You just have to consummate with a woman from our Heavensword Sacred Palace.”","“I don’t think the Heavensword Sacred Palace would allow such power to fall into the hands of an outsider, right?”","“Indeed, but neither are we that inflexible. We allow those who fulfill our conditions to join us, too,” Tianjian Canhua said.","“Is that so? Why don’t you recommend someone to me then?” Chu Feng joked.","“What do you think about me?”","Chu Feng froze up. He was just joking.","But Tianjian Canhua seemed serious about this."]},{"number":6347,"title":"Chapter 6347: Chapter 6345: Changes in the Depths of Space","paragraphs":["Chapter 6345: Changes in the Depths of Space","“Am I hearing things? Tianjian Canhua looks prim and proper, so why is she making such a shocking request? You really can’t judge a person by their cover.”","Eggy was also shocked after hearing Tianjian Canhua’s words, but her expression was gloating. She wanted to see Chu Feng deal with this tricky situation.","“Miss Canhua is pulling my leg,” Chu Feng hurriedly replied. He averted his eyes to the humongous sword floating in the sky out of a guilty conscience.","“Do I look like I’m joking?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","Chu Feng turned to Tianjian Canhua. He didn’t say a word, but he reined in his smile and assessed her solemnly. He could tell that she was serious about it.","“Your decision seems a bit reckless,” Chu Feng pointed out.","“I, Tianjian Canhua, always think things through before making a move. Our Heavensword Sacred Palace has a secret art that requires a dao companion to learn. It’d be best if the dao companion is from our sect, but they don’t have to be. The most important requirement is that the dao companion has to be sufficiently strong. I want to marry you to advance my cultivation.","“I never thought I would ever need a man, but I have heard about your deeds and witnessed your strength. I believe you can help me advance further. I can’t guarantee success, but I’m willing to try, and I’ll honor our couple relationship even if we fail. I’ll fulfill my responsibility as your wife, and we will support each other in our cultivation.”","Chu Feng wanted to turn her down, but Tianjian Canhua added, “You aren’t married yet, right? There shouldn’t be a problem with me becoming your only wife.”","“My apologies, Miss Canhua. I’d like to focus on developing my bloodline instead,” Chu Feng replied.","“I understand. Your Heavenly Lightning Bloodline is formidable. There have been powerhouses with extremely powerful Heavenly Lightning Bloodline like yours in the Ancient Era too, but trust me, you’ll advance further if you obtain our Heavensword Sacred Palace’s bloodline,” Tianjian Canhua said.","The Divine Deer blurted out loud, “A frog in the well. Who told you that the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline is inferior to your Heavensword Sacred Palace’s bloodline?”","Those words weren’t just directed at Chu Feng; everyone could hear them.","Tianjian Canhua’s face turned livid, but she didn’t lose her temper. She quickly regained her composure and asked, “Are there other entities in your body? Is that your world spirit?”","Chu Feng was put in a spot. He didn’t expect the Divine Deer to refute Tianjian Canhua so bluntly, though he was planning to turn her down too.","“Miss Canhua, the one who has just spoken is an elder, but I’m afraid I can’t reveal his identity. However, I advise you not to say anything disrespectful to her. She’s not someone to be trifled with, and I won’t allow anyone to disrespect her either,” Chu Feng said.","He was blatantly shielding the Divine Deer.","“Oh? There’s a reason you’re so confident. Don’t worry, I don’t intend to disrespect your elder. Your elder is my elder too. However, I am only doing this out of respect for you. It doesn’t mean that our Heavensword Sacred Palace is intimidated by anyone. Even if not for our ancestor, our Heavensword Sacred Palace also wouldn’t fear any powers in the present world of cultivation,” Tianjin Canhua said confidently. There was a slight hint of threat in her voice.","Chu Feng smiled, but he didn’t respond to her remark.","“Is it because of Xianhai Yu’er? Are you reluctant to marry me because you’re in love with her? I’ll make an exception and allow you to take her as a concubine then,” Tianjin Canhua said.","“Miss Canhua, I don’t think you get what I mean. I’d like to focus on developing my Heavenly Lightning Bloodline,” Chu Feng replied.","“I don’t see a clash,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“My mind is made up.”","Tianjian Canhua froze. Disbelief flickered across her eyes, and her confidence waned. She realized that Chu Feng wouldn’t agree to the marriage no matter what she said.","The world fell silent.","It was a long time before Tianjian Canhua finally moved. She smiled helplessly. “I would have never thought that my first confession would end in a rejection. Young master Chu Feng, I hope you won’t regret the decision you made today.”","“I hope so too,” Chu Feng replied.","Tianjian Canhua turned around and walked out.","Chu Feng followed her and asked, “So, Miss Canhua, where’s my grandmother?”","“I showed you our Heavensword Sacred Palace’s bloodline power because I feared you would think that I’m lying to you and reject me. I didn’t think you would reject me even after seeing it.” Tianjin Canhua’s voice was filled with disbelief. She couldn’t understand why someone would turn down such a good deal.","Putting aside her bloodline power, just her status, talent, beauty, and strength should be enough to win over anyone.","“Were you lying to me?” Chu Feng halted as he frowned in displeasure.","Tianjian Canhua also stopped to look at him. “Will you attack me if I deceived you?”","“I won’t resort to that, but I fear we can’t be friends anymore,” Chu Feng replied as he made his way out.","Shoosh!","A scroll flew to him. It unfurled itself, revealing a map.","“Our Heavensword Sacred Palace did find your grandmother’s trail, but it isn’t here. Feel free to look for her, but I can’t guarantee that you’ll find her,” Tianjin Canhua said.","After leaving the building, Tianjian Canhua turned to Tianjian Jiumeng and said, “Elder, escort them out.”","“Escort them out?” Tianjian Jiumeng was taken aback. She quickly realized what had happened, but she couldn’t believe it.","“It is as you have thought. Perhaps I am lacking. Escort them out,” Tianjian Canhua said with a bitter smile.","Tianjian Jiumeng glared at Chu Feng.","The others sensed something amiss. Something must have happened between Chu Feng and Tianjian Canhua.","Little Fishy’s gaze also turned cold. She stood beside Chu Feng, her eyes focused sharply on Tianjian Jiumeng. It was as if she would do everything she could to take down Tianjian Jiumeng if the latter made the slightest move.","“What happened, brother?” Wang Qiang asked.","“It’s nothing.” Chu Feng shook his head.","Tianjian Jiumeng was angry at Chu Feng for rejecting Tianjian Canhua.","His rejection was bound to have hurt Tianjian Canhua, possibly even affecting her path of cultivation. However, he did have the right to turn her down, so Tianjian Jiumeng chose not to say or do anything despite her anger.","Chu Feng boarded the warship and began leaving the area.","Wang Qiang anxiously asked, “Aren’t we going to l-l-look for your grandmother? Why are we turning back n-n-now?”","“I already know where my grandmother is,” Chu Feng replied.","GRARRR!","Space, in its entirety, suddenly trembled. A bizarre noise reverberated from the depths of space. The crowd was horrified. They looked toward the source of the noise with fearful eyes.","Even Tianjian Jiumeng looked uneasy.","The earlier noise wasn’t from a human, a monstrous beast, or any animal; it was a noise they had never heard before. It sounded like it was from hell, and it left the crowd suffocated in terror.","The noise only lasted an instant, but the trembling continued. It felt like something terrifying was about to emerge from the depths of space!"]},{"number":6348,"title":"Chapter 6348: Chapter 6346: Immemorial Cemetery","paragraphs":["Chapter 6346: Immemorial Cemetery","A brilliant light shone from the depths of space, instantly enveloping everything. The desolate realms became as bright as stars. With the sky full of stars, this world resembled the world of cultivation.","But no one felt the slightest joy. If anything, their unease deepened.","Massive structures suddenly emerged out of nowhere in the depths of space. Taking a closer look, they were blank tombstones. These tombstones emanated auras that went further back than the Ancient Era, and even the smallest of them was comparable to a realm.","The largest tombstone was even the size of a smaller starfield.","And there were countless such tombstones there. The depths of space were no longer filled with realms but tombstones.","“Bloody hell! W-w-what’s going on? Did we fall i-i-into a cemetery?” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","Just then, a larger structure appeared. It was a stone archway that was even bigger than the largest tombstone, towering in front of all the tombstones. Four words were inscribed on the archway, revealing the origin of this place: Immemorial Cemetery.","“Immemorial Cemetery?”","Everyone, from Chu Feng to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s ancestor, Tianjian Qingyuan, murmured those words.","“Who could have triggered this commotion?”","Tianjian Qingyuan cast her eyes at Chu Feng and the others yet again. Unlike Chu Feng and the others, she was mentally prepared for this phenomenon. She had sensed the changes in the depths of this space from the moment Chu Feng and the others stepped in here.","However, she didn’t expect the change to be so huge that the entire space revealed its identity.","“Immemorial Cemetery. Elder, have you heard of this place?” Chu Feng asked the Divine Deer.","“No, but it feels unfathomable. It could be one of the stronger remnants that even the Ancient Era’s powerhouses can’t clear. Chu Feng, this is a massive fortuitous encounter, but it might be beyond you at the moment. I don’t advise you to get embroiled in this. You should leave right now,” the Divine Deer advised.","Chu Feng examined the nameless tombstones. He sensed that the tombstones weren’t truly nameless—it felt like they were cloaked or beyond their current means to read instead.","In truth, there was a tomb or a formation realm beneath each of the tombstones, and they were filled with treasures.","The Divine Deer was right—this was a massive fortuitous encounter. The fact that she had never heard about it meant that this was a place that even the Ancient Era’s powerhouses failed to find. Treasures that an entire era of experts failed to find were bound to be extraordinary.","A white fog drifted from the depths of space and veiled the light and the tombstones. Only the massive stone archway and its plaque remained visible.","“Hide!” a voice suddenly echoed—it was Tianjian Qingyuan.","Everyone from the Heavensword Sacred Palace immediately used their concealment means. Even the warship Chu Feng and the others were on also activated its concealment formation.","Chu Feng turned around and saw a massive crack appearing behind them. The crack was growing larger and larger. This space was opening its doors to the world of cultivation. The two spaces were linking together!","Chu Feng realized why the Heavensword Sacred Palace went into hiding right away.","The stronger powers were constantly surveilling the world of cultivation, and they wouldn’t overlook even the slightest detail. The commotion here would swiftly catch their attention.","And Chu Feng was right.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Zhao Immortal Clan had already noticed this place.","A bunch of elders arrived at the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s observation formation with grim faces. They could see a massive spatial rift reminiscent of a window appearing in the vicinity of the Ninth Galaxy.","Through the rift, they saw a world that was larger than they could imagine.","They couldn’t see the tombstones, but they could already tell something huge had happened from the fog that obscured the realms and the stone archway labeled ‘Immemorial Cemetery’.","Unlike God’s Era, this was an abrupt development. None of their records contained details about the Immemorial Cemetery, and they didn’t think it was a coincidence that it was so close to the Ninth Galaxy.","No matter how they looked at it, the Immemorial Cemetery’s significance didn’t pale in comparison to God’s Era. This was huge!","All of a sudden, the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion bowed deeply. Jie Tianran had descended from the sky.","Without glancing at the observation formation, he said, “Relay my orders. Everyone is to stay inside the mansion. Do not move without my permission.”","The others realized that their powerful mansion master must have already scanned the Immemorial Cemetery with his means.","Just then, the voice inside Jie Tianran asked, “It’s a huge fortuitous encounter. Why don’t you take a look?”","Jie Tianran replied, “It could be a huge fortuitous encounter, but it could also be a dangerous forbidden land. Someone is bound to go anyway. We’ll know whether it is a fortuitous encounter or a forbidden land soon enough. Let them fight over it. They’ll die if it’s a forbidden land, but if it’s a fortuitous encounter...”","Jie Tianran smiled confidently. “Once I obtain God’s Era’s power, I’ll be able to easily snatch the fortuitous encounter from their grasp.”","...","Meanwhile, Eighth Zhao and the others were also observing the Immemorial Cemetery through their observation formation.","“Immemorial Cemetery. Sounds inauspicious.” Zhao Zhuyin frowned.","“We’ll have to take a look regardless,” Eighth Zhao said. He turned to Zhao Daobin and ordered, “Contact that world spiritist.”","...","Most powers chose the same course of action as the Zhao Immortal Clan, as opposed to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","While other powers were rushing to the Immemorial Cemetery, Chu Feng and the others were already standing right outside it.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s warship had already returned to its base. Chu Feng and the others were currently riding on the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s warship. They had taken measures to conceal their warship to avoid unnecessary trouble.","After careful consideration, Chu Feng decided not to get involved with the Immemorial Cemetery. On the one hand, this place stoked his unease. On the other hand, he might lose this chance to find his grandmother if he didn’t rush over.","“Brother, I-I-I have something up. I shan’t accompany you to look f-f-for your grandmother,” Wang Qiang said.","“You’re planning to enter the Immemorial Cemetery, aren’t you?” Chu Feng asked."]},{"number":6349,"title":"Chapter 6349: Chapter 6347: Back to The Divine Body Galaxy Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 6347: Back to The Divine Body Galaxy Again","“I-I-I knew I couldn’t hide it from you. Risk and reward come hand in hand. You don’t have to worry about me; I have means to escape from danger,” Wang Qiang replied.","“I surveyed the area earlier. This place appears to have emerged on its own accord for cultivators to explore. There might not be many benefits at the start. Each tombstone contains a spatial realm within. Some are activated—you might get sucked in just by being in the vicinity. Some are sealed.","“The sealed tombstones should still be safe at this juncture, whereas the activated ones are likely to have danger lurking within. If you wish to explore the area, enter by the east and head down this path.”","Chu Feng thumped his palm against Wang Qiang’s forehead to transfer a map to his mind.","“Holy! B-b-brother, you’re the best!” Wang Qiang was overjoyed.","He had observed the Immemorial Cemetery’s activation too, but he didn’t decipher as much as Chu Feng did. With Chu Feng’s help, he was more confident than ever.","“There’s something weird and ominous about this place. It won’t be easy to obtain its treasures, and the dangers you face are potentially fatal. Make sure to conceal yourself, and don’t hesitate to retreat if you sense something amiss,” Chu Feng advised.","“Don’t worry. I am as resilient a-a-as a cockroach!” Wang Qiang grinned.","He turned around and made his way toward the Immemorial Cemetery. This world was massive, and they were still some distance away from the tombstones. It would take him some time to get there.","But what was more concerning was the ominous feeling this place gave off.","Chu Feng was worried about Wang Qiang even though he didn’t dissuade the latter earlier.","“Hm?” Chu Feng turned to Little Fishy and the others. He noticed something amiss with their expressions.","“Did something happen?” Chu Feng asked.","“We felt something in our bloodline. It feels like something has happened to our clan’s ancestral land,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“Don’t worry, big brother. This change seems to be for the better,” Little Fishy added.","“You should hurry back to take a look,” Chu Feng urged.","“You return first. I’ll accompany young friend Chu Feng,” Little Fishy’s grandfather said.","“I’m in no hurry either,” Little Fishy said.","But her parents simultaneously interjected, “Yu’er.”","Chu Feng could tell from their expressions that the transformation was good news, and they didn’t want Little Fishy to miss this fortuitous encounter. So, he turned to Little Fishy and said, “You have also seen how unfathomable the Immemorial Cemetery is. We still have a long path ahead of us, so you shouldn’t miss any chance to grow. You don’t have to worry about me. I stood confidently before the Zhao Immortal Clan because I had the means to protect myself.”","“All right, big brother. I’ll focus on my cultivation.”","Little Fishy’s response surprised everyone. It was decisive, and her voice sounded so sweet and obedient.","“Haa, I should have known that little sisters are unreliable. How long has it been since I last saw my little sister being so obedient to someone else?” Xianhai Shaoyu sighed.","Little Fishy rolled her eyes at Xianhai Shaoyu before turning back to Chu Feng. “Big brother, you must be careful.”","“I will,” Chu Feng replied.","At his insistence, it was decided that Little Fishy and the others would all return to their clan. They made their way to a realm with a teleportation formation before bidding farewell.","“Young friend Chu Feng, we’ll return to the Totem Dragon Clan after we’re done with our business at our ancestral land,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“I’ll probably head back there after I’m done, too,” Chu Feng replied.","With that, they parted ways.","Chu Feng entered the teleportation formation and traveled to a realm connected to the Nine Heavens Secret Domain, so that he could find his grandmother as soon as possible. That was an Upper Realm in the Divine Body Galaxy.","“Chu Feng, why would something happen to Little Fishy’s ancestral land the moment the Immemorial Cemetery emerged? Is it a coincidence? Or could Little Fishy’s ancestor be buried in the Immemorial Cemetery too?” Eggy asked.","“It should be a coincidence, I think. The Immemorial Cemetery feels ominous. I don’t want Little Fishy and the others to have anything to do with it,” Chu Feng replied.","...","A formidable Ancient Era power known as the Ye Immortal Clan had emerged in the Divine Body Galaxy.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen suddenly appeared all over the Divine Body Galaxy, looking as if they were searching for something.","A group of thirty Ye Immortal Clansmen was gathered on a Divine Body Galaxy’s Upper Realm. Even the weakest in the group was a pinnacle True God level cultivator, and there were three Heavenly Gods among them.","Their leader was a bald old man with red marks on his cheeks.","He didn’t exude the slightest air of transcendence despite being from an immortal clan. If not for his golden cloak, he could have even been mistaken for a demon.","Yet, the crowd treated him with utmost respect. Even the other two Heavenly Gods, who resembled immortals more, stood behind him.","No one dared to speak till the bald old man spoke.","The bald old man was holding onto an ancient compass. The compass had four arrows pointing in the same direction.","“It’s beneath the ground,” the bald old man said.","\"Milord, should we report this matter first?” an elder asked.","“Report? If we’re wrong, we’ll be berated by the clan chief. But if we’re right, we’ll be making a huge contribution by bringing the treasure back,” the bald old man said.","The crowd hurriedly agreed with him. “Milord is right.”","The Ye Immortal Clansmen quickly got into position and began constructing a formation together. The talismans they held in their hands all reflected the same word—’Reveal’.","The formation shot out a beam of light, causing the ground beneath to undulate like giant waves. Dust flew into the air.","Soon, an underground gate appeared.","The crowd was overjoyed to see that gate. They altered their formation to remove the seal on the underground gate before stepping in.","The underground palace was exquisite. Even its corridor was filled with treasures. The Ye Immortal Clan had no interest in such treasures either, but the corridor was so extravagantly ornate that even they wouldn’t do it.","It confirmed their conjecture that an amazing treasure lay here.","Soon, they arrived at a massive hall that gave off an air of divinity.","But their attention was drawn to the woman lying at the center of the hall. She was dressed gracefully, looking dignified and beautiful, but she was in a deep sleep. There was a hint of long-dried blood at the corner of her lips."]},{"number":6350,"title":"Chapter 6350: Chapter 6348: The God Mother Awakens","paragraphs":["Chapter 6348: The God Mother Awakens","She was the God Mother, the humongous avatar who awakened when Chu Feng was fighting the God Clan. What appeared then was only an avatar, but this was her real body.","She revealed astonishing power that day, but Chu Feng still slew her avatar with the Asura Sword and even inflicted damage on her main body. That was where the blood on the corner of her lips came from.","“She seems to be alive. Is she from the Ancient Era?”","The Ye Immortal Clansmen dared not to carelessly disturb the God Mother lying in the hall’s center.","“Milord.”","The Ye Immortal Clansmen looked at the bald old man with nervous looks. Even their words were relayed via voice transmission.","They weren’t fools.","This palace was extraordinary, so much so that it was likely to be where the Divine Body Galaxy’s greatest treasure lay, as their clan chief had previously mentioned. Yet, such a lofty figure reminiscent of a deity suddenly appeared here.","It was one thing if she were dead, but they would be in trouble if she were one of the powerhouses who survived the Ancient Era.","“Don’t make a reckless move. This person is alive,” the bald old man warned.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen felt so nervous that they dared not breathe loudly.","The bald old man pointed the compass at the copper object beneath the God Mother’s body. The copper object was a gate, and the treasure was located beneath it. If they wanted to reach the treasure, they would have to move the sleeping God Mother.","The bald old man looked conflicted, but he clenched his jaws and ordered, “This will be risky. Let’s inform our clan chief first.”","No one objected to his call. On the contrary, the crowd breathed a sigh of relief. They had known from the moment they stepped into this palace that it was extraordinary, and as soon as they saw the God Mother, they understood that she was not an entity they could trifle with.","There was nothing they wanted more than to retreat now.","But a cold aura suffused the palace just as they were about to leave.","The God Mother opened her eyes and stood up.","Sensing the God Mother’s awakening, the bald old man held his position. He could sense how immensely powerful the God Mother was. There was no way they could escape if she intended to take their lives.","Thus, he turned around and respectfully bowed. “I am an elder from the Ye Immortal Clan, Ye Zun. We came here in search of a treasure. We didn’t mean to disturb your rest. Please pardon us for our insolence.”","The bald old man knew it was better to speak the truth to entities like the God Mother than to find excuses. It was common for cultivators to explore remnants, after all.","Shoosh!","The God Mother waved her sleeves. There was a ‘bam’, and the bald old man was reduced to a blood mist. She obliterated him without saying a word.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s elders turned pale in fright, for the bald old man was the strongest among them. Thus, they turned tail and fled.","BAM!","...","Dull thuds echoed simultaneously. All the Ye Immortal Clansmen had turned into blood mist. They couldn’t even let out a squeak before their deaths.","“I was awoken by mere bugs? How displeasing,” the God Mother murmured in displeasure.","She had intended to hibernate for a while longer, but she would wake up right away if anyone arrived in this hall. She was infuriated because her plan was foiled. But soon, she remembered something that further angered her.","It was her descendants’ massacre.","“Chu Feng and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan... No, it won’t be just them. Everyone in the world of cultivation shall die for my God Clansmen!”","Her murderous intent flared. She was planning to go on a massacre to destroy everything in the world of cultivation.","She formed a hand seal. Her eyes suddenly became far keener, allowing her to see through almost everything in this world, and her ears became exceptionally sensitive.","She was planning to search for clues relating to Chu Feng, but her eyes soon widened in shock. She looked down at the gate she was stepping on.","Unable to believe what she had just seen, she quickly opened the gate and went in.","Beneath the gate was a humongous cavern realm. It was created by a treasure that made it unassailable and impossible to peer into. Yet, a hole had appeared inside the cavern realm.","She first glanced at the hole before looking toward the center of the cavern.","At the center of the cavern was a mountain made of countless stones, emanating faint golden lights. These stones harnessed incredible regenerative properties and could be used for cultivation.","These stones didn’t have much energy left, and it wasn’t easy to use them for cultivation. Nevertheless, there was still a person sitting at the corner of the mountain, assimilating the stones.","It was an old woman.","Chu Feng would have trembled in excitement if he had seen this old woman—it was his grandmother.","“A bug snuck in here?”","The God Mother’s astonishment dissipated. She didn’t ask any questions nor lose her temper. Instead, she thrust her palm and unleashed a powerful surge of martial power at Chu Feng’s grandmother.","Despite her composed attitude, this attack was intended to kill! To her, this was no different from swatting a bug to death.","Boom!","The strike landed. The cavern realm, despite being made out of a treasure, shook.","Yet, the God Mother was stunned. She was even more astonished than when she first noticed someone inside the cavern realm.","Much to her shock, Chu Feng’s grandmother was unharmed!","Chu Feng’s grandmother had released a bundle of flames to block the God Mother’s apocalyptic attack.","“Who are you?” the God Mother asked.","It dawned on her that the hole didn’t happen from the treasure’s wear and tear. It was the doing of this old woman. The other party’s ability to block her attack showed that she was a force to be reckoned with.","Chu Feng’s grandmother finally opened her eyes to look at the God Mother.","The God Mother looked down on her from above, her graceful robes fluttering imposingly.","Chu Feng’s grandmother sat on the ground. She looked dignified but unadorned.","Their attitudes, appearances, and positions paralleled a deity contrasted against a mortal. However, their reactions showed a completely different picture. Chu Feng’s grandmother was nonchalant and calm, unfazed by the God Mother, whereas the God Mother looked flustered.","“You are...” the God Mother asked, wanting to get to the bottom of the other party’s identity.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng’s grandmother waved her sleeves. There was a loud explosion as a wave of flames instantly enveloped the cavern realm.","The flames were so intense that even the cavern walls crackled under the heat. Everything, except for the golden stones that could be used for cultivation, was reduced to ashes.","And this included the God Mother too!"]},{"number":6351,"title":"Chapter 6351: Chapter 6349: God Curse","paragraphs":["Chapter 6349: God Curse","Chu Feng’s grandmother looked nonchalant as if killing the powerful God Mother was nothing worth mentioning. She wanted to sit down and continue assimilating the shattered stones, but she noticed something and raised her head to look at where the God Mother previously stood.","The God Mother had been reduced to ashes, but things weren’t over yet.","As the ashes scattered, a fingernail-sized bead that emanated a faint light floated out. There were ancient words inscribed on the bead—God Curse.","The God Mother’s feeble but furious voice echoed from the bead, “How dare a mere human murder a god? Don’t think that you can oppress me just because I’m from a weaker lineage among the God Clans! Can you take the consequences of killing a god?”","The God Mother’s voice was filled with killing intent, but she abruptly fell silent after. The bead shattered, transforming into streams of light that gushed toward Chu Feng’s grandmother.","Chu Feng’s grandmother compressed the flames in the cavern, focusing them on the streams of light. The heat in the cavern intensified, causing space to distort to an extreme degree.","However, the streams of light were unfazed by the intensified flames and surged into the head of Chu Feng’s grandmother.","Chu Feng’s grandmother frowned, but she didn’t feel any pain. Instead, her eyes suddenly became clearer as if she had regained her senses.","“What did she say earlier? Chu Feng? Chu Feng? Why does it sound so familiar?”","Conflict flickered in her eyes as she racked her brain for an answer. Countless voices echoed in her ears—these were the conversations she had overheard while wandering the world. She had ignored them then, but she found many clues in those voices.","As her mind cleared up, her eyes sharpened in clarity.","“He’s Xuanyuan’s son. Feng’er is my grandson! No, someone seeks to hurt my grandson. It’s the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!”","All of a sudden, two ancient words, ‘God Curse’, appeared on her forehead and glowed.","Her face warped in pain, and she soon fainted. At the same time, the flames in the cavern receded.","...","A gigantic warship was floating in another realm in the Divine Body Galaxy. The flag it flew revealed that it belonged to the Ye Immortal Clan.","The warship was huge enough to house a cluster of palaces, practically making it a floating city. Guards were patrolling everywhere.","Four figures were gathered in one of the smaller palaces.","A white-haired old man and an old woman floated in mid-air, their eyes closed in cultivation. They gave off an imposing air. They were grand elders of the Ye Immortal Clan, as well as the parents of the incumbent Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief.","There were two other people in the room, too.","One was a scholarly youth dressed in a golden robe. The other was cloaked from head to toe, though the outlines suggested a small physique. They sat opposite each other, playing a game of chess.","It was a peculiar chess set—the chess pieces were treasures manifested out of formations.","“Lord Clan Chief,” an elder’s voice sounded outside the room.","“Didn’t I say not to disturb me while I’m playing against the guest elder?” the youth coldly replied.","He didn’t look like the type to have a temper, but in his annoyance, he unleashed terrifying oppressive might. It turned out he was the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief.","The elder outside was frightened, but he clenched his jaws and said, “Lord Clan Chief, Elder Ye Zun and the others’ life tablets have shattered.”","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief immediately looked over. Even the two grand elders opened their eyes as well.","The door opened. The elder kneeling outside the door was holding a plate. There were 37 life tablets on the plate, each inscribed with a name, but all of them had shattered.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and the two grand elders couldn’t believe their eyes. They inspected the life tablets and were forced to conclude that their owners had lost their lives.","“Elder Ye Zun has a protective formation, but it didn’t even activate?”","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief looked at the two grand elders behind. Despite being the clan chief, his knowledge was still lacking compared to his parents. In particular, his father was the previous clan chief.","“The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion is the strongest power in the Divine Body Galaxy, but they don’t have the means to kill our elders,” the old man said.","“Could it be the Zhao Immortal Clan or the Heavensword Sacred Palace?” the clan chief asked.","“It’s unlikely. There’s no grudge between us. Maybe there are other Ancient Era’s powers in the Divine Body Galaxy that we don’t know about,” the old man said. He turned to the kneeling elder and asked, “Can you trace where they lost their lives?”","“Lord Grand Elder, it’s this place.”","The elder was prepared for this question. He took out a formation map with a location marked.","“You stay here. I’ll go there to take a look,” the old man said.","“Father, I’ll go with you,” the clan chief said.","Just then, the cloaked guest elder walked over and asked, “Can you bring me with you?”","It was a feminine voice.","The two grand elders looked at the clan chief.","“Let’s go together then,” the clan chief said.","So, the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief drove the warship toward where the 37 elders died.","It was already late at night. There were two majestic phenomena in the sky other than the stars. One was God’s Era’s silhouette, and the other resembled a massive spatial rift—the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance.","These two phenomena looked more conspicuous at night. They could be seen even without resorting to special means.","Most people had already heard about God’s Era, so they were more intrigued by the spatial rift.","The Ye Immortal Clan, being a major power with observation means, was already aware of the emergence of the Immemorial Cemetery. However, they chose not to join the commotion as there was something they coveted more in the Divine Body Galaxy.","The deaths of the 37 elders, which included three Heavenly Gods, were a huge deal to them. These were the Ye Immortal Clan’s elites. This was a matter they had to take seriously.","...","While the Ye Immortal Clan was setting off, Chu Feng also emerged from a teleportation formation. He arrived at the realm where the Ye Immortal Clan’s army was previously stationed."]},{"number":6352,"title":"Chapter 6352: Chapter 6350: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Prodigy, Rank Nine True God?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6350: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Prodigy, Rank Nine True God?","Chu Feng noticed the two phenomena when he walked out of the teleportation formation. He had seen God’s Era before, so he wasn’t surprised by it. Rather, he was intrigued by the huge spatial rift near the Ninth Galaxy. It was visible even with one’s bare eyes.","One was a brilliant light that ushered in a brilliant God’s Era.","The other was a spatial rift that signified the dark Immemorial Cemetery.","The two stood against each other in the sky, seemingly prophesying something. Chu Feng couldn’t help but think deeper into it.","“It looks oddly beautiful, though God’s Era has gotten brighter. Chu Feng, do you think there’s a connection between God’s Era and the Immemorial Cemetery?” Eggy asked.","That was also what Chu Feng was thinking. He was searching for a link between the two. However, he couldn’t find a clue and deduce anything.","“All I can see is a single word,” Chu Feng replied.","“What is it?” Eggy asked with curious eyes.","“Beautiful.”","“Tsk. You don’t say. I have eyes to see that for myself.”","Chu Feng chuckled as he continued his journey.","He already had the map in his head. With his exceptional sense of direction as a world spiritist, it didn’t take him long to arrive at the location Tianjian Canhua had marked out on the map.","The area was sealed off by a powerful formation, with many people standing guard. Those who approached the area would receive a warning. Someone had occupied the area.","“The Ye Immortal Clan? Just how many powers does the Ancient Era have? They’ll take over the world of cultivation at this rate,” Eggy mumbled in displeasure.","The fluttering flags and the identity tokens hanging on the guards’ waists revealed their identity.","Chu Feng constructed a formation to slip through the barrier.","The formation was powered by a treasure, but fortunately, the treasure wasn’t too potent. It didn’t take Chu Feng too long to infiltrate the formation.","Beyond the formation was a charred land. Chu Feng could tell from the remains that this used to be a forest, and a remnant was hidden beneath it. He slipped into the remnant, but he couldn’t find anything useful inside it.","“How is it? Is it your grandmother’s doing?” Eggy asked.","“It’s hard to tell now that the flame has been extinguished. My grandmother should have been here since the Heavensword Sacred Palace had a portrait of her. The Ye Immortal Clan might know something, given how they sealed this area off. Let me try asking someone.”","Chu Feng quickly got into action and found nine targets. They were all early True God level cultivators. He picked them because they appeared to be of a higher standing, which meant they could be privy to confidential information, while remaining weak enough for him to control them.","There were also Ye Immortal Clansmen who had reached mid True God, late True God, and even pinnacle True God here. He dared not lower his guard around these people. It was still beyond him to deal with cultivators of that level.","He picked nine targets so that he could strike any one of them when an opportunity arose.","Soon, his chance came.","To his surprise, all nine of his targets chose to travel together. They must be up to something.","None of them noticed Chu Feng even though he was tracking them closely.","The nine targets flew across the sky. They revealed in their conversation what they were up to, but Chu Feng had no interest in that, so he decided to make a move straight away.","The space around the nine targets distorted, and a powerful force assaulted them right after, causing them to lose control of their bodies. Nine formation chains appeared out of nowhere and bound them, leaving them bewildered.","Chu Feng disguised himself before appearing in front of them.","“Who are you? How dare you attack us? We are from the Ye Immortal Clan!”","The nine targets furiously shouted at Chu Feng, showing no fear whatsoever. They were confident that their identity as Ye Immortal Clansmen would protect them.","“Calm down, I don’t mean any harm. I’m just curious to know why you sealed off this place. What’s in there?” Chu Feng asked amicably.","An old man among the nine targets scoffed in disdain, “We have our pride as Ye Immortal Clansmen. Don’t even dream about getting any information from us!”","“Pride?”","Chu Feng didn’t bother wasting his breath. He formed a hand seal and manifested another powerful formation. The formation unleashed nine rays of light and dove into their foreheads. This formation would wear down their mind, compelling them to reveal everything they knew.","The nine targets might have talked big, but their willpower was nowhere near strong enough. It didn’t take long for their minds to collapse under the formation.","Chu Feng learned a lot from them.","The Ye Immortal Clan, like the Zhao Immortal Clan, proclaimed themselves an immortal clan because of their powerful bloodline. Their clan was very powerful, boasting many Heavenly God level cultivators.","They even had two rank four Heavenly God level grand elders.","But what surprised Chu Feng more was that their clan chief was a junior. Despite being a junior, the latter was a rank nine True God level cultivator.","“Chu Feng, ask them if it’s his base cultivation or his highest cultivation level after using all his means.”","Eggy couldn’t believe it when she heard the news. Even mid Half-God level juniors were considered prodigies in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. How could the Ye Immortal Clan have a rank nine True God level junior?","It was fortunate that Chu Feng and the others had grown fast, or else the gap between them would have been massive. Even so, there was still a lot of catching up to do.","Chu Feng asked several verification questions, and the nine targets confirmed their clan chief was at rank nine True God level, though they also revealed an important clue.","While their clan chief’s base cultivation was indeed at rank nine True God level, they had resorted to special means to raise his cultivation. It was called the Immortal Legacy."]},{"number":6353,"title":"Chapter 6353: Chapter 6351: Ye Xiancheng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6351: Ye Xiancheng","The Ye Immortal Clan stripped and stored the cultivation of their dying pinnacle True God level clansmen. Over the generations, the stored energy accumulated to a terrifying degree, and that became known as the Immortal Legacy.","Over the generations, the stored energy became incredibly powerful.","However, the fusion of so many energies, no matter how well they were combined, was bound to be violent.","According to the nine targets, their incumbent clan chief had fused with the Immortal Legacy more impeccably than anyone else had since the Ancient Era. He obtained supreme fighting prowess through that; no one was a match for their clan chief within the same cultivation rank.","But the downside was that their clan chief couldn’t raise his cultivation or fighting prowess through his bloodline. His base cultivation was his strongest state.","A junior becoming the clan chief, no matter how talented they were, was bound to invite skepticism from the other clansmen. The current strength of the clan chief was more important than their potential.","But it was a different story for this clan chief.","Chu Feng had placed the nine targets under his control, forcing them to speak their minds unreservedly. Yet, they were filled with compliments for their junior clan chief, saying that he had an excellent character. Even though he had a big temper and had berated many clansmen to date, none harbored any grudge against him for that.","Their clan chief, under the influence of the Immortal Legacy, was named Ye Xiancheng.","Chu Feng had asked those questions to get a grasp of the Ye Immortal Clan’s strength and situation, but what he was more concerned about was finding clues about his grandmother’s whereabouts.","And the Ye Immortal Clan did have clues on his grandmother.","The remnant torched by flames had contained cultivation resources, but no one noticed them until an abrupt inferno caught their attention. The flame went out shortly after, but the extreme temperature persisted, making it hard to approach the remnant.","But someone spotted an old woman walking out from that remnant, and she was none other than Chu Feng’s grandmother.","By the time the Ye Immortal Clan arrived, Chu Feng’s grandmother was already gone. They were able to enter the scorching remnant, but there were hardly any cultivation resources left in there.","They had sealed off the remnant to conduct a more thorough search of the area to see if there were other treasures in there. They seemed to be searching for a specific treasure, but none of the nine targets knew what that treasure was.","For that, their clan chief, grand elders, and other elites had traveled to this realm.","There was another important clue.","An important figure from the Ye Immortal Clan was frolicking alone in this realm. He was the clan chief’s older brother, born to the same father and mother. He was known as Ninth Young Master because he was the ninth sibling.","His talent paled far in comparison to Ye Xiancheng. He lacked ambition, and he had terrible character, too. He was the scum of the Ye Immortal Clan, committing all kinds of atrocities.","He was currently alone in this realm’s Flowing Sun City. It was not that the clan didn’t dispatch guards to protect him, but that he didn’t want people to follow him and get in the way of his fun.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen weren’t fond of Ninth Young Master, but they dared not disobey him.","Ninth Young Master was nine thousand years old, but his cultivation was still stuck at early True God level.","Chu Feng asked a few more questions before erasing the nine targets’ memories about him and lifting the formation.","The nine targets didn’t sense anything amiss; they continued their journey right away.","Chu Feng remained on the spot, deep in thought.","“Sounds like your grandmother was here, Chu Feng. The Ye Immortal Clan must be looking for your grandmother since they covet what was inside the remnant,” Eggy said.","“We might be able to use Ninth Young Master to get more useful information. Otherwise, we can also have him order the Ye Immortal Clan to search for my grandmother’s whereabouts. It helps to have more people looking for her,” Chu Feng said.","“Let’s go capture him. Why are there scums in every clan? Such people are a waste of space in the world. We’d be doing the world a favor by vanquishing him from the face of the world,” Eggy said.","“Milady Queen, why did you become such a caring person?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have always been a caring person,” Eggy scoffed.","“Of course, of course.” Chu Feng dared not refute her.","He moved carefully despite those nine saying that no one was protecting Ninth Young Master. Just because they were being honest didn’t mean their information was accurate. Thus, he constructed a more potent concealment formation around him.","With his prowess as a world spiritist, even Heavenly God level cultivators would struggle to find him unless he revealed himself.","But Chu Feng failed to find Ninth Young Master in Flowing Sun City—the latter had moved elsewhere. Fortunately, Ninth Young Master had left some clues about his trail, so Chu Feng could still track him down.","While Chu Feng was searching for Ninth Young Master, the Ye Immortal Clan’s army arrived outside the remnant where the God Mother died.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, the two grand elders, and the guest elder entered the remnant together. A while later, they stumbled upon Chu Feng’s unconscious grandmother.","“It’s her?”","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and the two grand elders were astonished.","“Father, mother, is she the one who killed our elders?” the clan chief asked.","They had long noticed this old woman, but the Ye Immortal Clan paid no heed to her, thinking that she couldn’t pose a threat to them. But now, they had no choice but to take her seriously. Putting all things aside, the heat lingering here was much stronger than the other remnant they sealed off.","The terrifying flames had appeared in not just one remnant but two. And this old woman just so happened to be lying unconscious here. It was hard to believe that she didn’t have anything to do with those flames.","“It’s hard to say, but it is highly suspicious that she has appeared in both remnants. We can’t underestimate her,” one of the grand elders said.","“It’s her,” the guest elder suddenly remarked.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief turned over and asked, “Guest elder, do you recognize her?”","“You must have heard about Chu Feng, right?” the guest elder asked.","“I have. There are all kinds of rumors about him. Not only is he the strongest junior in the present world of cultivation, but it’s also said that he has obtained the legendary Genesis Bloodline?” the clan chief replied.","“The rumors are true, and this old woman is likely to be Chu Feng’s grandmother,” the guest elder replied."]},{"number":6354,"title":"Chapter 6354: Chapter 6352: The Ye Clan’s Decision","paragraphs":["Chapter 6352: The Ye Clan’s Decision","“Miss, how do you know that?”","The Ye Immortal Clan’s grand elders looked at the guest elder.","“I have some history with Chu Feng, so I have been keeping tabs on his affairs. His grandmother’s sect was destroyed by a clan many years back, but just recently, that clan was destroyed in the same way her sect was destroyed. That old woman is likely to be Chu Feng’s grandmother, and the chances are that she’s fairly powerful,” the guest elder replied.","“Do you know her cultivation level?” the male grand elder asked.","“I’m not sure, but you should tread carefully. If you trust me, I can put her under my control. I have a treasure that can bind a person,” the guest elder said as she took out a transparent item.","It fitted within her palm, and it resembled a tiny crystal coffin.","The two grand elders examined the item with skepticism. People of their stature were more inclined to trust their means.","But the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief replied, “It goes without saying that I trust you, guest elder. Use your means to bind her.”","The two grand elders were surprised.","The clan chief turned to them and said, “Father, mother, you think so too, right?”","The two grand elders swallowed the words sitting on the tip of their tongue and expressed that they trusted the guest elder too.","The guest elder formed a hand seal and tossed the item down.","The item enlarged during its fall, and it passed through the body of Chu Feng’s grandmother and trapped her within it. Then, the guest elder changed her hand seal, and the item contracted until it was the size of Chu Feng’s grandmother.","Then, the guest elder lifted Chu Feng’s grandmother out of the remnant.","“Are you able to wake her up?” the male grand elder asked.","“There’s no point waking her up. Rumor has it she’s insane,” the guest elder replied.","“Insane?” The clan chief and the two grand elders were taken aback.","“Yes, she’s insane.” The guest elder doubled down on her reply.","“She’s most likely responsible for the deaths of our elders. We’ll have to pin the blame on her if we can’t get to the bottom of the matter,” the male grand elder said.","“Pin it on her if you wish, but I don’t recommend awakening her. I should have been able to expand and contract my treasure at will, similar to a spatial realm, but I’m unable to contract it any further than this. She’s pushing back against my treasure. I suspect she’s stronger than I expected. It’s possible that even the two grand elders won’t be able to curb her if she goes on a rampage,” the guest elder said.","“Miss, are you saying that there are present-era cultivators who are above rank four Heavenly God level?” the female grand elder asked with a mocking smile.","“Grand elders, you can ascertain her cultivation if you have the means to. If you don’t fear her rampage, you can go ahead and awaken her as well. But allow me to take my leave first. I don’t want to get caught up in it,” the guest elder replied.","The two grand elders doubted the guest elder’s words and intended to make a move, but the clan chief quickly interjected, “Father, mother, I know how strong you are, but our Ye Immortal Clan has only just emerged from seclusion. The guest elder possesses a deeper understanding of the cultivation world than we do. We should tread carefully for now.","“Let’s bring her back to our warship first. We can use our ancestral formation to curb her if she turns out to be overwhelmingly powerful. Our warship is right outside anyway, so it won’t be too much trouble.”","“Xiancheng, do you believe that the present-era cultivators are stronger than your parents?” the female grand elder asked.","“I have confidence in your cultivation, but there’s no harm in taking caution,” the clan chief replied.","“Let’s go with Xiancheng’s suggestion,” the male grand elder replied.","They moved Chu Feng’s grandmother to the warship.","Following that, the two grand elders attempted to wake Chu Feng’s grandmother and assess her cultivation level, but to no avail. This surprised them. This forced them to concede that there was some credibility behind what the guest elder said.","But the female grand elder refused to give up and tried to attack Chu Feng’s grandmother.","The guest elder interjected, “Pardon my frankness, guest elder, but I doubt you can wake her with brute force when other means failed to work. You’ll only anger her instead.”","“So what if I anger her? If she dares retaliate, I’ll kill her with a single smack to avenge our elders,” the female grand elder scoffed.","“You can kill her if you wish to, but that will be a huge waste. You can put her to better use,” the guest elder replied.","“What are you thinking, guest elder?” the clan chief asked.","“Chu Feng possesses the Genesis Bloodline and the Ruler’s Bloodline. There’s a good chance he might have other valuable treasures too. He’s known to be a sentimental man who puts his life on the line for his friends. He will rush here and hand over what we demand if he learns his grandmother is in our hands. Just his Genesis Bloodline is already worth the effort. How many treasures in the world can compete with that?” the guest elder said.","“So, you want us to announce this to the world and wait for Chu Feng to come knocking?” the clan chief asked.","“If you don’t fear Chu Feng, that is,” the guest elder replied.","“Hah...” the clan chief sneered. “I have never feared anyone.”","Having made up their minds, they returned to their palace to rest with Chu Feng’s trapped grandmother. Meanwhile, the warship made its way back to the realm where Chu Feng was.","The clan chief continued playing chess with the guest elder, while the two grand elders cultivated by the side.","The female grand elder struggled to focus. She opened her eyes and eyed the guest elder. Then, she sent a voice transmission to her husband, “Old man, this doesn’t look good. Our Xiancheng is mesmerized by that vixen. We can’t let this continue.”","“Don’t worry, old woman. Xiancheng still needs to go through more storms to toughen up. I passed my clan chief position down to him to hasten his growth. She won’t be able to do much as long as we’re keeping an eye on her.","“Besides, you shouldn’t think the worst of her. What if she truly intends to support our Xiancheng? She might be from a dubious background, but she has her means. As long as she’s earnest about helping Xiancheng, there’s no reason we cannot keep her in our clan.","“You shouldn’t underestimate our Xiancheng either. There’s no hope for our other children. Xiancheng is the only one our Ye Immortal Clan can rely on,” the male grand elder replied.","“You’re right. Xiancheng is surprisingly meticulous despite his honest face. Old man, you stand guard here. I’ll go adjust the formation.” The female grand elder stood up and headed out.","“Adjust the formation?” The male grand elder was confused.","The female grand elder glanced at Chu Feng’s grandmother. “We can’t underestimate that ugly hag. None of our means worked on her. She must either be very powerful or possess formidable treasures. That lass is right. We can’t let down our guard. It’s one thing for a mishap to befall us, but Xiancheng hasn’t recovered from his injuries. We’re at a critical stage in his treatment. We have to make sure nothing goes wrong.”","“You’re right. Something is amiss about Chu Feng’s grandmother. Don’t hold back. Let’s reinforce our ancestral formation,” the male grand elder said.","“I know.” The female grand elder walked out.","...","Sometime later, Chu Feng finally located the Ye Immortal Clan’s Ninth Young Master."]},{"number":6355,"title":"Chapter 6355: Chapter 6353: He Was Already Here","paragraphs":["Chapter 6353: He Was Already Here","Chu Feng heard much about the Ninth Young Master’s deeds along the way. The latter was not a good person, but he was not thoroughly bad either. It was fine to spare his life, though it wouldn’t weigh on Chu Feng’s conscience to kill him either.","Chu Feng finally found the Ninth Young Master in a tavern.","The Ninth Young Master looked youthful and dashing even though he was no longer young. He had reserved the entire tavern and was drinking alone in the main hall. When he saw Chu Feng, he tossed a Cosmos Sack over without asking anything.","“I have booked this place. Don’t spoil my mood,” the Ninth Young Master said without glancing at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng grabbed the Cosmos Sack and peeked in out of curiosity. The Ninth Young Master was surprisingly generous. None of the items inside the Cosmos Sack were useful to Chu Feng, but it would be a fortune to ordinary cultivators.","“You’re from the Ye Immortal Clan, right?” Chu Feng asked.","The Ninth Young Master immediately sat upright and assessed Chu Feng. “Who are you?”","“I’d like to ask you some questions. Have you seen this person?” Chu Feng asked as he unfurled his grandmother’s painting.","But the Ninth Young Master didn’t answer. He thrust his palm forth, his martial power weaving into a net to capture Chu Feng. He was at rank five True God level.","Chu Feng released his spirit power and incinerated the martial power net.","Sensing the disparity in their strengths, the Ninth Young Master didn’t continue his attack and instead asked, “Are you an enemy of our Ye Immortal Clan?”","Chu Feng flitted up to the Ninth Young Master, grabbed his head, and activated Protection Bane. It would hinder his subsequent plan if the Ninth Young Master had a powerful protective formation.","To his surprise, the Ninth Young Master had no protective formation.","Chu Feng removed his hand and saw that the Ninth Young Master’s face was pale with fright. The latter must have thought that Chu Feng was going to kill him.","“Cooperate with me, and I’ll consider sparing your life,” Chu Feng said.","The Ninth Young Master scoffed, “I am a Ye Immortal Clansman. I don’t fear anyone! I might not have many strengths, but I have spunk! Don’t even dream about prying any information from my mouth...”","Whoosh!","Chu Feng pulled out an assortment of torture tools with a wave of his sleeves.","“Please ask me anything.” The Ninth Young Master changed his tune.","Chu Feng ignored him and picked up a thorned dagger.","The Ninth Young Master panicked. “What are you doing? I’ve already said that I’ll tell you anything you want. Honesty is my greatest strength! But I don’t know the person you’re asking about!”","“How’s your standing in the Ye Immortal Clan?” Chu Feng asked.","“Ah? My standing... The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief is my father. I’d advise you to think thrice before making a move. My parents won’t spare you if you make a move against me,” the Ninth Young Master said.","“Wasn’t the clan chief position passed down to Ye Xiancheng?” Chu Feng asked.","“You know that as well? Indeed, the current clan chief is my little brother, Ye Xiancheng. My father passed down his position to him, but I don’t acknowledge him as the clan chief. He might appear nice and obedient, but he’s far more scheming than you can imagine. He’s the most cunning one of us all, despite being the youngest! Do you have a grudge against him? If so, I can help you deal with him!” the Ninth Young Master said.","“Sure,” Chu Feng replied.","“How do you intend to deal with him?” the Ninth Young Master asked.","“You just have to cooperate with me. Otherwise, I’ll make you suffer a fate worse than death.”","Chu Feng began constructing a formation to take full control of the Ninth Young Master.","The Ninth Young Master was indeed cowardly. He stood obediently without making a move while the formation was being constructed. When the formation was completed, he said, “Brother, I haven’t lived enough yet. I don’t know what you’re up to, but please spare my life.”","Chu Feng suddenly raised his head and peered through the ceiling to look at the sky.","Words had appeared in the sky. They were already visible to everyone on this realm, but they were still growing at a considerable pace, such that it was only a matter of time before everyone on this starfield saw it.","Chu Feng tensed up. The words were addressed to him.","To Chu Xuanyuan and Jie Ranqing’s son, Chu Feng:","Your grandmother is alive and in the hands of our Ye Immortal Clan. Head to the Divine Body Galaxy’s Reverent Upper Realm’s Reverent Mountain Range if you wish to save her.","“They really captured your grandmother? But how do they know that’s your grandmother?” Eggy was surprised.","“My personal information is no longer a secret. Any competent person investigating me can piece together their intelligence to figure out my family background, friends, and acquaintances. It wouldn’t be surprising for the Ye Immortal Clan to know about that when the Heavensword Sacred Palace has figured out as much. Now, it’s just a matter of whether my grandmother is truly in their hands or not. It’d be best if it’s true,” Chu Feng remarked.","With the Divine Deer’s power, he was confident about saving his grandmother.","“Regardless, we should vanquish the Ye Immortal Clan in the future.” Eggy’s killing intent flared. She wouldn’t spare anyone who dared stand against Chu Feng.","Chu Feng activated the formation and soon had the Ninth Young Master fully under his control. He hid within the Ninth Young Master’s body and controlled the other party toward the location stated in the message.","Everyone he met along the way was discussing the matter.","Chu Feng was well-known in the present era, far more than the Ye Immortal Clan, but not much was known about his background. Most people didn’t know that his grandmother was still alive, or that his father’s name was Chu Xuanyuan.","With the Ninth Young Master’s identity, Chu Feng quickly arrived at the warship and entered a palace. There, he saw the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and his parents.","However, he had little interest in those people. He was only concerned about the person lying inside the crystal coffin. He could tell with a glance that it was his grandmother, Song Luoyi.","This was not his first time meeting his grandmother. Back when he was still in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Reincarnation Upper Realm, he ventured into Mount Ivory Valley because he needed a huge amount of Spirit Spring Water to raise his spirit power.","There, he met a mysterious old woman. She was dressed neatly and gave off an imposing air, but her face was disfigured. She tried to wash her face with poison, and Chu Feng stopped her.","He realized that the old woman was not in the right state of mind, despite possessing unfathomable cultivation. He couldn’t communicate with her, but he felt an inexplicable intimacy toward her.","Later, he learned that the old woman was his grandmother.","He felt different emotions now that they were reunited. She was his close kin. Looking at her disfigured face left him with a heartache as if someone had stabbed needles into his heart, as he recalled her painful past.","But he remained calm. He could tell that from his grandmother’s stable breathing that she wasn’t injured, even though she was unconscious.","And there were two people in this palace that posed a great threat to him.","“Do you need something, ninth brother?” the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief asked, not knowing someone was controlling his ninth brother.","The two grand elders didn’t utter a word. They scorned their son so much that they weren’t willing to speak to him.","Chu Feng ignored the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and instead asked the Divine Deer, “Elder, are you confident?”","He could tell that the two grand elders were at least rank four Heavenly Gods. This concerned his grandmother, so he couldn’t afford any slip-ups here.","“I can take your grandmother away. Should I do it now?” the Divine Deer asked.","“Let’s go.” Chu Feng made up his mind.","Weng!","So, the Ninth Young Master suddenly vanished in front of the clan chief’s and his parents’ eyes.","“Huh?”","This sight shocked the two grand elders. When did their useless son become so formidable as to vanish under their watch?","An instant later, their faces warped in horror. The crystal coffin remained inside the room, but Chu Feng’s grandmother had vanished from it.","“What’s going on?”","The clan chief and his parents were dumbfounded. They wondered if they were hallucinating. They quickly spread their senses out and scanned their surroundings, but they couldn’t find Chu Feng’s grandmother anywhere.","It was then that the guest elder spoke up in a relatively more composed tone, “You can withdraw the message now. There’s no need to call for him anymore. He... was already here.”"]},{"number":6356,"title":"Chapter 6356: Chapter 6354: The God Curse Can’t Be Lifted","paragraphs":["Chapter 6354: The God Curse Can’t Be Lifted","“Chu Feng? You’re saying that Chu Feng saved his grandmother?” the female grand elder looked at the guest elder as she asked.","The male grand elder and the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief found that hard to believe too. They were certain that the person who had just entered the palace was the Ninth Young Master.","They saw no Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng is a talented world spiritist. It is within his means to control the Ninth Young Master. However, I didn’t expect him to rescue his grandmother without breaking my treasure,” the guest elder said as she raised her hand, and the crystal coffin contracted and flew onto her palm.","She turned to the clan chief and said, “I’m sorry.”","“Why are you apologizing?” The clan chief was confused.","“I had you lure Chu Feng here because he was carrying many treasures. I thought obtaining those could bulk up the Ye Immortal Clan. However, I underestimated his means. I didn’t expect him to rescue his grandmother so easily. He’s not the type to let things slip. The Ye Immortal Clan has made an enemy out of him without getting anything in return. I... am remorseful,” the guest elder said.","“Guest elder, are you sure Chu Feng was behind this? Could it not be that Chu Feng’s grandmother has regained consciousness and escaped while holding my ninth brother hostage?” the clan chief asked.","He still found it hard to believe that Chu Feng had pulled that off.","“Based on what I know, Chu Feng’s grandmother is not in the right state of mind, and she doesn’t hesitate to attack anyone who provokes her. She wouldn’t leave quietly if she regained her consciousness, especially if she had the means to slip away without us noticing. She would have made a move against us.","“Chu Feng must have been behind this. He was controlling the Ninth Young Master, which was why the latter ignored your question. His goal was to rescue his grandmother,” the guest elder replied.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and his parents thought those words made sense. Thinking about it now, there was something off about the Ninth Young Master.","“Doesn’t that mean that Chu Feng was in this realm all along? He wouldn’t have gotten here so quickly otherwise,” the clan chief said.","While the message they had sent out had enveloped this realm, it would take time for it to propagate further. Chu Feng arrived shortly after they released the message, which meant that he must have been in this realm too.","“Chu Feng has been searching for his grandmother all along. Someone spotted his grandmother in this realm, so it isn’t surprising for him to find this place,” the guest elder replied.","“Looks like the one who rescued that old woman is indeed Chu Feng. We have nothing to fear then. Think about it. Why would Chu Feng escape when he possesses such means?” the clan chief asked.","“Why?” the guest elder asked.","“It means that he fears and dares not confront us,” the clan chief replied.","“You’re right.” The guest elder nodded.","Just then, an elder’s excited voice echoed from outside the palace, “Lord Clan Chief, grand elders, I have returned.”","It was a white-haired old man. He was of considerable stature in the Ye Immortal Clan, and he had received an important mission not too long ago.","“Did you find it?” the clan chief asked.","“I have accomplished the task entrusted to me,” the elder gleefully replied as he took out a transparent sphere that was the size of a watermelon and lifted it with both hands.","Inside the sphere was a spatial realm. In the spatial realm was a silver mountain peak enveloped in a gaseous substance that resembled the breath of an immortal.","“Wonderful! We have everything in place now!” The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief was delighted. He turned to the guest elder and said, “Guest elder, you can recover your body now.”","“Lord Clan Chief, the preparations will take some time, right?” the guest elder asked.","“Yes, but it won’t take too long,” the clan chief replied.","“I need to make some preparations too,” the guest elder replied.","The clan chief’s face darkened. The guest elder had given him a heads-up that she would need some time alone to prepare once everything was in order. In other words, she needed to leave temporarily.","“Guest elder, can’t you make your preparations here? We have already activated our ancestral formation. There’s no place safer than here in the world,” the clan chief said.","“Lord Clan Chief, I’d like to make my preparations alone due to my peculiar constitution. I seek your understanding for that,” the guest elder replied.","“All right. Don’t take too long,” the clan chief replied.","The guest elder bowed before taking her leave.","“This lass is full of trouble. Who knows what she’s up to? Xiancheng, you need to tread carefully. She might have saved your life, but that doesn’t change the fact that she’s an outsider,” the female grand elder warned.","The clan chief’s smile vanished, replaced with a confident smirk. “Don’t worry, mother. Everything is within my grasp.”","...","The Divine Deer took Chu Feng somewhere safe, though they didn’t leave the realm.","“There’s something weird about that crystal coffin. I nearly failed to save your grandmother from there,” the Divine Deer remarked.","She had planned to escape from this realm, but she consumed so much energy rescuing Chu Feng’s grandmother from the crystal coffin that she couldn’t do so anymore.","“Looks like the Ye Immortal Clan has quite the means. Thank you, elder.”","Chu Feng was grateful to the Divine Deer. He couldn’t have rescued his grandmother from the Ye Immortal Clan’s clutches without her incredible means.","Wuu!","Chu Feng’s grandmother suddenly frowned in pain. The words ‘God Curse’ appeared on her forehead.","“Grandmother!”","Chu Feng hurriedly channeled his spirit power to diagnose his grandmother’s condition. Her body was extremely healthy, but the God Curse had sealed off her brain, making it impossible for him to peer in with his spirit power.","He felt uneasy, for the God Curse was likely responsible for his grandmother’s current pain. What further unnerved him was that the familiar aura he felt from the God Curse—it was the God Clan’s aura.","“It’s the God Clan. They are behind this curse. But why?” Chu Feng was perplexed.","“The God Clan? Chu Feng, are you certain?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, it’s the God Clan. I’m certain,” Chu Feng replied.","He began constructing a formation to lift the God Curse, but soon, he crumbled into despair. He was unable to do anything about the God Curse.","Just then, a voice echoed from the sky, “God Curse? Is that what those two characters mean?”","Chu Feng’s heart clenched up. The Ye Immortal Clan’s guest elder was floating in the sky, but he didn’t notice her at all before she spoke."]},{"number":6357,"title":"Chapter 6357: Chapter 6355: Rank Five True God Level","paragraphs":["Chapter 6355: Rank Five True God Level","“Chu Feng, let me out,” Eggy said.","She also realized something was amiss about the guest elder, or else the latter couldn’t have found Chu Feng so quickly. Whether she had planted a tracking item that Chu Feng failed to see through or that she possessed other means, it would be unwise to let down their guard against an enemy of this caliber.","“Don’t worry, I can handle it.”","Chu Feng looked at the guest elder, neither making a move nor opening his World Spirit Space.","Shoosh!","The guest elder suddenly exerted her oppressive might, causing her robe to flutter wildly. Her cultivation was at rank seven True God level!","That was nowhere near enough to make Chu Feng flinch. Without budging a step, he blocked the oppressive might with his spirit power with ease.","But then, he suddenly felt a chill on his back.","The guest elder had flitted behind him with daggers in both hands. Both daggers were God Armaments shrouded in dark red auras. She simultaneously attacked with both daggers with incredible speed, one aiming for his waist and the other aiming for his neck.","Chu Feng didn’t bother dodging. He manifested two formation swords in his hands and turned around to block the attack.","What happened next shocked him.","He successfully blocked the guest elder’s daggers, but both his formation swords shattered as a result of the clash. This showed just how strong the other party’s daggers were.","This prompted him to retreat.","But the guest elder wouldn’t give him a chance to get away. She gave chase and continued pressuring him with her daggers.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng stopped his retreat, manifested two formation swords in his hands, and launched a counterattack. Slashes rained down on the guest elder, leaving her no room to escape.","It looked as if the guest elder had fallen for Chu Feng’s trap.","But the next moment, Chu Feng’s sword silhouettes suddenly shattered like glass.","Chu Feng hurriedly retreated.","To his shock, the guest elder had crushed his attack with her oppressive might. Her cultivation had increased further to rank nine True God level. It would be impossible for him to deal with her with normal means.","But the guest elder didn’t continue her assault. She stowed away her daggers and said, “Big brother Chu Feng is as formidable as ever. I’d have been killed if not for my cultivation being slightly higher than yours.”","Chu Feng was bewildered, but he recognized the voice and asked probingly, “Song Yun?”","“That’s me.”","The guest elder took off her cloak, revealing a clean, radiant face. She was none other than Song Yun.","“How did you appear at the Ye Immortal Clan? And how did your cultivation grow by so much?” Chu Feng asked.","While Song Yun had to resort to special means to raise her cultivation to rank nine True God level, her base cultivation was still higher than his. Otherwise, there was no way she could have raised her cultivation so far.","Song Yun’s smile widened. She was just about to speak when she suddenly vomited. A huge amount of blood spurted each time she vomited. In a short moment, a huge puddle of blood had formed at her feet.","Her blood was black, and it bubbled like lava.","“You’re ill?” Chu Feng asked.","He could tell that Song Yun’s condition was not the result of an injury but an illness.","At the same time, Song Yun’s aura faded, revealing her base cultivation of rank five True God level.","Song Yun didn’t answer right away. She took a few steps back and sat down on the ground. She wiped off her blood, though her smile persisted as if nothing had happened. “I’m fine, big brother Chu Feng. It’s just that... I’m dying.”","Chu Feng asked, “What happened?”","“It’s a long story, but I’ll make it short. I obtained a fortuitous encounter in the Netherworld Sect, and my cultivation surged, but that drew the envy of the new faction. They schemed against me. They killed a huge number of prodigies from both the conservative and new factions and framed me for it. I couldn’t prove my innocence, so I had to escape.","“It was by chance that I rescued the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and received an invitation to join the Ye Immortal Clan as their guest elder. This illness of mine was caused by the backlash of the fortuitous encounter I obtained from the Netherworld Sect,” Song Yun explained.","“Chu Feng, take that lass’ words with a pinch of salt,” Eggy reminded.","Song Yun continued, “Big brother Chu Feng, I grasped a special means in that fortuitous encounter. Do you still have your Netherworld Embryo? I can awaken your Netherworld Embryo’s potential. I dare not promise much, but it should at least raise your cultivation by a rank.”","“What do I have to do?” Chu Feng asked.","“All you have to do is let me fuse my energy into your Netherworld Embryo,” Song Yun replied.","“That’s all?” Chu Feng asked.","“Big brother Chu Feng, I hope you can trust me. My cultivation surpasses yours; I don’t have to beat around the bush to harm you. Besides, with your sharp control, I believe you can stop me if I try to cause any harm with my energy,” Song Yun said with a smile.","Chu Feng couldn’t tell what Song Yun was thinking, but he decided to give it a try.","“I trust you. Come.”","Chu Feng stepped forward.","Song Yun placed her palm on Chu Feng’s back and formed a hand seal.","Chu Feng felt a peculiar wave of energy entering his body. The energy quickly located his Netherworld Embryo and flowed into it. His Netherworld Embryo then unleashed a tremendous amount of power into his dantian.","He felt the impetus for a breakthrough.","Song Yun removed her hand and said, “The rest is up to you, big brother Chu Feng.”","She took out a black cloth with a wave of her sleeves and tossed it over Chu Feng and herself. The cloth expanded in mid-air, covering them entirely.","Their surroundings turned pitch black. The black cloth wasn’t just a simple cover; it seemed to transport them into a dark world.","Chu Feng could tell that the black cloth had the power to block phenomena. Song Yun must have known that the phenomenon arising from his breakthrough would catch the attention of the Ye Immortal Clan, which was why she used this treasure.","Chu Feng sat down and channeled his martial power. Nine-colored lightning soon appeared above him, but it was limited to the area covered by the black cloth. No one outside the black cloth could see the phenomenon.","The lightning descended. Chu Feng withstood the trial.","It was easier than before.","But the growth in Chu Feng’s cultivation didn’t stop there.","Soon, an even stronger nine-colored lightning manifested. It fell on Chu Feng too, and he, once again, withstood it.","After the phenomenon cleared, Song Yun removed the black cloth, and everything reverted to normal.","“Two consecutive breakthroughs. As expected of my big brother Chu Feng!” Song Yun looked at Chu Feng with a satisfied smile.","Chu Feng’s cultivation had consecutively risen two ranks to rank five True God level."]},{"number":6358,"title":"Chapter 6358: Chapter 6356: Unraveling the Truth","paragraphs":["Chapter 6356: Unraveling the Truth","Song Yun smiled joyously, but her surprise was only limited to her words—she didn’t look surprised in the least. She had expected Chu Feng to make consecutive breakthroughs here.","But Chu Feng was surprised.","Making consecutive breakthroughs in True God level was no easy feat, not to mention he was already at rank three True God level. It would take a significant fortuitous encounter for him to achieve such a feat.","Yet, Song Yun easily achieved it.","On top of that, she had many formidable treasures as well. The bizarre daggers were one, but that black cloth that concealed phenomena was a big deal too. Chu Feng had sensed that he had entered another space. He had never seen such a treasure before.","He couldn’t help but wonder what kind of fortuitous encounter Song Yun had attained.","Is it the Netherworld Tower?","The Netherworld Tower was a place created by the Netherworld Sect’s founder, and so far, almost no one had returned alive from it. The last time he heard, Song Yun had entered the Netherworld Tower.","“That’s quite a fortuitous encounter. Did you obtain it from the Netherworld Tower?” Chu Feng asked.","He figured it would be better to ask her straight than to speculate. There was no need for him to beat around the bush, considering their relationship.","“How do you know about the Netherworld Tower, big brother Chu Feng?” Sign Yun asked.","“That Netherworld Envoy who brought you into the Netherworld Sect told me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Him? He was handsomely rewarded for bringing me into the Netherworld Sect, though it seems like he is dead,” Song Yun said.","“Dead?”","“Mmhm. I couldn’t find him anywhere.”","“I see...”","“Hold on, big brother Chu Feng. Did you meet him after I entered the Netherworld Tower?”","“I did.”","Chu Feng didn’t withhold information. He told her about his encounter with the Netherworld Envoy, including the latter talking about Song Yun’s imprisonment and coercing him into taking the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar’s trial.","“You have been to the Netherworld Embryo Spirituality Summoning Altar? And you went there because of me?” Song Yun asked.","“Why do you sound so shocked?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","Song Yun’s expression had changed. She didn’t look as calm as before anymore.","“I didn’t think I was so important to you,” Song Yun teased.","“What are you saying? Do I look that heartless to you?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","Song Yun didn’t say a word, but her smile looked more radiant than before. She even looked a little shy. All of a sudden, she frowned and murmured, “Wait a moment.”","“What’s wrong?” Chu Feng asked.","“Big brother Chu Feng, you were the one who induced the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar’s red cloud phenomenon, right?” Song Yun asked.","“Red cloud phenomenon? What does it look like?” Chu Feng asked.","“The sky would be covered in red clouds. You weren’t the one behind it?”","“I don’t think so. I didn’t induce a phenomenon.”","“That can’t be. It must be you. You appeared around the same time as the red cloud phenomenon, and that Netherworld Envoy disappeared around that time, too. Baili Zilin must have killed that Netherworld Envoy to silence him, so that he can take credit for the red cloud phenomenon.”","“What’s going on?” Chu Feng asked.","“The Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar’s name comes from a saying. ‘ When the red clouds cover the sky, the Netherworld God shall ascend to his throne. ’ The person who induced the red cloud phenomenon is said to be the successor to the Netherworld King.","“Baili Zilin now commands the full support of the new faction, and some in the conservative faction are even wavering. And that’s all because he induced the red cloud phenomenon. It happened around the same time you visited the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar. The time and location fit. I’m guessing that Baili Zilin challenged you afterward to silence you. He knows that you’re the only one who knows the truth other than the Netherworld Envoy.","“Yes, that must be the case.” Song Yun sounded increasingly certain.","She was a vigilant person. She investigated the Netherworld Envoy’s disappearance because the latter was related to her. She wanted to know if someone made a move on the Netherworld Envoy because they intended to harm her.","And now, it all made sense.","The Netherworld Envoy was killed not because of her but Chu Feng.","“I see.” Chu Feng nodded in realization.","“Hm?” Song Yun was surprised by Chu Feng’s sudden show of confidence.","“I sensed a powerful phenomenon emerging when I was standing before the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar, but I suppressed it because I didn’t want to cause a commotion. My suppression worked, and no phenomenon emerged. But it looks like the phenomenon still emerged after I left. That explains Baili Zilin’s actions,” Chu Feng replied.","Chu Feng thought that Baili Zilin had challenged him out of arrogance, but Song Yun’s words made more sense.","“That must be the case. I should find a chance to embarrass Baili Zilin since he is unable to awaken the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar,” Song Yun said.","“What a pity it is for the Netherworld Envoy.”","Chu Feng knew there was a good chance the Netherworld Envoy was dead.","Even though the Netherworld Envoy had tricked him into activating the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar, only to renege on his promise and refuse to divulge the Netherworld Tower’s location afterward, he knew that the Netherworld Envoy wasn’t a bad person.","If anything, the Netherworld Envoy had helped them a lot.","For instance, he was the one who brought Song Yun into the Netherworld Sect. If not for that, she would have never reached her current level in a place like the Nine Souls Galaxy.","Similarly, Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo was planted by that Netherworld Envoy. He was initially averse to it, but he had advanced his cultivation through the Netherworld Embryo more than once. Naturally, it could be considered a fortuitous encounter for him.","“There’s no need to pity him. He benefited from us, too.”","Song Yun didn’t feel grateful to the Netherworld Envoy even though the latter had contributed more to her growth.","Chu Feng didn’t think much about it since everyone had their own perspective on matters.","Song Yun suddenly stared intently at Chu Feng. A smile like never before formed on her lips. It was very faint, but it looked beautiful. It felt far more sincere than her usual beaming smile.","“Why do you look so happy?”","“Big brother Chu Feng infiltrated the Netherworld Sect and took the risk to awaken the Netherworld Embryo God Summoning Altar for me. Isn’t that something worth being happy about?” Song Yun asked.","“I’m sure you wouldn’t leave me to the lurch if you knew something had happened to me, too. Besides, I wasn’t of any help to you,” Chu Feng said.","“I’m sure you could have helped me if the Netherworld Envoy told you where I was,” Song Yun replied.","“So, was your fortuitous encounter related to the Netherworld Tower?” Chu Feng asked once more.","“That’s right.” Song Yun nodded.","Chu Feng didn’t probe any further after satisfying his curiosity.","All of a sudden, Song Yun grimly bowed to Chu Feng. “I’m sorry, big brother Chu Feng.”","Chu Feng was confused by her action.","Song Yun explained, “I was the one who told the Ye Immortal Clan to capture our grandmother.”"]},{"number":6359,"title":"Chapter 6359: Chapter 6357: Song Yun’s Plan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6357: Song Yun’s Plan","Chu Feng narrowed his eyes. “You did that?”","“I did, but I had a reason for that. The life tablets of many Ye Immortal Clan’s elders suddenly shattered. We were investigating that matter when we stumbled upon your grandmother. She was already unconscious by then and was lying there. I recognized her as our grandmother, so I told the Ye Immortal Clan to bring her back.","“My goal was just to lure you out to help me. Besides, the Ye Immortal Clan believed our grandmother was the culprit behind their elders’ death, and the only way out was to reveal her relationship with you. They already knew you possessed the Genesis Bloodline, so they would have spared her until you arrived.","“The Ye Immortal Clan wanted to get to the bottom of their elders’ death, but our grandmother was unconscious. They tried ways to awaken her, but to no avail. They even wanted to torture her. I had to firmly state the pros and cons to deter them from doing so.","“Big brother Chu Feng, you can check our grandmother’s condition if you doubt my words. There should be no injuries on her,” Song Yun explained.","Chu Feng’s grandmother was indeed unharmed, and Song Yun’s explanation checked out.","So, Chu Feng didn’t pursue the matter and instead asked, “Do you know where the two characters on my grandmother’s forehead originate from?”","His priority was to help his grandmother regain consciousness.","“I don’t know. It had already been there by the time we got to her,” Song Yun replied.","Eggy’s voice echoed in Chu Feng’s ear, “Chu Feng, do you think your grandmother’s condition has something to do with the God Curse?”","“It’s possible,” Chu Feng replied. He turned to Song Yun and said, “You said you wanted to lure me out to help you. What do you need my help with?”","“It’s a long story. The current Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, Ye Xiancheng, inherited the Ye Immortal Clan’s legacy, allowing him to reach rank nine True God level at a young age and wield fighting prowess surpassing his peers.","“However, there are downsides to that legacy. One, his base cultivation is his limit; he’s unable to raise his cultivation beyond that. Two, a problem has cropped up with his body, and his days could be numbered if not resolved.","“The Ye Immortal Clan has prepared a powerful recovery formation for him. It is built around a catalyst treasure, which will be depleted once the recovery formation is activated. This means that the formation can only be activated once.","“For that reason, the Ye Immortal Clan wants to ensure everything goes well, so they are preparing other treasures to further enhance the effects of the recovery formation. They won’t activate the recovery formation until everything is in place.","“The Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief wants to repay the favor he owes me for saving his life by using the recovery formation to treat my injuries, too, but I suspect he just wants to use me. He might have noticed the unique nature of my martial power and wants to use me as a treasure to enhance the recovery formation.","“However, I’m in a terrible condition too, and this recovery formation is an opportunity for me. So, I decided to play along and see how it goes. My plan is to defeat the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief after the recovery formation is activated and take control of it, but I am not confident of pulling it off. If big brother Chu Feng helps me, I’m sure everything will go well.","“Besides, our grandmother needs to be treated too, right? That recovery formation is extremely potent. You can bring our grandmother there and give it a try,” Song Yun said.","“How can I help you?” Chu Feng asked.","“Once the recovery formation is activated, the catalyst treasure will create a powerful barrier to isolate the formation. Only Ye Xiancheng and I will be inside the formation. I just have to bring you in and wait for the formation to be activated before dealing with him.","“The catalyst treasure is bound to Ye Xiancheng, so we’ll have to defeat and control him. I can deal with that. Big brother Chu Feng, what I need you to do is far more important. You need to slip into the auxiliary formation, channel it with this treasure, and stop Ye Xiancheng from using the recovery formation’s energy to suppress us.”","Song Yun took out an ordinary-looking token that appeared to be forged out of a black stone.","Chu Feng took the token and noticed it harnessed tremendous energy. This energy wasn’t from the present era but the Ancient Era.","“How can you be certain no one other than Ye Xiancheng will be inside the formation?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have inspected the catalyst treasure. Anyone in the formation will be either sacrificed or healed. The formation can be adjusted to focus the healing on an individual, but having an additional person inside the formation inevitably diminishes the healing effect.","“The Ye Immortal Clan has staked everything on Ye Xiancheng; they are determined to ensure that he makes a full recovery. They have probed me many times before, and I reckon they don’t see me as a threat to Ye Xiancheng,” Song Yun replied.","Eggy said to Chu Feng, “Let’s go, Chu Feng. It’ll be best if she’s speaking the truth. Otherwise, I’ll kill that wrench.”","Her confident voice suggested that she had the means to pull that off. She had also mentioned something similar when he went to the God Clan to rescue Little Fishy, but such powerful means were bound to take a toll on her. It might even put her in danger.","For that reason, Chu Feng wouldn’t let her make a move unless he was cornered.","But he quickly made up his mind after taking a glance at his grandmother.","“You said that you’re confident you can control the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief?” Chu Feng asked.","“I am. He’ll have no choice but to obey me once I force this pill down his throat,” Song Yun replied as she took out a pill.","Chu Feng took the pill to inspect it. It was a powerful gu pill from the Ancient Era. He stowed away the pill and said, “You handle the auxiliary formation. I’ll deal with the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief.”","Supposing Song Yun was telling the truth, the crux of this operation would be the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. They had to control the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief before everything else could proceed. Thus, he decided to personally handle it to ensure the operation’s success.","He made this choice because he didn’t completely trust Song Yun.","Song Yun didn’t complain about Chu Feng stowing away her gu pill. Instead, she smiled radiantly and said, “All right, I’ll heed your words.”","She sounded so obedient that those who didn’t know better might think she was Chu Feng’s wife."]},{"number":6360,"title":"Chapter 6360: Chapter 6358: Milady Queen’s Trump Card","paragraphs":["Chapter 6358: Milady Queen’s Trump Card","“When do we make a move?” Chu Feng asked.","“We can do it right now,” Song Yun replied.","“I’ll construct a spatial formation. You bring me and my grandmother back.”","Chu Feng constructed a spatial formation. It was imbued with a strong concealment effect, and it allowed those inside to see what was happening outside. Once the formation was complete, he took his grandmother and went in.","The spatial formation then contracted until it was only the size of a fingernail, making it easy for Song Yun to take it with her.","Song Yun took the spatial formation and returned to the Ye Immortal Clan’s warship.","“Chu Feng, let’s alter our contract,” Eggy suddenly said.","“Alter our contract?” Chu Feng was confused.","“This is not the first time you have refused to open your World Spirit Space to let me out. You seem to have gotten arrogant now that you have gotten better at your world spiritist techniques. You’re even using it against me now. I want the right to freely open your World Spirit Space,” Eggy demanded grudgingly.","“What are the side effects of the new skill you have grasped?” Chu Feng asked.","“What do you mean by that?”","“Don’t feign ignorance. You must have grasped a new skill. Ever since your recovery, you have offered to stand up for me each time I’m in danger. You must have learned a powerful skill. But I bet it comes at a price, right? I’m willing to accept your help, but you must tell me what the side effects are,” Chu Feng said.","“Fine. I thought I hid it well,” Eggy replied with a grin. “You’re at rank five True God level now, right?”","“Don’t you already know that?” Chu Feng replied.","“Let me show you my cultivation.”","Eggy unleashed her cultivation, and Chu Feng widened his eyes in astonishment.","She was also at rank five True God level despite only being at rank one True God level not too long ago! He had been feeling guilty about that, and he had been thinking that he would have to find a way to raise her cultivation, though it looked like there was no need for that now.","She was no weaker than him despite his recent breakthroughs.","“Eggy, have you been hiding your cultivation?” Chu Feng asked.","“I didn’t hide anything. I gained a better grasp of my Godsoul after reaching True God level. Now, I can cultivate normally through my soul without devouring origin energies. With my talent, it shouldn’t come as a surprise that I have reached rank five True God level. I thought I could help you deal with some enemies, but you refuse to give me a chance to showcase my skills,” Eggy grumbled.","“It’s my fault. I’ll let you make a move next time we encounter an enemy,” Chu Feng replied with a grin. “So, your hidden card is the Godsoul?”","He couldn’t help but worry as he was familiar with the Godsoul.","There were nine Godsouls in the world, each nurtured by a galaxy. They were the strongest natural oddities in the world, but they could only be used by world spirits.","Eggy received her Godsoul from Taotie, World Spiritist Emperor’s world spirit.","Taowu mentioned that a world spirit fused with a Godsoul would gain a massive boost in their intelligence, which would aid them in grasping a special cultivation method that allowed them to raise their cultivation without devouring origin energies.","Eggy had once tapped into the Godsoul’s power—it was formidable, but it nearly took her life.","“That’s right. Other than that, I can also temporarily gain a huge amount of power through the Godsoul. That should be enough to protect you,” Eggy said.","“But you’ll suffer a severe backlash from that, right?”","“Yes. I would have used it a long time ago if not for the backlash, but as I have told you, I have gained a better grasp of the Godsoul after reaching True God level. I can now control the extent I tap into the Godsoul’s power. As long as I don’t go overboard, it won’t pose a danger to my life.","“Don’t worry, I don’t plan on dying. I’m waiting for the day you stand at the peak of the world of cultivation, so I don’t plan on using the Godsoul unless required. But a good recovery formation is hard to come by, and your grandmother needs it. You shouldn’t miss this opportunity. I’ll back you if anything happens,” Eggy said.","Chu Feng projected his consciousness into his World Spirit Space and swiftly constructed a contract formation.","Eggy was delighted. She quickly got up and entered the contract formation. This new contract allowed her to freely enter and leave Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space.","Soon, the contract was sealed.","“Great! I’m free now!” Eggy danced in glee.","Chu Feng had become more mature over the years after all the storms he had weathered, but Eggy remained the same as ever, be it her appearance or personality. It was rare for someone to remain themselves despite external pressures.","Her cheerful dance in her black-feathered dress and with bare legs left Chu Feng staring in a daze. Her beauty never failed to awe him no matter how many times he saw her. Looking at her evoked old memories, as he was brought back to the day when they first met.","Chu Feng had always been searching for his family members. He wanted to converse normally with his grandmother, and he also wanted to meet his mother, who loved him dearly but couldn’t be with him due to extenuating circumstances.","But the one who had accompanied him through tough times was the woman in front of him.","Friends and family were important to him. He cherished every goodwill he received, and he would put his life on the line to protect them. But the person who meant the most to him was still none other than Eggy.","“Whee, I’m free!” Oblivious to Chu Feng’s thoughts, Eggy celebrated this moment.","“You speak as if I have imprisoned you all this while,” Chu Feng joked.","“I’ll decide when I make a move now,” Eggy said with a mischievous grin.","“Yes, Milady Queen. You call the shots. But I’d like you to remember this. My grandmother is important to me, but so are you. You have to prioritize your safety, no matter what happens. It would be meaningless for me to become strong if you are no longer around,” Chu Feng said.","“Such sappy words! Are you in love with me?” Eggy smirked.","“Ah? I thought it was plenty obvious,” Chu Feng replied.","Eggy’s expression stiffened up. She knocked Chu Feng’s head and said, “Audacious! How dare you covet my beauty? I shall have you know that I’m a dangerous woman!”","“Oh? I’d like to see how dangerous you are.” Chu Feng also raised his fist to knock her head.","Eggy didn’t dodge, but she closed her eyes and cowered backward. To her surprise, Chu Feng didn’t smack her head but instead gently patted her.","“You aren’t dangerous at all. You’re obedient and adorable,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Obedient? I’ll wallop you!” Eggy raised her fist menacingly.","“Be good, Milady Queen. Don’t be so naughty. Hahaha!” Chu Feng snickered before withdrawing his consciousness from his World Spirit Space.","“Good, your head!” Eggy waved her fist indignantly, but beneath her puffed cheeks was a hint of happiness."]},{"number":6361,"title":"Chapter 6361: Chapter 6359: Let’s See If It’s Real or Not","paragraphs":["Chapter 6359: Let’s See If It’s Real or Not","Chu Feng had some grasp of Song Yun’s character. Beneath her innocent exterior lay a highly calculative mind. It would be wise to remain vigilant around her. He couldn’t tell if she sincerely wanted to help him or if this was a way to dupe him back to the Ye Immortal Clan.","Despite having known each other for a long time, he couldn’t say for certain if she was a friend or a foe. She did join the Ye Immortal Clan, and her explanation was her one-sided words.","But it was not entirely a blind gamble on Chu Feng’s part that he chose to go with Song Yun.","For instance, Song Yun was present when he rescued his grandmother, so she knew he possessed powerful escape means. Yet, she didn’t probe about that as if it were of no interest to her.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s warship reappeared in Chu Feng’s line of sight. They would soon learn whether Song Yun was reliable or not.","Song Yun entered the warship without a hitch with her token. Soon, she was welcomed by familiar figures—it was the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, Ye Xiancheng, and his parents.","“You’re back, guest elder. Have you completed your preparations? We can wait longer if you need more time to reach your ideal condition,” Ye Xiancheng said with a fawning attitude.","Despite addressing Song Yun as a guest elder, his attitude spoke a different story. It looked almost as if he were a lapdog faced with his goddess.","“Thank you for your concern. I am ready. May I know if the formation is ready too?” Song Yun asked.","“Everything is proceeding more smoothly than we have anticipated. We can activate the recovery formation right away if you’re ready,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Let’s activate it then,” Song Yun replied.","“All right.”","Ye Xiancheng led them deeper into the warship. He continued chatting nonstop with Song Yun along the way, much to the chagrin of his mother.","His father, on the other hand, was unfazed as if he was already used to it.","“Chu Feng, do you think the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief is in love with Song Yun, or he’s just putting on a very convincing act?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","“It looks real, but he could just be a good actor. What do you think, Eggy?” Chu Feng returned the question.","“I’m asking you because I don’t know. You’re the one with Heaven’s Eye. Can’t you see through him?” Eggy asked.","“Know a person but not his heart. The Heaven’s Eye can easily see through formations, but the same can’t be said about a human’s heart,” Chu Feng replied.","Soon, they arrived at the heart of the warship. Ye Xiancheng disabled a protective formation, and a majestic palace came into sight.","This palace had a unique design. It was black on one side and white on the other. An ancient aura and recovery energy wafted out of the palace.","The recovery energy was so potent that a whiff of it could heal a terminally ill patient to full health and even expand their lifespan by several hundred years. Without a doubt, this must be the recovery formation Song Yun mentioned.","As the door slowly opened, more recovery energy poured out.","Chu Feng saw that the palace was much bigger inside than it appeared on the outside. The recovery formation in the palace was indeed a formidable one. It was linked to the palace, and there were many formation cores in the surroundings.","Only one of the formation cores was empty; the others contained invaluable treasures, ranging from extreme yang treasures to extreme yin treasures. These treasures were carefully chosen to ensure a synergetic effect among them.","Ye Xiancheng first entered the palace, and Song Yun followed suit.","As she was about to step into the palace, the female grand elder said, “Miss, this formation is very important to our clan. You must listen to the clan chief once you’re inside. There will be dire consequences if you don’t follow instructions and impede the recovery formation’s activation.”","Her words were reasonable, but there was a threatening edge to her tone.","“Rest assured, grand elders. I am grateful to the clan chief for allowing me to use this recovery formation. You can trust me to follow his instructions,” Song Yun said.","“Mother, you can come in with us if you’re worried,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“I’ll take away a share of the recovery energy if I enter. We specially prepared this recovery formation for you. It’d be a waste for me to enter when I’m not injured,” the female grand elder replied.","“Mother, we’re already wasting the recovery energy just by keeping the door open,” Ye Xiancheng said.","He was indirectly telling his mother to stop making things difficult for Song Yun and let her enter.","The female grand elder caught his drift. She rolled her eyes and waved her hand in resignation. “Go in.”","Song Yun bowed to the two grand elders before stepping into the palace.","Ye Xiancheng quickly formed a hand seal to close the palace’s doors. He changed his hand seal, and the walls became transparent. This allowed those outside to see what was happening within, and vice versa.","Such a function wasn’t necessary for the recovery formation; the two grand elders must have made it that way out of worry.","Ye Xiancheng turned to Song Yun with deeply sentimental eyes. “Are you ready, guest elder?”","“Mm.” Song Yun nodded. She waved her sleeve, and a cloth flew out. The cloth transformed into a powerful surge of spirit power that sealed off the palace from within.","Outside, the female grand elder exclaimed in alarm, “What are you doing?”","The male grand elder didn’t utter a word, but his eyebrows shot up as a murderous aura flared from him.","Countless figures appeared in the vicinity. They were the Ye Immortal Clan’s army. They had been on standby, and they quickly moved to seal off the surroundings as soon as they sensed that something was amiss.","But Song Yun remained unfazed. She tossed out the spatial formation Chu Feng was hiding in.","Chu Feng quickly stepped out of the formation and took his stance beside Song Yun, though he didn’t take his grandmother out.","Ye Xiancheng was surprised to see another person appearing out of nowhere. He carefully assessed Chu Feng before asking, “You’re Chu Feng?”","“Yes, I am,” Chu Feng replied.","“Guest elder, did he get to you too?” Ye Xiancheng asked Song Yun.","He thought that Chu Feng had taken control of Song Yun like the Ninth Young Master.","“Control? My silly son, do you still not understand what’s going on? That lass is in cahoots with Chu Feng!” the female grand elder shouted as she formed a hand seal.","A golden light covered the world.","Chu Feng could sense the tremendous oppressive might exerted by the golden light despite being inside the recovery formation. In fact, they would have been dead if they hadn’t been in the recovery formation.","“We have activated our clan’s ancestral formation. You can’t escape now. Lass, I’ll consider leaving you with an intact corpse if you surrender now.” The female grand elder glared at Song Yun.","“We can’t escape? Old woman, you must be getting senile. Hasn’t my big brother Chu Feng already slipped through your ancestral formation once when rescuing our grandmother?” Song Yun took off her cloak and sneered at the female grand elder."]},{"number":6362,"title":"Chapter 6362: Chapter 6360: The Sentimental Ye Xiancheng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6360: The Sentimental Ye Xiancheng","“You little beast! I’ll shred you into pieces!” the female grand elder roared through gritted teeth.","Song Yun had acknowledged her relationship with Chu Feng when she mentioned ‘our grandmother’. It turned out that they were extremely close.","“Guest elder, what do you mean by that?” Ye Xiancheng was taken aback too.","His look of disbelief made him look extremely pitiful.","But Song Yun was unfazed. “Big brother Chu Feng and I need the recovery energy. Ye Xiancheng, you can spare yourself from unnecessary pain if you obediently heed our orders and hand over the recovery energy.”","“So you’re after the recovery formation.” Ye Xiancheng turned to Chu Feng and clasped his hand. “You’re an incredible one. I have heard a lot about your outstanding talent, but I didn’t expect you to be so skilled at using women, too.”","He spoke in a sarcastic tone, and tears brimmed in his eyes. He seemed to be heartbroken by Song Yun’s act of betrayal.","“You’ve misunderstood. I’m not making use of her. It’s a mutually beneficial deal,” Chu Feng corrected.","“What a way to phrase things. It doesn’t change the fact that you’re making use of her. I can’t accept this,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Oh?” Chu Feng was perplexed.","“My looks, capability, and background are superior to yours. Why did she choose you over me?” Ye Xiancheng turned to Song Yun and said, “Is there a misunderstanding between us? I wish to help you from the bottom of my heart. Why are you doing this to me?”","“That won’t work on me,” Song Yun replied. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Big brother Chu Feng, do you want to do it, or should I do it?”","Their plan was for one of them to enter the formation core and use Song Yun’s treasure to seal off the recovery formation’s energy, lest Ye Xiancheng use it against them.","And Song Yun was already standing in the formation core.","“I’ll do it,” Chu Feng said.","He thought it would be safer for him to deal with Ye Xiancheng.","Song Yun channeled her treasure, and bizarre energy suffused the palace. The crowd could sense the changes happening in the recovery formation.","“A sealing formation. I see you came prepared. Why do you refuse to trust me? Have I ever mistreated you?” Ye Xiancheng asked in confusion.","“Look at his eyes, Chu Feng. He looks so aggrieved and indignant. It doesn’t look like he’s putting on an act. Is he earnest about helping Song Yun?” Eggy asked.","“It could be an act... but even I am starting to think that he is truly in love with Song Yun,” Chu Feng said.","But Song Yun was unfazed by Ye Xiancheng’s remark. Instead, she turned to Chu Feng and urged Chu Feng to make a move. “Big brother Chu Feng.”","“My apologies, but I truly need this formation,” Chu Feng said.","The Ye Immortal Clan might have captured his grandmother, but their actions were reasonable considering the circumstances.","If Song Yun was right, and the Ye Immortal Clan intended to use her as tribute, Chu Feng would be justified in standing up for her as a friend. But if Song Yun had misunderstood Ye Xiancheng, they would be the villains here.","“Apologies? Why are you apologizing to me?” Ye Xiancheng asked.","“I’ll be borrowing this formation,” Chu Feng said.","Ye Xiancheng’s melancholy suddenly faded, replaced by a sinister smile.","Boom!","A powerful golden aura burst forth from Ye Xiancheng’s body and swiftly filled up the palace. Song Yun was astounded.","Both she and Chu Feng felt immense pressure. This pressure surpassed the limits of True God, exceeding even ordinary Heavenly Gods!","Many pairs of glowing eyes appeared in the golden aura as if countless souls were lurking within it. They were the source of this immense pressure.","“You’re underestimating me, Ye Xiancheng, too much. Do you think you can subdue me by taking control of the recovery formation?” Ye Xiancheng sneered.","Boom!","A black aura suddenly gushed from Chu Feng’s body, and it pushed back the golden aura from his vicinity. Taking a closer look, a gate had appeared beside him.","Eggy emerged from the gate. She was emanating an endless stream of black aura, and the Godsoul’s imprint had appeared on her forehead.","“How gorgeous!” Ye Xiancheng was stunned not by Eggy’s might but by her beauty. His melancholic eyes glowed with newfound vigor. He turned to Chu Feng and asked, “I-is she your world spirit?”","Before Chu Feng could answer, he exclaimed in dissatisfaction, “Were you a peach blossom in your previous life?!”","“Huh?” Chu Feng was baffled.","“How can you have such terrific peach blossom luck? My guest elder calls you big brother, and you have such a ravishing world spirit on top of that! How can the world be so unfair?”","“Is that fellow ill in the head?” Eggy was rendered speechless. This was not the time to be rambling about such nonsense.","For some reason, Ye Xiancheng suddenly retracted his golden aura.","Chu Feng turned to Eggy and said, “Eggy, you can stop for now.”","Eggy retracted her black aura as well, and the Godsoul imprint on her forehead vanished. She began gasping for air, and her face looked frighteningly pale.","Chu Feng’s heart ached. Activating the Godsoul must take a massive toll on her, given how she was already strained despite having only maintained it for a short time.","“Miss, it looks like that skill takes a toll on you. You don’t need to go that far. I’m not trying to harm Chu Feng. I just want them to know it won’t be that easy for them to deal with me.”","Ye Xiancheng looked pained when he said those words, almost as if he shared a special bond with Eggy.","His concern left Eggy revulsed, but he paid no heed to it and instead turned to Chu Feng. “Let’s negotiate.”","“What do you want to negotiate?” Chu Feng asked.","His confidence was waning. There was something peculiar about the energy Ye Xiancheng unleashed—it had nothing to do with his bloodline, but it wasn’t a protective formation. It felt like a bundle of energy that was deposited in his body.","Chu Feng deduced it was the Immortal Legacy.","This meant his Protection Bane wouldn’t work against it, so they would have to resort to brute force if they wanted to subdue Ye Xiancheng.","But exerting the Godsoul took a huge toll on Eggy. Resorting to brute force might not be a wise decision here."]},{"number":6363,"title":"Chapter 6363: Chapter 6361: So-so Indeed","paragraphs":["Chapter 6361: So-so Indeed","“I won’t tap into my ancestors’ powers, but you shan’t let your beautiful world spirit intervene either. Let’s have a fair duel between us. If you defeat me, I’ll let you use this formation however you want to. Not only will I cooperate with you, but I’ll also ensure your safe departure.”","“Xiancheng, what nonsense are you spouting?! They have infringed on our Ye Immortal Clan’s honor by barging into our territory! You should kill them straight as the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief! There’s no need to negotiate with them!” the female grand elder bellowed.","Even Chu Feng, despite being in the palace, found her voice jarring.","The female grand elder was panicking. She had prepared this recovery formation for her son, and she couldn’t accept anyone else using it. No matter how wealthy they were, they shouldn’t be squandering their wealth like that!","The Ye Immortal Clan didn’t have a second catalyst treasure at hand!","But Ye Xiancheng had already made up his mind. “Father, mother, let me deal with this since I’m the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief.”","Seeing Ye Xiancheng’s determined gaze, the male grand elder tugged the female grand elder and said, “Let Xiancheng deal with this.”","“We can’t let him have his way for something as important as this!” The female grand elder glared at the male grand elder with eyes of disbelief.","“We’re letting him deal with it because of the severity of the situation. How can he get a firm foothold as the clan chief if we don’t trust his judgment?” the male grand elder said.","The female grand elder froze. She could also see the pros and cons of the situation. In the end, she lowered her head and sighed in reluctance. “Why is my child so foolish?”","“Why are you so certain Xiancheng will lose? He’s our Ye Immortal Clan’s future!” the male grand elder said.","The female grand elder finally snapped out of her daze. She realized she had been too narrow-minded. Chu Feng was a junior like Ye Xiancheng, but he had a resounding reputation. If Ye Xiancheng could defeat Chu Feng, he could take the latter’s place as the strongest junior. That would build his influence not just within the clan but beyond, too.","Seeing that his mother had acquiesced, Ye Xiancheng turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Do you dare to do it?”","“What if I lose?” Chu Feng asked.","“I won’t make things difficult for you if you lose. Just release my ninth brother and hand over your Genesis Bloodline, and I’ll let you leave safely,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Chu Feng, don’t waste your breath on him. I’ll vanquish him,” Eggy said.","Ye Xiancheng scoffed, “Are you a wimp who lets a woman fight on your behalf? Did you earn your reputation by mooching off women?”","Chu Feng laughed. “Let’s do as you say. But if you can’t uphold your promise, I’ll make sure that your Ye Immortal Clan’s lineage ends here.”","Ye Xiancheng’s response rendered Chu Feng speechless. “If I fail to uphold my promise, I’ll sever it myself.”","He gestured to his genitals as he spoke, making his intent clear.","But he failed to understand what Chu Feng was getting at. That was not what Chu Feng was referring to.","“Raise your cultivation to the highest level. I’ll suppress my cultivation to match yours,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“What’s your cultivation level?” Chu Feng asked.","“Me?” Ye Xiancheng smiled confidently.","His robe fluttered, and a powerful aura swept across the palace. The rumors were true. He was at rank nine True God level, just a step away from reaching Heavenly God level.","Chu Feng revealed a faint smile. Lightning crackled around him. Even the area outside the palace was illuminated by nine-colored lightning. He had unleashed Lightning Mark, Lightning Armor, Lightning Wings, and Lightning Armor.","“Lightning Aura! That Chu Feng...” The male grand elder stared in utter shock.","The female grand elder’s lower jaw slackened. She could hardly believe her eyes.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen who had surrounded the area were dumbfounded, too.","Chu Feng had raised his cultivation by four ranks, up to rank nine True God level. As Ancient Era cultivators, they understood the significance of that. In particular, very few cultivators in the Ancient Era had grasped Lightning Aura, and those who did became renowned powerhouses.","Ye Xiancheng was dumbstruck too, but a smirk slowly formed on his lips. “Interesting. No wonder my guest elder calls you big brother. But I wonder if your cultivation is superficial, or if you have the strength to back it up.”","Clang!","Ye Xiancheng flicked his arm, and a spear appeared in his right hand. The emergence of the spear caused the energies in the palace to stir. It was clear at a glance that the spear was a formidable God Armament.","Putting aside its imposing aura, the spear was also exquisitely designed. It had a golden body embedded with pieces of emerald jade, making it look like an artwork. It could be seen from its appearance that it was an invaluable treasure.","Ye Xiancheng didn’t make a move right away. Instead, he stroked the spear and said, “This spear is our Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary treasure, Jade Immortal. Our clansmen respectfully address it as Lord Jade Immortal. No one has been able to wield Jade Immortal since the start of the present era. Even I only won its favor after obtaining the Immortal Legacy.”","He pointed the spear at Chu Feng and said, “You’re fortunate to be the first person to have your blood spilled by the Jade Immortal in my hands.”","“Is that so?”","Chu Feng raised his arms, and the Frenzy Tsunami Saber and the Dragonflame Divine Blade appeared in each of his hands. These were the God Armaments he had received from Little Fishy’s grandfather and the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief.","Ye Xiancheng shook his head. “Your weapons are so-so.","“Is that so?” Chu Feng smiled.","He dashed up to Ye Xiancheng and simultaneously swung both weapons at the latter’s waist.","Ye Xiancheng hurriedly blocked the attacks with his spear.","Clang!","Sparks flew.","Ye Xiancheng skidded backward under the impact.","He had managed to withstand Chu Feng’s attack, but he was pushed very far back. When he finally regained his balance, he looked at Chu Feng with grim eyes.","Chu Feng’s attack was formidable.","Ye Xiancheng realized his opponent was the real deal. His impression of Chu Feng also improved as the latter didn’t exploit his carelessness to push him further. It was the act of a gentleman.","But Ye Xiancheng soon realized Chu Feng wasn’t a gentleman.","“Your weapon is indeed so-so,” Chu Feng sneered."]},{"number":6364,"title":"Chapter 6364: Chapter 6362: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Formless Spearmanship","paragraphs":["Chapter 6362: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Formless Spearmanship","“Interesting. I’ll be getting serious.”","A golden aura surfaced from Ye Xiancheng’s body, flowing down his arm and into his spear. Their auras became identical as if they had become one entity.","“Our Ye Immortal Clan specializes in the spear. Created by our founder and tempered by many generations of ancestors, we eventually developed an invincible spear skill known as Formless Spearmanship. I’ll let you have a taste of it today.”","Ye Xiancheng charged at Chu Feng and swung his spear downward. The spear curved almost like a whip from the immense force.","Chu Feng stood his ground and attempted to deflect the attack with his saber, but the falling spear suddenly vanished, reappearing as a thrust aimed at Chu Feng’s waist.","It was a good thing Chu Feng was prepared for it, and he deflected it with his other blade.","“You have good reflexes, but how long can you continue that?”","Ye Xiancheng continued his assault. Like before, his spear would abruptly vanish just as it was about to strike Chu Feng before reappearing from a completely different direction.","So far, Chu Feng, with his swift reflexes, had stood his ground against Ye Xiancheng’s bizarre spearmanship.","Meanwhile, Eggy and Song Yun observed the battle from the side.","“Is it an illusion? How does he do that?” Eggy was perplexed.","Ye Xiancheng’s parents smiled proudly.","“Chu Feng does live up to his reputation to withstand Xiancheng’s Formless Spearmanship,” the male grand elder remarked.","“Xiancheng has already mastered Formless Spearmanship. Once he gets serious, Chu Feng won’t stand a chance anymore. If Chu Feng thinks he can best Xiancheng in a weaponry duel, he’s sorely mistaken,” the female grand elder sneered.","The other Ye Immortal Clansmen couldn’t conceal their excitement as they watched Chu Feng and Ye Xiancheng’s duel. So far, no other Ye Immortal Clansman had been able to execute the Formless Spearmanship to Ye Xiancheng’s level at his cultivation level.","Even though Ye Xiancheng wasn’t exerting his full prowess, he was still using the Formless Spearmanship. He couldn’t help but feel increasingly amazed by Chu Feng as the latter firmly stood his ground.","“What’s that saber art you’re using, Chu Feng? I’m surprised it can stand against my Formless Spearmanship.”","“I don’t have a fixed saber art. It’s merely the way I deal with my enemies,” Chu Feng replied.","“Aren’t you being too secretive, Chu Feng? I can tell it’s much more than that. Your saber art has already neutralized my attacks many times.” Ye Xiancheng didn’t believe Chu Feng.","“It isn’t a saber art because it works with a saber, a sword, a spear, or a stick. These are the moves I have developed from the combat experience I have accrued. Your spearmanship is amazing indeed. Your so-called Formless Spearmanship is about mixing real attacks with feints, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“You’re able to see through parts of it? Tell me more. Let me see if you’re right or not,” Ye Xiancheng urged.","“Your feints aren’t illusions but attacks that can be changed instantaneously. It would require extreme physical control to pull them off. It must have taken you quite some time to master this spearmanship, right?” Chu Feng said.","“Indeed, I spent more time learning this spearmanship than other means. You have a sharp eye, but can you tell whether I have gotten serious yet?” Ye Xiancheng asked.","“You are serious, but you have yet to reveal your full strength,” Chu Feng replied.","“You saw through that? Interesting. Not only can you match me in fighting prowess, but you have a sharp eye as well. Chu Feng, you are a good rival. I can hardly bear to hurt you. Why don’t you surrender? It’ll at least spare you from some pain,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Do you know why I haven’t used any martial skills?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’d prove that you’re inferior to me if you resort to martial skills first. You don’t want to embarrass yourself in front of my guest elder,” Ye Xiancheng pointed out.","“The result is what matters in a fight between cultivators. I don’t care about the rest,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why don’t you tell me the reason?” Ye Xiancheng’s curiosity was piqued.","“Your spearmanship and fighting prowess are formidable. It’s hard to come by an opponent like you. I ought to use this opportunity to temper myself,” Chu Feng replied.","He meant it. It was difficult to find an opponent who was strong and skilled. This was a rare chance for him to hone and advance his weaponry mastery.","“Hah! You’re treating me as a sparring partner? My spear won’t show mercy. Don’t blame me for not holding back if you fail to dodge in time!”","Ye Xiancheng laughed. He seemed to enjoy sparring with Chu Feng. His spearmanship suddenly became sharper and more aggressive. To outsiders, it looked as if he was raining a barrage of attacks on Chu Feng.","But Chu Feng remained unscathed under Ye Xiancheng’s relentless attacks. He didn’t even retreat a single step. He proved to be capable of standing on equal ground with Ye Xiancheng. In fact, he was beginning to transition from defense to offense.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen couldn’t believe that Chu Feng was rivaling the Formless Spearmanship’s offensive prowess.","Even the two grand elders’ proud smiles were fading. Their son was formidable, but somehow, his attacks failed to faze Chu Feng no matter how hard he struck, as if he were striking a bed of cotton.","This could only mean one thing—Chu Feng wasn’t exerting his full strength either. He was still holding back even at this point. This didn’t bode well for them.","The strongest junior of the present era was far more unfathomable than they had imagined.","“Xiancheng, this concerns our clan’s recovery formation. You mustn’t get careless. Quickly go all out and conclude this duel!” the male grand elder sent a voice transmission over.","“Chu Feng, I acknowledge you as a rival, but it’s time to end this fight. Don’t blame me for this.”","Boom!","Furious flames and waves of water suddenly gushed forth from Chu Feng’s weapons—these were the special means of his God Armaments. The clash between fire and water produced a thick fog that blocked one’s vision.","“Hmph!”","Ye Xiancheng was unfazed. He closed his eyes to use his other senses to track Chu Feng’s movements. He had undergone special training to enhance his other senses in preparation for such a situation.","Uwa!","He suddenly felt a sharp pain in his chest.","Chu Feng had kicked him in his chest, sending him flying.","“You have lost.” Chu Feng stared at Ye Xiancheng while fiddling with his God Armaments.","His meaning was clear.","Ye Xiancheng would have died if the earlier attack had not been a kick but a slash."]},{"number":6365,"title":"Chapter 6365: Chapter 6363: Not Even Three God Taboos Are Enough to Triumph Over Chu Feng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6363: Not Even Three God Taboos Are Enough to Triumph Over Chu Feng","“Why couldn’t I sense you earlier?” Ye Xiancheng stared at Chu Feng in disbelief after steadying his posture.","Chu Feng smiled as he revealed his spirit power.","“A formation?” Ye Xiancheng looked conflicted.","“The fog was a feint; it was my formation that obstructed your vision. If my formation can hinder your vision, it goes without saying that it can hinder your senses too,” Chu Feng replied.","Ye Xiancheng was baffled. “You’re a rank three True Dragon World Spiritist. How can you obstruct my senses?”","“That’s the power of formations,” Chu Feng replied.","“Forget it. It doesn’t matter how you did it. I got careless and paid the price for it, but the same goes for you as well, Chu Feng. Do you get what I mean?” Ye Xiancheng said, refusing to admit defeat.","“I won’t go easy the next time,” Chu Feng replied with a smile, but his eyes turned cold.","The change in Chu Feng’s gaze sent shivers down Ye Xiancheng’s spine. He felt a tinge of fear. He knew that he couldn’t let his guard down anymore, especially with the upper echelons of his Ye Immortal Clan spectating this battle.","This battle was not just about the recovery formation; it also concerned Ye Xiancheng’s standing in the Ye Immortal Clan.","Ye Xiancheng formed a hand seal.","An orb of golden light floated from his fingertip, and it expanded until it was over ten thousand meters in diameter. The palace was huge, but its space was limited. The orb filled up the palace as if the sun had descended upon the world.","Ye Xiancheng didn’t activate the orb right away. He changed his hand seal, and a golden aura seeped from his finger and shrouded his body. This resembled Chu Feng’s Lightning Armor, but the golden aura carried a tinge of divinity.","“This is rank three God Taboo, Heaven Protection,” Ye Xiancheng explained.","He changed his hand seal, and another surge of golden aura seeped from his fingertip. This time, the golden aura transformed into divine runes. These runes flowed through his Immortal Protection and into his legs.","“This is rank three God Taboo Heaven Footwork,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“What about that? I don’t think that’s just for decoration, is it?” Chu Feng pointed to the golden orb floating above them.","Ye Xiancheng had introduced the latter two means, but he neglected to talk about the golden orb he had first summoned.","“You’ll find out if you prove to be strong enough, but I’ll tell you that my rank three God Taboo Martial Skills serve to facilitate it.”","Ye Xiancheng raised his spear once more and pointed it at Chu Feng. His aura was completely different from before. It had become much more domineering, reminiscent of a deity.","“You shall have the honor of witnessing the true prowess of our Ye Immortal Clan’s Formless Spearmanship,” Ye Xiancheng said as he prepared to make a move.","Chu Feng suddenly raised his hand and said, “Wait.”","Ye Xiancheng asked, “Are you going to surrender?”","Chu Feng smiled. “What other means do you have? You can go ahead and use them all. I’m going to get serious too, so you should bring out everything you have lest you regret it later.”","“Hah! These are my hidden cards, Brother Chu Feng. Why don’t you show me what you have?” Ye Xiancheng said. He stopped here to give Chu Feng a chance to reveal his means.","“I’m already using it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? I don’t sense anything at all.” Ye Xiancheng was confused, but he remained vigilant.","Nothing was different about Chu Feng, but he was so confident that it felt like there was more than meets the eye.","Chu Feng sensed Ye Xiancheng’s unease and said, “We can stop here if you surrender now. Otherwise, I won’t hold back anymore.”","“Please don’t, Brother Chu Feng, for I am not going to hold back either.”","Shoosh!","Ye Xiancheng morphed into a surge of golden light and instantly arrived before Chu Feng. He flung his spear toward Chu Feng’s arm with such great force that it would shatter the latter’s arm if it landed.","All of a sudden, his face warped in horror. He anxiously retracted his spear and retreated frantically.","But Chu Feng didn’t make a move at all. He was still maintaining the same stance as before.","The female grand elder thought Ye Xiancheng had gone easy on Chu Feng, so she sent a voice transmission, “Xiancheng, there’s no need to hold back.”","“I’m not holding back. I sensed an intense murderous aura. It was not coming from Chu Feng but his God Armament. It felt extremely dangerous. My gut feeling told me that I’d die if I clashed with it,” Ye Xiancheng replied.","“He’s a world spiritist. He is capable of all kinds of lowly means. Don’t fall for his tricks,” the female grand elder said.","“Xiancheng, you need to trust our ancestors’ martial skills. You have already mastered the Formless Spearmanship and activated the three God Taboos. Chu Feng might be formidable, but he can’t possibly be a match for you,” the male grand elder reminded.","Ye Xiancheng dropped his hesitation and attacked once more.","But this time, he didn’t charge at Chu Feng. He stood his ground and unleashed a barrage of spear thrusts at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng stood his ground, not bothering to dodge. He casually brandished his swords, unleashing a burst of flame and water that formed a protective barrier to keep the spears at bay.","All of a sudden, Ye Xiancheng appeared behind Chu Feng. It turned out the earlier attack was merely a feint.","“This battle is over.”","Ye Xiancheng thrust his spear toward Chu Feng’s back.","But Chu Feng suddenly turned around and looked at him with an eerie smile.","Ye Xiancheng was stunned. Before he could figure out what was going on, he felt a gust of wind, and a God Armament saber flew toward his flank. He hurriedly changed his spear trajectory via the Formless Spearmanship.","But Chu Feng predicted his response and struck with the other saber too.","Ye Xiancheng had no choice but to hold his spear vertically to deflect the two attacks.","Clang!","The weapons clashed, and sparks flew. Ye Xiancheng was knocked back.","Ye Xiancheng felt his hands turning numb. Chu Feng’s sabers were much heavier than he had expected.","Before he could steady his posture, Chu Feng chased after him and unleashed a barrage of slashes at him.","Ye Xiancheng was able to deflect the attacks, but he was shocked by how the situation had played out. He was the one who launched a surprise assault, but not only did he fail, but the tables were turned on him in an instant, and he was forced to go on the defensive.","Fortunately, he was much stronger now after activating his God Taboos, allowing him to withstand Chu Feng’s sharp attacks.","“Is it my imagination? He seems to have grown stronger.” Ye Xiancheng frowned.","“How can Chu Feng keep up with our Xiancheng after he has unleashed his God Taboos?”","The female grand elder couldn’t believe her eyes. She could also tell that Chu Feng had gotten stronger than before. Has he been this strong all along, just that he was holding back earlier?","“What’s going on, Chu Feng?”","Even Eggy was confused. She knew Chu Feng better than anyone else in the world, but even she could tell he was stronger than before."]},{"number":6366,"title":"Chapter 6366: Chapter 6364: A Competition of Speed? Who’s Afraid of Who?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6364: A Competition of Speed? Who’s Afraid of Who?","Despite her curiosity, Eggy refrained from asking to avoid distracting Chu Feng. Instead, she kept a close eye on Ye Xiancheng’s movements, ready to intervene lest the latter hurt Chu Feng.","That said, she would not make a move unless Chu Feng’s life was at risk, as her intervention spelled Chu Feng’s defeat.","“It’s an Ancient Era’s secret skill,” Chu Feng told Eggy via voice transmission. He was explaining it to her because he sharply noticed that she was curious.","“You still have the energy to chat with me?” Eggy asked excitedly.","The fact that Chu Feng could still pay attention to her in an intense battle showed that he was nowhere near cornered.","“The third God Taboo, Heaven Suppression,” Ye Xiancheng suddenly said.","The golden orb on the ceiling suddenly exerted immense pressure, suppressing Chu Feng’s fighting prowess. It worked in a way similar to Chu Feng’s Divine Might—its suppression was not as strong, but its effect was continuous.","If both sides were equally matched, the weakening of one party’s fighting prowess was bound to affect the result of the duel.","Naturally, the tides of the battle changed. Ye Xiancheng claimed the initiative and unleashed a barrage of spear thrusts at Chu Feng.","The true prowess of the Formless Spearmanship showed in his fierce assault.","Chu Feng was forced to retreat. He dodged all the killing blows, but he was no longer as relaxed as before.","“I see. So this is the power of your third God Taboo. I’ll let you have a taste of my power too then,” Chu Feng said.","Both his God Armaments glowed golden, and his fighting prowess further increased.","“What’s that? A secret art?”","Ye Xiancheng noticed that the God Armaments’ glow came from Chu Feng’s body.","Weapon avatars manifested behind Chu Feng, and his fighting prowess increased correspondingly. By the time nine weapon avatars appeared, his fighting prowess had already reached a terrifying level.","Despite having unleashed Heaven Suppression, Ye Xiancheng found himself struggling with Chu Feng’s attacks. In the end, he failed to block one of Chu Feng’s slashes and was struck in the shoulder.","Shoosh!","Ye Xiancheng suddenly vanished as if an apparition and reappeared at the opposite end of the palace.","Chu Feng noticed golden runes on Ye Xiancheng’s legs. The same runes had appeared when he activated Heaven Footwork earlier.","“Oh? So you haven’t truly used Heaven Footwork yet?” Chu Feng asked.","“Chu Feng, did you think my strongest means is Heaven Suppression? You’re wrong. It’s my Heaven Footwork. My cultivation is stuck at True God level, but through Heaven Footwork, I am capable of achieving speed comparable to a rank one Heavenly God. You can’t defeat me, and I doubt that secret skill of yours will last long. Victory will be mine in the end,” Ye Xiancheng said.","He was putting on a brave front. By now, it had become clear to him that it wouldn’t be easy for him to defeat Chu Feng. Formless Spearmanship was strongest at close-quarter combat. It was possible to employ it from a distance, but it wouldn’t be enough to faze Chu Feng.","His only option was to stall for time, till Chu Feng ran out of energy.","Right after he said those words, Chu Feng’s voice echoed behind him, “Is that so?”","But Chu Feng was still in his line of sight a second ago, and there was a safe distance between them. How could the other party suddenly appear behind him without him realizing it?","“You!!!” Ye Xiancheng was horrified. He quickly used Heaven Footwork, causing the golden runes on his legs to glow with greater brilliance than before.","Yet, he failed to escape from Chu Feng.","Chu Feng flitted up to him like a specter, stowed away his God Armament saber, and thrust his palm forth. The attack had come so abruptly that Ye Xiancheng had no time to dodge.","Ye Xiancheng thought Chu Feng was going easy on him, but he quickly realized he was mistaken when a black aura seeped from Chu Feng’s palm into his body.","“What did you do?” Ye Xiancheng panicked.","He sensed something was being siphoned away from his body. It felt bizarre, and it unnerved him.","“I said I won’t go easy on you,” Chu Feng sneered.","He was using his secret skill, Dark Plunder. It allowed him to steal skills that were shown to him and even utilize them at a higher mastery than the person whom he stole the skills from.","That was why Chu Feng had been so patient with Ye Xiancheng. It was to lay the groundwork needed for him to acquire Ye Xiancheng’s skills. The more Ye Xiancheng revealed, the more he could steal through Dark Plunder.","“Chu Feng, don’t even dream about escaping alive if you dare hurt Xiancheng!” the female grand elder bellowed.","It was an empty threat. Ye Xiancheng was already in Chu Feng’s grasp, after all.","“Don’t worry. I still need his formation. I won’t hurt him just yet.”","Chu Feng retracted his palm after using Dark Plunder.","In truth, he had a much better impression of Ye Xiancheng now. The latter could have tapped into his Immortal Legacy to kill him instead of engaging in this battle—that was also the reason Eggy had been eyeing him vigilantly.","Despite having sensed Dark Plunder’s peculiarity, Ye Xiancheng still didn’t tap into his ancestor’s powers. This showed that he kept his promises, even though he refused to admit defeat earlier when Chu Feng kicked him down.","“What did you just use on me? Is it just to intimidate me? I sensed you were taking something from me, but somehow, I’m unharmed?” Ye Xiancheng stood up to assess his body while eyeing Chu Feng with narrowed eyes.","“It’s a secret.” Chu Feng smiled.","If Ye Xiancheng learned that the exclusive skills of the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief he had spent many years learning had just been stolen by Chu Feng, he wouldn’t be able to take it."]},{"number":6367,"title":"Chapter 6367: Chapter 6365: Treatment Failed?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6365: Treatment Failed?","“Forget it. How were you able to move so fast? That’s beyond what a True God level cultivator is capable of,” Ye Xiancheng remarked.","“I have my tricks too. I have never been outdone by cultivators of the same level in terms of speed,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","His earlier burst of speed was from the Divine Deer’s Divine Flitting. He was already faster than all True God level cultivators by the time his cultivation reached rank six True God level, and his cultivation was now at rank nine True God level.","Even rank two Heavenly Gods would struggle to keep up with him.","Ye Xiancheng’s God Taboo was formidable, but the Divine Deer’s means were far superior.","“Brother Chu Feng, you live up to your reputation. You possess far stronger skills than I could have expected, and such skills can’t be grasped by just anyone. You are truly formidable. I have underestimated you.”","Ye Xiancheng altered his hand seal, and the recovery formation’s energy gushed out. He pointed his finger at Chu Feng, and the formation’s energy was transferred through him as a medium toward Chu Feng.","“You’re keeping your promise,” Chu Feng remarked.","“I’d have to castrate myself if I don’t uphold my promise. I still intend on having children,” Ye Xiancheng replied.","“A person of your character is bound to have plenty of offspring,” Chu Feng said.","“Haa, I’ve already thought things through. There’s no point being bound by my feelings,” Ye Xiancheng said as he eyed Song Yun.","But Song Yun acted as if she didn’t notice his gaze.","“Brother Chu, I’ll let you use the formation’s energy, but I ask you to spare my big brother,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“No problem. I’ll release your Ninth Brother if I can safely leave this place,” Chu Feng replied as he eyed the area outside the palace.","Ye Xiancheng looked like a trustworthy person thus far; there was no need for him to transfer the recovery formation over if he wasn’t planning to uphold his promise in the first place. But the same was not necessarily true about his parents.","“Mm.” Ye Xiancheng understood Chu Feng’s concern and nodded. “Hurry up and use the formation’s energy to treat my guest elder.”","Chu Feng didn’t make a move right away. He opened a spirit formation gate and brought his grandmother out from within. Then, he finally channeled the formation.","The formation’s energy simultaneously imbued Chu Feng’s grandmother, Ye Xiancheng, Eggy, and Song Yun.","Ye Xiancheng was surprised. On the one hand, he didn’t expect Chu Feng to use the formation on him. On the other hand, he was shocked that Chu Feng was simultaneously treating four people with different conditions.","This would have been beyond his means, but Chu Feng did it with ease. He remarked, “As expected of a world spiritist.”","Shortly after, Chu Feng began to frown.","The one who fared the best among the four was Ye Xiancheng, as his condition wasn’t that severe in the first place. The recovery energy was more than enough to nurse him back to full health; the Ye Immortal Clan was being wasteful going to such lengths.","That explained why Ye Xiancheng was willing to gamble with the recovery formation. He understood his condition the best.","Next was Eggy. She had received a backlash from using the Godsoul’s power. The recovery formation could alleviate her symptoms, but it couldn’t treat the root of the problem. Ultimately, she still had to suffer the pain of the backlash.","Chu Feng felt a sharp pain in his chest. Eggy was putting on a calm appearance despite the pain she was suffering from the backlash. Her strong front only made him more worried.","The God Curse planted on Chu Feng’s grandmother was extremely potent, such that the recovery formation couldn't lift it. However, it was a separate issue from his grandmother’s mental state.","That said, his grandmother was in a highly unstable mental state that even the recovery formation, which had easily resolved the flaws in Ye Xiancheng’s inheritance, couldn’t do much about it.","But the one who was in the worst state wasn’t Chu Feng’s grandmother but Song Yun.","Even though she looked fine on the surface, her body was practically hollowed out. Her days were numbered. She must have paid a terrible price for the fortuitous encounter.","Chu Feng looked at Song Yun.","Sensing his gaze, Song Yun smiled radiantly at him. “It’s fine, big brother Chu Feng. You can try your best. I was just grasping at straws in the first place.”","She read his thoughts.","“I’ll try my best,” Chu Feng replied.","While Chu Feng was treating the four of them with the recovery formation, the female grand elder turned around and took her leave. The male grand elder tried to stop her, but the female grand elder was so determined that he eventually gave in.","...","As time passed, the recovery formation’s energy was swiftly depleted.","Ye Xiancheng and Eggy’s issues had already been resolved. Only Chu Feng’s grandmother and Song Yun were still imbued by the recovery formation’s energy.","Chu Feng couldn’t believe how difficult it was to heal his grandmother’s mental state. It made him wonder if there were other reasons behind his grandmother’s madness other than the shock she had suffered back then.","Could she have been too obsessed with raising her strength that she suffered a cultivation deviation?","As for Song Yun, Chu Feng had concluded that the recovery formation was incapable of resolving her issue at its root, so he sought to alleviate her symptoms and extend her lifespan instead.","That would buy her time to venture into the Ninth Galaxy. The current eight galaxies were shells of their former glory; only the Ninth Galaxy retained its original state. What was impossible in the eight galaxies could be possible in the Ninth Galaxy.","Eventually, all the energy in the recovery formation was depleted.","Ye Xiancheng nodded in awe.","He had been observing Chu Feng all this while. Despite simultaneously treating multiple people, Chu Feng still managed to utilize the recovery formation’s energy to its fullest potential and didn’t waste it in the slightest.","“You’re incredible, big brother Chu Feng!”","Song Yun headed over to Chu Feng’s side with a brilliant smile. She could sense from her current condition that she was at least temporarily free from her ailment.","“That’s all I can do, but there’s still hope. The Ninth Galaxy is the true heart of the world of cultivation. You might find a cure for your condition there,” Chu Feng said.","“I have heard about that, and I was intending to head there too. I didn’t have enough time back then, but now... I am confident. It’s all thanks to you, big brother Chu Feng,” Song Yun said with an earnest smile.","“Thank you, Brother Chu.” Ye Xiancheng clasped his fist and thanked Chu Feng.","“Why are you thanking me? I should be the one thanking you for allowing me to use your recovery formation to treat my grandmother,” Chu Feng replied.","“I promised to relinquish the recovery formation to you if I lost, but you still healed me nevertheless. It’s only right for me to thank you for that,” Ye Xiancheng said."]},{"number":6368,"title":"Chapter 6368: Chapter 6366: Grandmother Waking Up, the Cemetery’s Summon?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6366: Grandmother Waking Up, the Cemetery’s Summon?","“This fellow is an interesting one. I wonder if he’ll still be grateful to you if he knows that you have stolen his Heaven Suppression, Heaven Protection, Heaven Footwork, and Formless Spearmanship with your Dark Plunder,” Eggy snickered behind Chu Feng.","Needless to say, only Chu Feng could hear her words.","“How’s our grandmother?” Eggy and Song Yun turned to look at Chu Feng’s grandmother.","Chu Feng’s grandmother was still unconscious.","“Her condition is stable now, but I’ll have to find other ways to treat her.”","Chu Feng looked at his grandmother with pained eyes. Through the treatment, he realized that his grandmother was not only mad, but she was also constantly tortured by her mental state.","She must have been living in anguish all this while.","“My clan’s recovery formation failed to work on her?” Ye Xiancheng was surprised.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng released an unconscious figure with a wave of his sleeves. It was the Ninth Young Master, whom he had taken control of a while back.","“He’s unconscious due to the effects of my formation, but he’ll recover soon,” Chu Feng explained.","“Brother Chu, I suspect that my mother has headed off to channel our clan’s ancestral formation. My parents are stubborn in their ways. I might be the clan chief, but they are still the ones who call the shots in the Ye Immortal Clan.","“My parents would have realized you’re not to be underestimated after you slipped past our defenses and rescued your grandmother. They will spare no effort in channeling our ancestral formation this time around.","“You can hold me hostage. They won’t dare to hurt you as long as I’m in your hands. They should let you leave,” Ye Xiancheng told Chu Feng via voice transmission.","“Thank you, Brother Ye.”","Chu Feng was intending to do that. The last thing he wanted was for Eggy to put her life on the line to withstand the Ye Immortal Clan’s ancestral formation. It was one thing for him to do it, but it was another thing for Ye Xiancheng to offer himself to be held hostage.","Ye Xiancheng smiled. He turned to Song Yun and asked, “Guest elder, are you still reluctant to tell me your real name?”","“Song Yun,” Song Yun replied.","“That’s a wonderful name.” Ye Xiancheng nodded. He turned to Eggy and asked, “What about this miss? May I know your name?”","Eggy ignored him.","But Ye Xiancheng was unfazed. He replied with a smile, “Beautiful women ought to have spunk, especially one as gorgeous as you.”","All of a sudden, Chu Feng, Song Yun, and Ye Xiancheng raised their heads to look at the sky. The male grand elder and the other Ye Immortal Clansmen did the same too.","Something was happening with the Immemorial Cemetery. Its phenomenon was becoming increasingly clearer, and bizarre flashes of light shone from within. It looked even more majestic than God’s Era.","“What’s happening there?” Ye Xiancheng murmured.","Chu Feng’s grandmother suddenly opened her eyes and stood up.","“Grandmother!” Chu Feng called out.","But his grandmother suddenly vanished. She reappeared outside the palace, above the warship. She looked at the Immemorial Cemetery with deep eyes that emanated some sort of power.","Even outsiders could tell that she was observing the changes in the Immemorial Cemetery using some kind of means.","“Capture her,” a voice echoed.","Several Ye Immortal Clan’s elders charged at Chu Feng’s grandmother. They knew how important she was to Chu Feng, so they wanted to capture her to blackmail him.","Boom!","Flames suddenly ignited around Chu Feng’s grandmother, suffusing the world with its intense heat.","The elders vaporized before they could even come close to the flames.","“Hold your ground!” the male grand elder furiously bellowed. “Who asked you to make a move?”","None of the Ye Immortal Clansmen would have dared to make a move even if he didn’t tell them to hold their ground. Even though the flames had extinguished, the crowd still felt intimidated as if death was staring right at them.","“Chu Feng.”","Eggy looked at Chu Feng with fury in her eyes. She wanted to make a move since the Ye Immortal Clan had already bared their fangs at them.","“I doubt they will be able to do anything to my grandmother.”","Chu Feng was much calmer in comparison. He wasn’t worried about his grandmother’s safety.","Just then, a golden light sprouted from the ground and manifested into several humongous avatars that were tens of thousands of meters tall. They commanded transcendent auras and harnessed tremendous power within them.","These avatars continued to expand until they surrounded this realm.","“It’s our ancestral formation. My mother has put all our treasures into awakening our ancestral formation.” Ye Xiancheng frowned.","But Chu Feng remained unfazed.","There was no question that the ancestral formation was formidable—its aura surpassed even rank four Heavenly Gods. But he noticed how his grandmother had calmly turned her attention back to the Immemorial Cemetery after dealing with the Ye Immortal Clan’s elders.","Her composure was so unwavering that it didn’t seem to be just because she was not in the right state of mind. Her composure was grounded in her strength.","“I wonder how strong my grandmother is,” Chu Feng murmured out of curiosity.","She didn’t reveal her cultivation even when she unleashed the devastating flames that burnt the Ye Immortal Clan’s elders to a crisp. This showed how formidable she was.","“Ye Immortal Clansmen, heed my orders. Capture that woman!”","The female grand elder suddenly appeared in the sky with a golden token in hand. That golden token emanated the same aura as the hundreds of golden avatars that sealed off this realm.","The male grand elder also took out a similar token, and his body radiated a golden glow. He rose into the air and stood next to the female grand elder.","“You really used it all?” the male grand elder asked.","“Xiancheng might be foolish, but we can’t be the same as him. We can’t let Chu Feng get away,” the female grand elder said.","“Father, mother, what are you doing? I made a deal with Chu Feng to let them leave safely if he defeated me. Are you going to make me break my promise?” Ye Xiancheng asked from the palace.","“Xiancheng, you have inherited our clan’s Immortal Legacy. Our ancestors are protecting you. He doesn’t have the means to hurt you. You might have held back earlier because you wanted to pit your strength against Chu Feng’s, but if you let him capture you now, I’d have no choice but to think that you’re putting on an act with him. Don’t blame me if I ignore your safety if so,” the female grand elder said.","“Mother, you...” Ye Xiancheng felt helpless.","He didn’t expect his mother to see through their ploy."]},{"number":6369,"title":"Chapter 6369: Chapter 6367: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Ancestral Formation? I’ll Make Quick Work Of It!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6367: The Ye Immortal Clan’s Ancestral Formation? I’ll Make Quick Work Of It!","“Xiancheng, Chu Feng possesses extraordinary means. The rumors must be true. He must have obtained the Genesis Bloodline. That’s a legendary power! If we obtain it, our clan can surpass our ancestors and reach an unprecedented height. This concerns our clan’s future. It’s not the time for you to be wilful. We must capture Chu Feng!” the female grand elder said.","The other Ye Immortal Clansmen whipped out similar tokens. Their bodies radiated golden glows, and the hundreds of humongous avatars sealing off the realm grew even larger.","It might look as if they were receiving power from their ancestral formation, but they were also channeling it as well. Under the Ye Immortal Clan’s channeling, the humongous avatars’ auras became increasingly powerful, and their forms started to change as well.","Brilliant eyes that were as large as the sun glowed spiritedly as they looked toward the warship.","Chu Feng felt stifled under their gaze. It was as if he was facing the judgment of gods. A mortal’s soul would have dissipated under those eyes.","It was not difficult to imagine the terrifying prowess they wielded. They could easily destroy a realm at their whim.","Even Chu Feng was starting to feel intimidated. But when he looked at his grandmother, who was still assessing the Immemorial Cemetery, unfazed by everything that was happening here, he regained his confidence and turned to Ye Xiancheng’s parents.","“To think the most reasonable person in the Ye Immortal Clan is a junior. You covet the Genesis Bloodline, yet you don’t have the eyes to see that my grandmother towers above you. You have lived in vain if you can’t even tell as much.","“Even beasts choose their enemies, but you two are worse than beasts. Just two blind, old dogs at best,” Chu Feng sneered.","Ye Xiancheng interjected, “Brother Chu, those are my parents. You shouldn’t insult them.”","“Brother Ye, I see you as a friend, but your parents are after my life. Should I be praising them for doing a good job?” Chu Feng replied.","Ye Xiancheng was rendered speechless. Those words made perfect sense.","“Hah! You’re saying your grandmother is stronger than us and our ancestral formation? Your head is in the clouds after slipping away from us once. Open your eyes wide and take a good look! Witness the prowess of our ancestral formation! Mere mortals can never defy immortals like us! You won’t escape from here no matter how despicable your means!” the female grand elder sneered.","“You should open your eyes to how ignorant you are,” Chu Feng sneered.","“Continue barking. The more you bark, the worse your grandmother suffers.”","The female grand elder formed a hand seal. The world shook. The hundreds of humongous golden avatars surrounding the realm had begun moving. Gigantic hands appeared above the clouds, reaching for the warship.","Space distorted. The earth cracked.","Those residing in this realm were panicking. No one was paying heed to the Immemorial Cemetery anymore, and they couldn’t even if they wanted to. Their line of vision was blocked by the gigantic hands. To them, they thought the end of the world had arrived.","And it was not just this realm.","This phenomenon was even grander when the God Clan’s God Mother awakened back then. Should the Ye Immortal Clan wish for it, they could destroy the surrounding realms, too. This was the prowess of their ancestral formation.","Chu Feng’s grandmother sensed the ancestral formation’s hostility, so she turned her gaze from the Immemorial Cemetery to the female grand elder.","A mere gaze was all it took for the female grand elder’s face to turn pale. She had never felt so pressured by anyone’s gaze before. She had chosen the wrong enemy to mess with!","Boom!","Intense flames suddenly ignited around Chu Feng’s grandmother. They split into hundreds of flame dragons that gushed toward the sky at amazing speeds!","These flame dragons coiled around the descending palms before climbing up the humongous avatars’ arms. It didn’t take long for all the avatars to be bound in flames.","The humongous avatars thrashed in fright, a stark comparison to their earlier majesty.","Before the crowd could even process the situation, flames suddenly erupted around the humongous avatars, obliterating them all.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s ancestral formation had been breached!","Flames engulfed the sky.","Uwa!","All Ye Immortal Clansmen, who had been channeling the ancestral formation via their tokens, spurted blood. This was the backlash from the destruction of the ancestral formation.","Even Ye Xiancheng’s parents were no exception, though they fared better than the other clansmen. They were the only ones floating in the sky while the others plummeted to the ground. Only the Heavenly God level cultivators managed to retain their consciousness.","But Ye Xiancheng’s parents didn’t have the spare attention to worry about their injured clansmen. They looked at the sky with eyes filled with despair.","The flames that had engulfed the sky were descending upon them.","The female grand elder fell to her knees. She finally realized that Chu Feng’s words weren’t just a threat. How could she have been so foolish as to fail to recognize the terror before her?","Even Chu Feng was stunned. He had guessed his grandmother was strong, but he didn’t expect her to be this powerful.","The Ye Immortal Clan’s ancestral formation was, by no means, weak. Yet, it was completely powerless against his grandmother.","It was a completely one-sided obliteration!","And that meant that they weren’t even on the same level.","“Just how strong are you, grandmother?” Chu Feng murmured out of curiosity.","“Chu Feng, please spare my clan.”","A pair of hands suddenly clutched Chu Feng’s thighs. Chu Feng looked over and saw Ye Xiancheng kneeling before him with pleading eyes.","Chu Feng looked to the sky and shouted, “Grandmother!”","He would have to intervene even if Ye Xiancheng didn’t utter a word. His grandmother was irrational—her attack was going to destroy everything in this realm, including him and Eggy.","His shout worked.","Chu Feng’s grandmother was momentarily dazed as if she had just awoken from a dream. Then, she abruptly turned her eyes to Chu Feng. Her gaze changed when she saw him.","Her domineering demeanor gave way to a doting grandmother gazing upon her grandson."]},{"number":6370,"title":"Chapter 6370: Chapter 6368: Brief Reunion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6368: Brief Reunion","“Feng... Feng’er,” Song Luoyi called out to Chu Feng carefully as if worrying that she would frighten him if she was too loud.","“It’s me, grandmother. It’s me,” Chu Feng quickly replied.","He was both surprised and overjoyed. He thought his grandmother wouldn’t recognize him, and that he would have to explain himself. He didn’t think she would recognize him at a glance.","“Feng’er. It really is Feng’er!”","The flames covering the sky went out. Even the heat dissipated.","Ye Xiancheng’s parents breathed a sigh of relief.","Song Luoyi looked at Chu Feng with trembling lips as tears brimmed in her eyes. She looked choked up with emotion.","“Grandmother.”","Chu Feng flew forth from the palace and went up to Song Luoyi.","“Am I dreaming?” Song Luoyi murmured in self-doubt.","She couldn’t believe her eyes, especially since she was often in the wrong state of mind. Such blissful reunions had only existed in her dreams, but she would then wake up and revert to her mindless state.","“Grandmother, this isn’t a dream. I am Chu Feng,” Chu Feng said.","He also felt choked up, seeing his grandmother’s reddened eyes and disbelieving gaze. She was so often in a frenzied state that she shouldn’t have recognized him, but it would appear that she was still taking in news from her surroundings. That would explain why she recognized him right away when her mind cleared up.","His grandmother’s suffering was greater than he could have imagined.","She wanted to regain her clarity of mind to protect the people she cared about, but she was unable to do so. That was her greatest regret.","“Feng’er, y-you have suffered.”","Song Luoyi couldn’t hold back her feelings, and tears streamed down her cheeks. She gently touched his cheeks with trembling hands. Her body was quivering too.","Chu Feng must have been important to her for someone of her strength to break down like that.","“Grandmother, I’m fine.”","Chu Feng shook his head. It was as if he had transformed from the strongest junior in the world of cultivation into an obedient child, Song Luoyi’s grandson.","That made Song Luoyi’s lips quiver even more. Countless words and questions were at the tip of her tongue, but she struggled to voice them aloud at this moment.","Just then, another change happened to the Immemorial Cemetery.","The words ‘God Curse’ reappeared on Song Luoyi’s forehead. The concern in her eyes gave way to impassiveness. She turned from Chu Feng as if he were a mere stranger to look at the Immemorial Cemetery.","“Grandmother!” Chu Feng called out as he quickly formed a hand seal.","He had planted a formation inside his grandmother’s mind via the recovery formation while treating her. The purpose of the formation was to help her temporarily regain her clarity of mind.","Yet, his means failed.","Song Luoyi didn’t react at all. She vanished the next instant.","Chu Feng sensed that she had left for the Immemorial Cemetery.","“Is it the God Curse? Is there a connection between the God Curse and the Immemorial Cemetery? Or has my grandmother sensed something inside the Immemorial Cemetery?” Chu Feng murmured with a conflicted look.","It hadn’t been easy for him to reunite with his grandmother, but they parted ways over this inexplicable reason.","“Chu Feng, where did your grandmother go?” Eggy flitted over to Chu Feng’s side and asked.","“She probably went to the Immemorial Cemetery,” Chu Feng replied.","“The Immemorial Cemetery? Why is she going there? Hold on. Now that I think about it, your grandmother seemed to have regained consciousness because of the Immemorial Cemetery’s phenomenon. Is your grandmother drawn to something there?” Eggy asked.","“That appears to be the case,” Chu Feng replied.","Song Yun flitted over to Chu Feng’s side too.","“We should leave now.”","She whipped out a talisman paper and crushed it. A surge of teleportation energy enveloped Chu Feng and Eggy.","The next moment, they appeared a very far distance away from the warship.","Song Yun was worried the Ye Immortal Clan would threaten Chu Feng once more after Song Luoyi left, so she thought it would be safer to leave.","Seconds later, an amplified voice echoed from the warship, reaching every nook and cranny of the realm. “Young hero Chu Feng, pardon my offense. Our Ye Immortal Clan owes you a favor, and we’re willing to compensate you generously.”","It was from the female grand elder.","“Are they seeking a reconciliation now? Looks like my worry is in vain,” Song Yun said.","“Of course! Chu Feng’s grandmother breached their ancestral formation with such ease. They would be risking extinction if they continued to go after us,” Eggy scoffed.","“Big sister world spirit is right.” Song Yun turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Big brother Chu Feng, did our grandmother head to the Immemorial Cemetery?”","“I think so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Big brother Chu Feng, do you intend to enter the Immemorial Cemetery too?” Song Yun asked.","“I have to find my grandmother,” Chu Feng replied.","Long Zhuoyan had warned Chu Feng against entering the Immemorial Cemetery, saying that she couldn’t see through it even with her means. Chu Feng had also heeded her words, leaving after discovering that the Immemorial Cemetery was the place she mentioned.","But things were different now.","He was worried about his grandmother venturing into the enigmatic Immemorial Cemetery even though she had displayed incredible prowess. He would have to go to the Immemorial Cemetery too now. Perhaps this was all fated.","“Our grandmother is in danger. Big brother Chu Feng, you should rush over. I have other matters to attend to, so I’ll look for you later,” Song Yun said as she passed a tracking talisman over.","This tracking talisman would allow Song Yun to pinpoint Chu Feng’s location once they were within a certain radius of each other. Chu Feng had also given something similar to Little Fishy and Wang Qiang.","“What do you intend to do?” Chu Feng asked as he accepted the tracking talisman.","“I’m just settling a few things. I’ll be done in a jiffy,” Song Yun replied.","“Take care of yourself,” Chu Feng said.","“You too, big brother Chu Feng.” Song Yun smiled. She turned to Eggy and said, “Byebye, big sister world spiritist who is more beautiful than me.”","With that, she left."]},{"number":6371,"title":"Chapter 6371: Chapter 6369: Making Up His Mind","paragraphs":["Chapter 6369: Making Up His Mind","Looking at Song Yun’s departing figure left Chu Feng with conflicting emotions.","Song Yun couldn’t be said to be a good person, but she had always treated him well. She was a villain to others, but not him.","Her illness was no joking matter. He might have extended her lifespan, but as long as the root of the problem wasn’t resolved, it wouldn’t be long before her life snuffed out.","“Chu Feng, is Song Yun’s illness severe?” Eggy asked, sensing Chu Feng’s worry.","“It is very severe. That recovery formation could only alleviate her symptoms but not treat her,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is it that bad? She must have paid a heavy price for her fortuitous encounter.” Eggy sighed.","“Seems so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is your grandmother’s condition severe too?”","“It is tricky, but the God Curse appears to be more of a problem. I have planted a formation in her mind to temporarily grant her clarity of mind, but that formation failed to work against the God Curse.”","“That is a problem. I don’t think you have to worry too much about her for the time being. With her strength, I doubt most people in the world of cultivation can hurt her.”","“Mm. I’ll eventually find a way to treat her. Let’s head to the Immemorial Cemetery.”","“You go ahead. I’m going to rest.”","Eggy opened the World Spirit Space, stepped in, and went to sleep.","Chu Feng stood up and made his way to the nearest teleportation formation. Seconds later, he suddenly halted his footsteps and projected his consciousness into his World Spirit Space.","Whenever Eggy said she was going to rest, she would usually cultivate in the World Spirit Space. Yet, she was lying on the ground, fast asleep. This wasn’t exhaustion but weakness from the Godsoul’s backlash.","She was frowning even in her sleep, which showed just how much pain she was in.","Even though Chu Feng had treated her with the recovery formation, he could only alleviate the symptoms as far as possible. He couldn’t remove the backlash itself.","Just using the Godsoul for a while had made her so weak. It was not hard to imagine what would happen to her if she went all out.","He took out a rug, placed it on the ground, and lifted Eggy onto it. This rug was a treasure that could alleviate her pain. Even so, his heart still ached.","“I won’t give you a chance to use this power for the time being.”","Chu Feng made up his mind.","...","Meanwhile, the Ye Immortal Clan’s warship was making its way to a teleportation formation. Many of their clansmen were still in coma and were receiving treatment, but the stronger ones had regained consciousness.","All the Ye Immortal Clan’s upper echelons were gathered in a hall, with Ye Xiancheng sitting in the clan chief’s position and his parents sitting beside him.","Aside from Ye Xiancheng, everyone, including his parents, had their heads lowered like children who had committed a mistake.","“Do you understand my intention now? Some people can be eliminated, but some people can’t be trifled with. I didn’t befriend Chu Feng out of the kindness of my heart. He’s not someone we should mess with,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Xiancheng, it’s a relief you didn’t turn against Chu Feng, or else this would have spelled the end of our Ye Immortal Clan,” Ye Xiancheng’s father said.","Thinking about the earlier situation sent a chill down his back.","“You made an attempt on his life. This matter can’t be resolved with just an apology or some compensation,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Xiancheng, you decide our next step. Your mother and I will heed your words from now on,” Ye Xiancheng’s father said.","“Do you mean it?” Ye Xiancheng looked at his mother.","His mother’s imposing attitude had vanished without a trace. Her mother looked beaten down like an eggplant withering before the frost. Sensing Ye Xiancheng’s gaze, she lifted her head and said, “Xiancheng, I have made a hasty decision. It’s a relief you were around to guard our Ye Immortal Clan. I have underestimated your competency, but I can see now that you’re more than worthy to become the clan chief. Do whatever you want. I’ll support you.”","“All right, I shan’t beat around the bush then. Chu Feng must be a friend, not a foe. Exploring the Immemorial Cemetery is only one of our aims for this expedition. If we meet Chu Feng, we’ll devote our effort to helping him and let everyone know that we’re on his side. We must do our best to resolve the conflict between us. Clutching on this big tree will help our Ye Immortal Clan grow more smoothly. Otherwise, I fear I won’t have the chance to rise to prominence even with the Immortal Legacy,” Ye Xiancheng said.","His decision was an extreme one, but not a single person opposed him. On the contrary, they supported him.","...","More powers were making their way to the Immemorial Cemetery, including the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. They had previously told Chu Feng that they would head to the Totem Dragon Clan after resolving the issue with their ancestral land, but for some reason, they were making their way to the Immemorial Cemetery.","...","Meanwhile, Song Yun remained in the same realm. She was heading toward a mountain range with another person.","That person was none other than the Godwish Grandmother.","The Godwish Grandmother was the master of the Godwish Palace, a renowned figure in the Eastern Region. Once, a Holy Light Clan’s grand elder had besmirched the Godwish Palace, so she single-handedly charged into the Holy Light Clan and stirred a huge fuss.","In the end, the Holy Light Clan’s Clan Chief had no choice but to kill that grand elder to resolve the matter.","On top of being the master of the Godwish Palace, she was also Song Yun’s mother.","After Song Yun rose to prominence in the Netherworld Sect, she returned to the Eastern Region to take her mother with her. However, the Godwish Grandmother’s strength was only formidable in the Eastern Region; it was nowhere enough beyond it.","This left her with no choice but to follow her daughter’s arrangements.","“Yun’er, I heard a voice in the sky mentioning Chu Feng earlier. Is Chu Feng here as well?” the Godwish Grandmother asked.","“Yup, but he’s all right. You don’t need to worry about him. Big brother Chu Feng is an amazing person. He’s no weaker than me,” Song Yun replied with a smile."]},{"number":6372,"title":"Chapter 6372: Chapter 6370: Song Yun’s Decision","paragraphs":["Chapter 6370: Song Yun’s Decision","“I knew from the moment I saw Chu Feng that he would do great things in the future, but I still underestimated him. I didn’t expect him to go this far. There are so many monstrously talented prodigies in the world of cultivation, yet he still rose to the top,” the Godwish Grandmother said.","She had to be protected by Song Yun and thus had hardly any freedom, but Song Yun would still share recent news with her. That was why she knew about Chu Feng’s accomplishments too.","“Big brother Chu Feng is Jie Ranqing’s son. His father is likely an extraordinary individual as well. I reckon he was pretending to be weak in the Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm. With such parents, it’s no wonder he became so strong,” Song Yun said with a beaming smile.","“Haa, Chu Feng has led such a tough life. Despite his incredible background, he had to slowly climb his way and undergo much suffering just because he had an unreasonable grandfather,” the Godwish Grandmother said with a sigh.","She had witnessed in person the tribulations Chu Feng had to go through.","Soon, Song Yun brought her mother to a discreet cavern. The cavern was wide and deep, reminiscent of a naturally formed palace.","But the Godwish Grandmother felt uneasy. She turned to Song Yun and reminded, “Yun’er, I sense an air of malevolence here. You must tread carefully.”","“Don’t worry, mother, I have been here. There’s no danger here,” Song Yun replied.","The Godwish Grandmother put her heart at ease. Her daughter was now far stronger than her, so her judgment was bound to be more reliable.","Venturing deep into the cavern, they stumbled upon a mural that strung into a story.","“What’s that?” The Godwish Grandmother was curious.","“It took me a long time to decipher this story. It talks about a monster in the Ancient Era, who was dying from a nigh incurable illness. It was versed in a demonic skill that allowed it to be free from its illness if it absorbed a close kin’s soul, but the monster’s only close kin was its mother.","“Upon learning of the matter, the monster’s mother willingly offered her soul to eradicate the monster’s illness. Mother, don’t you think this story is moving?” Song Yun asked.","Song Yun coughed violently, spewing a huge amount of blood before her mother could reply. Her condition was more drastic than what Chu Feng had seen earlier.","Soon, she caved in and collapsed to the floor, rolling around in pain. Her hair became unkempt, and somehow, her body became covered in some kind of bizarre blood.","The Godwish Grandmother was horrified, but she was too weak to help Song Yun. She could only rush forward to support Song Yun after she regained herself.","“I’m fine, mother,” Song Yun said feebly.","“This is not fine! Yun’er, what happened? Are you ill? Did someone beat you up? Who did this?” The Godwish Grandmother was worried. No mother could remain unfazed after seeing her child in such a state.","Instead of answering the question, Song Yun turned to her mother and feebly asked, “Mother, will you be willing to offer your life to me if I’m ill and require your life to be treated?”","The Godwish Grandmother froze up and stared at Song Yun in a daze. Conflicted emotions rippled in her eyes—there was worry, shock, and a slight hint of anger too—but she didn’t voice her thoughts aloud.","Moments later, she seemed to have come to terms with the situation. The shock and anger in her eyes faded.","“Yun’er, your illness looks tricky. You don’t have to beat around the bush if you need to take my life for your treatment. Just give the word, and I’ll offer my life to you.”","The Godwish Grandmother smiled as she reached out to tidy up Song Yun’s messy hair.","“Yun’er, you don’t have to explain anything to me. I’m useless. I can’t protect you from your enemies or shield you from the storm. If my life can heal you, please take it. You don’t have to feel guilty. At least I’m finally able to help you.","“You are the continuation of my life. From the moment you were born, I thought to myself that it doesn’t matter what happens to me for the rest of my life. All that matters is for you to grow up healthily and happily.","“Yun’er, I know you aren’t the kind of person to hold back against anyone. I know that you won’t hold back against me if I were to stand in your way. I hope you can continue being yourself and don’t get soft-hearted even toward me.”","The Godwish Grandmother closed her eyes with a smile after finishing her piece.","“Go ahead, Yun’er.”","Song Yun stared at her mother for a long time. Then, she smiled.","With a wave of her sleeves, she removed the bloodstains on the ground and her clothes with her spirit power.","“Mother, I’m joking with you. I’m perfectly fine. You can examine my condition if you don’t believe me.”","Song Yun grabbed the Godwish Grandmother’s hand and placed it on her pulse.","The Godwish Grandmother had been ready to give up her life when she heard those words. She opened her eyes and saw Song Yun’s radiant and mischievous smile, and that left her a little dazed.","Song Yun’s earlier condition didn’t seem to be an act, but her gleeful smile looked as if she was feeling triumphant after pulling off a prank.","The Godwish Grandmother couldn’t tell if Song Yun was lying or not.","Thus, she released her spirit power to inspect Song Yun’s body—the latter was indeed healthy.","“You brat! How can you scare your mother like that?!”","The Godwish Grandmother angrily smacked Song Yun’s elbow.","“Hehehe, it’s rare that I can spend time with my mother. I’m just trying to spice things up. Mother, you should head to this place. I prepared a surprise for you.”","Song Yun handed a map over.","“Is this why you brought me here?” the Godwish Grandmother looked at the map as she asked.","“Of course. Mother, you should hurry along!”","Song Yun pushed the Godwish Grandmother out of the cavern.","As soon as the Godwish Grandmother flew off, Song Yun’s smile vanished.","She re-entered the cavern and waved her sleeves. The cavern suddenly turned incredibly dark. A sinister, black formation surfaced with wails of agony. Taking a closer look, at least ten thousand souls were struggling within the formation.","These souls had been assimilated inside the formation, causing them to lose their sense of self, but they continued to suffer nevertheless.","The formation had been operating here since a long time ago.","Song Yun took out a talisman paper and tossed it into the formation. The formation transformed into a wisp of smoke and dissipated with the talisman paper.","She had just destroyed the formation.","“Haaa!” Song Yun sighed. “It’d have been much better if I’m vicious through and through.”"]},{"number":6373,"title":"Chapter 6373: Chapter 6371: The Spirit God and the Brush God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6371: The Spirit God and the Brush God","It was a guess on Chu Feng’s part that his grandmother was heading to the Immemorial Cemetery, but he could confirm it now. Since he could plant a formation inside his grandmother, he could leave an imprint inside her too.","He sensed the imprint he had left on his grandmother approached the Immemorial Cemetery at a shocking speed.","If he wanted to get to the Immemorial Cemetery as quickly as he could, he would have to rely on the Nine Heavens Secret Domain.","He was standing before the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s Conqueror Steeles. He had been frequenting this place ever since he grasped the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s power, but he would still take a good look at the three Conqueror Steeles every time he was here.","The Three Conqueror Steeles represented the Immemorial Era, the Ancient Era, and the present era. Those who had left their names on the Conqueror Steeles could control the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formation.","Only Chu Feng’s name was on the present era’s steele, whereas there were six names on the Ancient Era’s steele.","First: Qin Jiu","The second name was blurred as if the person was concealing their identity.","Third: Song Shu’an","The fourth name was blurred too.","Fifth: Ba Jiutian","Sixth: Zhongli Bahuang","Little needed to be said about Qin Jiu. He was the renowned World Spiritist Emperor. He was well-known even in the present era. A huge reason Chu Feng was able to accomplish so much as a world spiritist was due to Qin Jiu’s legacy.","The other five might have come after Qin Jiu, but they had to be formidable figures to have left their names in the Nine Heavens Secret Domain.","The Immemorial Era’s Conqueror Steele had already shattered, making it impossible to see the names on it. Nevertheless, from its remnants, Chu Feng could tell that it had been full of names. This hinted that the Immemorial Era’s cultivators towered above the Ancient Era’s cultivators.","Chu Feng was examining the steeles because of the Immemorial Cemetery’s emergence. He thought he might find something useful, but there was nothing there.","So, he formed a hand seal.","Weng!","Eight Constellation Gates appeared around the Conqueror Steeles. They represented the Eight Galaxies. Chu Feng could head to any of the galaxies by stepping into them.","He was about to make a move when a voice echoed behind him, “You’re a busy fellow. You’re always headed somewhere. You’re really putting the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s power to good use.”","It was an adorable girl with twintails, who looked to be around twelve or thirteen. She wore a golden dress that made her look mischievous, though it didn’t diminish her air of divinity either.","“You are?” Chu Feng asked.","“You don’t recognize me anymore? Who do you think helped you put your name on the Conqueror Steele?” The girl crossed her arms and tilted her head upward.","“Elder, are you that brush?” Chu Feng was surprised.","He had used a thousand-meter-long brush to write his name on the Conqueror Steele. That brush was not to be underestimated. It had also talked to him back then, but its voice was much more mature.","“My master was using me as a medium to talk to you,” the girl replied.","“I see. How should I address you?” Chu Feng asked.","“You may call me Lord Brush God,” the girl replied.","“Chu Feng pays respect to Lord Brush God.” Chu Feng bowed.","The girl might appear young, but she was far older than she let on. It would be unwise to underestimate her. At the very least, Chu Feng couldn’t see through her.","“Chu Feng,” another voice suddenly echoed.","It was a mature, pleasant-sounding voice.","An older woman manifested next to the girl who proclaimed herself the Brush God. She was also dressed in a simple golden dress that accentuated her disposition. Her clothes were not tight-fitting, but her marvellous figure still showed through.","She wore a golden veil that concealed her face, though her eyes showed through. Her eyes were unique—they contained three colors, purple, blue, and golden. They were beautiful and mysterious. They looked to be the eyes of a god rather than a mortal.","Even Chu Feng was enchanted by her.","“Paying respect to master.” The girl hurriedly bowed.","“Paying respect to elder.” Chu Feng did the same too.","This woman was the one who had previously communicated with him through the Brush God; she was the Brush God’s master.","The Brush God was already a big deal, but the woman with tricolored eyes was even more extraordinary. He had known that the Nine Heavens Secret Domain was an amazing place, but he didn’t expect there to be such formidable figures lurking here.","None of them showed themselves when he tried calling for them back then. Their appearance now could be a fortuitous encounter.","“What elder? Call my master Lord Spirit God!” the Brush God said.","“Junior Chu Feng pays respect to Lord Spirit God,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, are you heading to the Immemorial Cemetery?” the Spirit God asked.","“Yes, I am,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’m unable to see through that place, but I sense a malevolent aura seeping out. Will you heed my advice if I tell you not to go?” the Spirit God asked.","“That’s even more reason for me to go, elder. Someone I care about is heading there,” Chu Feng replied.","“Since that’s the case, let me bring you to meet two people.”","Chu Feng’s surroundings began morphing even when the Spirit God’s voice was still echoing in his mind. By the time her voice faded, he was no longer standing before the Conqueror Steele but amid a peculiar land.","This place was surrounded by a thick, beautiful fog that comprised seven colors, resembling an iridescent rainbow.","Chu Feng was perplexed. Somehow, he felt like his connection with the Nine Heavens Secret Domain had been severed here.","“We meet again,” a boy’s voice echoed from the seven-colored fog.","Chu Feng looked over and saw a brawny figure. The other party was two meters tall and was dressed in black armor. The black armor was not made of metal but rather of black wood, but it still looked imposing.","“We meet again, elder,” Chu Feng clasped his fist and greeted the other party."]},{"number":6374,"title":"Chapter 6374: Chapter 6372: The Monstrous God Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6372: The Monstrous God Appears","Chu Feng had to go through many difficult trials before he arrived before the Conqueror Steele. This black-armored figure was an opponent in one of the trials.","To think that they would reunite once more after the trial.","The black-armored figure felt as unfathomable as the Spirit God and the Brush God. Not a person dwelling in the Nine Heavens Secret Domain was to be underestimated.","“You can call me Black Soul,” the black-armored man said.","“Lord Black Soul,” Chu Feng greeted.","“Just Black Soul will do.”","“Black Soul.”","“That’s more like it. Come with me. I’ll bring you to meet Lord Monstrous God.”","Black Soul turned around and led the way.","“Monstrous God?” Chu Feng’s curiosity was piqued.","“Have you met Lord Spirit God?” Black Soul asked.","“Yes, it’s Lord Spirit God who sent me here.”","“The Nine Heavens Secret Domain is ruled by Lord Spirit God and Lord Monstrous God. I am Lord Monstrous God’s subordinate, and it was under Lord Monstrous God’s order that I tested you back then. Lord Monstrous God’s favor has graced you,” Black Soul said.","The Brush God roared from the void, “Oi, what nonsense are you spouting, Black Soul? Lord Spirit God has also shown favor to Chu Feng, all right?”","“My mistake, my mistake. That’s not what I mean.”","The imposing Black Soul bowed profusely toward the voice. His clumsy movements and his young, boyish voice were at odds with his imposing image.","He leaned toward Chu Feng’s ear and whispered, “That lass, Brush God, is Lord Spirit God’s subordinate, so you mustn’t talk badly about Lord Spirit God in front of her.”","Chu Feng chuckled.","Black Soul suddenly said, “Chu Feng, you’re a world spiritist too. Let me ask you a question. Formations require energy, which a world spiritist supplies in the form of spirit power. If a world spiritist wishes to maintain a formation even after he has left, he would require external energy. Do you think the formation will last longer when powered by treasures or living entities?”","“That’s hard to say. It depends on how potent the treasure or the living entity is,” Chu Feng replied.","“What if they are equivalent?” Black Soul asked.","“The living entity would be better. Be it treasures or natural oddities, they will eventually be depleted. But living entities can absorb energy from their surroundings and supply a constant stream of spirit power into the formation. It’s just that treasures and natural oddities are easier to find than a living entity that can be used to power the formation,” Chu Feng replied.","“How do you think the Nine Heavens Secret Domain powers its incredibly fast teleportation formations?” Black Soul asked.","“Could it be a powerful monstrous beast? It can’t be... Lord Monstrous God or Lord Spirit God?” Chu Feng asked.","Both the Spirit God and the Monstrous God were extraordinary individuals. Given that they ruled over this place, it wouldn’t be surprising if they were the ones powering it too.","“Of course not.” Black Soul shook his head.","“It has to be a living entity powering the formation, even if it isn’t Lord Spirit God or Lord Monstrous God.”","“Oh? Why do you think so?”","“There must have been a purpose behind your earlier question. I’m guessing this place is powered by a living entity, and that living entity must be extremely powerful and difficult to control. That said, I’m sure you have the power to suppress this living entity,” Chu Feng said.","“You’re right. The ones powering the Nine Heavens Secret Domain are immemorial monstrous beasts known as the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts. Any one of them can easily destroy the present world of cultivation, and there are over ten million of them here,” Black Soul replied.","“Ten million?” Chu Feng widened his eyes in astonishment.","He had known this place was formidable, but he didn’t expect it to be to this extent. A single Immemorial Realm Origin Beast could destroy the present world of cultivation, but there were ten million of them here?","“Black Soul, that doesn’t include the Ninth Galaxy, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course. The Ninth Galaxy isn’t that simple. Massacring that place would take...” Black Soul suddenly paused and looked at Chu Feng with a smile. “Are you trying to get information out of me?”","“No, I was merely wondering how strong you must be to suppress such formidable monstrous beasts,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re trying to get information out of me again,” Black Soul said.","“I’m just curious,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“I can tell you the answer, but not now. What I’m saying is that Lord Spirit God and Lord Monstrous God are extremely powerful individuals.”","While they were chatting, Black Soul brought Chu Feng to a cliff. Right beside the cliff was a boundless abyss.","Chu Feng’s heart suddenly jolted. He suddenly felt killing intent so intense that it made him subconsciously retreat a few steps. It was so intense that anyone else in his place could have gone mad or even died from it.","The killing intent persisted, but Chu Feng faced no aggression. That emboldened him to take a look.","“Are the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts down there?”","Chu Feng activated his Heaven’s Eye to take a look. He deduced the killing intent was from the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts, for it didn’t come from an individual but a massive army.","Soon, he spotted a pair of blood-colored eyes that looked as big as the sun in the depths of the abyss. Its eyes looked humongous despite being extremely far away from Chu Feng. Its body must have been bigger than even a larger Upper Realm.","And unlike mere avatars, this was its true body!","But what Chu Feng feared more than its size was its strength. He sensed that the other party could easily disintegrate his soul with a mere thought before he could even process what was going on.","This was a truly powerful entity.","“Lord Monstrous God, I have brought Chu Feng here.” Black Soul bowed at the abyss.","“Junior Chu Feng pays respect to Lord Monstrous God.” Chu Feng bowed to the cliff.","He could already guess as much that Lord Monstrous God was the one suppressing the ten million Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts. The latter must have been the one suppressing their power within the abyss.","“You need not be so restrained, Chu Feng. You have already received our preliminary recognition to be able to stand before me. You can be somewhat considered one of us now,” a deep voice echoed from the abyss.","The world shook. It felt as if a deity was issuing his divine decree.","It was a relief that the Monstrous God’s tone was gentle."]},{"number":6375,"title":"Chapter 6375: Chapter 6373: Something to Rely On","paragraphs":["Chapter 6373: Something to Rely On","“Has Black Soul told you about us?” the Monstrous God asked.","“Milord, I have only informed him about the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts. I dare not divulge too much about the other details,” Black Soul replied.","“The Nine Heavens Secret Domain originates from the Immemorial Era. The four of us have been here since the very start,” the Monstrous God said.","“So... the four lords have existed since the Immemorial Era?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","There had been a resurgence of Ancient Era’s races in the present world of cultivation, but not many of them were from the Ancient Era itself. Those who survived since the Ancient Era were all formidable individuals wielding incredible means.","Yet, there were entities who survived the Immemorial Era here? How many years must they have lived? What kind of means could they have grasped?","These four entities were far stronger than Chu Feng had expected.","“There’s no need to be nervous. There’s nothing special about us other than being a bit older and stronger than the others. Hahaha.” The Monstrous God laughed.","Just then, Eggy’s voice echoed in Chu Feng’s ears, “That fellow still likes to brag despite having lived for so long.”","“Eggy, you’re awake! How are you feeling?” Chu Feng asked out of concern.","“What could happen to me? Don’t worry, I’m good. You should focus on your conversation with that big fellow. He might have some information about the Immemorial Cemetery,” Eggy said.","Just then, the Monstrous God continued, “We called you over because you’re heading to the Immemorial Cemetery. That place is unfathomable. Even the Spirit God, who possesses the Three Realms Divine Eyes, is unable to see through it. It's not something you can deal with at your level. You must be careful if you insist on heading there.”","“I understand.” Chu Feng quickly asked, “Elder, you are from the Immemorial Era. Surely there must be some information about the Immemorial Cemetery back in your era?”","“This is my first time seeing the Immemorial Cemetery. I have never heard about it before,” the Monstrous God said.","“Even those from the Immemorial Era have never heard about it?” Chu Feng was bewildered.","God’s Era had appeared many times before in the Ancient Era. Even the present-era cultivators had learned about it before its recent reappearance.","But the Immemorial Cemetery was shrouded in a sea of mystery. Its appearance was abrupt, and no one knew anything about it.","“We didn't call you over just to warn you about the dangers of the Immemorial Cemetery. We believe you wield great potential as someone who has left his name on the Conqueror Steele, but some things cannot be divulged prematurely, or it’ll weigh you down. We can only tell you when you are strong enough. Growth is important, but so is surviving,” the Monstrous God said.","Chu Feng understood what the Monstrous God was saying. They might require his help for something in the future, but he would have to become much stronger to be of help to them. They were still evaluating whether he could reach the level they wanted.","“Don’t worry, elder. I cherish my life a lot. If I could make a bold statement, if you are truly worried and harbor high expectations of me, you can bestow me with some life preservation means. I am not an inflexible person who insists on doing everything myself,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“Shall I release an Immemorial Realm Origin Beast to help you overcome the Immemorial Cemetery?” the Monstrous God suggested.","“That’s a good idea,” Chu Feng replied.","“Good idea, your head! Those things don’t even listen to me. Do you think they’ll heed your command? Cough cough cough ...”","The humongous Monstrous God suddenly convulsed and coughed violently. When it raised its head once more, Chu Feng noticed the light in its eyes had dimmed significantly.","“Chu Feng, it’s not that I don’t want to help you, but suppressing these Immemorial Origin Beasts is taking a toll on me. I don’t have the strength to aid you. You must work hard to become strong. Otherwise, I’ll have to end myself with the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts when I can no longer suppress them. That will spell the end of the Nine Realms Secret Domain, and you’ll no longer be able to use the convenient teleportation formations,” the Monstrous God said with a much weaker voice than before.","Eggy scoffed, “What nonsense is this? He was still bragging about his strength a moment ago, but he becomes frail as soon as you ask him for benefits. I reckon he just doesn’t want to help you. Besides, the Nine Realms Secret Domain will become useless to you once you enter the Ninth Galaxy.”","In contrast, Chu Feng had no complaints. “Take care of yourself, elder. I have and will never loosen up when it comes to my cultivation.”","“I believe in you.” The Monstrous God looked at the sky above. “Spirit God, I am done speaking my piece. You can take him away now.”","Chu Feng’s surroundings morphed. An instant later, he returned before the Conqueror Steeles. The Spirit God and the Brush God were still standing where they were before.","Before Chu Feng could utter a word, the Spirit God’s eyes suddenly emanated a mysterious light that seeped into his eyes.","Chu Feng’s heart skipped a beat. He noticed his vision become exceptionally bright, and he felt like he could see through anything in the world. This was far stronger than his Heaven’s Eye.","“Remember these methods,” the Spirit God said as she relayed the methods to activate and deactivate the eyes.","Chu Feng quickly used the deactivation method. By then, he was already gasping for air. There was a sharp pain in his eyes, a sign that he had overexerted himself.","He quickly constructed a spirit gathering formation on his palms and placed it over his eyes to soothe them.","“This is a portion of the Three Realms Divine Eyes’ power. It strengthens your sight. I can only bestow this much given your current cultivation level. You won’t be able to withstand any more than this. I believe you have already felt it yourself,” the Spirit God said.","“It is an incredible power.” Chu Feng was impressed.","His eyes were already aching from the power of the Three Realms Divine Eyes. That was why he rushed to deactivate it. It was not a skill he could use for an extended time.","“Use it prudently, and it will only be a temporary burden. You know your body better than anyone else, so don't go beyond your limit. Otherwise, you may permanently lose your sight, and no one will be able to treat you,” the Spirit God said.","“I understand. I feel much more confident navigating the Immemorial Cemetery with your power. Thank you, Lord Spirit God,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“You don’t have to flatter me. I bestowed my Three Realms Divine Eyes on you because I’m curious about the Immemorial Cemetery. I’ll be able to look into that place through your eyes. That’s all there is to it,” the Spirit God replied.","“Regardless, you are still doing me a huge favor.” Chu Feng smiled.","“You have a glib tongue.” The Spirit God smiled as well. “You should get going. Stay safe.”","With that, the Spirit God disappeared.","“You must take care of yourself, or else it’ll be a long time before anyone comes here again,” the Brush God said before disappearing as well.","Only Chu Feng was left standing before the Conqueror Steeles. He began making his way toward the Immemorial Cemetery.","The Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formations were faster than anything Chu Feng had seen before, but they were linked to specific places. This meant that he could only teleport to the realm closest to the Immemorial Cemetery. It would still take some time for him to travel over.","“Elder, do you know those two people?” Chu Feng asked the Divine Deer after entering the teleportation formation."]},{"number":6376,"title":"Chapter 6376: Chapter 6374: Opportunity and Danger Co-exist","paragraphs":["Chapter 6374: Opportunity and Danger Co-exist","“You're referring to the Spirit God and the Monstrous God? I have never heard of them, but I can tell they are formidable. They emanate a primeval aura. They could be from the Immemorial Era. To think the Nine Heavens Secret Domain is guarded by such entities. Chu Feng, I don’t think this place is just a medium for teleportation formations,” the Divine Deer said.","“If they have existed since the Immemorial Era, perhaps they might know what happened in the final years of the Ancient Era?” Chu Feng murmured.","“Perhaps, but I doubt they’d tell you. They could have easily helped you but chose not to. I suspect they are reluctant to help you too much, at least not at the moment,” the Divine Deer said.","“That’s normal. I’d be grateful if they helped me, but they aren’t obliged to,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s true. It’s good to have such a mindset,” the Divine Deer said.","...","After Chu Feng left, the Spirit God paid a visit to the Monstrous God.","“Monstrous God, are you burdened by the suppression of the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts? You can eliminate a couple of them to lighten the burden if need be. Don’t push yourself too far. I can also help you,” the Spirit God said.","“You’re underestimating me, Spirit God. I’m merely hoodwinking that lad. I can easily suppress these Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts,” the Monstrous God said with a displeased tone.","“Monstrous God, it’s of utmost importance that nothing goes wrong in your suppression of the Immemorial Realm Origin Beasts. I don’t mean anything by it; I just don’t want anything to go wrong,” the Spirit God explained.","“I held on even during the toughest time, let alone now. Don’t worry about it, Spirit God,” the Monstrous God replied.","Hearing that, the Spirit God chose not to harp on this matter. Instead, she asked, “I thought you had a high opinion of Chu Feng. Why didn’t you offer him any help?”","“I do have high expectations of him, but he needs to walk his path. If he dies, it would only mean that he’s not the person we want,” the Monstrous God replied.","“Does that mean you won’t intervene if something happens at the Immemorial Cemetery?” the Spirit God asked.","“Will you make a move?” the Monstrous God asked.","“No. I won’t leave the Nine Heavens Secret Domain,” the Spirit God replied.","“That lad won’t die that easily. He’s not as simple as he appears, right?” The Monstrous God had phrased this statement as a question because the Spirit God had far keener eyes than him.","The Spirit God didn’t reply, but there was a faint curl at the corners of her lips.","...","After some traveling, Chu Feng finally returned to the Immemorial Cemetery. The area was much more bustling than when he was last here, though space was vast enough for the place not to feel crowded.","Warships, floating palaces, war chariots, and humongous monstrous beasts could be spotted everywhere. It was an impressive lineup. Many present-era and Ancient Era powers had gone, many of which Chu Feng had never seen before.","There were more Ancient Era powers than Chu Feng imagined.","There were surprisingly no conflicts among these powers. They were still observing the Immemorial Cemetery, not daring to carelessly enter the area. This was also why they were gathered around the entrance.","Chu Feng paid no heed to them and entered the Immemorial Cemetery.","He was getting a clearer sense of his grandmother’s aura upon arriving at the vicinity, to the point where he could even pinpoint her location. But as he was about to enter the Immemorial Cemetery, he suddenly heard some voices.","He was now sharp enough to sieve out the voices he wanted to hear amid a huge sea of voices. Someone was talking about him.","In the present world of cultivation, Chu Feng’s name was bound to be mentioned where groups of people were gathered, but this time, they were not talking about Chu Feng’s feats, but that a mysterious power was searching for him.","According to them, those people wore hooded world spiritist cloaks, and a pair of deer horns extended from their hoods. A pair of yellow eyes could be seen within their hoods, a sign that they weren’t humans. No one knew where they were from, but their strength was formidable.","“Looks like there are plenty of Ancient Era powers who covet your treasures,” Eggy said.","She didn’t think that power harbored good intentions.","“It’s fine. They can come at me all they want.”","Undeterred, Chu Feng ventured deeper into the Immemorial Cemetery. The place was massive, unlike any other remnant he had been to. Every tomb here was comparable to a realm, and the larger ones were even the size of a starfield.","Despite Chu Feng’s cultivation and the aid of treasures, he still needed a lot of time to traverse this region.","As he flitted by the humongous tombstones that were comparable to realms, he started to feel increasingly uneasy. There was something sinister about the tombstones. He couldn’t help but pay attention to them as he passed them by, and he was able to glean some things about them.","Every tombstone contained an independent remnant, and the fortuitous encounter contained in them was proportionate to their risk. The Immemorial Cemetery was a treasure vault never seen before in the world of cultivation, containing countless fortuitous encounters.","But the danger lurking in the Immemorial Cemetery couldn’t be understated.","Should there be anyone alive in those tombstones, given their means to construct these remnants, they could make sure that no cultivator walked out of the Immemorial Cemetery alive if they willed so."]},{"number":6377,"title":"Chapter 6377: Chapter 6375: Spirit Sword Reverent’s Tomb","paragraphs":["Chapter 6375: Spirit Sword Reverent’s Tomb","“Don’t worry, Chu Feng. I am here. It doesn’t matter what monsters lurk inside these tombs. It’ll be best if they obediently stay put, but if they dare to mess with you, I’ll make sure to grind them into dust!” Eggy hurled her little fists confidently.","There was a tinge of excitement in her voice. She seemed to look forward to crossing blows with the Immemorial Era’s old monsters.","“What’s there to fear when my Eggy is here? But you mustn’t use that power of yours carelessly. Your safety comes first,” Chu Feng reminded.","“I know, I know. I haven’t lived long enough yet. I know what I’m doing, so you don’t need to worry about me,” Eggy replied.","“Are you sure?” Chu Feng sounded skeptical.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng’s face darkened, and he hastened his footsteps.","He had already been moving at his fastest speed in his normal state. To accelerate further than that meant putting a toll on his body.","“What’s wrong, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked, sensing something was amiss.","“My connection with my grandmother has been severed,” Chu Feng replied.","“Severed? How? Is there a formation preventing you from sensing your grandmother?” Eggy asked.","“I don’t sense anything of that sort, but my connection with my grandmother still got severed anyway—and it’s a thorough severing,” Chu Feng said.","“Don’t worry, Chu Feng. Your grandmother is strong. She’ll be fine. Could your grandmother have entered an isolation formation?” Eggy consoled.","There could only be two possibilities.","The first possibility was what Eggy postulated: his grandmother had entered an isolation formation, making it impossible for him to continue pinpointing his grandmother’s location.","The second possibility was disastrous: the formation he had implanted in his grandmother had been erased. If his grandmother were going to erase it, she would have done so a long time ago instead of waiting so long. It was more likely that someone else had erased that formation.","And that was what Chu Feng was worried about.","Fortunately, he remembered his grandmother’s last location.","When he finally arrived at the pinpointed location, he realized it was at a tombstone. It was one of the smaller tombstones in the Immemorial Cemetery, but it was still comparable to a realm.","The tombstone was imposing, boasting a massive size and a majestic presence. On top of that, it emanated a faint light. There were words on the tombstone.","Tomb of the Spirit Sword Reverent.","“There’s a name on this tombstone. What could this mean?” Eggy asked.","The tombstones they passed by along the way were empty. This was the first tombstone they saw that carried a name.","“Someone might have cleared this tombstone’s remnant,” Chu Feng replied as he continued flitting toward the tombstone.","It didn’t matter to him whether someone had cleared the remnant or not; he had to get to the bottom of why his grandmother’s signal had ended here.","As he drew close to the tombstone, the tombstone suddenly vanished, and he found himself surrounded by a thick fog.","It was a formation!","It turned out that the tombstone was projected by a formation. The situation inside must be very different.","Passing through the fog, he found himself entering a vast realm. It was a beautiful world that contrasted against its sinister tombstone outer appearance. There were majestic mountains and flowing rivers, chirping birds, rare plants, and spirit beasts that Chu Feng had never seen before.","The spirit beasts possessed cultivation, but they were incapable of human speech. They appeared to be animals who had been residing inside this tombstone realm. Some of them were treasures from head to toe, including their fur, bones, blood, and flesh.","Though they weren’t of much use to Chu Feng at his current cultivation.","“I can faintly sense my grandmother’s location now.” Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief.","He couldn’t help but be worried about his grandmother despite knowing how powerful she was. If he could sense her again, the chances were that she had entered an isolation formation here.","To avoid unnecessary trouble, he remained concealed and even reinforced his concealment formation.","As he ventured deeper into the realm, he noticed some familiar figures.","A group from the Heavensword Sacred Palace was busy catching spirit beasts, presumably for their sect members’ cultivation.","The deeper he went, the more people from the Heavensword Sacred Palace he spotted. Some were catching spirit beasts, some were harvesting herbs, and some were exploring the area.","“There are quite a few of them here. Were they the ones who activated this tombstone?” Eggy asked.","“It’s possible,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is the Heavensword Sacred Palace this formidable?” Eggy asked.","“They must be quite capable if they can activate this tombstone.”","Chu Feng ventured further into the realm and spotted an eerie fog in the distance.","The fog extended to the sky, forming a wall that sealed off the area. This fog emitted a dangerous aura that seemed to warn them against advancing further. Bizarre noises would echo from it now and then; it sounded jarring like fingernails scratching a wall.","Chu Feng’s grandmother was inside the fog.","“Oh? A familiar face,” Eggy remarked.","There was a majestic altar in front of the fog. The altar was surrounded by a formation, but the formation had been breached, and many members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace were gathered on top of the altar.","Among them was Tianjian Canhua.","“Looks like they were the ones who activated this realm,” Chu Feng said.","The formation around the altar was extremely difficult to breach, and the altar was a legacy formation. The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace were gathered on the altar, waiting to inherit the legacy.","However, it would appear that the Heavensword Sacred Palace hadn’t fully activated the legacy formation."]},{"number":6378,"title":"Chapter 6378: Chapter 6376: Tianjian Qingyuan’s Condition","paragraphs":["Chapter 6376: Tianjian Qingyuan’s Condition","Chu Feng entered the fog without revealing himself.","While he was also curious to know what benefits the Heavensword Sacred Palace would receive, that was not his priority at hand.","The fog was treacherous. Not only was it like a labyrinth, but there were also dangers lurking at every corner. Fortunately, Chu Feng’s Heaven’s Eye worked inside the fog, allowing him to pick the right path.","It didn’t take him long to pass through the fog and arrive before a vast grassland. A breeze caused the grass to sway, sending ripples across the green field. This made a distant object even more conspicuous.","It was a tombstone!","It resembled the tombstone outside, but it was much smaller. It might not be as huge as an Upper Realm, but it resembled a sharp sword piercing into the sky. Anyone who stepped into this grassland was bound to notice it.","There were words on the tombstone too.","The tombstone outside only contained the word ‘Tomb of the Spirit Sword Reverent’, but this tombstone had peculiar runes inscribed around those six words as if an army. On top of that, these runes danced around as if they had a life of their own.","The tombstone harnessed something important, possibly the crux of this place.","But Chu Feng’s heart tensed up when he stepped into this grassland. His connection with his grandmother had been severed again.","He turned around and headed into the fog before walking back out. After repeating this a few times, he became certain that this grassland had some kind of isolation formation that even he couldn’t perceive. When inside the fog, he could faintly sense that his grandmother was in the grassland, but the feeling disappeared as soon as he entered the grassland.","As he made his way toward the tombstone, he noticed a white-robed lady floating not too far away from the tombstone. Her cultivation was concealed, and she didn’t emanate the slightest pressure.","Yet, Chu Feng could tell from her disposition that she was a formidable cultivator.","“That woman feels strong. Is she from the Heavensword Sacred Palace, or is she here to guard the tombstone?” Eggy also sensed something amiss about the woman. She stood up warily and prepared to make a move.","Chu Feng stopped approaching the tombstone and instead wandered the grassland in search of his grandmother, but he couldn’t find any traces of her. At the same time, he also circled the tombstone and saw the woman’s face.","She had a pair of light blue eyes reminiscent of frost. With eyes like that, her discernment was likely to be exceptional.","Despite being concealed, Chu Feng didn’t think he could escape that woman’s notice. He suspected that she had long noticed him, though her eyes remained fixed on the tombstone, not sparing a glance at him.","This was good news as it meant she harbored no hostility toward Chu Feng.","So, Chu Feng revealed himself and bowed to the woman. “Elder, I am Chu Feng. I am here to look for someone; I don’t mean to disturb you.”","He introduced himself as a sign of respect, but the white-robed woman continued ignoring Chu Feng as if she couldn’t see him. He intended to ask her identity, but since she wasn’t paying him any heed, he decided to skip the pleasantries and get to the point.","“May I know if you have met an old woman here?”","The woman didn’t respond.","“Is she deaf or blind? She’s putting on quite the act,” Eggy scoffed.","She wouldn’t hesitate to classify anyone who disrespected Chu Feng as an enemy, though she knew better than to make a reckless move here. She believed Chu Feng had his way of dealing with this situation.","Chu Feng wasn’t bothered by the woman’s lack of response. He flitted next to the white-robed woman, followed her gaze, and examined the tombstone as well. The tombstone’s runes were profound. He could discern something with his Heaven’s Eye, but it would take him a lot more time to decipher it entirely.","The white-robed woman was probably trying to decipher the runes too, which was why she ignored Chu Feng. She couldn’t be distracted, or else her efforts would be in vain.","“No wonder she ignored me. Deciphering the tombstone’s runes requires one’s complete attention, so she couldn’t respond to me,” Chu Feng explained.","“Is that so?” Eggy grunted.","Chu Feng knew he had to do something. His Heaven’s Eye was not necessarily stronger than that woman’s special eyes.","Thus, he activated the Three Realms Divine Eyes bestowed from the Spirit God and quickly saw through the tombstone. He hurriedly retracted the Three Realms Divine Eyes and constructed a formation.","The white-robed woman first glanced at the formation before finally looking at Chu Feng. “You can decipher the runes?”","“Yes, I was able to decipher it,” Chu Feng replied.","“You live up to your reputation.” The white-robed woman was delighted to hear that.","“Elder, have you heard about me?” Chu Feng asked.","“I doubt there’s anyone in the world of cultivation who hasn’t heard about you. Is the old woman you speak about your grandmother?” the white-robed woman asked.","“Yes, she is,” Chu Feng replied.","“I am Tianjian Qingyuan. I’m from the Heavensword Sacred Palace. I... know where your grandmother is.”","Tianjian Qingyuan led Chu Feng deeper into the grassland, but a short moment later, they descended to the ground. There was nothing special about this place; Chu Feng had already passed by this area during his earlier search.","“Wait for a while. It’s almost time,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng didn’t know what was going on, but he waited patiently.","A furious wind soon blew across the grassland, and a sinister black vortex appeared in the sky. The vortex was humongous, spanning over ten thousand meters.","Chu Feng felt incomparably small before the vortex. Their differences lay not just in their sizes, but also in their strengths. The vortex harnessed great destructive prowess that could decimate him if he dared step into it.","“This vortex can be found in every tombstone realm, and it would appear at a specific time. I saw your grandmother entering it,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng frowned.","He was confident in his grandmother’s strength, but the vortex’s destructive prowess was too terrifying. He couldn’t help but worry about his grandmother once more.","Just then, Tianjian Qingyuan stepped into the black vortex too.","The black aura manifested into countless sharp claws that swiped at her, but they dissipated before they could reach her. None of the attacks could get to her. She was extremely powerful, far surpassing ordinary Heavenly Gods!","“Help my descendants obtain the legacy here, and I’ll enter the black vortex and find your grandmother on your behalf,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","That was the reason she stepped into the vortex. She was demonstrating her strength to negotiate with Chu Feng."]},{"number":6379,"title":"Chapter 6379: Chapter 6377: Trusting the Right Person?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6377: Trusting the Right Person?","“Elder, I’ll help you decipher the tombstone’s content, but can you bring me into the vortex with you?” Chu Feng asked.","“Take a closer look. I’m not deflecting the energy but withstanding it. This destructive energy targets living entities. I can’t protect you if your cultivation is too low,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied.","Chu Feng took a closer look and realized she was right. No wonder Tianjian Qingyuan said she would enter the vortex on his behalf; she knew that he wouldn’t be able to enter.","“I’m counting on you, elder,” Chu Feng replied.","“You don’t need to be so polite. I won’t help you if you can’t fulfill my request,” Tianjian Qingyuan said as she flew out from the vortex and landed next to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng quickly constructed a formation that manifested into a fifty-meter-long chain. He connected one end of the chain to his forehead.","“Let me share my sight with you, elder,” Chu Feng said.","Tianjian Qingyuan understood what Chu Feng was getting at.","He was the brain, and she was the brawn. In truth, she could have deciphered the tombstone’s content even without Chu Feng’s help, but it would take an inestimable amount of time.","Thus, she replied, “All right.”","Chu Feng and Tianjian Qingyuan made their way to the tombstone again.","Tianjian Qingyuan attached the other end of the chain to her forehead, and her eyes began to glow brightly. The obscure content of the tombstone suddenly became comprehensible to her. She looked at Chu Feng in astonishment, curious to know what means he possessed, but his eyes looked perfectly normal.","“Elder, you might have to hurry. This skill takes a toll on me. I’ll try my best to hold on, but I don’t know how long I’ll last,” Chu Feng urged.","He was using the Three Realms Divine Eyes right now. Not only did it take a toll on him, but he also didn’t know how long he could continue using it. It was a borrowed power, after all, so it was bound to run out eventually.","Tianjian Qingyuan understood what he meant and smiled. She formed a hand seal and fused her energy into the tombstone.","The world suddenly shook.","A humongous sword of light manifested behind Tianjian Qingyuan. It was of the same size as the tombstone.","“A sword? Is this her bloodline power?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","That sword was just a phenomenon arising from her bloodline power, but this phenomenon already boasted tremendous power. Her bloodline itself could only be more formidable.","Sword silhouettes flew forth from the tombstone. These swords were of normal lengths. It started with one, but it quickly grew to dozens, followed by thousands and tens of thousands...","These swords fused into the humongous bloodline sword behind Tianjian Qingyuan. The bloodline sword swiftly expanded, surpassing the tombstone in the blink of an eye, and that still wasn’t its limit yet.","Tianjian Qingyuan had begun breaching the formation to siphon the power inside the tombstone, and it was proceeding smoothly. Soon, her bloodline sword surpassed the tombstone by several fold.","Just then, her vision suddenly became a little blurry. This made her heart clench up.","This showed that Chu Feng was under great pressure and was reaching his limit.","Even though many of the tombstone swords had fused into her bloodline, the inheritance was not over yet. If a hiccup happened now, their efforts would be in vain. She might even lose the opportunity to obtain this legacy for good.","“Chu Feng, hold on,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng’s eyes were not only bloodshot, but blood itself was already oozing from them. He was at his limit.","“Elder, can I trust you?” Chu Feng asked.","“Is it about your grandmother?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“If I succeed, I’ll find your grandmother as long as there’s a breath left in me,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng smiled. “I’ll entrust my grandmother to you, elder. Leave this to me.”","He changed his hand seal, and even more blood oozed from his eyes. But Tianjian Qingyuan realized her blurry vision had become clear once more.","The inheritance continued.","When the final tombstone sword fused inside the bloodline sword, the runes on the tombstone vanished, leaving only six words behind. The runes were gushing through Tianjian Qingyuan’s bloodline.","“Chu Feng, it’s done now,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng quickly formed a hand seal to deactivate the Three Realms Divine Eyes.","He succumbed to the backlash and collapsed to the ground, his face distorted and his teeth clenched from excruciating pain. His face was ghastly pale, and fresh blood seeped from his eyes. All these showed that he had been under immense pressure.","He endured the pain and began constructing another formation. He needed to treat his eyes right away, or else he might become blind.","“Don’t move,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Chu Feng felt a cooling sensation on his eyes. It was two glowing tree leaves that shared the same light blue color as Tianjian Qingyuan’s eyes.","The two leaves melted into light blue energy that seeped into Chu Feng’s eyes.","The excruciating pain Chu Feng felt in his eyes was greatly alleviated, and his injuries swiftly recovered.","Tianjian Qingyuan had used a priceless treasure to treat his injuries. No power would put a healing treasure of this caliber on the market—that was how invaluable it was.","“Looks like I have put my trust in the right person,” Chu Feng said with a smile."]},{"number":6380,"title":"Chapter 6380: Chapter 6378: Tianjian Canhua’s Pride","paragraphs":["Chapter 6378: Tianjian Canhua’s Pride","With Tianjian Qingyuan’s help, Chu Feng’s eyes quickly made a full recovery.","Chu Feng stood up and noticed Tianjian Qingyuan looking at him. Her eyes were no longer light blue but vacuous, though it didn’t seem to hinder her sight. Those light blue eyes were probably a manifestation of her means.","“Are you better now?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“I’m fully recovered. Thank you, elder.” Chu Feng bowed.","“You don’t need to thank me. You landed in that state helping me, so it’s only right for me to return the favor.”","“Elder, did the inheritance go smoothly?”","“Mm.” Tianjuan Qingyuan nodded. With a wave of her sleeves, she manifested the bloodline sword infused with the runes and plunged it into the tombstone.","“Why did she put it back?” Eggy was confused.","“She’s using the tombstone’s power to pass down the legacy to the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace,” Chu Feng replied.","The altar outside the fog lit up. The faces of the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members beamed with delight, including Tianjian Canhua.","“It’s finally beginning.”","All of them sat down. They could feel powerful energy flowing through the altar and surging into their bodies. They were receiving the legacy.","As the energy intensified, runes began to surface from the altar, followed by rune swords. However, the rune swords appeared to possess sentience as they chose to enter the bodies of different cultivators.","Some failed to attract even a single rune sword, whereas some enjoyed a steady stream of them.","Tianjian Canhua attracted the most rune swords.","Under the constant influx of the rune swords, the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members manifested a sword avatar behind them—it was their bloodline power. However, their sword avatars paled far in comparison to Tianjian Qingyuan’s.","Not only were their sword avatars pitifully small, but some swords weren’t even complete. Some only had the bare outline of a sword.","Even Tianjian Canhua, their most talented prodigy of the present era, could only manifest a thousand-meter-long sword. It had a complete form, but it paled in comparison to Tianjian Qingyuan’s. Nevertheless, it still stood out against the others.","“As expected of Miss Canhua!”","“She’s incredible!”","Those from the older generations nodded in approval, whereas the juniors looked envious. Tianjian Canhua looked unfazed as if she had long grown accustomed to these gazes.","The number of rune swords sprouting from the altar quickly declined until there was no more left, and the altar’s light dissipated. The legacy had come to an end.","However, the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members didn’t get up and leave. Instead, they remained seated on the spot as they attempted to assimilate the legacy they had just obtained. This included Tianjian Canhua.","Suddenly, Tianjian Canhua’s bloodline sword glowed with incredible brilliance, outshining other bloodline swords present in the vicinity.","A sword ray gushed into the sky, then a sword rain descended. The sword rain was concentrated from Tianjian Canhua’s bloodline sword. Her bloodline sword didn’t grow any larger, but it became increasingly complete.","Eventually, it took a form that was identical to Tianjian Qingyuan’s, though its size was still nowhere near as big.","“The Heavensword has formed. Canhua’s bloodline has fully awakened!” the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master exclaimed in excitement.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members cheered in delight. This meant that their lineage finally had a prodigy on par with Tianjian Qingyuan! Having such a prodigy in God’s Era was of utmost importance.","Even the palace master’s hands were trembling nonstop, and she could hardly suppress the grin on her face.","Soon, Tianjian Canhua opened her eyes. Her face remained impassive, but joy erupted in her heart.","It was no easy feat for members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace to awaken their bloodline, so she was excited by this feat too. She raised her head to look at the sky, where a sword rain continued to fall on her.","“It’s a pity Chu Feng isn’t around. If he were here, he would have regretted having rejected me, right? But it doesn’t matter now. I won’t give him another chance. I want him to regret it for life,” Tianjian Canhua murmured under her breath.","Despite her calm appearance, she was deeply shaken by Chu Feng’s rejection. It pricked her pride as a top-notch prodigy. The only way to heal her pride was to make Chu Feng regret his decision.","Hu!","The bizarre fog suddenly billowed. Two people soon emerged from it.","The crowd was taken aback, including Tianjian Canhua.","One of the two people was their ancestor, Tianjian Qingyuan. She had entered the fog to help them acquire the legacy, so it was no surprise to see her emerging from it.","What shocked them was the identity of the other person—Chu Feng!","“Why is Chu Feng with Lord Qingyuan?” Tianjian Canhua was bewildered.","The others were confused as well, but no one dared to ask about it. Even the lofty palace master was as obedient as a servant before Tianjian Qingyuan, not daring to question the latter.","Everyone was waiting for Tianjian Qingyuan to speak.","“You have awakened your bloodline?” Tianjian Qingyuan turned to Tianjian Canhua and asked.","Tianjian Canhua quickly stepped forward, knelt on the floor, and kowtowed. “It’s all thanks to Lord Qingyuan that I acquired the power of this land and awakened my bloodline.”","She took a humble stance, not daring to brag about her accomplishments in front of Tianjian Qingyuan.","“Don’t thank me. Thank him if you must,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","The crowd was taken aback. They couldn’t understand why Tianjian Qingyuan was asking Tianjian Canhua to thank Chu Feng.","“It’s Chu Feng’s credit that you obtained this land’s legacy so quickly.”","Tianjian Canhua thought her head was going to explode. She couldn’t believe that Chu Feng had contributed to the legacy she had inherited. To think that even the great Tianjian Qingyuan only unlocked this remnant’s legacy with Chu Feng’s help!","This made her pride collapse once more.","“I trust you have already met Chu Feng? Remember this, you owe Chu Feng a favor. Should Chu Feng require help in the future, you are obliged to help him,” Tianjian Qingyuan ordered.","The palace master took the lead and replied, “Rest assured, Lord Qingyuan. Chu Feng’s affairs shall be our Heavensword Sacred Palace’s affairs from this day on!”","Eggy was overjoyed to hear that.","“Waa, Tianjian Qingyuan is more impressive than I thought. You didn’t help her in vain,” Eggy said.","Tianjian Qingyuan relayed some instructions to the Heavensword Sacred Palace. In gist, she told them to leave this place without her. She had to stay behind to deal with other matters.","In the meantime, Tianjian Canhua looked at Chu Feng with conflicted eyes.","Chu Feng smiled at her. She responded with a smile as well. Aside from that, they didn’t exchange a word. It was not that she didn’t want to speak to him, but she dared not. Just Chu Feng’s ties with Tianjian Qingyuan made her dare not talk to him."]},{"number":6381,"title":"Chapter 6381: Chapter 6379: The Owner of the Copper Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 6379: The Owner of the Copper Sword","Tianjian Qingyuan brought Chu Feng back into the fog after issuing her command. She was going to fulfill her promise now.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members looked conflicted, especially Tianjian Canhua.","“Canhua, congratulations on awakening your bloodline,” Tianjian Jiumeng walked over and said.","Tianjian Jiumeng was one of the few people who knew about Tianjian Canhua’s intention to make Chu Feng her dao companion, only to be rejected. She was worried Tianjian Canhua’s state of mind would be shaken by Chu Feng.","“It was with his help that I awakened my bloodline. I don’t know if it’s a good thing or a bad thing. Elder, what do you think?” Tianjian Canhua asked.","“Canhua, it was Lord Qingyuan who helped you, not Chu Feng. And it doesn’t matter who helped you; what matters is that you have benefited from it,” Tianjian Jiumeng said.","“I know you’re worried about me. You don’t have to. I am not that frail as to stumble on something as minor as this. I know what I want.” Tianjian Canhua turned around to chat with the palace master. Her attitude was casual, as if nothing had happened.","...","Tianjian Qingyuan moved so fast that it didn’t take long for them to return to the grassland.","However, they needed to wait as the vortex Chu Feng’s grandmother entered only appeared once every interval. So, Tianjian Qingyuan stared in the distance with her vacuous eyes; it was impossible to tell what was on her mind.","“Elder, it was a trade. I’d help you decipher the tombstone while you help me look for my grandmother. You didn’t have to ask the others to help me. Doesn’t that mean that I owe you another favor? I don’t know when I’ll be able to return this favor,” Chu Feng said.","“You don’t need to repay me. It’s a bonus for your hard work. Their lineage isn’t particularly strong, but they should be able to help you in this part of the world of cultivation. What’s more important is that they have potential,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","“That makes me even more embarrassed,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“You don’t need to feel so. You deserve it,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied with a faint smile.","That made Chu Feng even more certain that Tianjian Qingyuan, despite her cold exterior, was someone worth befriending. She was thinking on Chu Feng’s behalf.","“Elder, what do you mean by potential?” Chu Feng asked.","“Tianjian Canhua is very talented. Even the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s main lineage will carefully nurture a talent like her,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","“She’s indeed very talented.” Chu Feng nodded, having witnessed Tianjian Canhua’s bloodline awakening.","However, he still couldn’t tell for sure whether he could be friends with Tianjian Canhua. Only through tribulations would one know whether their friends were reliable or not. Besides, he was barely acquainted with Tianjian Canhua, such that they couldn’t even be considered friends.","And truth be told, Chu Feng couldn’t care less how talented Tianjian Canhua was. He had never picked his friends by what they had, but by how they treated him.","So, Chu Feng continued, “Elder, do you belong to their lineage?”","He was more inclined to befriend Tianjian Qingyuan.","“I’m not, but I am, after all, from the Heavensword Sacred Palace too. I feel obliged to lend them a helping hand. You should be able to tell, right?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“Elder, are you referring to the legacy?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right.”","Chu Feng could tell that Tianjian Qingyuan didn’t share the entirety of the legacy with the others. She retained more than half of it for herself.","“Elder, you obtained that legacy with your means. You aren’t obliged to share any of it with anyone,” Chu Feng replied.","Tianjian Qingyuan smiled without saying anything, though that was enough to signal her agreement with Chu Feng’s viewpoint. Chu Feng’s bootlicking on point.","“Are there more Heavensword Sacred Palace lineages out there in the world of cultivation? Elder, are you from the main lineage?” Chu Feng asked, curious to know if there were stronger Heavensword Sacred Palaces out there in the present world of cultivation.","But Tianjian Qingyuan didn’t answer.","Chu Feng caught the drift and didn’t ask on.","Tianjian Qingyuan suddenly asked, “How much have you deciphered from the Immemorial Cemetery?”","“So far, I can only tell that a realm exists within every tombstone,” Chu Feng said.","“I advise you not to venture too deep into the Immemorial Cemetery. Some fortuitous encounters are within your means, but some will lead you to your doom,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","“I understand. I don’t intend to explore the Immemorial Cemetery. I only came here to look for my grandmother,” Chu Feng replied.","“You should look around since you’re already here. Someone of your talent should be able to reap some benefits,” Tianjian Qingyuan said as she hurled a talisman paper toward Chu Feng.","It was a location talisman.","Chu Feng understood what she meant. She was telling him not to wait around and instead explore the area; she would look for him after she found his grandmother. So, he stowed away the location talisman,","“Elder, have you deciphered something about the Immemorial Cemetery?” Chu Feng asked.","Tianjian Qingyuan’s light blue eyes were formidable. On top of that, she had breached this tombstone’s formation and acquired its legacy. She must have some insights regarding this place. Perhaps she could offer some advice.","“My judgment is the same as yours. I can’t see too deeply into this place,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Soon, the vortex reappeared, and Tianjian Qingyuan stepped in. She flicked her wrist, and a sword appeared in her hands. She disappeared in the vortex without bidding Chu Feng farewell.","Chu Feng stood on the spot, stunned.","“Chu Feng, that copper sword...” Eggy said.","“Yes, it’s the same one that appeared in God’s Era. She was the one who defeated all those monstrous beasts.” Chu Feng smiled.","Countless people were gathered around God’s Era when it first opened. Millions of Heavenly God level monstrous beasts rushed out from God’s Era, ready to massacre.","The crowd was plunged into despair.","At this crucial moment, a copper sword appeared out of nowhere and made quick work of the millions of Heavenly God level monstrous beasts.","The sword’s owner never appeared, but everyone knew that she had to be an extremely powerful individual, possibly even the strongest person in the world of cultivation. That copper sword displayed strength compared to a deity, transcending everyone’s imagination.","And Tianjian Qingyuan had the same copper sword.","Despite knowing that Tianjian Qingyuan was extremely strong, Chu Feng realized that he was still underestimating her, especially when he recalled the shock he had felt that day. This was a good thing, as she might just be able to find his grandmother and bring her back.","If even she couldn’t do it, it was unlikely that anyone would be able to."]},{"number":6382,"title":"Chapter 6382: Chapter 6380: Ambush!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6380: Ambush!","Even after Tianjian Qingyuan disappeared in the vortex, Chu Feng continued staring at the vortex with a contemplative look.","“What’s wrong? Why are you standing in a daze?” Eggy asked.","“I’ve been cultivating hard, but there are still so many things I’m unable to deal with. I thought I was making progress, but I’m still unable to protect the people I care about,” Chu Feng said with a sigh.","“That’s just life. There’ll always be things beyond your control, even if you wield unparalleled strength. You’ll still have the same troubled face as before,” Eggy said.","“I don’t have a troubled face,” Chu Feng pointed out.","“You might not be showing it, but I know you’re worried about your grandmother. Don’t worry too much about it. If you aren’t strong enough, you just have to work harder. I know your big sister told you to steer clear of this place, but since we’re already here, we might as well explore the area. Let’s see which tombstones contain fortuitous encounters that can further your strength,” Eggy said.","“My thoughts exactly. Let’s go,” Chu Feng said as he turned around and made his way out.","By the time they left the fog, the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace were already gone. They didn’t stop to wait for him. He wasn’t bothered by it as he wasn’t planning to travel with them in the first place.","Eggy, however, wasn’t happy with that.","“What’s wrong with the Heavensword Sacred Palace? How can they leave like that after Tianjian Qingyuan told them to help you? They have no gratitude at all!” Eggy grumbled.","“We didn’t tell them to wait for me, and they weren’t sure when I’d be coming out either. It’s normal for them to leave without me,” Chu Feng replied, thinking little about this matter.","When Chu Feng left the realm, he noticed the tombstone on the outside had become dull, though it didn’t become lifeless. It felt like an empty shell. It signaled that someone had claimed the tombstone’s legacy.","It was easy to tell whether a tombstone’s legacy had been claimed or not.","Tianjian Qingyuan likely chose this tombstone not because of its difficulty level, but because its legacy happened to be aligned with what they needed. It was not that hard to figure that out from the name of the tombstone’s owner, the Spirit Sword Reverent.","Since Chu Feng had decided to explore the Immemorial Cemetery, he should choose a tombstone that was helpful to him. Instead of venturing deeper in, he returned via the path he came from.","Soon, he arrived before one of the smaller tombstones in the Immemorial Cemetery. The tombstone looked ordinary and had no name on it, but Chu Feng still made his way toward it.","“Chu Feng, why did you choose this tombstone? It looks ordinary,” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","“While searching for my grandmother, I have also been assessing the tombstones along the way. I can’t see through some of the tombstones, and most of the ones I can see through aren’t of much use to me either. The ones that are useful to me exude different auras of danger.","“This tombstone is one of the less dangerous ones. Based on what I can see, it likely contains a fortuitous encounter related to world spiritist techniques,” Chu Feng explained.","“I thought you only had your grandmother in mind, but I guess that didn’t hinder your observations,” Eggy said with a laugh.","She thought Chu Feng had turned back because it was too dangerous to venture deeper into the Immemorial Cemetery. To think that he had already chosen a target.","Similar to the one before, this humongous tombstone was also shrouded in a layer of fog, and beyond the fog was a realm. This realm was monotonous in color, nowhere as beautiful as the one chosen by Tianjian Qingyuan.","The air felt heavy. The clouds, earth, mountains, and rivers were all gray. The realm felt suffocating and lifeless.","Whoosh!","A peculiar wind blew as soon as Chu Feng entered the realm, sweeping gray sand into the sky until it devoured him. The sand particles might be small, but they battered Chu Feng with great force reminiscent of little sharp knives. It was not lethal, but it ripped his skin.","At this rate, Chu Feng would be reduced to a pile of white bones.","“Are you fine, Chu Feng?”","Eggy wanted to rush out from the World Spirit Space when she noticed something was amiss about the sand, but Chu Feng exclaimed, “Don’t come out, Eggy. This is a formation. You won’t be able to withstand it either. I need to decipher the formation.”","So, Eggy stayed put and observed the situation. She trusted Chu Feng’s judgment.","Blood and flesh splattered from Chu Feng’s body. The sand bored countless holes in his body. The situation only seemed to worsen as time passed.","However, Chu Feng’s gaze remained unwavering as if he couldn’t feel any pain. He was focused on assessing the situation in search of a solution. It didn’t take long for his eyes to light up.","“Found it!”","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and released his spirit power in a special trajectory into the sand. His spirit power seemed to calm the sand. The sand fell back onto the ground, and the peculiar wind faded.","At the same time, a massive tombstone appeared in the distance.","“You’re incredible as always, Chu Feng,” Eggy complimented in excitement.","The tombstone should have been too far away for Chu Feng to see, but it seemed like the realm was guiding him to it as a reward for overcoming the trial.","“This must be a world spiritist’s tomb; there was a formation trial right after I entered this realm. On top of that, my concealment formation has been rendered useless,” Chu Feng said.","The master of this tombstone seemed to encourage competition.","“Chu Feng, how’s the difficulty level?” Eggy asked.","“It’s not easy, but I can handle it,” Chu Feng replied as he made his way to the tombstone.","Along the way, he noticed two fresh corpses devoid of origin energies. They must have failed to overcome the sand formation trial.","“Looks like some people have already entered this place,” Chu Feng said.","The sand formation posed a fatal danger to challengers, but it didn’t damage treasures. This could be seen from how Chu Feng’s clothes remained intact despite having countless holes bored into him earlier.","Most carcasses Chu Feng saw along the way had their clothes intact, but they were stripped of all their treasures. Chances were that their surviving companions had taken all their treasures.","Weng!","The sky suddenly glowed with incredible radiance, and humongous shackles emerged from the light and coiled around the realm. It was a sealing formation trapping everyone within the realm. However, this formation wasn’t intrinsic to this realm."]},{"number":6383,"title":"Chapter 6383: Chapter 6381: Jie Tian’s Father","paragraphs":["Chapter 6381: Jie Tian’s Father","Eight world spiritists appeared from all directions. They looked insignificant, like a grain of dust, but they were the ones behind the sealing formation. They were rank nine True Dragon World Spiritists.","But Chu Feng was unfazed by their presence. No one beneath Heavenly God level could faze him now.","“Is that the present-era prodigy Chu Feng?”","“The formation in this realm dispels all concealment. There’s no mistake. I doubt there’s anyone else in the world who looks the same as Chu Feng, right?”","“We lucked out!”","The eight world spiritists spoke among themselves instead of conversing with Chu Feng. They looked so relaxed as if he were prey snagged in their net.","Chu Feng could tell from their words that they were Ancient Era’s world spiritists.","Most of the powerful present-era world spiritists were in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, such that there were very few rank nine True Dragon World Spiritists not affiliated with them, and all of them were renowned throughout the world of cultivation.","These eight world spiritists didn’t conceal their faces, and they were all foreign faces. On top of that, they had also termed Chu Feng a ‘present-era prodigy’, which further suggested they were from the Ancient Era.","“You...”","Chu Feng was about to speak when a golden light flashed past the eight world spiritists.","Pu! Pu! Pu...","The eight world spiritists exploded into blood fogs.","Chu Feng frowned.","A gate opened beside Chu Feng, and Eggy stepped out from within. She sensed something was amiss, and she was prepared to make a move.","An even stronger entity had killed those eight world spiritists.","With the death of the eight world spiritists, the sealing formation disintegrated, but Chu Feng’s attention was set in another direction. An area of warped space could be spotted, and a figure dressed in a world spiritist cloak emerged.","“There’s no need to be nervous.” It was a middle-aged man’s voice. He pulled down his cloak and revealed his face. “You should call me uncle.”","“Uncle? You are Jie Tian’s father?”","Chu Feng could see the similarities between this middle-aged man and Jie Tian, and the other party’s words confirmed it. The other party must be Jie Tiannian’s husband, Jie Tian’s father, Jie Mubai.","Jie Mubai was a renowned world spiritist prodigy who dominated the era before Jie Ranqing rose to prominence.","“Indeed.” Jie Mubai smiled. With a wave of his sleeve, the blood fogs converged into a blood orb in his hand. “So these are the means of the Ancient Era’s world spiritists. How tenacious. They have a formation that would activate and destroy their treasures and origin energies as soon as they die. There’s nothing useful at all.”","He then turned to Chu Feng and smiled. “Calm down, Chu Feng. I know about your conflict with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and Tian’er, and while I am a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion too, I am on Tiannian’s side. If I wished to harm you, I wouldn’t have bothered conversing with you.”","He released a whiff of his spirit power, revealing himself to be a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. He was showing Chu Feng that he bore no animosity, or else he could have made a move and apprehended Chu Feng right away instead of engaging in a conversation.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has hidden its cards well. I didn’t expect there to be another Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist aside from Jie Tianran,” Chu Feng remarked.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t have any Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist before, but with the changes arising from God’s Era, we can’t continue holding back anymore. We used all our resources to push for a breakthrough. Right now, there are more than just two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Mubai said.","“Sounds like my opponent is getting stronger,” Chu Feng said.","“I don’t think your grudge with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has reached an irreconcilable stage. I hope you can sit down with Lord Mansion Master and have a good chat with him. We’re a family, after all. We can always talk things out,” Jie Mubai said.","“A family? Does Jie Tianran recognize his own family? Are you unaware of what he did to my aunt?” Chu Feng asked.","“Tiannian? What... happened to Tiannian?” Jie Mubai was taken aback.","“You don’t know?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s been a while since I returned to the Sacred Mansion. I don’t know what happened,” Jie Mubai replied nervously.","Chu Feng informed Jie Mubai about what Jie Tianran had done to Jie Shanxian, Daoist Starseizer, and Jie Tiannian. At the same time, he also told Jie Mubai how he entered and left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Those were no secrets, so there was no need to hide it from him.","“I didn’t expect Lord Mansion Master to be this obstinate.” Jie Mubai looked conflicted. He worriedly turned to Chu Feng and asked, “How is Tiannian and those two elders?”","“They are out of danger,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Mubai breathed a sigh of relief. “It’s a good thing you were lucky to have met that expert. Is that expert here at the Immemorial Cemetery, too?”","“I’m afraid I can’t divulge her affairs,” Chu Feng replied.","There was no way Chu Feng would reveal that Long Zhuoyan had left for the Ninth Galaxy.","“I understand.” Jie Mubai smiled. He turned to the tombstone and said, “I arrived ahead of you and found some clues. You must have chosen this tombstone because you think that its owner is a world spiritist.”","“Is that not the case? “Chu Feng asked.","“Your judgment is on the mark. A formidable world spiritist from the Immemorial Era is buried here.” He turned to Chu Feng and added, “But this tombstone isn’t that easy to breach. If you trust me, why don’t we work together and split the rewards?”","“Sure,” Chu Feng replied.","The two of them made their way to the tombstone. With Jie Mubai leading the way, it didn’t take them long to arrive before the tombstone.","Chu Feng first observed the surroundings before turning to the tombstone. He could tell that the crux of the fortuitous encounter was detailed on the tombstone.","“Either one of us can breach the tombstone, but it will be harder if you do it. The owner of the tombstone prefers to pass his legacy down to a junior,” Chu Feng said.","“My talent is lacking compared to yours, and I’ll leave the breaching to you. I won’t take advantage of you, however. You can request my help wherever needed. If I’m unable to contribute much, you can feel free to take all the rewards,” Jie Mubai replied coolly."]},{"number":6384,"title":"Chapter 6384: Chapter 6382: Inside the Coffin","paragraphs":["Chapter 6382: Inside the Coffin","“Sure.” Chu Feng accepted the deal before observing the tombstone once more.","Jie Mubai knew there were too many clues on the tombstone that it wouldn’t have been easy to decipher, so he didn’t rush Chu Feng. Instead, he observed the tombstone alongside him.","Moments later, Chu Feng began frowning. The more he observed, the tighter his frown became.","“Are you unable to decipher the tombstone?” Jie Mubai asked.","“I can decipher it, but it won’t be easy to breach it. I’ll require your help,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s a cooperation. Feel free to ask anything of me,” Jie Mubai replied.","“I’ll need these materials. Do you have them?”","Chu Feng conjured many materials with a wave of his sleeves—some were for constructing formations, whereas some were for other purposes. They were materials commonly used by world spiritists, but Chu Feng needed high-quality ones.","Without any hesitation, Jie Mubai took out all the required materials.","“Elder, you have all of them?” Chu Feng was surprised.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is the strongest world spiritist power in the world of cultivation, after all. We have no lack of materials,” Jie Mubai replied.","“Things might get a little dangerous later while breaching the formation. We’ll have to prepare a teleportation formation. My strength is limited, so I’ll leave it to you, elder.” Chu Feng conjured a formation blueprint with a wave of his sleeves.","“That’s quite an interesting teleportation formation.” Jie Mubai was mesmerized.","Constructing teleportation formations was easy for a world spiritist of his caliber, but Chu Feng’s formation blueprint was far more ingenious than any method he knew about. It was slightly more complicated, but the effects were much stronger.","“Elder, I know that it’s easy for you to construct a teleportation formation, but the danger we may encounter here cannot be underestimated. I implore you to construct the teleportation formation using the method I have entrusted to you,” Chu Feng said.","“Don’t worry. Leave it to me.”","Jie Mubai got to work. It would take him some time to construct a teleportation formation using Chu Feng’s blueprint.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng continued observing the tombstone.","When Jie Mubai was done constructing the teleportation formation, he took out two talisman papers and handed one to Chu Feng. By activating the talisman paper, Chu Feng could enter the teleportation formation right away and be transported to a safe location.","“That’s fast. Elder, you can leave the rest to me.”","Chu Feng formed a hand seal. Spirit power gushed out of his body and swiftly formed a massive formation.","Jie Mubai’s eyes glowed with satisfaction.","Chu Feng hadn’t been idling while he was constructing the teleportation formation—he, too, was constructing a formation, just that he did it within his body.","A formation constructed inside one’s body tended to be weaker, but Chu Feng’s formation perfectly resonated with the tombstone. It felt like a key fitting into a lock.","The brilliant light glowing from the tombstone told Jie Mubai that Chu Feng was on the right path. This formation had to be constructed inside one’s body. Doing it outside would instead result in failure.","Hu!","As the two formations fused, the peculiar wind appeared once more. It was stronger than before, almost cloaking the entire world in a sandstorm.","Only the area where Chu Feng and Jie Mubai were at remained safe.","“Is it a purging? I doubt anyone else in this realm can survive that,” Jie Mubai remarked.","This sandstorm was different from the trial they had encountered when they first entered this realm. Not only was it stronger, but it was also far more difficult to breach. It was practically a death sentence to anyone else who was still in this realm.","At the same time, a coffin rose from the ground beneath the tombstone.","This coffin was extremely eerie. It was covered in a sinister gray aura that occasionally formed gazing eyes and let out bizarre howls.","“Don’t get close to it, Chu Feng,” Jie Mubai warned as he retreated to a distance away. He sensed that the gray aura would proactively attack anything within range.","Chu Feng changed his hand seal and released his spirit power.","Without any hesitation, the howling gray aura surged toward Chu Feng’s spirit power and gnawed at it. However, Chu Feng’s spirit power immediately emanated a golden light that caused the gray aura to scream in agony and retreat to the coffin.","Chu Feng quickly constructed another formation to seal off the gray aura and the coffin.","“His observation is extremely thorough!” Jie Mubai was startled.","Chu Feng must have learned the method to deal with the gray aura from the tombstone. Yet, despite being a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, Jie Mubai was unable to decipher that even though he had been studying the tombstone as well.","“Elder, give me a spirit power enhancing pill!” Chu Feng shouted.","Jie Mubai knew that it would take a lot of spirit power to deal with a powerful formation, so he reached into his Cosmos Sack and tossed many potent spirit power pills over.","But what Chu Feng did next shocked Jie Mubai.","Chu Feng stowed them into his Cosmos Sack without eating a single one. Sensing Jie Mubai’s questioning gaze, he explained, “Just in case.”","Jie Mubai didn’t harp on the matter. “Don’t get distracted.”","The gray aura remained extremely dangerous in his eyes despite knowing that Chu Feng had likely deciphered the method to deal with it. The slightest carelessness could spell not just Chu Feng’s doom but his as well.","He was already clutching onto the talisman paper of the teleportation formation Chu Feng had told him to construct.","Soon, he realized his worry was unfounded.","When Chu Feng changed his hand seal once more, his formation began to devour the eerie gray aura. It didn’t take long for the gray aura to be completely devoured, and the coffin finally revealed its true form.","There was nothing special about the coffin aside from its antiquated appearance.","Chu Feng stepped forward and opened the coffin. More gray aura immediately spurted out. However, this gray aura was different from the one outside. Not only did it not feel dangerous, but it was also emanating a faint light.","“Eggy, it’s origin energies,” Chu Feng said as he opened the gate to his World Spirit Space.","A powerful suction force pulled all the origin energies through the gate.","Jie Mubai stared intently at the opened coffin to see what was inside. However, the origin energies, despite being harmless, obstructed his view. It was only after Eggy absorbed all the origin energies that he was able to see what was in the coffin.","The coffin was empty.","“Is it empty?” Jie Mubai asked.","“Seems so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is there... nothing else?” Jie Mubai examined the tombstone once more.","Chu Feng had already breached the tombstone, so the rewards should be lying within the coffin. Yet, there was nothing in the coffin aside from the origin energies.","“There’s only origin energies?” Jie Mubai asked again.","“Seems so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Then... why didn’t you leave some for me? I’m a world spiritist too. I have world spirits,” Jie Mubai replied.","Chu Feng stared at him. “Why should I give you any origin energies? You didn’t contribute.”","“What did you say?” Jie Mubai stared at Chu Feng with widened eyes, wondering if he had misheard.","“You said you wouldn’t take anything if you didn’t contribute enough. Your words, not mine,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6385,"title":"Chapter 6385: Chapter 6383: You Are the Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6383: You Are the Treasure","Jie Mubai was first stunned before he snorted in anger, “I didn’t contribute? Who constructed the teleportation formation?”","“What does constructing that teleportation formation have to do with breaching this formation?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Mubai was stumped. “Fine. Even if the teleportation formation has nothing to do with breaching the formation, you have taken a lot of my items for it.”","“I did, but I didn’t use them,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Mubai was irked. “Chu Feng, why are you so irritating? I thought you were a sentimental person. This doesn’t align with what the rumors say about you.”","“I am a sentimental person, but only to humans,” Chu Feng replied.","“What do you mean by that?” Jie Mubai asked.","“What do you think about my discernment?”","“You have sharp eyes. I don’t know how you do it, but I’ll concede as much your eyes are keener than mine.”","“Then why do you think I can’t see through your tricks?”","“What tricks? Get to the point.”","“You should know better whether those eight world spiritists are humans or formations.”","“You’re saying that the eight world spiritists are formations, and you suspect I conjured them to win your goodwill?”","“What else could it be?”","“Chu Feng, you’re too cautious. I might be from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but I should have made it clear I’m on Tiannian’s side. It’s good to be wary, but you shouldn’t push aside those who are on your side.”","“I’ll concede as much as your formation is ingenious. I couldn’t tell that those eight world spiritists were formations at first. You sold yourself out when you said that they had prepared formations to destroy their origin energies and treasures while collecting their blood fogs. But I didn’t sense any formations when their bodies shattered. They had no such formations on them. You were just trying to conceal they didn’t have origin energies,” Chu Feng said.","Jie Mubai laughed helplessly. “Why don’t you tell me what reason I have for doing this?”","“You arrived at this place long ago, and you discovered that it’ll be easier for a junior to breach this place than to do it yourself. You noticed me as soon as I arrived here, so you staged that show to win my goodwill. You wanted to use me to breach this tombstone,” Chu Feng replied.","“A plausible theory, but you’re thinking too much. Those eight world spiritists aren’t conjured from formations. I don’t have the means to conjure eight pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists. They do have a formation that destroys their treasures and origin energies, but they are deeply hidden. You were probably too tense to notice it then,” Jie Mubai explained.","“Continue the act. I’m listening,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, there’s no need for me to go through so much trouble just to deal with you. Do you think you would stand a chance against my spirit power?” Jie Mubai asked.","“Are you stronger than Jie Tianran? And what makes you think I’m alone?” Chu Feng asked, intending to intimidate Jie Mubai.","He had intentionally refused to answer Jie Mubai’s question about Long Zhuoyan to make the latter wonder if he still had Long Zhuoyan’s backing at the moment.","“I have no fear, even if you have that powerhouse’s backing. Someone of that stature won’t attack me over your skepticism.” Jie Mubai clasped his fist at the sky and said, “Elder, please reveal yourself and judge this matter. Do the eight world spiritists exist, or did I conjure them from a formation?”","“You aren’t worthy of meeting that person,” Chu Feng replied.","He could tell that Jie Mubai was trying to probe him to see if he truly had someone behind him.","“Forget it. It’s just some origin essences and resources. You can take them if you wish. I’ll think of them as an introduction gift,” Jie Mubai replied with a helpless sigh.","“Why is that fellow still acting? What is he up to? I have already devoured the origin energies, so there shouldn’t be anything else for him to take,” Eggy asked.","“No, there’s still something else. I underestimated him. I thought he couldn’t see through it, but he must have noticed,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is there more to the reward?” Eggy was surprised.","“Yes. I’ve been suppressing it with my formation, but I’m at my limit now. It looks like I’ll have to share the treasure with him.”","Chu Feng withdrew his formation, and the coffin shattered. Spirit power gushed into the air, swirling in the sky before forming a gigantic map. The map marked a tombstone and the way to breach it.","Jie Mubai smirked upon seeing the map. “I knew the origin energies couldn’t have been all there is to the treasure. But why is it only appearing now? I see, you must have been suppressing, but you have reached your limit now.”","Even his tone had changed.","“You’re finally dropping your act?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Mubai sneered, “You’re right. I arrived a long time ago, and I refrained from making a move because I wasn’t confident of breaching the formation. I conjured the eight world spiritists using a treasure to win your trust. You might have seen through my act, but you still did my bidding. This is still the outcome I wanted. But what I want the most isn’t the treasure here. You are the true treasure here.”","Jie Mubai looked at Chu Feng with eyes brimming with viciousness and greed."]},{"number":6386,"title":"Chapter 6386: Chapter 6384: Soul Talisman Locked","paragraphs":["Chapter 6384: Soul Talisman Locked","“Chu Feng, I’ll handle him,” Eggy said with a murderous aura from the World Spirit Space.","“Having Milady Queen deal with him would be flattering him,” Chu Feng replied before turning to Jie Mubai. “You want my treasures? Give it a try.”","Boom!","Jie Mubai’s spirit power gushed like a volcanic eruption, manifesting as a behemoth and charging toward Chu Feng. However, the spirit power was blocked by an invisible wall before it could reach Chu Feng.","At the same time, the sand suddenly assaulted Jie Mubai. Its attack was much more ferocious than what Chu Feng faced earlier in his test.","The sandstorm should have brought Jie Mubai down, no matter how strong he was, for the sand passed through spirit power and treasures.","But soon, Chu Feng widened his eyes in shock.","The sand stopped just a meter away from Jie Mubai. It was blocked by a ray of light coming from Jie Mubai’s hand. It was a copper candle that emitted a green light, and it was keeping the gray sand at bay.","The candle possessed the same aura as the tombstone.","Chu Feng realized that Jie Mubai had made some progress, even though he wasn’t confident in breaching the formation. He must have obtained the candle before Chu Feng arrived.","The candle served as a death immunity token, making the sandstorm no threat to him.","“Is that the source of your confidence?” Jie Mubai asked.","Chu Feng’s ability to control the sandstorm was a reward for breaching the tombstone, but it also revealed that the powerhouse was not with Chu Feng. Otherwise, Chu Feng wouldn’t have to go through so much trouble here.","Jie Mubai waved his sleeves, and the surrounding ground cracked. Massive light pillars rose from the ground, each one comparable to the tombstone. The light pillars converged to form what resembled a massive lantern, sealing off this realm.","This was the sealing formation Jie Mubai had prepared long ago.","“As formidable as the sandstorm is, it can only damage living beings. Your control over the formation here is also limited. You can only use it for self-defense against attacks within a radius. Let’s see how you can deal with my sealing formation,” Jie Mubai said with a smirk.","Chu Feng took out a teleportation talisman with a flick of his wrist. It was the teleportation formation he had instructed Jie Mubai to construct earlier. Squeezing the talisman paper would immediately transport one into the formation.","“Hahahaha!” Jie Mubai burst into laughter upon seeing the talisman paper.","Only the talisman paper he kept worked. The one he had given Chu Feng was ineffective.","What Chu Feng did next made his smile freeze.","Chu Feng tore the talisman paper.","“Do you think I can’t tell that your talisman paper doesn’t work?” Chu Feng asked.","“Then you should know that you’re cornered,” Jie Mubai scoffed.","“Who told you I need a talisman paper to activate a teleportation formation?” Chu Feng replied with a smile. He formed a hand seal and vanished into thin air. He had entered the teleportation formation.","“That fellow!” Jie Mubai quickly ripped his talisman paper,","Much to his shock, he remained on the spot. He wasn’t transported into the teleportation formation.","“Damn it!” Jie Mubai realized he had underestimated Chu Feng.","He was the one who constructed the teleportation formation, but he lost control over the formation just because he followed Chu Feng’s method.","The teleportation formation was so fast that even Jie Mubai would struggle to catch up with it. He looked up at the sky with determination in his eyes. He reached into his Cosmos Sack and took out a bizarre talisman paper.","This talisman paper emanated an Ancient Era’s aura, and it was shrouded in a light that continuously flickered between red and green. Its runes resembled specters, making it look incredibly sinister.","“Soul Talisman lock on. You have nowhere to hide,” Jie Mubai murmured.","The talisman paper burst into flames, transforming into an eerie aura that first coiled around where Chu Feng was before vanishing.","...","It didn’t take long for Chu Feng to leave the tombstone realm and return to space, thanks to the teleportation formation.","He didn’t stop after leaving the teleportation formation. He continued flitting ahead, making his way toward the location pinpointed on the map inside the tombstone realm. That was where the true treasure or legacy was.","He thought he could kill Jie Mubai with the sand and monopolize the treasure, but he didn’t expect Jie Mubai to acquire the candle that made him immune to the sandstorm.","Jie Mubai would surely head to that location too, but Chu Feng wouldn’t surrender the treasure easily to him. He might encounter Jie Mubai there, but it should be fine as long as he didn’t get into a direct confrontation with the latter.","If he could leverage the initiative he had claimed from deciphering the earlier tombstone, he might be able to stand up against Jie Mubai then.","That said, their earlier clash made him realize that Jie Mubai was no pushover, so he dared not let his guard down. Even while making his way toward the location, he extended his senses to the largest possible radius.","Shortly after, he sensed a dangerous aura approaching. It was Jie Mubai.","“How did you find me?” Chu Feng turned around and asked aloud.","He activated his Lightning Mark, Lightning Armor, Lightning Wings, and Lightning Aura, raising his cultivation from rank five to rank nine True God level. There was nothing in the direction he was looking.","“Kikiki...”","Space suddenly warped, and Jie Mubai appeared. “I didn’t expect you to sense me.”","He stopped and assessed Chu Feng from afar. “You’re not just a talented world spiritist but a prodigious cultivator too. You do have a bright future ahead of you. It’s a pity it will all end in my hands today.”","“Do you think you have the means to end my future?” Chu Feng mocked.","“Where can you escape now that you don’t have a teleportation formation?” Jie Mubai was confident in his ability as a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. He didn’t think Chu Feng could give him the slip a second time.","He wouldn’t even fear a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator, let alone a rank nine True God level Chu Feng.","“How did you find me?” Chu Feng asked.","His teleportation formation had a bizarre configuration that should have made it impossible for Jie Mubai to trace his exit location. On top of that, Chu Feng had been concealing his aura with a concealment formation.","It shouldn’t have been possible for Jie Mubai to find Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had only extended his senses out of vigilance.","Yet, Jie Mubai still found him somehow.","“There are countless fortuitous encounters in the world. You aren’t the only lucky one.”","Instead of answering Chu Feng’s question, Jie Mubai raised his hand, and his spirit power morphed into a behemoth that reached forth to grab Chu Feng."]},{"number":6387,"title":"Chapter 6387: Chapter 6385: High Regard","paragraphs":["Chapter 6385: High Regard","There should have been no way for Chu Feng to dodge the means of a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. No matter how far away he was, it was only a matter of time before he was captured.","But Chu Feng flitted off with a harrumph, expanding the distance between him and Jie Mubai.","Astounded, Jie Mubai quickly withdrew his attack and plastered two talisman papers on his thighs. He formed a hand seal, and his thighs blazed with golden flames. These flames didn’t burn his clothes, but they greatly enhanced his movement speed.","Even so, Chu Feng still got further and further away from him. It didn’t take long for Chu Feng to disappear before his eyes.","Only Chu Feng’s mocking voice could be heard in his surroundings. “That isn’t much of a fortuitous encounter you have there.”","Jie Mubai clenched his jaws and stopped his pursuit, knowing he couldn’t catch up with Chu Feng. He finally understood why Jie Tianran struggled to deal with Chu Feng. The latter was indeed as slippery as an eel.","It turned out that Chu Feng could escape from him even without a teleportation formation.","...","“Elder, it’s thanks to your Divine Flitting that I could escape from him,” Chu Feng expressed his gratitude to the Divine Deer.","After raising his cultivation to rank nine True God level, his maximum speed with Divine Flitting surpassed that of a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator.","“He must have used some means to lock onto you. He’ll likely find you again soon. While you can outrun him with Divine Flitting, this won’t work in the long run. Using Divine Flitting takes too much of a toll on you,” the Divine Deer said.","“I’ll just have to take a step at a time. Maybe he’ll give up in due time,” Chu Feng replied.","“What about the location on the map? Are you going to give up on it?”","It would be extremely dangerous for Chu Feng to head to the location pinpointed by the tombstone realm. If Jie Mubai had truly locked onto him, it would only take moments for the other party to find him.","There was no chance for Chu Feng to claim the initiative there.","“Elder, would you believe me if I said that I don’t fear him? I just don’t want to waste too much time on someone unworthy,” Chu Feng said.","“What’s your plan?” the Divine Deer asked.","“It’ll be great if I can find a helper, but the chances are likely that Jie Mubai will head to the location straight. That means that I won’t make it in time even if I find a helper. Haa, perhaps the treasure is fated not to be mine.”","Chu Feng decided to give up on the treasure.","There was no lack of tombstones in the Immemorial Cemetery anyway. With his competency, there was no need to fuss over a fortuitous encounter. He could simply look for another suitable tombstone to work on.","Thus, he began looking for another tombstone realm.","He proceeded carefully, knowing Jie Mubai was tracking him. But no matter how he looked, he couldn’t find any lingering spirit power on him. He had also inspected the items he had received from Jie Mubai, but there were no tracking formations on them.","Jie Mubai did possess peculiar means, so it would be best for Chu Feng to keep his guard up.","Fortunately, Jie Mubai didn’t continue chasing him. Jie Mubai must have figured out that he couldn’t capture him, so he went to the location pinpointed on the map to obtain the fortuitous encounter instead.","“That is...?”","Chu Feng soon spotted several warships swiftly cruising through space. They flew the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s flags.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan is here. Chu Feng, do you think they’ll help you?” Eggy was even more excited than Chu Feng to see them.","They started on the wrong foot, but Chu Feng later solicited the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s help to deal with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect. In exchange, he helped Huangfu Shengyu make a breakthrough in his bloodline. They were on good terms now.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan should have gone to the Fortuitous Bloodline Mountain too, but they were nowhere to be seen when Chu Feng arrived. They must have left in advance.","Chu Feng didn’t expect to bump into them here.","“Let me give it a try.”","Ultimately, he was still reluctant to hand the fortuitous encounter to Jie Mubai for free.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan was not to be underestimated, and their clan chief was a rank three Heavenly God level cultivator. If they were willing to step in, Chu Feng would have no fear of Jie Mubai.","Thus, he constructed a formation to catch the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s attention. They were cruising at such a fast speed that it would be hard for Chu Feng to catch up with them even with Divine Flitting. Their clan chief must have been personally driving the warship.","Fortunately, Chu Feng’s formation quickly caught the attention of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s warships. They turned around and flew toward where Chu Feng was.","Chu Feng revealed himself.","As the warship approached, several figures flitted out to meet him. Among them were familiar faces like Huangfu Zhantian, Huangfu Shengyu, and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, too.","“It really is you, Chu Feng. What a coincidence to bump into you in the massive Immemorial Cemetery!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were overjoyed to see Chu Feng, especially Huangfu Zhantian. However, Chu Feng noticed the conflicted look in their eyes despite their delight.","“Chu Feng, are you alone?” Huangfu Shengyu asked.","“Yes, I am,” Chu Feng replied. “You seem to be in a rush. Did something happen?”","“It’s a long story. Do you have anything on hand right now? If not, why don’t you travel with us? We can at least look after each other,” Huangfu Shengyu said.","“I do have something up at the moment, but since you’re in a rush, why don’t we settle your problem first? Chu Feng said as he made his way toward the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s warship.","“We have bumped into some trouble, but it’s nothing major. You mentioned that you have something up. What is it? Is it something we can help you with?”","“Why don’t you tell me what it is first?” Chu Feng asked.","Huangfu Shengyu looked conflicted.","The impatient Huangfu Zhantian berated, “Stop being so wishy-washy. This is nothing to hide!”","Huang Zhantian sat down next to Chu Feng and asked, “Chu Feng, how are your ties with the Divine Body Sacred Mansion?”","“The Divine Body Sacred Mansion? Are you referring to the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes yes, the power that specializes in Divine Bodies,” Huangfu Zhantian replied.","“I have a friend there. We are on close terms,” Chu Feng replied.","“I see. Our elder found a fortuitous encounter in a tombstone realm, but there happened to be Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s members there as well. We asked them to back off, but they refused to listen and even injured our elder. We’re heading there to deal with the matter,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“Are there any casualties?” Chu Feng asked.","“None at all.” Huangfu Zhantian shook his head.","“Is the elder severely wounded?” Chu Feng probed on.","“It’s not severe, but it’s a matter of pride. We can’t appear weak, especially not in front of a present-era power,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“I understand that, but since the damage isn’t severe, could you resolve this matter amicably on my account?” Chu Feng asked.","“Uh...” Both Huangfu Zhantian and Huangfu Shengyu dared not make that decision. They turned their heads to the clan chief.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief laughed.","“We have heard you’re on close terms with someone from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, and we’re heading there to demand an explanation. We weren’t planning to do anything as long as they didn’t go overboard. Rest assured, Chu Feng. We have high regard for not just you but your friends, too,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said."]},{"number":6388,"title":"Chapter 6388: Chapter 6386: Yuwen Yanri’s Legacy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6386: Yuwen Yanri’s Legacy","“Chu Feng, it’s a good thing we met you. It’ll be easier to resolve our conflict with the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion if you mediate between us,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Chu Feng’s heart finally rested at ease.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion had advanced significantly as well, but it was still lacking compared to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. If the Huangfu Heavenly Clan decided to massacre them, they wouldn’t stand a chance at all. That was why Chu Feng intervened.","If words didn’t work, he would have to resort to other measures.","Since Wang Qiang was indebted to the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, Chu Feng couldn’t stand still when someone sought to harm it. Not to mention he had a good impression of Yuwen Yanri, too.","“Chu Feng, they aren’t going to come to blows, and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion isn’t going to be of any help. Why don’t you take the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to the location and vie for the treasure first?” Eggy was more concerned about whether Chu Feng could obtain the fortuitous encounter or not.","“No rush. The map contains clues on how to obtain the treasure. The clues are extremely obscure; I have been thinking about them along the way, but I haven’t been able to decipher them yet. Even if Jie Mubai arrives first, he won’t be able to decipher it that quickly. If anything, his effort would only benefit me,” Chu Feng said.","“What if Jie Mubai deciphers it before you do?” Eggy asked.","“Then I’d have made a mistake, and I ought to bear the consequences of it,” Chu Feng replied.","“You say that, but I bet you’re confident in your conjecture. I trust your judgment,” Eggy said with a chuckle.","Meanwhile, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen continued chatting with Chu Feng. They were so friendly that they were practically fawning on him. It was not just Huangfu Shengyu and Huangfu Zhantian, but even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, too.","Chu Feng felt slightly awkward. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan was nowhere as friendly as the last time they met.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan had been regretting not deepening their ties with Chu Feng ever since they parted ways, which was why they were being extremely friendly now. It was only after meeting Chu Feng that they chose to reconcile with the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","Otherwise, they would have made sure the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion paid a heavy price for slighting them. Even an all-out massacre was not out of the question.","One would have to be naive to expect kindness from a power that dared wreak havoc at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","...","One of the tombstone realms in the Immemorial Cemetery was enveloped in an iridescent light. That was the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s defensive formation.","The defensive formation consisted of three layers, with the innermost layer being the strongest.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s experts were gathered under a humongous tombstone. They sat with crossed legs as they channeled their martial power into the defensive formation.","The only ones not channeling the defensive formation were the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master and his grandson, Yuwen Yanri.","The mansion master sat on the ground. His face, neck, hands, and other unclothed areas were covered in horrifying scars. These scars appeared old, but they weren’t there before he entered God’s Era.","He held a thick, golden stick in his hand. This stick seemed more like a treasure than a weapon.","The mansion master didn’t conceal his aura; he had made a breakthrough and reached rank two Heavenly God level. Yet, his eyes remained vigilant as if he were facing the biggest crisis in his life.","And it was all because of Yuwen Yanri.","Yuwen Yanri stood in front of the tombstone.","A name was inscribed on the tombstone—’Skyblaze Lord’. The runes on the tombstone flew forth like an army of snakes and surged into Yuwen Yanri’s body.","Yuwen Yanri was inheriting a legacy.","That was why the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion was so uptight.","To make things worse, they had just gotten into a fight with a Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder. They had only retaliated after the latter injured one of their members, but even so, they had still spared his life.","That said, the Ancient Era’s races scorned the present-era cultivators so much that they were reluctant to reason things out with them.","The mansion master had no idea how strong the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was or whether they would seek vengeance or not, but it would be a disaster if they did, especially since Yuwen Yanri was at the critical phase of inheriting the legacy.","“They really came?”","The mansion master suddenly stood up with a frown. Everyone from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion devoted their all into channeling the defensive formation, further reinforcing it.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s warship had appeared in distant space and was swiftly approaching them.","Boom!","Terrifying oppressive might suddenly crushed down on the defensive formation. Everyone from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, including the mansion master, was horrified.","It was a rank three Heavenly God level cultivator!","Against such an opponent, their defensive formation wouldn’t last long even if they desperately channeled all their martial power into it.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan is that powerful?”","Many people felt despair.","“Keep calm and don’t panic. We shouldn’t embarrass ourselves in front of the enemy!” the mansion master bellowed. If a cultivator was already trembling in cowardice before the battle, there would be no point in taking the fight.","Yuwen Yanri spoke up, “Grandfather, let them have this legacy. We shouldn’t put our mansion’s future on the line over a single legacy.”","“If only things were that simple, Yanri. The Ancient Era’s races view us, present-era cultivators, with animosity. I doubt they will let us go even if we give them the legacy. Besides, our Divine Body Heavenly Mansion has many powerful Divine Bodies. I bet they covet those...”","The mansion master sounded helpless despite having just reprimanded everyone else.","Just then, a familiar voice echoed through the oppressive might. It was not from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief but Chu Feng. “Brother Yuwen, you may inherit that legacy at ease. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan isn’t an enemy.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief had unleashed his oppressive might to allow Chu Feng’s voice to pierce through the defensive formation and reach every nook and cranny of the tombstone realm.","Chu Feng had to relay the message urgently because he noticed that the legacy inheritance had already begun.","The tombstone’s owner had been revealed to be the Skyblaze Lord.","The name itself suggested that he specialized in fire, and Yuwen Yanri’s Divine Body was the Blazing Sun Divine Body, which happened to be related to fire, too.","Judging by how the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion was desperately guarding the tombstone realm, the legacy must be very compatible with Yuwen Yanri.","Yuwen Yanri was already at the crucial phase of the inheritance and mustn’t be interrupted, or else he would be in danger. That was why Chu Feng chose to relay the message despite being still some distance away."]},{"number":6389,"title":"Chapter 6389: Chapter 6387: True Prodigy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6387: True Prodigy","“Chu Feng? Is it Chu Feng?”","“It is him! Was he kidnapped or what?”","As the warship came closer, the members of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion could see Chu Feng and the others. They saw Chu Feng standing alongside the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s experts. However, their first reaction was bewilderment.","Chu Feng might have explained the situation, but this whole thing seemed unbelievable to them. They knew Chu Feng had a grudge with the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“Is that... Huangfu Shengyu? He isn’t dead?” Yuwen Yanri noticed Huangfu Shengyu standing next to Chu Feng.","“Huangfu Shengyu is alive?”","The others from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion were baffled.","Huangfu Shengyu’s voice echoed, “Yuwen Yanri, Chu Feng didn’t kill me that day. Instead, he helped me make a breakthrough in my bloodline. I see him as a close friend now. I know you’re on good terms with Chu Feng. We had our differences, but we didn’t come seeking vengeance. Rather, we wish to talk things through. You can receive your legacy with ease of mind. If anyone dares disturb you, our clan will destroy them on your behalf.”","The members of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion felt like they were in a dream.","It was one thing for them to doubt Chu Feng’s words, but if even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was saying the same thing, there was no reason for them to remain skeptical.","There was no reason for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to lie to them when they had a rank three Heavenly God on their side. If they wanted vengeance, they could have made a move straight away. There was no need for them to resort to trickery.","So, Yuwen Yanri received the legacy with ease of mind.","Soon, the crowd turned their eyes toward the tombstone. It had suddenly ignited with raging, golden flames that roared ferociously like a heaven-devouring beast. This raging flame flowed into Yuwen Yanri’s body along with the legacy’s energy.","Yuwen Yanri’s face warped in pain.","“This doesn’t look good. Most people won’t be able to withstand the legacy,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","He had already concluded that Yuwen Yanri would fail. It was not that he looked down on Yuwen Yanri, but that the flames were so potent that even he was not confident of withstanding them.","The one who was most worried about Yuwen Yanri was his grandfather.","“Yanri, let’s give up,” he said, knowing they couldn’t continue like that.","But Yuwen Yanri’s eyes hardened in determination. He formed a hand seal and allowed the flames to flow freely into his body. The flames swiftly incinerated his specially-made robes and burned large swathes of his martial power-cloaked skin.","But Yuwen Yanri didn’t back down. Instead, he said, “Tell the others to stay away from me!”","“Yanri, are you certain?”","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master realized what Yuwen Yanri was going to do, and the worry in his eyes deepened. Nevertheless, he still ordered all their members to stay away from the tombstone.","The defensive formation also transformed to protect against what was inside rather than outside.","“Haaa!” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief sighed. “The Blazing Sun Divine Body is ranked seventh in the Divine Body Ranking, but its violent and domineering power is beyond the means of most people to withstand. Yuwen Yanri is decently talented to be able to withstand it, but it’s a pity he doesn’t understand that it’s not worth losing his foundation over a fortuitous encounter.”","Many agreed with that judgment.","No matter how great the legacy was, it couldn’t be as great as the Blazing Sun Divine Body. There was no need for Yuwen Yanri to put his life on the line for this fortuitous encounter when he already had the Blazing Sun Divine Body.","“He might have wanted that legacy initially, but that’s not the case anymore,” Chu Feng said.","“Oh?”","The crowd was confused.","“Yuwen Yanri hasn’t been able to fully assimilate the Blazing Sun Divine Body, resulting in his body being constantly wrecked by its power. He’s using the legacy’s energy to temper his body and counteract the Blazing Sun Divine Body, so that he can finally fully assimilate it,” Chu Feng said.","“This... Won’t he die if he fails?”","“That explains it.”","The crowd was initially taken aback, but they soon understood the reason behind the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s tension.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion must have understood Yuwen Yanri’s intention.","“He might have a clear intent in mind, but the result is the same.” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief still didn’t have a high opinion of Yuwen Yanri.","“Elder, what makes you think so?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s recorded in the annals that the Blazing Sun Divine Body can be passed down, but very few are capable of truly controlling it. For their survival, those who inherited the Blazing Sun Divine Body would not hold onto it for too long. In the first place, it’s impossible to fully assimilate the Blazing Sun Divine Body. If so many powerhouses in the Ancient Era failed to do it, I doubt it’ll be any different for him,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","The sky suddenly turned pitch-black. There was not the slightest light to be seen, as if they had all been plunged into absolute darkness.","While the crowd was bewildered, a blinding light shone from the tombstone.","A brilliant sun emerged from the tombstone. Blazing flames rushed into the sky, ascending higher and higher until they pierced through the tombstone realm, but even so, they continued to expand.","It was a phenomenon!","The emergence of the phenomenon brought light back to the dark surroundings.","The flames from the legacy could no longer seep into Yuwen Yanri’s body, for he was releasing flames identical to those of the phenomenon. This was the power of the Blazing Sun Divine Body!","“Did he succeed?”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were in disbelief.","With a wave of his sleeves, Yuwen Yanri siphoned all the flames on the tombstone into his palm. The phenomenon vanished, and the flames around Yuwen Yanri dissipated.","Yuwen Yanri put on his robe as soon as he was done, but the crowd still noticed the burn scars previously on his body vanishing, and his disposition felt vastly different.","Many years of being tortured by the Blazing Sun Divine Body had given him a sickly appearance despite his tall stature, especially due to his emaciated physique and pale face. Now, he was still as emaciated as before, but his complexion looked much healthier, and his eyes glowed with spirit.","He was no longer the sickly youth he was before.","“He managed to pull it off,” Chu Feng remarked.","“To think there’s such a figure in the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and elders were stunned. They were forced to reassess Yuwen Yanri. The latter had accomplished a feat that they had always thought was impossible. His talent was astonishing!","“Looks like Chu Feng isn’t the only outstanding junior among the present-era cultivators,” Huangfu Zhantian remarked.","“Is that legacy so formidable?”","Unlike the others, who were awed by Yuwen Yanri’s transformation, Eggy was more interested to know how potent the Immemorial Cemetery’s legacies were.","“This legacy does complement Yuwen Yanri well, but his ability to fully assimilate the Blazing Sun Divine Body is also testimony to his talent,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He might have taken the crown at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, but Yuwen Yanri’s performance was also equally incredible. The latter’s talent was undeniable.","Chu Feng’s face suddenly warped in shock. He borrowed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief’s means to shout, “Be careful, Brother Yuwen!”","At the same time, he anxiously flew toward Yuwen Yanri."]},{"number":6390,"title":"Chapter 6390: Chapter 6388: A Warning From the Immemorial Cemetery’s Master?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6388: A Warning From the Immemorial Cemetery’s Master?","But it was already too late.","A brilliant light reminiscent of the sun shone from the tombstone realm, lighting up even the Immemorial Cemetery. An imprint flew forth from the earth and seeped into Yuwen Yanri’s chest.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s experts descended along with Chu Feng, allowing Chu Feng to arrive before Yuwen Yanri extremely quickly.","Yuwen Yanri also sensed something was amiss. He hurriedly tore off his clothes to check his chest. A massive, black rune imprint covered his entire chest, pulsating rhythmically like a heart, but it was not at the same frequency as his heartbeat.","It was alive.","“What is that?” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master asked in horror.","No one was more worried about Yuwen Yanri than him. Yuwen Yanri was the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s future and his grandson. He couldn’t accept a mishap befalling Yuwen Yanri moments after he fully assimilated the Blazing Sun Divine Body.","“Chu Feng.” Yuwen Yanri looked at Chu Feng with pleading eyes. He was flustered, too.","“Is it a curse?” Huangfu Zhantian asked Chu Feng.","They all trusted Chu Feng’s judgment.","“Do you feel unwell?” Chu Feng asked Yuwen Yanri.","“I don’t. It’s on my body, but I can’t feel it. It’s almost as if it doesn’t exist,” Yuwen Yanri said.","Chu Feng was already inspecting the rune imprint, but he couldn’t discern much from it. It was bizarre how the imprint was right in front of him, but he couldn’t discern it with his senses, as Yuwen Yanri had mentioned.","Since his other means didn’t work, he decided to use the Three Realms Divine Eyes to inspect the rune imprint on Yuwen Yanri’s body.","As soon as he unleashed the power of the Three Realms Divine Body, his surroundings suddenly morphed as a suction force dragged him into a pitch-black world.","He sensed a pair of gigantic eyes looking at him. It was a humongous entity whose size surpassed even a realm, but it was so far away that he couldn’t make out the other party’s features. Even after activating Heaven’s Eyes, he could only vaguely discern its outline.","The humongous entity sat on the ground with countless tendrils wriggling around it. It felt strong but malevolent.","“Didn’t someone warn you not to set foot here? Humans are greedy,” an earth-shattering voice echoed. It felt like the other party could destroy the world with just its voice.","But Chu Feng was more surprised by its words. It knew that someone had once warned him not to set foot here.","“You know my big sister?” Chu Feng asked.","Long Zhuoyan had previously warned him not to set foot here, but how did the other party learn about it? In any case, the humongous entity was terrifyingly powerful, such that he couldn’t hope to oppose the other party, no matter how he struggled.","So, Chu Feng intentionally mentioned Long Zhuoyan, knowing she was one of the strongest figures in the Ancient Era. He wanted to see if the humongous entity would spare him on Long Zhuoyan’s account.","But the humongous entity ignored his words and said, “The benefits here aren’t that easy to obtain, but it’s a good thing you came. Otherwise, they will all have to die. Remember, the only way to overcome this tribulation is the Seven Stars Orb. Head to the place marked on the map. You’ll find something there.”","The voice continued to echo in Chu Feng’s mind, but he had already been transported back.","“Who’s that, Chu Feng? Is that the master of this place?” Eggy asked.","“I’m not sure. It’s possible. It felt so strong that I couldn’t gauge its limits,” Chu Feng replied.","“It mentioned a map. Is it the same map you and Jie Mubai found?” Eggy asked.","“That’s most likely it,” Chu Feng replied.","What Chu Feng didn’t know was that a powerful suction force had dragged all observing powers outside into the Immemorial Cemetery. Then, the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance closed.","...","“Everyone, we might be in trouble,” Chu Feng addressed the crowd.","“What did you see?” the crowd asked.","“What’s happening to Brother Yanri isn’t just limited to him. It concerns all of us. I tried to observe his rune imprint earlier, but I was dragged into a spatial realm. There, I encountered a powerful entity. I’m not sure if it is the master of this place, but it told me that we might all die here,” Chu Feng said.","“We might all die here?”","The crowd looked unnerved. They didn’t come here to die. They would have been skeptical if those words had come from anyone else, but they trusted Chu Feng’s judgment.","Chu Feng had already demonstrated his superior discernment and judgment.","“What should we do, Chu Feng? Is it too late to leave right now?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder asked.","“I’m not sure if we can make it in time if we leave now,” Chu Feng replied.","“Lord Clan Chief, the entrance has closed!” a Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder shouted from the warship.","There was an observation formation on the warship, and through it, they saw that the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance had closed.","The experts from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion hurriedly checked with their observation means, and they found that the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance had indeed closed. They were all trapped here now.","“Chu Feng is right. We might all die here.”","The crowd panicked even more.","“Everyone, please follow me to a place. We might find a solution there.”","Chu Feng told the crowd about his encounter with Jie Mubai. He was planning to engage the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s help to claim the fortuitous encounter, but it was more than that now."]},{"number":6391,"title":"Chapter 6391: Chapter 6389: The Shocked Jie Mubai","paragraphs":["Chapter 6389: The Shocked Jie Mubai","They immediately set off after coming to a decision.","The further they were from the earlier tombstone realm, the more spectacular it looked. A humongous light halo shrouded the realm, looking brighter than most stars.","Despite having its legacy claimed, the tombstone realm looked much more divine than before, overshadowing all other realms they passed by along the way. It was as if it wanted everyone to see it.","“Could that tombstone realm be related to the Seven Stars Orb?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng observed the tombstone realm with his Heaven’s Eyes. He realized that the tombstone realm harnessed extraordinary energy that was waiting to blow up.","“That could be one of the Seven Stars. We might have to wait for all Seven Stars to emerge to truly understand what’s going on,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is this considered a trial? Will that humongous thing give you some reward if you clear it?” Eggy asked.","“I hope so,” Chu Feng replied with a smile, but he didn’t expect much.","The Immemorial Cemetery still felt as enigmatic and sinister as before, and so was the humongous entity he encountered in that bizarre space.","A while later, Chu Feng sat down to cultivate. He relayed their destination to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and entrusted the navigation to the latter.","He was cultivating not to raise his cultivation. He had reached a level where it would take him extremely long to make a breakthrough if he cultivated normally. What he needed more were impetuses and fortuitous encounters.","Besides, raising his cultivation by a rank or two wouldn’t help them much in a place like the Immemorial Cemetery.","He was cultivating toward something else. This had been the case since God’s Era emerged.","...","The Immemorial Cemetery was as vast as the world of cultivation. It contained countless tombstones, each one containing a massive realm.","Within it was a tombstone realm that looked ordinary on the surface, but within it, everything emanated a faint luster. The space was suffused with an extremely old aura. The realm was a humongous formation, and at its center was a gigantic, glowing tomb serving as the formation core.","A person stood before the tombstone—Jie Mubai.","He had arrived here some time back. To his delight, he discovered that this world didn’t just contain a simple legacy. It was likely connected to the core of the Immemorial Cemetery. If he could decipher the tombstone, he might be able to unravel the secret behind it.","He had already made some progress in the deciphering. He formed a hand seal and released his spirit power. It didn’t take long for his little body to unleash enough spirit power to suffuse the entire realm.","He changed his hand seal, and his spirit power manifested into a humongous formation that made the tombstone look small in comparison. This was the prowess of a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","He didn’t activate the formation right away.","Instead, he flicked his wrist and whipped out ten talisman papers emanating the Ancient Era’s aura. He tossed them at his formation’s ten formation cores, causing his formation to become even stronger.","“Activate!” Jie Mubai roared.","His formation finally whirred into action. His spirit power relentlessly washed over the tombstone, till the tombstone finally reacted.","Countless runes emerged from the tombstone like billions of fishes swimming freely in the sky. The key to deciphering this formation was to order these runes in the right sequence. This was a highly time-consuming activity, but Jie Mubai’s smile further deepened.","“Chu Feng, you mocked my fortuitous encounters for being so-so, but I’m still the one claiming this treasure. I’m sure you can decipher this formation too, but you don’t have the strength to conquer this land. This is life. This is fate. The Immemorial Cemetery’s fortuitous encounter is destined to be mine, Jie Mubai’s!” Jie Mubai declared excitedly.","It couldn’t be clearer that the Immemorial Cemetery’s fortuitous encounter was a huge deal.","But Jie Mubai’s eyes soon widened as he looked outside the realm.","“Who is it?”","He had constructed a formation around the realm to detect if anyone was in the vicinity, and the reaction he was getting unnerved him. He sensed several powerful auras, including ones above his.","“I guess the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists aren’t too shabby. You noticed us even from a distance away,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said from afar.","Several warships descended into the realm.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan?”","Jie Mubai frowned when he noticed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s flags on the warship. Jie Tianran had once killed a Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Heavenly God level cultivator, which meant there was a grudge between them. He hurriedly said, “I was from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but I have left it for many years now. If you’re here for vengeance, you’re knocking on the wrong door.”","“Hahahaha!” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief burst into laughter.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen laughed mockingly as well.","“Who could have thought the famous Jie Mubai would be a coward?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief sneered.","But Jie Mubai remained unfazed. He calmly explained, “I am merely speaking the truth.”","“Jie Mubai, our Huangfu Heavenly Clan didn’t come here to settle our scores with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. We came here to settle the scores with you,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Settle the scores with me?” Jie Mubai was confused.","“You offended someone you shouldn’t have.”","Jie Mubai frowned. Who did I offend? I don’t recall ever offending anyone from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","Just then, several more warships entered the realm. These warships were from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","Jie Mubai’s face quickly distorted. Chu Feng was on one of the warships, standing beside the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master and Yuwen Yanri!","“Chu Feng?!” Jie Mubai’s face twisted in anger.","It finally dawned on him that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was here to support Chu Feng.","“Oh? You didn’t notice me approaching despite having locked onto me? Ah, I get it. You can only sense me if you actively channel your treasure, right?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","He had told the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief to enter the tombstone realm ahead of him to avoid alarming Jie Mubai. From the looks of it now, his worry was unfounded.","“Chu Feng, I’ve underestimated you. You have the backing of not just the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion but an Ancient Era’s power, too. But you should have known that the Ancient Era’s powers view us, present-era world spiritists, with enmity. How can you join hands with them? How can you call yourself a present-era world spiritist?” Jie Mubai sneered.","“I judge people by their character, not their affiliation. Jie Mubai, you are a disgrace to all present-era world spiritists,” Chu Feng scoffed.","“Chu Feng, should I capture that man alive or kill him straight?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“Kill him. He has some good stuff on him. We can split them equally,” Chu Feng replied.","But Jie Mubai abruptly vanished, though his voice echoed, “Chu Feng, you said my fortuitous encounter is so-so, but I wonder if you can stop me from escaping.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief hurriedly enveloped the realm with his martial power, but he couldn’t find any traces of Jie Mubai at all."]},{"number":6392,"title":"Chapter 6392: Chapter 6390: A Battle of Pride","paragraphs":["Chapter 6390: A Battle of Pride","“That fellow is fast!” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was taken aback.","Even the difference in a single cultivation rank could spell an unbridgeable disparity in strength, which was why he was confident of capturing Jie Mubai. He didn’t expect the latter to be able to escape under his watch.","“He’s using a treasure. He has plenty of good stuff with him,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Mubai was no ordinary rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. He must have had a significant fortuitous encounter that granted him strength surpassing that of his peers. He might have chosen to flee, but it would be unwise to underestimate him.","Chu Feng would have rather eliminated Jie Mubai right now to avoid potential problems in the future. This situation was not ideal. He and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan already had a grudge with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so it didn’t make a difference to them.","But the same couldn’t be said about the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","He had tried persuading the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion not to reveal themselves; the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was more than enough to deal with Jie Mubai. But the latter insisted on standing on the same front as him.","“Don’t wallow in self-reproach, Chu Feng. The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion insisted on revealing themselves. This has nothing to do with you,” Eggy said.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master relayed a voice transmission to Chu Feng as well, saying, “Young friend Chu Feng, I revealed ourselves because I wanted to make my stance known. Jie Mubai’s escape could bring the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s wrath upon our Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, but you don’t need to worry about it.","“I nearly lost my life in God’s Era, but in exchange, I learned some secrets. The world of cultivation has changed since the Ancient Era. The natural energies around us are weaker than ever, which is why we struggle to raise our cultivation. It’s not because we’re lacking talent, but the environment limits our progress.","“Only the Ninth Galaxy retains the original form of the world of cultivation. The natural energies there are more suited for cultivators. I’m too old to harbor wild ambition, but someone of Yanri’s talent shouldn’t be buried in a place like this. We only came to the Immemorial Cemetery to see what opportunities there are; if not for that, we would have entered the Ninth Galaxy straight.","“Most of our members are already waiting for us at a realm near the Ninth Galaxy. We were planning to enter the Ninth Galaxy straight after leaving the Immemorial Cemetery.”","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief after hearing that. That explained the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s decision to reveal themselves. They didn’t fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s retribution because they were already planning to leave.","“What about Wang Qiang? Is he leaving with you?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have informed Wang Qiang of the matter. He doesn’t plan to travel with us, but he said he’ll enter the Ninth Galaxy in due time and meet us there. Chu Feng, someone as talented as you shouldn’t limit himself here. You should come to the Ninth Galaxy after resolving your conflicts with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master said.","“I will head there,” Chu Feng replied.","He didn’t jump into deciphering the formation. Instead, he observed the runes floating around the tombstone. These runes appeared to be imbued with life, each containing a secret. If he could string these secrets correctly, he might just unravel the Immemorial Cemetery’s secret.","But that was not all.","“There is martial enlightenment concealed here,” Chu Feng remarked.","“Martial enlightenment?”","The faces of the crowd turned grim.","The two most important things to advancing one’s cultivation were martial power and martial enlightenment. Accumulating martial power was required to raise one’s power level, but to make a breakthrough, martial enlightenment was necessary.","Martial enlightenment became increasingly elusive as one’s cultivation advanced. Furthermore, it was wisdom that couldn’t be relayed with mere words.","The natural energies in the world contained martial enlightenment, but it was insignificant. This was why many cultivators still struggled to make a breakthrough despite cultivating for tens of thousands of years.","“There is martial enlightenment in there? I don’t sense it.” Huangfu Zhantian was perplexed.","“I’ll use a special method to activate the runes. Make sure to take a close look, as you’ll have a chance to grasp the martial enlightenment contained within. However, I advise you to avert your eyes if you start feeling uncomfortable, or it might hurt your state of mind and body,” Chu Feng said.","“Ah, we have to grasp it ourselves? Bring it on! I can’t wait.” Huangfu Zhantian was excited.","Even though he was not a junior, he had been the most talented prodigy in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan prior to the appearance of Huangfu Shengyu and the others. He was extremely confident in his talent.","And he was not the only one.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master were also incredible prodigies in their own right. They couldn’t have reached their level of cultivation without outstanding talent.","Chu Feng formed several hand seals and unleashed a formation.","Unlike most formations, this one was intangible like the wind, but it stirred the runes floating in the air. The runes initially swayed with the wind, but before long, it was twirling around the crowd like a tornado.","“Ugh, I’m already at my limit!”","Many were already feeling vexed before observing the runes. They felt like they would go insane if they attempted to decipher the runes, so they quickly flew away and kept their eyes averted from the runes.","The process had barely begun, but most people had already been eliminated.","Those who remained began observing the runes, but more soon caved in. The feeling of vexation only intensified while looking at the runes. Even gathering their concentration was tough, let alone deciphering anything from it. The more they tried, the more vexed they felt. There was no chance of them getting accustomed to it at all.","So, more people backed out.","The sea of people gathered in the tornado of runes soon reduced to just several hundred. These people were either elders in important positions or prodigious juniors, with the latter being the majority.","But it didn’t take long for more to back down, too.","“There aren’t many people left. We’re the only two in the older generation who can stand our ground here,” Huangfu Zhantian excitedly told the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief.","As a Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s prodigy, he had been through similar trials in the past, and he had always been able to last till the very end. He relished being able to prove himself.","“Focus. Grasp whatever you can from the runes,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief replied. Even someone as strong as him wasn’t confident of grasping anything from the runes. He was barely holding on, with the feeling of vexation gradually getting the better of him.","He had to focus and gather his thoughts to decipher the runes, or else it wouldn’t matter how long he stared at them. In truth, he already knew he would likely walk away empty-handed from this fortuitous encounter. He was only persisting here to uphold his pride.","Many who remained shared the same thought as the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. They didn’t think they could grasp the martial enlightenment; they were merely holding on for their pride."]},{"number":6393,"title":"Chapter 6393: Chapter 6391: Willpower","paragraphs":["Chapter 6391: Willpower","The rune tornado gradually grew brighter, and the danger level rose to a terrifying level.","More people were forced to retreat. Only 21 people remained.","“Haa, I must be getting older.” The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master heaved a helpless sigh before taking his leave.","With his departure, everyone from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, except for Yuwen Yanri, had given up on deciphering the runes.","“Zhantian, you have to uphold the older generation’s dignity for us,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief sent a voice transmission to Huangfu Zhantian before retreating as well.","He had reached his limit, and he would put himself at risk of a cultivation deviation if he persisted. That mustn’t happen, or else the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s reputation would be sullied.","“Don’t worry. I have already grasped something,” Huangfu Zhantian replied confidently.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was not surprised. It was not without reason that Huangfu Zhantian was renowned as a prodigy within their clan. He might be the clan chief, but even he had to bow in defeat to Huangfu Zhantian’s talent.","Whoosh!","The raging winds suddenly became even louder as if a ferocious beast’s howl. Even Huangfu Zhantian, despite having deciphered parts of the runes, found himself struggling to hold on.","“Haa, the era has changed.”","With a helpless sigh, Huangfu Zhantian departed from the rune formation. He didn’t feel embarrassed as he lasted longer than most juniors.","Soon, there were only three people left on the field—Chu Feng, Yuwen Yanri, and Huangfu Shengyu.","“Are you two still doing fine?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’m fine. I don’t know if it’s due to my lacking intelligence or that the fortuitous encounter is insufficient, but the martial enlightenment contained inside the runes doesn’t seem to be potent. I don’t think I’ll be anywhere close to a breakthrough even if I decipher everything,” Huangfu Shengyu said.","“I can hold on,” Yuwen Yanri replied concisely.","“What you have experienced is the appetizer. The true show has yet to begin. If you two are feeling fine, I’ll begin the trial. Remember, don’t force yourself to hold on if you’re already at your limit,” Chu Feng said.","“What? We were eliminated even before the real trial began?” Huangfu Zhantian and the others were bewildered.","Huangfu Shengyu and Yuwen Yanri signalled that they were ready.","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and the rune tornado further accelerated.","The faces of the crowd turned grim. The runes in the tornado manifested into a complete formation. Roaring aura bodies emerged and lunged at Chu Feng and the others. It turned out the roars they had heard earlier weren’t just from the winds!","These aura bodies dove through the bodies of Chu Feng and the others, inflicting mental damage on them.","Chu Feng’s face remained impassive as if unfazed. Yuwen Yanri frowned, but the mental attacks failed to shake him up. Huangfu Shengyu, however, looked increasingly strained as more aura bodies passed through his body.","“Damn it!”","Unwilling to give up, Huangfu Shengyu gritted his teeth and held on. Veins popped on his temples, his complexion turned ghastly pale, and his face scrunched from the pain. Killing intent even flared from him.","Even so, he refused to give up.","“Shengyu, don’t force yourself!” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief shouted, fearing Huangfu Shengyu’s mind would crumble at this rate.","But Huangfu Shengyu seemed unable to hear him.","Flustered, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief tried exerting his martial power to drag Huangfu Shengyu out, but to his astonishment, his martial power dissipated when approaching the rune formation.","This left him with no choice but to personally head into the rune formation and drag Huangfu Shengyu out.","Before he could get close, an aura body flew over and passed through his body, causing his movements to immediately stop. His mind went blank, and he forgot about the danger his son was in.","“Damn it!”","Upon seeing the situation, Huangfu Zhantian activated the Lightning Mark and Lightning Armor, raising his cultivation from rank one to rank three Heavenly God level. But before he could make a move, Chu Feng emerged from the rune formation with Huangfu Shengyu in his arms.","It just so happened that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief regained consciousness at this moment.","“He’s fine. He just needs time to recover,” Chu Feng said as he handed Huangfu Shengyu over to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief.","“Chu Feng, you...” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was startled.","“I’m sorry, Chu Feng,” Huangfu Shengyu regained consciousness and apologized.","The runes had to be deciphered in a single go, or else one would have to start anew. By carrying Huangfu Shengyu out of the rune formation, Chu Feng’s earlier efforts had gone down the drain, and he would have to start from scratch.","Not to mention the difficulty level would be much higher now that the runes had formed a formation. He would have to withstand the formation’s attacks while deciphering the runes.","This would be extremely difficult, even for Chu Feng.","“Don’t worry about it. Have a good rest.”","Chu Feng patted Huangfu Shengyu’s shoulder with a smile before returning to the rune formation. He continued observing the runes as if nothing had happened.","However, the crowd noticed that Chu Feng was being attacked twice as much as Yuwen Yanri even though the two were standing side by side. Before he had escorted Huangfu Shengyu out of the rune formation, the attacks from the aura bodies were equally distributed between them.","“Haa! My obstinacy has harmed Chu Feng!” Huangfu Shengyu felt ashamed he had dragged Chu Feng down.","“That rune formation is frighteningly powerful. No one other than young friend Chu Feng could have saved you. Our Huangfu Heavenly Clan owes young friend Chu Feng a huge favor,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said with a sigh.","“You do owe him a favor, but you’re thinking too much. Take a closer look. Even Yuwen Yanri is frowning now, but do you see the slightest crease on Chu Feng’s face?” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“He’s completely unfazed. What kind of willpower does he possess?!” someone from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion exclaimed in disbelief.","Yuwen Yanri was constantly tortured by the Blazing Sun Divine Body before his complete assimilation of it, but that also tempered his willpower, allowing him to stand strong in the face of adversities.","And this rune formation was a trial of one’s willpower and concentration.","Both Chu Feng and Yuwen Yanri possessed the required concentration, so the question was whether they had the willpower to withstand the rune formation’s mental attacks.","Yuwen Yanri’s willpower was already at an insurmountable level, towering over most prodigies, but Chu Feng’s willpower was even stronger than that. How could the crowd not be shocked by this?","No one was born with strong willpower; it had to be slowly tempered over time.","Even the experts present couldn’t fathom how anyone could train their willpower to this extent."]},{"number":6394,"title":"Chapter 6394: Chapter 6392: Rank Six True God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6392: Rank Six True God","While attacking Chu Feng and Yuwen Yanri, the rune formation continued to transform, becoming increasingly brilliant. Eventually, it emanated a brilliant light that manifested as an opaque light sphere, isolating the two from the others.","“The runes do harness martial enlightenment!”","The crowd could sense the martial enlightenment now, but they couldn’t grasp it outside the rune formation. Even if they were inside the rune formation, the martial enlightenment was so profound that it was beyond their reach.","“The rune formation is complete now. They are now at a critical phase,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","Whoosh!","The light sphere suddenly shattered. Countless light fragments scattered like glowing butterflies. The runes reverted to their original form.","Chu Feng and Yuwen Yanri finally reappeared.","Yuwen Yanri was dripping sweat and gasping for air, but his aura was stable. He had a rare, excited grin on his face. Even though he didn’t make a breakthrough, he gained a lot from this. Even the experience itself was valuable, perhaps even more so than his other gains.","As for Chu Feng, he didn’t even break a sweat.","“It was exhilarating even though the martial enlightenment wasn’t enough for a breakthrough. Don’t you agree, Brother Chu Feng?” Yuwen Yanri turned to Chu Feng with a smile. He enjoyed the process of deciphering the runes together with the latter.","To his surprise, Chu Feng was seated with crossed legs.","Boom!","There was suddenly a flash of lightning. By the time the crowd raised their heads, the sky had already turned pitch black. Nine-colored lightning bolted through the storm clouds as if flaunting its overwhelming destructive prowess.","It was a phenomenon.","The lightning bolted down on Chu Feng before dissipating.","Yuwen Yanri revealed a conflicted smile. “I guess there’s still a gap between me and Brother Chu Feng.”","Chu Feng had made a breakthrough to rank six True God level.","“There’s a huge gap even among prodigies,” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master remarked.","He had always thought his grandson, Yuwen Yanri, was in no way inferior to Chu Feng, just that Yuwen Yanri preferred to keep a low profile and was thus not as well-known. But this incident made him realize that despite Yuwen Yanri’s talent, he was still lacking compared to Chu Feng.","“How are you feeling?” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief smiled at Huangfu Zhantian.","“There’s no way to compete with that monster,” Huangfu Zhantian replied with a smile. He switched to voice transmission and added, “That’s why it was the right call to befriend Chu Feng.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief nodded in response. He agreed with that sentiment.","“That’s all there is to the bonus. I’ll be deciphering the secret here now,” Chu Feng said.","He was feeling revitalized after his breakthrough. Rank six True God level still wasn’t enough for him to rival Heavenly Gods, but he was at least a step closer to that. Once he reached Heavenly God level, he wouldn’t have to continue treading so carefully anymore.","Chu Feng began arranging the runes. It was a straightforward trial, but it would take some time for him to get the correct sequence.","...","Jie Mubai had been in a bad mood since fleeing from that realm.","It was beyond his means to deal with a rank three Heavenly God level. He considered seeking the Zhao Immortal Clan’s help, but he had heard they were on close terms with Chu Feng, too.","So, despite his indignation, he could only give up on the treasure and scour the Immemorial Cemetery for other fortuitous encounters.","Soon, he noticed an extraordinary tombstone realm. A name had surfaced on the tombstone realm, suggesting that someone had deciphered the tombstone.","Thus, he entered the tombstone realm.","A group was inheriting the legacy, and they were on the verge of completion. That was exactly what he wanted. He could kill them and steal their gains.","But he hesitated upon taking a closer look. Not only did he not reveal himself, but he even reinforced his concealment formation.","It was a small group, numbering only 1111 people. They wore hooded world spiritist cloaks, but deer horns could be seen extending from the hoods. Masks concealed their faces, though their golden eyes remained visible.","They weren’t humans.","“It’s them? I didn’t expect them to be this powerful.”","Jie Mubai had heard that a mysterious power was publicly searching for Chu Feng, and their appearances resembled the group before him. But he held back not because they were involved with Chu Feng but because of their strength.","To his bewilderment, these 1111 people were all rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were extremely rare in the world of cultivation, so it was unthinkable for this small group of 1111 to be all rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. Anyone else in his place would have been astonished.","But that was also not why he dared not plunder them. The true reason was that the formation they were constructing harnessed the strength of a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“The world of cultivation is filled with many hidden experts,” Jie Mubai remarked.","He had always viewed himself as a highly knowledgeable and talented individual. He believed that he would have surpassed Jie Tianran if not for his young age. There was also very little in the world of cultivation that he didn’t know about.","But he had never heard about these people.","Not even an army of rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists could construct a formation comparable to that of a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. This group of people must possess some kind of special power that allowed them to pull off that feat.","Jie Mubai quietly observed the golden-eyed, deer-horned world spiritists till they completed the legacy inheritance. Before he could show himself, a woman’s voice echoed from the group, “You have been observing us for some time now. What do you want?”","All the world spiritists simultaneously turned their gaze to Jie Mubai.","The one who had just spoken was likely the leader of their group.","“My apologies. I was awed by your incredible means. May I know which power do you belong to?” Jie Mubai asked.","He stepped out and revealed himself, though he wrapped his world spiritist cloak around his face to hide his appearance. Those world spiritists might have seen through his concealment formation, but his world spiritist cloak was an extraordinary treasure. He didn’t think they could see through it.","“You should introduce yourself before asking about someone’s background. Surely you shouldn’t be foreign to basic etiquette?” the woman spoke once more.","The air turned cold. Jie Mubai understood that the other party would attack him if he couldn’t provide them with a satisfactory answer.","“It was by coincidence I stumbled upon this tombstone realm, but I have news for you. You are searching for Chu Feng, right? I know where he is,” Jie Mubai said.","“You know where Chu Feng is?” the woman asked.","“I do, but may I know what you want from him?” Jie Mubai asked.","“We have a mission to capture him alive,” the woman replied."]},{"number":6395,"title":"Chapter 6395: Chapter 6393: The Spirit God Clan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6393: The Spirit God Clan","“That’s good. I have a grudge against Chu Feng, too. I know where he is, and I can bring you there, but it won’t be easy to capture him. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion are protecting him. The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion isn’t a threat, but the Huangfu Heavenly Clan has a rank three Heavenly God. Are you able to deal with that?”","Jie Mubai had no idea why this group wanted to capture Chu Feng, and he didn’t think they would tell him even if he asked. However, he could fathom a guess.","The Immemorial Cemetery was filled with fortuitous encounters, but the greatest fortuitous encounter was still none other than Chu Feng. Who didn’t covet the treasures Chu Feng had?","No world spiritist could resist the allure of Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline, the strongest world spiritist bloodline.","“A rank three Heavenly God doesn’t pose a threat to us, but why should we trust you?” the woman asked.","“Even a rank three Heavenly God doesn’t pose a threat to you. A rank two Heavenly Dragon like me would be courting death by deceiving you,” Jie Mubai pointed out.","Those words were convincing.","“What do you stand to gain by leading us to Chu Feng?” the woman asked.","“I worked with Chu Feng to activate a tombstone, but that despicable fellow turned on me once the tombstone was activated so that he could monopolize the rewards. You can have Chu Feng, but I want the tombstone’s legacy,” Jie Mubai replied.","“Lead the way,” the woman said.","...","Some time passed.","Chu Feng was still arranging the runes. He did make some progress, but the high difficulty of the trial left him a little unnerved. It further drove in how unfathomable the Immemorial Cemetery was to him.","He wasn’t confident of overcoming this challenge.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","A golden light suddenly appeared on the horizon. Golden rays pierced through the air, and it only took moments for the entire sky to be suffused in golden light.","“Get in formation!” a Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder shouted as he rushed into their warship.","The other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen followed suit. Huangfu Zhantian even activated his Lightning Mark and Lightning Armor. They were using their bloodline powers to channel the warship’s formation.","They were uptight because they sensed that the golden light was a formation harnessing a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist’s spirit power. This wasn’t going to be an easy battle.","Even Chu Feng stopped arranging the runes to look at the horizon.","1111 world spiritists emerged from the golden light, but there was an individual accompanying them who looked out of place.","“Jie Mubai?” Chu Feng recognized the individual even though his face was concealed. “You have returned with helpers.”","He knew that Jie Mubai wouldn’t let things rest so easily, but he thought the latter would not dare to make a move in the Immemorial Cemetery out of deference for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","But he had underestimated Jie Mubai.","He, too, could tell that these mysterious world spiritists were the ones who had been looking for him.","“Chu Feng, you only have yourself to blame for making so many enemies,” Jie Mubai sneered as he took off his hood and revealed his face.","Much to everyone’s surprise, the mysterious world spiritists took off their hoods and masks to reveal their faces as well. They weren’t humans, evident from their deer horns, ears, noses, and golden eyes, but they didn’t look terrifying or ugly. Instead, they had an exotic kind of beauty.","The most beautiful one in the group was the leader. She had a tall stature and a dignified demeanor.","The others also commanded an air of loftiness.","All of them simultaneously formed a hand seal.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief tensed up. He was ready to give the order for his clansmen to channel their formation to deal with those world spiritists at any moment... but that order was never issued.","The mysterious world spiritists’ formation transformed into a chain, and that chain surged toward not the Huangfu Heavenly Clan nor Chu Feng, but Jie Mubai!","It was a formation harnessing spirit power comparable to a rank three Heavenly Dragon, not to mention it was cast at close range. Jie Mubai was bound before he even had the time to react.","The crowd, including Jie Mubai, was dumbstruck.","“Why are you capturing me?” Jie Mubai glared at the mysterious world spiritists.","But none of the mysterious world spiritists paid him any heed. All of them descended to the ground and bowed deeply to Chu Feng.","“I am Shen Hui from the Spirit God Clan. I have come with my Spirit God Clansmen to pay respect to Lord Chu Feng,” the woman said.","The others behind her greeted, “Paying respect to Lord Chu Feng.”","“Ah? Are they on our side? And it’s the leegndary Spirit God Clan at that! Chu Feng, where do you find such formidable subordinates from? You should have told us earlier!” Huangfu Zhantian exclaimed.","“It’s... my first time meeting them,” Chu Feng explained.","“Huh? What does that mean? Are they trying to trick us?”","Startled, Huangfu Zhantian looked at the Spirit God Clansmen with wary eyes. The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s members tensed up. They feared that the Spirit God Clansmen were feigning intimacy to launch a surprise assault.","“Lord Chu Feng, Lord Xue Ji has ordered us to aid you,” the woman named Shen Hui added.","“You harlots! You said earlier that you received a mission to capture Chu Feng alive! How did it turn into aiding him? How dare you lie to me!” Jie Mubai cursed through gritted teeth.","He didn’t even lash out when Chu Feng one-upped him twice. He must have been truly infuriated to start cursing like that.","Shen Hui paid no heed to him and continued her report, “Lord Chu Feng, we couldn’t find you, so we went to decipher a remnant instead. This person suddenly appeared and told us your whereabouts.","“I sensed he harbors ill will toward you, so I claimed we were under orders to capture you alive to see how he would respond. He confessed that he harbors a grudge against you, and he wants our help to steal this legacy.","“Despite our skepticism, we still followed him because we were anxious to find you. We were pleasantly surprised to see you here. Lord Chu Feng, allow me to hand this man over to you to deal with.”","“Kill him,” Chu Feng said.","“Understood.”","Shen Hui formed a hand seal.","The chains binding Jie Mubai transformed into knives and shredded him into pieces. Blood splattered all over the place."]},{"number":6396,"title":"Chapter 6396: Chapter 6394: Xue Ji’s News","paragraphs":["Chapter 6394: Xue Ji’s News","“Something is not right.”","Chu Feng and Shen Hui narrowed their eyes.","Jie Mubai’s corpse scattered as spirit power. A piece of talisman paper drifted out from his body and was burned into ashes.","Jie Mubai’s voice echoed from space, “You’ll regret this, Spirit God Clan. You’ll soon come to learn who you have offended. Chu Feng, you shouldn’t be too smug either. I’ll show you what I’m capable of in due time.”","Shen Hui formed a hand seal. The golden light enveloping the tombstone realm dispersed into countless golden dragons, and these golden dragons surged in the direction Jie Mubai’s voice originated from.","“Don’t bother giving chase. You won’t catch him,” Chu Feng said.","Shen Hui soon dispelled the formation as she realized Chu Feng was right.","The voice had come from a formation; Jie Mubai wasn’t there. Jie Mubai was infuriated at having been tricked by the Spirit God Clansmen, but the truth was that he had never trusted them, which was why he used a talisman paper clone instead.","And despite being rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, Shen Hui and the others failed to see through the talisman paper clone.","Shen Hui hung her head in shame as she bowed to Chu Feng once more. “Lord Chu Feng, please punish me for my incompetence.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, Huangfu Zhantian, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, and the others flitted to Chu Feng’s side.","“Chu Feng, I don’t think they are feigning loyalty to you. Do you know the ‘Lord Xue Ji’ they mentioned?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","They weren’t bothered about Jie Mubai’s escape, as this group of mysterious world spiritists was the bigger threat here. They needed to ascertain their motive first.","“Yes, I know her,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is she your friend?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“You can say so.” Chu Feng smiled.","His relationship with Xue Ji was complicated.","Both Xue Ji and Eggy were world spirits his mother had captured and placed in his World Spirit Space. Unlike Eggy, Xue Ji was much more rebellious. She left Chu Feng’s side as soon as her seal was removed.","At the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm, she was captured by Old Cat, but Old Cat didn’t make things difficult for her and instead became her friend.","Later, Xue Ji found a helper called the Demon Spirit King.","Initially, Chu Feng doubted Old Cat’s words and wanted to meet Xue Ji to get to the bottom of the matter. It was during then he bumped into one of the World Spiritist Emperor’s world spirits, Taowu, who gave Eggy the Godsoul.","Xue Ji could have competed with Eggy over the Godsoul, but she gave up.","Since then, Chu Feng had never met Xue Ji.","Even though Chu Feng knew Xue Ji had the ability to thrive no matter her environment, he didn’t expect her to be related to the Spirit God Clan. The Spirit God Clan was extremely powerful—they had 1111 rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, and they were capable of constructing a formation rivaling that of a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","Their special means reminded Chu Feng of the God Clan, who kidnapped the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","At the same time, he was also reminded of another entity—the Spirit God. That was the woman in the Nine Heavens Secret Domain who bestowed him the Three Realms Divine Eyes.","The Spirit God looked humanlike—she didn’t have any deer traits—but there were some similarities between her Three Realms Divine Eyes and the Spirit God Clansmen’s eyes.","The Three Realms Divine Eyes contained three colors—purple, blue, and golden. The golden shade was similar to the Spirit God Clansmen’s golden eyes, to the point where Chu Feng wondered if they were from the same lineage.","“Elder, you seem to have heard about the Spirit God Clan,” Chu Feng asked Huangfu Zhantian.","“I have heard about them. The Spirit God Clan is powerful but enigmatic. They have few clansmen and are very elusive, to the point where they were considered a myth in the Ancient Era. They specialize in world spiritist techniques, possessing formidable spirit power and highly discerning eyes. These women carry the traits of the Ancient Era’s Spirit God Clan.","“I did hear a group of people was looking for you, though I didn’t think much into it when I first heard about their traits. Judging from their appearance and their proficiency as world spiritists, there is a good chance they are truly the legendary Spirit God Clansmen,” Huangfu Zhantian replied.","Meanwhile, the Spirit God Clansmen remained perfectly still in their kneeling positions. It was shocking to see experts of their caliber putting themselves so low, to the point where Chu Feng felt a little embarrassed.","After hearing Huangfu Zhantian’s analysis, Chu Feng quickly turned to them and said, “Hurry up and get up. There’s no need for such formalities.”","“Thank you, Lord Chu Feng.”","Only then did the Spirit God Clansmen stand up.","“It’s not that I don’t trust you, but there are too many people in the world of cultivation who wishes harm upon me. I have to be vigilant,” Chu Feng explained","“Lord Chu Feng, it hasn’t been long since we emerged from closed-door training, but we have heard about your affairs and understand the plight you are in. Please feel free to ask anything to verify our identities,” Shen Hui said.","“You said Xue Ji sent you to me. Do you know how Xue Ji looks?” Chu Feng asked.","A sliver of spirit power flew forth from Shen Hui’s palm to form the image of a beautiful woman. It was indeed Xue Ji.","“You addressed Xue Ji as your lord earlier. May I know how you met Xue Ji, and what kind of relationship you have with her that compels you to follow her order to help a stranger like me?”","Shen Hui sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng explaining their relationship with Xue Ji.","To summarize, the seal that isolated the Spirit God Clan from the rest of the world was far stronger than those isolating other powers. That prevented them from keeping tabs on what was happening outside despite their high proficiency in world spiritist techniques.","Xue Ji somehow entered their domain, and many things happened afterward. In gist, the Spirit God Clan owed their lives to her. Before she left, Xue Ji told them to look for him if they wanted to repay the favor.","So, they left the domain they had been sealed in and traveled around the world in search of Chu Feng.","“Lord Chu Feng.” Shen Hui walked up to Chu Feng.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and Huangfu Zhantian didn’t stop her, but they continued staring at Shen Hui with wary eyes.","Shen Hui flicked her wrist, and a bead drifted toward Chu Feng. “This is from Lord Xue Ji.”","As a world spiritist, Chu Feng could tell the bead posed no danger; it merely contained a message. He pressed the bead against his head. The bead shattered, and its fragments disintegrated into an aura and seeped into his head.","Through the bead, Chu Feng sensed Xue Ji’s aura and saw her silhouette in his mind. She was as ravishing as before, but her disposition had gotten stronger.","Even though he had always called Eggy ‘Milady Queen’, it was more of a joke. Eggy was more like an eccentric girl.","Rather, Xue Ji felt more like a queen.","The Xue Ji in Chu Feng’s mind smiled at him, displaying neither enmity nor adoration. It felt like she was speaking to an acquaintance instead. “You two owe me a favor. I expect the favor to be returned when you get to the Ninth Galaxy in the future... assuming that you can catch up with me.”","Xue Ji’s silhouette dissipated from his mind.","She didn’t bother explaining her relationship with the Spirit God Clan; there was no need for her to do so, as no one could imitate her disposition. The bead was enough to prove the Spirit God Clansmen’s reliability."]},{"number":6397,"title":"Chapter 6397: Chapter 6395: The Spirit God Clan’s Capability","paragraphs":["Chapter 6395: The Spirit God Clan’s Capability","“Oh? It sounds like Xue Ji has gotten very powerful?” Eggy remarked.","Xue Ji’s words suggested that she was far ahead of Chu Feng and Eggy.","“Regardless, we owe her a favor for this.” Chu Feng felt moved.","It would be a lie for him to say that he had no feelings for Xue Ji. She had grown up with him, even though she had been sealed inside him, and there was no interaction between them then.","Xue Ji had a legitimate reason for wanting to kill Chu Feng, since she was captured by his mother to serve him. To Chu Feng, that was his mother’s show of affection, but to Xue Ji, she was kidnapped and exploited. Her family must have been worried about her, or else Yu Sha wouldn’t have traveled here to look for her.","In this aspect, Chu Feng owed Xue Ji.","He wouldn’t have any complaints even if Xue Ji viewed him as her enemy, but the latter didn’t do so. Instead, she turned around and helped him. That was why he was moved.","“I have troubled you.” Chu Feng bowed to the Spirit God Clansmen.","Even though Xue Ji had already left, they still heeded Xue Ji’s instructions and traveled here to help him. This showed that the Spirit God Clan was a highly credible clan.","“Lord Chu Feng, we’re just doing what we should. We have the means to help Lord Chu Feng attain spirit power comparable to a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. Do you require it?” Shen Hui asked.","“How did you obtain such an ability?” Chu Feng was startled.","“In essence, it is just me temporarily lending my spirit power to Lord Chu Feng,” Shen Hui explained.","“Will it be easy to pull off?” Chu Feng asked.","“It won’t be too difficult.”","“I’ll be troubling you for it.”","Spirit power was the foundation of a world spiritist. The stronger his spirit power was, the stronger his foundation would be. Naturally, his observation prowess would be strengthened even with just a temporary boost in his spirit power.","“I’ll need some time, Lord Chu Feng,” Shen Hui said before she began constructing a formation.","Everyone closely observed the formation, hoping to learn a thing or two from it. They quickly realized they couldn’t use the formation to achieve the same effect, and this included Chu Feng too.","This formation was built on the Spirit God Clan’s bloodline power, so this means was unique to them.","Once the formation was completed, Chu Feng stepped into the formation core and felt tremendous spirit power surging into his body. It was extremely gentle, allowing him to fuse with it impeccably.","The spirit power swiftly surged into his body, and when it overpowered his spirit power, his spirit power was sealed off. Fortunately, he still retained his abilities, so he could still construct formations, activate Heaven’s Eyes, and employ the Three Realms Divine Eyes he had received from the Spirit God.","The only downside was that he had lost his superior fighting prowess, though it was worth noting that the Spirit God Clansmen were decently strong as well.","“You rivaled a rank three Heavenly God earlier. Can I do the same?” Chu Feng asked.","In truth, he already had an answer to that question—it was unlikely he could employ the Spirit God Clan’s means. However, it was still worth asking.","“Lord Chu Feng, that’s our clan’s means. I’m afraid both means cannot be used simultaneously,” Shen Hui replied.","“I understand.”","Chu Feng continued arranging the runes, but this time, he was much faster than before. Even the rank three Heavenly God level Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief struggled to follow his movements, let alone the others.","And it was not just about the speed but the complexity as well.","“Damn. I can’t imagine what Chu Feng will be capable of once he becomes a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist!” Huangfu Zhantian exclaimed.","He had already raised his cultivation to rank three Heavenly God level to follow Chu Feng’s movements, but like the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, he was unable to follow the runes when so many of them were simultaneously moving.","He did have some understanding of formations too, albeit to a shallow level, but he could still easily tell that Chu Feng’s world spiritist techniques were vastly different from those of other world spiritists.","The advancement in spirit power greatly boosted Chu Feng’s efficiency.","Soon, he finished arranging all the runes, but the runes immediately scattered around the tombstone realm. The runes flickered between a black light and a golden light, as if symbolizing a fight between the light and the dark as they wrestled for control.","“This feeling!”","Horror appeared on the crowd’s faces, be it the Spirit God Clansmen or the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen. Even the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragons panicked. They felt death pulsating from those runes, and it was so overpowering that they dared not dream of fighting against it.","It was a hopeless fight.","In their despair, they turned to Chu Feng. No one understood these runes better than Chu Feng, so he was the only one who could resolve this issue.","“Please don’t make a reckless move. Leave it to me,” Chu Feng said as he began constructing a formation. The formation swiftly expanded to the point where it covered the sky.","“Chu Feng, this formation is very dangerous. Do you have to do this?” Shen Hui asked.","She had already realized what Chu Feng planned to do.","Chu Feng was seeking to draw the runes into his body through his formation to finish the arrangement of the runes. However, that was an extremely dangerous thing to do. The slightest misstep could result in the dissipation of his soul.","“This is the only way,” Chu Feng replied as he drew the vast formation into his body.","He changed his hand seal.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The runes swiftly converged into his body like shooting stars."]},{"number":6398,"title":"Chapter 6398: Chapter 6396: The Ninth Galaxy’s Entrance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6396: The Ninth Galaxy’s Entrance","Everyone was worried for Chu Feng.","There were countless runes around them, and each of them harnessed devastating energy. Even one was already beyond their means to deal with, but so many of them were converging into Chu Feng’s body at a shocking speed.","Fortunately, Chu Feng seemed to harness another realm inside him, allowing him to hold those runes without worrying about his capacity. He remained perfectly calm as those runes entered his body, not showing the slightest pain at all.","The crowd had no choice but to trust him.","The runes were finally all drawn into Chu Feng’s body, but no one dared to utter the word. Not only did the dangerous aura not disappear, but it felt even more intense than before now that they were concentrated in a single spot.","The threat wasn’t over yet.","The earlier arrangement of the runes served to draw out their true power, and Chu Feng drawing them into his body was only the first step. What he needed to do now was to fuse the runes inside his body together to form a complete formation.","This formation couldn’t be manifested outside. It needed a medium, and the medium had to be a person. And Chu Feng was the medium.","He had to construct the formation to peer into the Immemorial Cemetery’s secrets.","Soon, the dangerous aura vanished.","Yuwen Yanri’s gaze changed. A brilliant light shone from his chest.","“Yanri, what’s wrong?”","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s experts gathered around Yuwen Yanri, afraid that the latter would meet with a mishap. Fortunately, his condition remained stable despite the light shining from his chest, and even the light soon disappeared.","It felt like the light was merely to draw their attention.","Yuwen Yanri took off his shirt and noticed a change in the rune imprint on his chest.","This rune imprint had fallen on his chest when he accepted the legacy from the earlier tombstone realm. Shortly after, the entire tombstone realm glowed as if he had obtained some kind of tremendous power.","Back then, the rune imprint was pitch black, and there was nothing special about it. Now, it was emanating a dim light, and it felt much more divine than before.","“I can feel it now. Chu Feng, I can feel it now!” Yuwen Yanri exclaimed.","Chu Feng must have done something to result in the change in his rune imprint.","“You’re indeed one of them, Brother Yuwen.” Chu Feng looked at Yuwen Yanri with a smile, his expression suggesting that he must have figured something out.","“One of them? What are you referring to?” Yuwen Yanri asked.","Chu Feng descended to Yuwen Yanri’s side as he explained, “The Seven Stars Orbs are the crux to escaping from this place. The Seven Stars Orbs refer to seven tombstone realms, and the tombstone realm you inherited a legacy from is one. As you received the rune imprint, the tombstone realm was imbued with star power. Your rune imprint is the key to channeling that star power.”","“I sense the star power, but I don’t think I can control it yet. It seems to be sealed,” Yuwen Yanri said.","“That tombstone realm’s star power has been unsealed, but you’ll only be able to channel it after the remaining six tombstone realms have been unsealed,” Chu Feng explained.","“So, we have to unseal the seven stars, channel the star power, and break the Immemorial Cemetery’s seal in order to escape from this place?” Yuwen Yanri clarified.","“That’s right,” Chu Feng replied.","“Where are the six remaining stars?” Huangfu Zhantian and the others walked over and asked.","They were concerned about this as their lives were at stake.","“I can sense the locations of the first three stars. The first one is the tombstone realm, where Brother Yuwen obtained his legacy. The second one is further away, deep in the Immemorial Cemetery, and it appears someone has obtained it. The third one is not too far away from us, and someone is currently deciphering its legacy,” Chu Feng explained.","“What should we do, Chu Feng?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“The second star is too far away, and someone has already obtained it. There’s no point heading there now. Let’s head to the third star.”","The others agreed with Chu Feng’s decision, and they immediately set forth.","Chu Feng, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, Huangfu Zhantian, Huangfu Shengyu, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, Yuwen Yanri, Shen Hui, and the other Spirit God Clansmen were gathered inside one of the warships’ palaces.","“Why do you look so worried?” Chu Feng asked.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you mentioned we’ll need all seven stars, but someone else has obtained the second star. Only the person who deciphered that tombstone can wield its star power, right? We’ll need that person to escape from the Immemorial Cemetery, but finding an individual in this vast space is as good as searching for a needle in the ocean,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“You don’t need to worry about that. The rune formation in my body connects me to the Seven Stars Orbs. I can only sense three stars at the moment, but the connection deepens with time. Eventually, I’ll be able to pinpoint the locations of those who have obtained keys to the star power. On top of that, the key returns to the star when a key holder dies, so we can reclaim it,” Chu Feng replied.","“I see. I guess there’s no need for us to worry too much.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master heaved a sigh of relief. This meant they could locate all key holders to cooperate with them, and if they refused to listen, they could just kill them and re-obtain the keys.","“But there’s something we need to worry about.”","“Something we need to worry about?”","The crowd became tense once more. Something Chu Feng needed to worry about must be extremely concerning for them.","“Each person can only obtain one legacy of the Seven Stars Orbs. Now that Brother Yuwen has obtained one, he won’t be able to claim the legacies of the other stars. I can take on one legacy as well, but only one. Brother Shengyu, you might have to take on a legacy too,” Chu Feng said.","“Haa. I’m not confident about that. I’ll give it my all, but I might still require your help in the end,” Huangfu Shengyu said.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief felt bitter inside.","Huangfu Shengyu had thought he was an extraordinary person from a young age due to his superior bloodline. Confidence was something he had never lacked. Yet, to think a day would come when he declared his strength was limited! His failure to grasp the martial enlightenment earlier must have been a huge blow to him.","Huangfu Zhantian placed his hand on the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief’s shoulders and relayed a voice transmission, “It’s not a bad thing for him to know his shortcomings.”","“Mm.” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief nodded.","“Chu Feng, are you worried that we won’t be able to claim the remaining legacies? Is there an age restriction to the Seven Stars Orbs’ legacies?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“There is no age restriction, but it’s no easy feat to obtain one. However, our biggest concern is not the legacies,” Chu Feng replied.","“Ah? What is it?”","“Lying in the Immemorial Cemetery is an entrance to the Ninth Galaxy.”"]},{"number":6399,"title":"Chapter 6399: Chapter 6397: Heaven Gate","paragraphs":["Chapter 6397: Heaven Gate","“An entrance to the Ninth Galaxy? Aren’t we already able to enter the Ninth Galaxy from the world of cultivation? Is there a difference between this entrance and directly entering the Ninth Galaxy from the world of cultivation?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master and Yuwen Yanri looked at Chu Feng with curious eyes. They were already planning to enter the Ninth Galaxy, so this matter was of great interest to them.","“That’s right. This entrance transports us to a location in the Ninth Galaxy that is highly suitable for cultivation—it is rich in resources and natural energies, and it contains great treasures and fortuitous encounters, too. Cultivating at a place like that will be highly beneficial. That’s why this entrance is also known as the Heaven Gate.”","The eyes of Huangfu Zhantian and the others lit up.","“Holy shit! Isn’t that the same as getting to choose where we reincarnate? Others are randomly assigned to different places, but we get to pick a winning hand right away!” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“Err... The analogy isn’t very apt, but the idea is there.” Chu Feng chuckled.","Reincarnation implied starting from scratch, but they were merely entering a foreign place with their memories and cultivation intact.","...","“Eesh. At least my idea was there!","“Chu Feng, this is a rare opportunity. Why don’t we just enter the Ninth Galaxy from here? There’s no point fussing about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion at this juncture. You should prioritize raising your cultivation. With your talent, I’m sure you can quash them with a finger in due time. We can also just ignore the God’s Era; no one was able to claim it in the Ancient Era anyway.”","Huangfu Zhantian was excited. He was already imagining a brilliant life in the Ninth Galaxy.","“This is a huge fortuitous encounter. I should have brought all my members here with me,” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master remarked. He was regretful that not all their members were currently here with them.","“Hold on and hear me out first. I don’t mean it as good news,” Chu Feng clarified.","“Ah?” The crowd was baffled.","“The Heaven Gate has to be activated first, and only one person can enter,” Chu Feng said.","Those words chilled everyone’s expectations.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you really have to say that faster next time. You lit a fire in my heart, only to put it out right away. I’m getting old and can’t take such excitement,” Huangfu Zhantian grumbled in disappointment.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked, “How is the Heaven Gate activated?”","“There should be multiple ways to activate it, but I only know one right now, and that’s to sacrifice all lives within the Immemorial Cemetery,” Chu Feng said.","“Sacrifice all lives?”","The faces of the crowd crumbled. But what Chu Feng said next further drove in the stake.","“I had to make a choice earlier when I obtained the rune formation,” Chu Feng added.","“Ah. That explains why the runes kept flickering between light and dark. Young friend Chu Feng, what did you choose?”","The crowd looked at Chu Feng with worried eyes. Chu Feng would benefit no matter the decision he made, but the ‘dark’ option was likely detrimental to all of them. Thus, they were concerned about his decision.","“I chose the light path,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He raised his palm and revealed a golden rune that glowed with a divine light.","“Young friend Chu Feng, what do the choices mean?” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master asked.","“For the light path, I’ll have to complete the Seven Stars Orb, lift the seal, and bring everyone out safely. However, I need to accomplish this feat within a limited time. For the dark path, the goal is to hinder the completion of the Seven Stars Orbs till time runs out, and everyone will be sacrificed to open the Heaven Gate for them. There should be more to the dark path, but I have no way of knowing, as I didn’t pick that. Also, I have a feeling that someone has grasped the rune formation before me,” Chu Feng said.","“You’re saying that someone obtained that terrifying rune formation like you did?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master was taken aback. “That can’t be, right? Someone other than young friend Chu Feng deciphered the rune formation as well?”","“The rune formation may manifest in different forms, but its difficulty level should be similar. Yes, I am certain someone else has grasped the secret of this place. We have a formidable opponent here,” Chu Feng said.","“This...”","The crowd looked grim. It would take someone incredible to grasp the formation, but it would be disastrous if that person had chosen the dark path.","‘Young friend Chu Feng, can you sense that person’s decision? Could that person have chosen the light path like us?” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master asked.","“I can’t sense that person’s decision, but it is possible. I just fear that person might have chosen the dark path,” Chu Feng said.","“What’s there to guess? Not everyone is as sentimental as Chu Feng. That is an opportunity to leap ahead of others in the Ninth Galaxy! How can anyone resist that temptation? To put things bluntly, I would have chosen the dark path without any hesitation if there were no other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen here. If that decision was presented to me now, I’d likely still hesitate quite a bit,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","Those words were blunt, but no one criticized him. It was normal to be conflicted when presented with such a decision. Romance and kinship meant little before such tremendous benefits.","Countless brothers had fallen out over their parents’ inheritance. Countless children had forsaken their parents over a bit of money. Humans were innately selfish, and one shouldn’t underestimate one they were capable of when the allure was this big."]},{"number":6400,"title":"Chapter 6400: Chapter 6398: Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint’s Tombstone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6398: Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint’s Tombstone","That was why selfless people shone brightly. They defied human nature, and that was something most people were incapable of.","Chu Feng didn’t think he was a selfless person, as he wouldn’t hesitate to prioritize his friends over others, but he would occasionally step in to help the weak despite not being obliged to. That was why many thought that he was a selfless person.","To him, his friends were always the highest priority. Benefits were secondary. Many times, he had put his life on the line to rescue his friends. This was why so many people acknowledged him.","Huangfu Zhantian’s words jolted the crowd awake.","People like Chu Feng numbered in the minority. If someone else had grasped the rune formation, the chances were that they had chosen the dark path.","“It looks like we’re in a dire position. We shouldn’t have come in here.” The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master’s voice sounded regretful.","They were already planning to enter the Ninth Galaxy, and with Yuwen Yanri’s talent, his cultivation would surely leap ahead once they were there. It was only a matter of time before the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion became known throughout the world.","It was out of a moment of greed that they stepped into the Immemorial Cemetery. They did stumble upon a fortuitous encounter and obtained it, but it also plunged them into fatal danger. They could very well become someone else’s stepping stone into the Ninth Galaxy.","“Haa, what’s the point of saying that now? There’s no need to be so down. We have Chu Feng on our side. We have seen what Chu Feng is capable of. With him around, the enemy should be the one despairing. I’m sure he will have a way out, right?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","He was the most optimistic of everyone present.","“It’s only a conjecture that we might have a strong adversary, but even if that’s true, we have a shot at victory. We just need to grasp the Seven Stars Orbs,” Chu Feng replied.","“What’s the time limit?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“I can’t sense it at the moment, but I should feel it as the deadline approaches,” Chu Feng said.","“We’ll make it work,” Huangfu Zhantian declared.","“Of course.” Chu Feng nodded with a smile.","The things he had shared unnerved the powerhouses present, but he remained calm from the start to the end. Even though his power was meager in the unfathomable Immemorial Cemetery, he believed he could surmount the challenge.","This was the confidence he had built up through the experiences he had been through. These hurdles only looked tall because they were blocking his path; once he overcame them, it would be nothing more than a road he had walked past.","He had been through such situations many times before.","Traversing across vast space, the third star soon came into sight.","They couldn’t peer into the tombstone realm due to the formation around it, but they could see words on the tombstone from a far distance away—the Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint’s Tombstone.","To avoid attention, the Spirit God Clan constructed a formation to conceal the group. They had already retracted the spirit power they had granted Chu Feng, as it would take a toll on them to maintain it for a long time.","The group entered the tombstone realm and soon arrived at the tombstone within.","“Brother Bai?”","Chu Feng was startled. The person standing beneath the tombstone was a familiar face—Bai Yunqing!","Bai Yunqing had constructed a profound formation to accept the legacy. Much to Chu Feng’s shock, Bai Yunqing was a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist!","“How did Bai Yunqing become so powerful?” Eggy was taken aback.","“Chu Feng, isn’t that person your friend? I think his name is Bai Qingqing or something, right?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“What Bai Qingqing? He’s Bai Yunqing,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief corrected him.","They had done a thorough investigation on Chu Feng—they knew Chu Feng’s friends, his roots with the Chu Heavenly Clan, and that his father was Chu Xuanyuan. Naturally, they knew about Bai Yunqing too.","“Right right, Bai Yunqing! He’s your friend, right?” Huangfu Zhantian asked once more.","This was good news for them. They needed to gain control over the seven stars, so it would be ideal if the one inheriting the legacy were Chu Feng’s friend.","“He is indeed my friend.” Chu Feng nodded.","But as he approached Bai Yunqing, his heart began to sink. He sensed that Bai Yunqing’s aura was mixed with someone else’s aura—Ouyang Kongyu’s.","Ouyang Kongyu was a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist specializing in medicine. To get to the bottom of the Pill Dao Immortal Sect’s destruction, Chu Feng looked for someone to treat Jia Lingyi, and that was when he stumbled upon Ouyang Kongyu.","With Ouyang Kongyu’s help, he verified that the culprit behind the Pill Dao Immortal Sect’s destruction was his grandmother.","Ouyang Kongyu later took Bai Yunqing in as his disciple and supported Chu Feng when he fought against Baili Zilin in the Luck Saint Realm.","“What happened to Elder Ouyang Kongyu?” Chu Feng murmured.","The bulk of Bai Yunqing’s spirit power appeared to be from Ouyang Kongyu. But Chu Feng didn’t dwell too much on the matter and instead observed the tombstone. Then, he turned to Shen Hui and asked, “Elder, can you lend me your spirit power once more?”","“Of course. Lord Chu Feng, you can just call me Shen Hui,” Shen Hui said.","“All right. I’ll be troubling you, Shen Hui,” Chu Feng said.","Shen Hui constructed a formation and imbued her rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist’s spirit power into Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had to borrow Shen Hui’s powers because he sensed that the legacy here was extremely potent, likely beyond Bai Yunqing’s means to withstand. If Bai Yunqing failed, he would be killed by the legacy’s energy.","He needed to decipher the tombstone to help Bai Yunqing, and it would be much faster if he borrowed Shen Hui’s spirit power.","While Shen Hui was constructing the formation, Chu Feng had already deciphered the gist of the tombstone. Once his cultivation was raised to rank two Heavenly Dragon, he quickly picked up on the details.","However, he didn’t reveal himself and offer advice to Bai Yunqing right away.","Shouldering the legacy’s burden was beneficial to Bai Yunqing’s growth, so Chu Feng wanted Bai Yunqing to take on as much as he could.","As time passed, Bai Yunqing’s face warped under the strain. As Chu Feng had expected, it would be tough for him to withstand the legacy here on his own.","Bai Yunqing realized that himself and murmured tearfully, “Am I... going to die here? I am useless. Master, you have chosen the wrong person. Big brother Chu Feng, I won’t be able to repay the debt I owe you in this life.”","He resigned. He closed his eyes and stopped channeling the formation. He had given up.","Just then, Chu Feng’s voice echoed from the sky, “What nonsense are you spouting? How can you give up so easily?”"]}]);
